window.TWG_B1C={"level":1,"track":"beer","exam":{"questions":30,"minutes":45,"pass":70,"written":false,"tasting":false},"ch":{"b01":{"it":"Che cos'è la birra","fr":"Qu'est-ce que la bière ?","en":"What beer is"},"b02":{"it":"Malto e altre fonti di zucchero","fr":"Malt et autres sources de sucre","en":"Malt and other sugar sources"},"b03":{"it":"Le tappe della birrificazione","fr":"Les étapes du brassage","en":"The brewing steps"},"b04":{"it":"Luppolo e altri aromi","fr":"Houblon et autres aromates","en":"Hops and other flavourings"},"b05":{"it":"Il lievito","fr":"La levure","en":"Yeast"},"b06":{"it":"Degustare la birra","fr":"Déguster la bière","en":"Tasting beer"},"b07":{"it":"Stili di malto: solo malti base","fr":"Styles de malt : malts de base seuls","en":"Malt-driven styles: base malts only"},"b08":{"it":"Stili di malto: con malti speciali","fr":"Styles de malt : avec malts spéciaux","en":"Malt-driven styles: some speciality malts"},"b09":{"it":"Stili di luppolo","fr":"Styles de houblon","en":"Hop-driven styles"},"b10":{"it":"Stili di lievito","fr":"Styles de levure","en":"Yeast-driven styles"},"b11":{"it":"Stili acidi","fr":"Styles acides","en":"Sour styles"},"b12":{"it":"Conservazione e difetti","fr":"Conservation et défauts","en":"Storage and faults"},"b13":{"it":"Servire la birra","fr":"Servir la bière","en":"Serving beer"},"b14":{"it":"Birra e cibo","fr":"Bière et mets","en":"Beer and food"}},"groups":[{"k":"p","w":13,"n":{"it":"Ingredienti e produzione","fr":"Ingrédients et production","en":"Ingredients and production"},"c":["b01","b02","b03","b04","b05"]},{"k":"s","w":13,"n":{"it":"Gli stili di birra","fr":"Les styles de bière","en":"Beer styles"},"c":["b06","b07","b08","b09","b10","b11"]},{"k":"t","w":4,"n":{"it":"Conservazione, servizio e cibo","fr":"Conservation, service et mets","en":"Storage, service and food"},"c":["b12","b13","b14"]}],"bank":[{"id":"b1db39292","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Quali sono i quattro ingredienti principali della birra?","Quels sont les quatre ingrédients principaux de la bière ?","What are the four main ingredients of beer?"],"o":[["Malto, acqua, luppolo, lievito","Malt, eau, houblon, levure","Malt, water, hops, yeast"],["Riso, kōji, acqua, lievito","Riz, kōji, eau, levure","Rice, kōji, water, yeast"],["Malto, zucchero, luppolo, alcol neutro","Malt, sucre, houblon, alcool neutre","Malt, sugar, hops, neutral alcohol"],["Orzo, uva, acqua, lievito","Orge, raisin, eau, levure","Barley, grapes, water, yeast"]],"e":["Malto, acqua, luppolo e lievito sono i quattro ingredienti principali.","Malt, eau, houblon et levure sont les quatre ingrédients principaux.","Malt, water, hops and yeast are the four main ingredients."],"d":["Riso e kōji sono gli ingredienti del sake. Lo zucchero si usa a volte, ma non è uno dei quattro; l'uva è del vino.","Riz et kōji sont les ingrédients du saké. Le sucre s'utilise parfois mais n'est pas l'un des quatre ; le raisin, c'est le vin.","Rice and kōji are sake ingredients. Sugar is sometimes used but is not one of the four; grapes belong to wine."]},{"id":"b13db935d","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Durante la fermentazione, il lievito trasforma lo zucchero in alcol e produce anche…","Pendant la fermentation, la levure transforme le sucre en alcool et produit aussi…","During fermentation, yeast turns sugar into alcohol and also produces…"],"o":[["anidride carbonica e aromi","du dioxyde de carbone et des arômes","carbon dioxide and aromas"],["amido ed enzimi","de l'amidon et des enzymes","starch and enzymes"],["luppolo e colore","du houblon et de la couleur","hops and colour"],["ossigeno e acqua","de l'oxygène et de l'eau","oxygen and water"]],"e":["Il lievito crea alcol, anidride carbonica (CO2) e aromi.","La levure crée alcool, dioxyde de carbone (CO2) et arômes.","Yeast creates alcohol, carbon dioxide (CO2) and aromas."],"d":["Amido ed enzimi vengono dal malto. Il colore viene soprattutto dal malto e il luppolo è un ingrediente aggiunto.","Amidon et enzymes viennent du malt. La couleur vient surtout du malt, et le houblon est un ingrédient ajouté.","Starch and enzymes come from the malt. Colour mostly comes from malt, and hops are an added ingredient."]},{"id":"b1723773e","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Una birra ha il 5% vol. In quale fascia alcolica si trova?","Une bière titre 5 % vol. Dans quelle catégorie d'alcool se situe-t-elle ?","A beer is 5% abv. Which alcohol band is it in?"],"o":[["Media","Moyen","Medium"],["Bassa","Faible","Low"],["Alta","Élevé","High"],["Molto alta","Très élevé","Very high"]],"e":["Media = da 4,1 a 5,9%.","Moyen = de 4,1 à 5,9 %.","Medium = 4.1–5.9% abv."],"d":["Bassa è fino al 4%, alta 6–9%, molto alta oltre il 9%.","Faible jusqu'à 4 %, élevé 6–9 %, très élevé au-delà de 9 %.","Low is up to 4%, high 6–9%, very high above 9%."]},{"id":"b1081fc5c","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Da quale grado alcolico una birra è considerata «molto alta»?","À partir de quel degré une bière est-elle « très élevée » en alcool ?","Above what alcohol level is a beer 'very high' in alcohol?"],"o":[["Oltre il 9%","Au-delà de 9 %","Above 9%"],["Oltre il 4%","Au-delà de 4 %","Above 4%"],["Oltre il 6%","Au-delà de 6 %","Above 6%"],["Oltre il 15%","Au-delà de 15 %","Above 15%"]],"e":["Molto alta = sopra il 9% vol.","Très élevé = au-delà de 9 % vol.","Very high = above 9% abv."],"d":["Dal 6 al 9% la birra è «alta»; 4,1–5,9% «media».","De 6 à 9 %, la bière est « élevée » ; 4,1–5,9 %, « moyenne ».","6–9% is 'high' and 4.1–5.9% 'medium'."]},{"id":"b1a2aa95b","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["In volume, qual è l'ingrediente principale della birra?","En volume, quel est l'ingrédient principal de la bière ?","By volume, what is the main ingredient in beer?"],"o":[["L'acqua","L'eau","Water"],["Il malto","Le malt","Malt"],["Il luppolo","Le houblon","Hops"],["Il lievito","La levure","Yeast"]],"e":["L'acqua è di gran lunga l'ingrediente più abbondante: per questo serve una fonte affidabile.","L'eau est de loin l'ingrédient le plus abondant : il faut donc une source fiable.","Water is by far the largest ingredient, so breweries need a reliable supply."],"d":["Il malto dà zucchero e colore, il luppolo amaro e aromi, il lievito alcol: ma in quantità sono tutti molto meno dell'acqua.","Le malt donne sucre et couleur, le houblon amertume et arômes, la levure l'alcool : mais tous sont en bien moindre quantité que l'eau.","Malt gives sugar and colour, hops bitterness and aroma, yeast alcohol: but all are far smaller in quantity than water."]},{"id":"b153a7579","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Per quale motivo si usava il luppolo all'inizio nella birra?","Pour quelle raison utilisait-on d'abord le houblon dans la bière ?","Why were hops originally used in beer?"],"o":[["Per le proprietà antibatteriche, che conservavano la birra","Pour ses propriétés antibactériennes, qui conservaient la bière","For their antibacterial properties, to help preserve the beer"],["Per dare colore scuro","Pour donner une couleur sombre","To give a dark colour"],["Per fornire zucchero","Pour fournir du sucre","To provide sugar"],["Per creare alcol","Pour créer de l'alcool","To create alcohol"]],"e":["All'inizio il luppolo serviva a conservare; oggi si apprezza soprattutto per amaro e aromi.","Au départ, le houblon servait à conserver ; aujourd'hui on l'apprécie surtout pour l'amertume et les arômes.","Hops were first used to preserve; today they are prized mainly for bitterness and aroma."],"d":["Colore e zucchero vengono dal malto, l'alcol dal lievito.","La couleur et le sucre viennent du malt, l'alcool de la levure.","Colour and sugar come from malt, alcohol from yeast."]},{"id":"b18f30463","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Perché il lievito non può usare direttamente l'amido del malto?","Pourquoi la levure ne peut-elle pas utiliser directement l'amidon du malt ?","Why can yeast not use the starch in malt directly?"],"o":[["Perché l'amido è fatto di zuccheri legati in lunghe catene","Parce que l'amidon est fait de sucres liés en longues chaînes","Because starch is sugars bonded into long chains"],["Perché l'amido è troppo amaro","Parce que l'amidon est trop amer","Because starch is too bitter"],["Perché l'amido è già alcol","Parce que l'amidon est déjà de l'alcool","Because starch is already alcohol"],["Perché il lievito mangia solo luppolo","Parce que la levure ne consomme que du houblon","Because yeast only eats hops"]],"e":["Il lievito può consumare solo zuccheri più corti: l'amido va prima spezzato dagli enzimi.","La levure ne consomme que des sucres plus courts : l'amidon doit d'abord être coupé par les enzymes.","Yeast can only eat shorter sugars: the starch must first be broken up by enzymes."],"d":["L'amido non è amaro né alcolico, e il lievito si nutre di zuccheri, non di luppolo.","L'amidon n'est ni amer ni alcoolisé, et la levure se nourrit de sucres, pas de houblon.","Starch is neither bitter nor alcoholic, and yeast feeds on sugars, not hops."]},{"id":"b1a1eafee","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Nella birra, da dove vengono gli enzimi che convertono l'amido in zucchero?","Dans la bière, d'où viennent les enzymes qui convertissent l'amidon en sucre ?","In beer, where do the enzymes that convert starch to sugar come from?"],"o":[["Dal malto","Du malt","The malt"],["Dal luppolo","Du houblon","The hops"],["Dal kōji","Du kōji","Kōji"],["Dall'acqua","De l'eau","The water"]],"e":["Il malto porta sia l'amido sia gli enzimi necessari per convertirlo.","Le malt apporte à la fois l'amidon et les enzymes nécessaires à sa conversion.","Malt supplies both the starch and the enzymes to convert it."],"d":["Il kōji fornisce gli enzimi nel sake, non nella birra. Luppolo e acqua non portano gli enzimi della conversione.","Le kōji fournit les enzymes du saké, pas de la bière. Ni le houblon ni l'eau n'apportent les enzymes de conversion.","Kōji supplies the enzymes in sake, not beer. Hops and water do not bring conversion enzymes."]},{"id":"b1068387a","c":"b01","p":0,"q":["Che cosa sono gli enzimi?","Que sont les enzymes ?","What are enzymes?"],"o":[["Sostanze che accelerano reazioni, come la conversione dell'amido","Des substances qui accélèrent des réactions, comme la conversion de l'amidon","Substances that speed up reactions, such as starch conversion"],["Tipi di lievito","Des types de levure","Types of yeast"],["Varietà di luppolo","Des variétés de houblon","Hop varieties"],["Batteri che rendono la birra acida","Des bactéries qui rendent la bière acide","Bacteria that make beer sour"]],"e":["Gli enzimi sono catalizzatori: qui spezzano l'amido in zuccheri.","Les enzymes sont des catalyseurs : ici, ils coupent l'amidon en sucres.","Enzymes are catalysts: here they break starch into sugars."],"d":["Non sono microrganismi come lievito e batteri, né piante come il luppolo.","Ce ne sont pas des micro-organismes comme la levure ou les bactéries, ni des plantes comme le houblon.","They are not microorganisms like yeast or bacteria, nor plants like hops."]},{"id":"b1bd16dff","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Qual è il cereale più importante per i birrai?","Quelle est la céréale la plus importante pour les brasseurs ?","Which grain is the most important for brewers?"],"o":[["Orzo","Orge","Barley"],["Riso","Riz","Rice"],["Mais","Maïs","Maize (corn)"],["Sorgo","Sorgho","Sorghum"]],"e":["L'orzo è il cereale più usato e quello maltato più spesso.","L'orge est la céréale la plus utilisée et la plus souvent maltée.","Barley is the most used grain and the one most often malted."],"d":["Riso, mais e sorgo si usano anche, ma come complemento.","Riz, maïs et sorgho sont utilisés aussi, mais en complément.","Rice, maize and sorghum are also used, but as extras."]},{"id":"b1389f79b","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Quali sono le tre fasi chiave della maltazione?","Quelles sont les trois étapes clés du maltage ?","What are the three key steps of malting?"],"o":[["Macerazione, germinazione, essiccazione","Trempe, germination, touraillage","Steeping, germination, kilning"],["Macinatura, ammostamento, bollitura","Concassage, brassage, ébullition","Milling, mashing, boiling"],["Levigatura, lavaggio, cottura a vapore","Polissage, lavage, cuisson à la vapeur","Polishing, washing, steaming"],["Fermentazione, carbonazione, confezionamento","Fermentation, carbonatation, conditionnement","Fermentation, carbonation, packaging"]],"e":["Il chicco si bagna, germoglia e poi si essicca in forno.","Le grain est trempé, germe, puis est séché dans la touraille.","The grain is soaked, sprouts, and is then dried in a kiln."],"d":["Macinatura, ammostamento, bollitura, fermentazione ecc. sono tappe della birrificazione, dopo la maltazione. La levigatura riguarda il riso del sake.","Concassage, brassage, ébullition, fermentation, etc. sont des étapes du brassage, après le maltage. Le polissage concerne le riz du saké.","Milling, mashing, boiling, fermentation and so on are brewing steps, after malting. Polishing applies to sake rice."]},{"id":"b11c7d636","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede durante la germinazione?","Que se passe-t-il pendant la germination ?","What happens during germination?"],"o":[["L'embrione cresce e nel chicco si formano enzimi","L'embryon pousse et des enzymes se forment dans le grain","The embryo grows and enzymes form inside the grain"],["Il chicco viene tostato fino al nero","Le grain est torréfié jusqu'au noir","The grain is roasted until black"],["Il lievito produce alcol","La levure produit de l'alcool","The yeast makes alcohol"],["Si aggiunge il luppolo","On ajoute le houblon","Hops are added"]],"e":["Con l'acqua assorbita l'embrione si risveglia e produce gli enzimi.","Avec l'eau absorbée, l'embryon se réveille et produit des enzymes.","With water absorbed, the embryo wakes up and produces enzymes."],"d":["La tostatura avviene dopo, per alcuni malti speciali. Lievito e luppolo entrano in gioco nel birrificio, non nella maltazione.","La torréfaction vient après, pour certains malts spéciaux. Levure et houblon interviennent à la brasserie, pas au maltage.","Roasting comes later, for some speciality malts. Yeast and hops come in at the brewery, not during malting."]},{"id":"b10f2177b","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Perché la germinazione va fermata con l'essiccazione?","Pourquoi faut-il arrêter la germination par le touraillage ?","Why must germination be stopped by kilning?"],"o":[["Altrimenti l'embrione consumerebbe l'amido","Sinon l'embryon consommerait l'amidon","Otherwise the embryo would use up the starch"],["Per creare alcol nel chicco","Pour créer de l'alcool dans le grain","To create alcohol in the grain"],["Per togliere gli enzimi","Pour éliminer les enzymes","To remove the enzymes"],["Per far crescere il luppolo","Pour faire pousser le houblon","To grow the hops"]],"e":["Se il chicco continuasse a crescere, l'amido che serve al birraio finirebbe nella piantina.","Si le grain continuait à pousser, l'amidon utile au brasseur partirait dans la plante.","If the grain kept growing, the starch the brewer needs would go into the plant."],"d":["L'essiccazione conserva gli enzimi (soprattutto nei malti base), non li toglie, e non crea alcol.","Le touraillage conserve les enzymes (surtout dans les malts de base), il ne les enlève pas, et ne crée pas d'alcool.","Kilning keeps the enzymes (especially in base malts) rather than removing them, and makes no alcohol."]},{"id":"b1634ab6c","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Oltre a fermare la germinazione, che cosa produce l'essiccazione?","En plus d'arrêter la germination, que produit le touraillage ?","Besides stopping germination, what does kilning produce?"],"o":[["Colore e aromi nel malto","De la couleur et des arômes dans le malt","Colour and aromas in the malt"],["Alcol e anidride carbonica","Alcool et dioxyde de carbone","Alcohol and carbon dioxide"],["Amaro di luppolo","Amertume de houblon","Hop bitterness"],["Acidità lattica","Acidité lactique","Lactic sourness"]],"e":["Il calore del forno crea colore e aromi; più calore, più colore.","La chaleur de la touraille crée couleur et arômes ; plus de chaleur, plus de couleur.","Kiln heat creates colour and aromas; more heat, more colour."],"d":["Alcol e CO2 vengono dal lievito, l'amaro dal luppolo, l'acidità lattica dai batteri.","Alcool et CO2 viennent de la levure, l'amertume du houblon, l'acidité lactique des bactéries.","Alcohol and CO2 come from yeast, bitterness from hops, lactic sourness from bacteria."]},{"id":"b1db69e1c","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Perché i malti base sono essiccati alle temperature più basse?","Pourquoi les malts de base sont-ils touraillés aux températures les plus basses ?","Why are base malts kilned at the lowest temperatures?"],"o":[["Per non danneggiare gli enzimi, che servono nell'ammostamento","Pour ne pas abîmer les enzymes, utiles au brassage","To avoid damaging the enzymes needed in mashing"],["Per ottenere un colore nero","Pour obtenir une couleur noire","To get a black colour"],["Per dare aromi di caffè","Pour donner des arômes de café","To give coffee aromas"],["Per eliminare l'amido","Pour éliminer l'amidon","To remove the starch"]],"e":["Calore basso = enzimi intatti, pronti a convertire l'amido nell'ammostamento.","Chaleur basse = enzymes intactes, prêtes à convertir l'amidon au brassage.","Low heat = intact enzymes, ready to convert starch in the mash."],"d":["Nero e caffè vengono da malti molto tostati, in cui gli enzimi sono distrutti. L'amido deve restare: è la fonte di zucchero.","Le noir et le café viennent de malts très torréfiés, aux enzymes détruites. L'amidon doit rester : c'est la source de sucre.","Black colour and coffee come from heavily roasted malts with destroyed enzymes. The starch must stay: it is the sugar source."]},{"id":"b1147804f","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi danno tipicamente i malti base?","Quels arômes donnent typiquement les malts de base ?","Which aromas do base malts typically give?"],"o":[["Cracker, pasta di pane, mollica, miele leggero","Cracker, pâte à pain, mie de pain, miel léger","Water cracker, bread dough, bread crumb, light honey"],["Caffè e cioccolato","Café et chocolat","Coffee and chocolate"],["Banana e chiodi di garofano","Banane et clou de girofle","Banana and clove"],["Pompelmo e pino","Pamplemousse et pin","Grapefruit and pine"]],"e":["I malti base danno aromi leggeri di pane e cereali, con un colore paglierino o dorato.","Les malts de base donnent des arômes légers de pain et de céréales, avec une couleur paille ou dorée.","Base malts give light bready, cereal aromas and a straw or gold colour."],"d":["Caffè e cioccolato vengono da malti speciali tostati; banana e chiodi di garofano dal lievito; pompelmo e pino dal luppolo.","Café et chocolat viennent de malts spéciaux torréfiés ; banane et girofle de la levure ; pamplemousse et pin du houblon.","Coffee and chocolate come from roasted speciality malts; banana and clove from yeast; grapefruit and pine from hops."]},{"id":"b19b9bab6","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Una birra fatta solo con malti base: di che colore sarà?","Une bière faite uniquement de malts de base : de quelle couleur sera-t-elle ?","A beer made with base malts only: what colour will it be?"],"o":[["Paglierino o dorato","Paille ou dorée","Straw or gold"],["Rame","Cuivre","Copper"],["Marrone","Brune","Brown"],["Nero","Noire","Black"]],"e":["Da soli i malti base danno una birra paglierina o dorata.","Seuls, les malts de base donnent une bière paille ou dorée.","On their own, base malts give a straw or gold beer."],"d":["Ambra, rame, marrone e nero richiedono malti speciali.","Ambre, cuivre, brun et noir demandent des malts spéciaux.","Amber, copper, brown and black need speciality malts."]},{"id":"b1715f448","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Come si ottengono i malti speciali?","Comment obtient-on les malts spéciaux ?","How are speciality malts made?"],"o":[["Con essiccazione più calda o lunga, oppure tostando il malto","Par un touraillage plus chaud ou plus long, ou en torréfiant le malt","By kilning hotter or longer, or by roasting the malt"],["Saltando la germinazione","En sautant la germination","By skipping germination"],["Aggiungendo luppolo durante la maltazione","En ajoutant du houblon pendant le maltage","By adding hops during malting"],["Bollendo i chicchi","En faisant bouillir les grains","By boiling the grains"]],"e":["Più calore (o tostatura) dà più colore e aromi, ma danneggia gli enzimi.","Plus de chaleur (ou la torréfaction) donne plus de couleur et d'arômes, mais abîme les enzymes.","More heat (or roasting) gives more colour and aroma but damages the enzymes."],"d":["La germinazione fa parte di ogni maltazione; il luppolo si aggiunge in bollitura, non in maltazione.","La germination fait partie de tout maltage ; le houblon s'ajoute à l'ébullition, pas au maltage.","Germination is part of all malting; hops go in during the boil, not malting."]},{"id":"b13014467","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede agli enzimi nei malti speciali?","Qu'arrive-t-il aux enzymes dans les malts spéciaux ?","What happens to the enzymes in speciality malts?"],"o":[["Vengono danneggiati o distrutti dal calore","Elles sont abîmées ou détruites par la chaleur","They are damaged or destroyed by the heat"],["Si moltiplicano","Elles se multiplient","They multiply"],["Diventano lievito","Elles deviennent de la levure","They turn into yeast"],["Restano più attivi dei malti base","Elles restent plus actives que dans les malts de base","They stay more active than in base malts"]],"e":["Le temperature alte dei malti speciali danneggiano o distruggono gli enzimi.","Les hautes températures des malts spéciaux abîment ou détruisent les enzymes.","The high temperatures for speciality malts damage or destroy the enzymes."],"d":["Per questo servono malti base nella ricetta: portano gli enzimi per convertire l'amido di tutto il mash.","C'est pourquoi la recette a besoin de malts de base : ils apportent les enzymes pour convertir l'amidon de toute la maische.","That is why a recipe needs base malt: it brings the enzymes to convert the starch of the whole mash."]},{"id":"b116c55e7","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi aromi viene tipicamente da un malto speciale tostato?","Lequel de ces arômes vient typiquement d'un malt spécial torréfié ?","Which of these aromas typically comes from a roasted speciality malt?"],"o":[["Caffè","Café","Coffee"],["Mollica di pane","Mie de pain","Bread crumb"],["Pompelmo","Pamplemousse","Grapefruit"],["Chiodo di garofano","Clou de girofle","Clove"]],"e":["Caffè e cioccolato sono aromi da malti molto tostati.","Café et chocolat sont des arômes de malts très torréfiés.","Coffee and chocolate are aromas of heavily roasted malts."],"d":["La mollica viene dai malti base, il pompelmo dal luppolo, il chiodo di garofano dal lievito.","La mie de pain vient des malts de base, le pamplemousse du houblon, le girofle de la levure.","Bread crumb comes from base malt, grapefruit from hops, clove from yeast."]},{"id":"b15792f2a","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Che effetto tendono ad avere riso e mais nella ricetta?","Quel effet ont en général le riz et le maïs dans la recette ?","What effect do rice and maize tend to have in the recipe?"],"o":[["Aromi meno intensi e corpo più leggero","Des arômes moins intenses et un corps plus léger","Lighter aroma intensity and lighter body"],["Più colore e aromi tostati","Plus de couleur et d'arômes grillés","More colour and roasted aromas"],["Consistenza cremosa e torbidità","Une texture crémeuse et du trouble","Creamy texture and haze"],["Più amaro","Plus d'amertume","More bitterness"]],"e":["Riso, mais e la maggior parte di zuccheri e sciroppi alleggeriscono aromi e corpo.","Riz, maïs et la plupart des sucres et sirops allègent arômes et corps.","Rice, maize and most sugars and syrups lighten aroma and body."],"d":["Cremosità e torbidità sono tipiche del frumento; colore tostato dei malti speciali; l'amaro del luppolo.","Crémeux et trouble sont typiques du blé ; couleur grillée des malts spéciaux ; amertume du houblon.","Creaminess and haze are typical of wheat; roasted colour of speciality malts; bitterness of hops."]},{"id":"b12986f65","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Quale cereale può dare una consistenza morbida e cremosa e contribuire alla torbidità?","Quelle céréale peut donner une texture douce et crémeuse et contribuer au trouble ?","Which grain can give a smooth, creamy texture and contribute to haze?"],"o":[["Frumento","Blé","Wheat"],["Riso","Riz","Rice"],["Mais","Maïs","Maize"],["Orzo molto tostato","Orge très torréfiée","Heavily roasted barley"]],"e":["Il frumento dà morbidezza e torbidità, come nelle birre di frumento.","Le blé donne douceur et trouble, comme dans les bières de blé.","Wheat brings smoothness and haze, as in wheat beers."],"d":["Riso e mais alleggeriscono; l'orzo tostato dà colore scuro e aromi di caffè.","Riz et maïs allègent ; l'orge torréfiée donne une couleur sombre et des arômes de café.","Rice and maize lighten; roasted barley gives dark colour and coffee aromas."]},{"id":"b1017a1f1","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è la «ricetta dei cereali» (grain bill)?","Qu'est-ce que la « recette des céréales » (grain bill) ?","What is the grain bill?"],"o":[["L'elenco di tipi e quantità di malti e cereali di una birra","La liste des types et quantités de malts et céréales d'une bière","The list of types and amounts of malts and grains in a beer"],["Il costo dei cereali","Le coût des céréales","The cost of the grain"],["L'elenco dei luppoli","La liste des houblons","The list of hops"],["La quantità di lievito","La quantité de levure","The amount of yeast"]],"e":["È la ricetta dei cereali: quali malti e cereali, e in che proporzione.","C'est la recette des céréales : quels malts et céréales, et en quelle proportion.","It is the cereal recipe: which malts and grains, and in what proportion."],"d":["Non riguarda costi, luppolo o lievito, solo i cereali.","Elle ne concerne ni les coûts, ni le houblon, ni la levure : seulement les céréales.","It is not about cost, hops or yeast, only the grains."]},{"id":"b1b3cbeb4","c":"b02","p":0,"q":["In una ricetta tipica, quale malto costituisce la maggior parte?","Dans une recette typique, quel malt en constitue l'essentiel ?","In a typical recipe, which malt makes up the majority?"],"o":[["Un malto base","Un malt de base","A base malt"],["Un malto nero tostato","Un malt noir torréfié","A black roasted malt"],["Un malto caramello","Un malt caramel","A caramel malt"],["Nessun malto: solo zucchero","Aucun malt : seulement du sucre","No malt: only sugar"]],"e":["Il malto base porta amido ed enzimi; i malti speciali si usano in piccole dosi.","Le malt de base apporte amidon et enzymes ; les malts spéciaux s'utilisent en petites doses.","Base malt brings starch and enzymes; speciality malts are used in small amounts."],"d":["Malti neri e caramello sono malti speciali, aggiunti in piccole quantità per colore e aromi.","Malts noirs et caramel sont des malts spéciaux, ajoutés en petites quantités pour couleur et arômes.","Black and caramel malts are speciality malts, added in small amounts for colour and aroma."]},{"id":"b1e5fab91","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Come si chiama il malto macinato?","Comment appelle-t-on le malt concassé ?","What is milled malt called?"],"o":[["Grist","Mouture (grist)","Grist"],["Mosto","Moût","Wort"],["Trebbie","Drêches","Spent grains"],["Kōji","Kōji","Kōji"]],"e":["I chicchi macinati si chiamano grist.","Les grains concassés s'appellent la mouture (grist).","The milled grains are called grist."],"d":["Il mosto è il liquido zuccherino, le trebbie i solidi rimasti; il kōji è del sake.","Le moût est le liquide sucré, les drêches les solides restants ; le kōji appartient au saké.","Wort is the sugary liquid and spent grains the leftover solids; kōji belongs to sake."]},{"id":"b19a38971","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Quale sequenza delle tappe di produzione è corretta?","Quel ordre des étapes de production est correct ?","Which order of production steps is correct?"],"o":[["Macinatura, ammostamento, bollitura, fermentazione, carbonazione, confezionamento","Concassage, brassage, ébullition, fermentation, carbonatation, conditionnement","Milling, mashing, wort boiling, fermentation, carbonation, packaging"],["Ammostamento, macinatura, fermentazione, bollitura, confezionamento, carbonazione","Brassage, concassage, fermentation, ébullition, conditionnement, carbonatation","Mashing, milling, fermentation, boiling, packaging, carbonation"],["Macinatura, fermentazione, ammostamento, bollitura, carbonazione, confezionamento","Concassage, fermentation, brassage, ébullition, carbonatation, conditionnement","Milling, fermentation, mashing, boiling, carbonation, packaging"],["Bollitura, macinatura, ammostamento, fermentazione, confezionamento, carbonazione","Ébullition, concassage, brassage, fermentation, conditionnement, carbonatation","Boiling, milling, mashing, fermentation, packaging, carbonation"]],"e":["Si macina, si ammosta, si bolle il mosto, si fermenta, si carbona e si confeziona.","On concasse, on brasse, on fait bouillir le moût, on fermente, on carbonate et on conditionne.","Mill, mash, boil the wort, ferment, carbonate and package."],"d":["Il lievito non può fermentare prima dell'ammostamento, perché lo zucchero non c'è ancora; bollire viene dopo l'ammostamento.","La levure ne peut pas fermenter avant le brassage, car le sucre n'existe pas encore ; l'ébullition suit le brassage.","Yeast cannot ferment before mashing because there is no sugar yet; boiling comes after mashing."]},{"id":"b1225a032","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede durante l'ammostamento?","Que se passe-t-il pendant le brassage (empâtage) ?","What happens during mashing?"],"o":[["Gli enzimi del malto trasformano l'amido in zuccheri nell'acqua calda","Les enzymes du malt transforment l'amidon en sucres dans l'eau chaude","Malt enzymes turn starch into sugars in hot water"],["Il lievito trasforma lo zucchero in alcol","La levure transforme le sucre en alcool","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol"],["Si aggiunge la maggior parte del luppolo","On ajoute l'essentiel du houblon","Most of the hops are added"],["La birra viene carbonata","La bière est carbonatée","The beer is carbonated"]],"e":["Grist + acqua calda: gli enzimi convertono l'amido e lo zucchero si scioglie.","Mouture + eau chaude : les enzymes convertissent l'amidon et le sucre se dissout.","Grist + hot water: the enzymes convert the starch and the sugar dissolves."],"d":["L'alcol si forma in fermentazione; il luppolo si aggiunge soprattutto in bollitura; la carbonazione viene dopo.","L'alcool se forme pendant la fermentation ; le houblon s'ajoute surtout à l'ébullition ; la carbonatation vient après.","Alcohol forms in fermentation; hops go in mainly during the boil; carbonation comes later."]},{"id":"b1998773b","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Alla fine dell'ammostamento, come si chiama il liquido zuccherino separato dai solidi?","À la fin du brassage, comment appelle-t-on le liquide sucré séparé des solides ?","At the end of mashing, what is the sugary liquid separated from the solids called?"],"o":[["Mosto (wort)","Moût","Wort"],["Grist","Mouture","Grist"],["Mash","Maische","Mash"],["Trebbie","Drêches","Spent grains"]],"e":["Il liquido zuccherino separato si chiama mosto.","Le liquide sucré séparé s'appelle le moût.","The separated sugary liquid is called wort."],"d":["Il mash è la miscela di grist e acqua prima della separazione; le trebbie sono i solidi rimasti.","La maische est le mélange mouture-eau avant séparation ; les drêches sont les solides restants.","Mash is the grist-and-water mix before separation; spent grains are the solids left."]},{"id":"b1e8a2862","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Che cosa sono le trebbie (spent grains)?","Que sont les drêches ?","What are spent grains?"],"o":[["I solidi rimasti dopo aver separato il mosto","Les solides restants après séparation du moût","The solids left after the wort is separated"],["I chicchi non ancora maltati","Les grains pas encore maltés","Grains not yet malted"],["Il sedimento di lievito in bottiglia","Le dépôt de levure en bouteille","The yeast sediment in the bottle"],["I coni di luppolo usati","Les cônes de houblon usagés","Used hop cones"]],"e":["Sono i resti solidi del mash, soprattutto bucce.","Ce sont les restes solides de la maische, surtout des balles.","They are the solid leftovers of the mash, mainly husks."],"d":["Il sedimento in bottiglia è lievito della rifermentazione; i chicchi non maltati e il luppolo sono altro.","Le dépôt en bouteille est de la levure de refermentation ; grains non maltés et houblon sont autre chose.","The bottle sediment is yeast from bottle-conditioning; unmalted grain and hops are different things."]},{"id":"b1fdafe9f","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Perché si fa bollire il mosto?","Pourquoi fait-on bouillir le moût ?","Why is the wort boiled?"],"o":[["Per uccidere i microrganismi e aggiungere il luppolo","Pour tuer les micro-organismes et ajouter le houblon","To kill microorganisms and add the hops"],["Per trasformare l'amido in zucchero","Pour transformer l'amidon en sucre","To turn starch into sugar"],["Per far germinare i chicchi","Pour faire germer les grains","To make the grains germinate"],["Per creare l'alcol","Pour créer l'alcool","To create the alcohol"]],"e":["La bollitura rende la birra sicura ed è il momento delle principali aggiunte di luppolo.","L'ébullition rend la bière sûre et c'est le moment des principaux ajouts de houblon.","Boiling makes the beer safe and is when the main hop additions happen."],"d":["La conversione avviene nell'ammostamento, la germinazione nella maltazione, l'alcol in fermentazione.","La conversion a lieu au brassage, la germination au maltage, l'alcool à la fermentation.","Conversion happens in mashing, germination in malting, alcohol in fermentation."]},{"id":"b1efab2c6","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si fa subito dopo la bollitura del mosto?","Que fait-on juste après l'ébullition du moût ?","What happens right after the wort is boiled?"],"o":[["Lo si raffredda rapidamente","On le refroidit rapidement","It is cooled rapidly"],["Lo si confeziona in lattina","On le met en canette","It is canned"],["Lo si macina","On le concasse","It is milled"],["Lo si lascia caldo per giorni","On le laisse chaud pendant des jours","It is kept hot for days"]],"e":["Il mosto va raffreddato in fretta a una temperatura adatta al lievito.","Le moût est refroidi vite à une température adaptée à la levure.","The wort is cooled quickly to a temperature suitable for the yeast."],"d":["Il lievito non sopravviverebbe a un mosto bollente; macinatura e confezionamento sono altre tappe.","La levure ne survivrait pas dans un moût bouillant ; concassage et conditionnement sont d'autres étapes.","Yeast would not survive in boiling wort; milling and packaging are other steps."]},{"id":"b155056d6","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["In quale tappa si aggiunge il lievito?","À quelle étape ajoute-t-on la levure ?","At which stage is yeast added?"],"o":[["Nella fermentazione, al mosto raffreddato","À la fermentation, au moût refroidi","At fermentation, to the cooled wort"],["Nella macinatura","Au concassage","At milling"],["Nell'ammostamento","Au brassage","At mashing"],["Durante la bollitura","Pendant l'ébullition","During the boil"]],"e":["Il mosto freddo passa nel fermentatore, dove si aggiunge il lievito.","Le moût refroidi passe dans la cuve de fermentation, où l'on ajoute la levure.","The cooled wort goes into a fermentation vessel, where yeast is added."],"d":["Nella bollitura il lievito morirebbe; nella macinatura e nell'ammostamento non c'è ancora mosto pronto da fermentare.","À l'ébullition, la levure mourrait ; au concassage et au brassage, il n'y a pas encore de moût prêt à fermenter.","The boil would kill yeast; at milling and mashing there is no wort ready to ferment yet."]},{"id":"b1875878b","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Che cosa fa la carbonazione?","Que fait la carbonatation ?","What does carbonation do?"],"o":[["Scioglie anidride carbonica nella birra sotto pressione","Elle dissout du dioxyde de carbone dans la bière sous pression","Dissolves carbon dioxide in the beer under pressure"],["Aggiunge alcol","Elle ajoute de l'alcool","Adds alcohol"],["Toglie l'amaro","Elle enlève l'amertume","Removes bitterness"],["Colora la birra","Elle colore la bière","Colours the beer"]],"e":["La CO2 disciolta dà bollicine in bocca e la schiuma nel bicchiere.","Le CO2 dissous donne les bulles en bouche et la mousse dans le verre.","Dissolved CO2 gives bubbles in the mouth and foam in the glass."],"d":["La carbonazione non cambia alcol, amaro o colore.","La carbonatation ne change ni l'alcool, ni l'amertume, ni la couleur.","Carbonation changes neither alcohol, bitterness nor colour."]},{"id":"b1c944fb5","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Da dove può venire l'anidride carbonica iniettata per completare la carbonazione?","D'où peut venir le dioxyde de carbone injecté pour compléter la carbonatation ?","Where can the CO2 injected to top up carbonation come from?"],"o":[["Comprata o recuperata da fermentazioni precedenti","Acheté ou récupéré de fermentations précédentes","Bought in or recovered from earlier fermentations"],["Dal luppolo bollito","Du houblon bouilli","From boiled hops"],["Dall'aria del birrificio","De l'air de la brasserie","From the brewery air"],["Dalle trebbie","Des drêches","From the spent grains"]],"e":["Si usa CO2 acquistata o recuperata da fermentazioni passate.","On utilise du CO2 acheté ou récupéré de fermentations passées.","Bought CO2 or CO2 recovered from earlier fermentations is used."],"d":["Luppolo, aria e trebbie non sono fonti di anidride carbonica per la carbonazione.","Ni le houblon, ni l'air, ni les drêches ne sont des sources de CO2 pour la carbonatation.","Hops, air and spent grains are not CO2 sources for carbonation."]},{"id":"b1ea63166","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è la rifermentazione in bottiglia (bottle-conditioning)?","Qu'est-ce que la refermentation en bouteille ?","What is bottle-conditioning?"],"o":[["Una seconda fermentazione nella bottiglia chiusa, che lascia sedimento di lievito","Une seconde fermentation en bouteille fermée, qui laisse un dépôt de levure","A further fermentation in the sealed bottle, leaving a yeast sediment"],["Conservare la birra in cantina","Conserver la bière en cave","Storing beer in a cellar"],["Aggiungere luppolo in bottiglia","Ajouter du houblon en bouteille","Adding hops in the bottle"],["Pastorizzare la bottiglia","Pasteuriser la bouteille","Pasteurising the bottle"]],"e":["Il lievito fermenta di nuovo in bottiglia: crea bollicine e un deposito sul fondo.","La levure fermente à nouveau en bouteille : elle crée des bulles et un dépôt au fond.","Yeast ferments again in the bottle, creating bubbles and a deposit at the bottom."],"d":["Non è una semplice conservazione, né un'aggiunta di luppolo o un trattamento termico.","Ce n'est pas une simple conservation, ni un ajout de houblon ou un traitement thermique.","It is not mere storage, nor a hop addition or heat treatment."]},{"id":"b178695a5","c":"b03","p":0,"q":["Quali sono i contenitori più usati per la birra?","Quels sont les contenants les plus utilisés pour la bière ?","What are the most widely used beer containers?"],"o":[["Lattine, bottiglie, fusti","Canettes, bouteilles, fûts","Cans, bottles, kegs"],["Botti di rovere e anfore","Fûts de chêne et amphores","Oak casks and amphorae"],["Cartoni e sacchetti","Briques et sachets","Cartons and pouches"],["Damigiane di vetro","Dames-jeannes en verre","Glass demijohns"]],"e":["Lattine, bottiglie e fusti sono i contenitori principali.","Canettes, bouteilles et fûts sont les principaux contenants.","Cans, bottles and kegs are the main containers."],"d":["Le altre opzioni esistono in casi particolari ma non sono le confezioni comuni della birra.","Les autres options existent dans des cas particuliers mais ne sont pas les conditionnements courants.","The other options exist in special cases but are not the usual beer packages."]},{"id":"b1c24bc31","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Quale parte della pianta del luppolo usano i birrai?","Quelle partie de la plante de houblon les brasseurs utilisent-ils ?","Which part of the hop plant do brewers use?"],"o":[["Il cono","Le cône","The cone"],["La radice","La racine","The root"],["Le foglie","Les feuilles","The leaves"],["Il seme","La graine","The seed"]],"e":["I coni di luppolo contengono le sostanze che danno amaro e aromi.","Les cônes de houblon contiennent les composés qui donnent amertume et arômes.","Hop cones contain the compounds that give bitterness and aroma."],"d":["Radici, foglie e semi non sono la parte usata in birrificio.","Racines, feuilles et graines ne sont pas la partie utilisée en brasserie.","Roots, leaves and seeds are not the part used in brewing."]},{"id":"b1ae964b7","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["In che forma i birrai usano più spesso il luppolo?","Sous quelle forme les brasseurs utilisent-ils le plus souvent le houblon ?","In what form do brewers most often use hops?"],"o":[["Pellet di coni secchi macinati e pressati","Pellets de cônes secs broyés et pressés","Pellets of dried, milled and pressed cones"],["Coni freschi appena raccolti","Cônes frais tout juste récoltés","Fresh cones straight from the field"],["Sciroppo di luppolo","Sirop de houblon","Hop syrup"],["Foglie essiccate","Feuilles séchées","Dried leaves"]],"e":["I pellet sono la forma più comune: occupano meno spazio.","Les pellets sont la forme la plus courante : ils prennent moins de place.","Pellets are the most common form: they save space."],"d":["I coni secchi interi si usano, ma di rado; i coni freschi marcirebbero presto.","On utilise des cônes secs entiers, mais rarement ; les cônes frais pourriraient vite.","Whole dried cones are used, but rarely; fresh cones would soon rot."]},{"id":"b183a0d41","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Perché il luppolo viene confezionato e refrigerato?","Pourquoi le houblon est-il emballé et réfrigéré ?","Why are hops packed and refrigerated?"],"o":[["Per conservare amaro e aromi","Pour garder amertume et arômes","To keep their bitterness and aroma"],["Per farlo germinare","Pour le faire germer","To make them germinate"],["Per trasformarlo in malto","Pour le transformer en malt","To turn them into malt"],["Per farne lievito","Pour en faire de la levure","To make yeast from them"]],"e":["Il freddo protegge le sostanze amare e aromatiche del luppolo.","Le froid protège les composés amers et aromatiques du houblon.","Cold protects the bitter and aromatic compounds in hops."],"d":["La germinazione riguarda i cereali da maltare, non il luppolo, che non diventa né malto né lievito.","La germination concerne les céréales à malter, pas le houblon, qui ne devient ni malt ni levure.","Germination is for grains being malted, not hops, which become neither malt nor yeast."]},{"id":"b18791c5e","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi sono tipici dei luppoli tradizionali tedeschi, cechi o britannici?","Quels arômes sont typiques des houblons traditionnels allemands, tchèques ou britanniques ?","Which aromas are typical of traditional German, Czech or British hops?"],"o":[["Sottili: speziati, floreali, erbacei, terrosi o fruttati","Subtils : épicés, floraux, herbacés, terreux ou fruités","Subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity"],["Intensi di frutta tropicale e pino","Intenses de fruits tropicaux et de pin","Intense tropical fruit and pine"],["Caffè e cioccolato","Café et chocolat","Coffee and chocolate"],["Banana e chiodi di garofano","Banane et clou de girofle","Banana and clove"]],"e":["I luppoli tradizionali europei sono discreti: spezie, fiori, erbe, terra, un po' di frutta.","Les houblons européens traditionnels sont discrets : épices, fleurs, herbes, terre, un peu de fruit.","Traditional European hops are restrained: spice, flowers, herbs, earth, a little fruit."],"d":["Tropicale e pino intensi sono tipici dei luppoli americani, neozelandesi e australiani. Caffè e cioccolato vengono dal malto, banana e chiodi di garofano dal lievito.","Tropical et pin intenses sont typiques des houblons américains, néo-zélandais et australiens. Café et chocolat viennent du malt, banane et girofle de la levure.","Intense tropical and pine notes belong to American, NZ and Australian hops. Coffee and chocolate come from malt, banana and clove from yeast."]},{"id":"b1c465c20","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Un birraio vuole note intense di agrumi, frutta tropicale e pino. Quali luppoli sceglie probabilmente?","Un brasseur veut des notes intenses d'agrumes, de fruits tropicaux et de pin. Quels houblons choisit-il probablement ?","A brewer wants intense citrus, tropical fruit and pine notes. Which hops are they likely to choose?"],"o":[["Americani, neozelandesi o australiani","Américains, néo-zélandais ou australiens","American, New Zealand or Australian"],["Tradizionali tedeschi","Allemands traditionnels","Traditional German"],["Tradizionali cechi","Tchèques traditionnels","Traditional Czech"],["Tradizionali britannici","Britanniques traditionnels","Traditional British"]],"e":["Questi luppoli tendono ad aromi intensi di agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, tropicale o pino.","Ces houblons tendent vers des arômes intenses d'agrumes, fruits à noyau, tropicaux ou pin.","These hops tend to give intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine aromas."],"d":["I luppoli tradizionali tedeschi, cechi e britannici sono più sottili: spezie, fiori, erbe, terra.","Les houblons traditionnels allemands, tchèques et britanniques sont plus subtils : épices, fleurs, herbes, terre.","Traditional German, Czech and British hops are subtler: spice, flowers, herbs, earth."]},{"id":"b1709c179","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Quando si aggiunge il luppolo per ottenere soprattutto AMARO?","Quand ajoute-t-on le houblon pour obtenir surtout de l'AMERTUME ?","When are hops added mainly for BITTERNESS?"],"o":[["All'inizio della bollitura","Au début de l'ébullition","Near the start of the boil"],["Alla fine della bollitura","À la fin de l'ébullition","Near the end of the boil"],["Dopo la fermentazione","Après la fermentation","After fermentation"],["Durante la maltazione","Pendant le maltage","During malting"]],"e":["L'amaro richiede calore e tempo: il luppolo va messo presto.","L'amertume demande chaleur et temps : on met le houblon tôt.","Bitterness needs heat and time, so hops go in early."],"d":["Alla fine della bollitura e dopo la fermentazione il luppolo dà soprattutto aroma. In maltazione non si usa luppolo.","En fin d'ébullition et après la fermentation, le houblon donne surtout de l'arôme. On n'en utilise pas au maltage.","Late in the boil and after fermentation hops give mainly aroma. No hops are used in malting."]},{"id":"b1dd36499","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Perché il luppolo per l'aroma si aggiunge verso la fine della bollitura?","Pourquoi ajoute-t-on le houblon aromatique vers la fin de l'ébullition ?","Why are aroma hops added near the end of the boil?"],"o":[["Perché gli aromi volano via se bolle troppo a lungo","Parce que les arômes s'envolent si l'ébullition dure trop","Because aromas escape if boiled too long"],["Perché così dà più amaro","Parce qu'il donne ainsi plus d'amertume","Because it gives more bitterness that way"],["Per sterilizzarlo","Pour le stériliser","To sterilise it"],["Per colorare la birra","Pour colorer la bière","To colour the beer"]],"e":["Gli aromi del luppolo sono volatili: una bollitura breve li conserva.","Les arômes du houblon sont volatils : une courte ébullition les préserve.","Hop aromas are volatile: a short boil keeps them."],"d":["Più amaro si ottiene bollendo più a lungo, cioè aggiungendo presto. Il luppolo non colora la birra.","On obtient plus d'amertume en faisant bouillir plus longtemps, donc en ajoutant tôt. Le houblon ne colore pas la bière.","More bitterness comes from boiling longer, i.e. adding early. Hops do not colour beer."]},{"id":"b17cc0a27","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è il dry hopping?","Qu'est-ce que le dry hopping (houblonnage à froid) ?","What is dry hopping?"],"o":[["Aggiungere luppolo durante o dopo la fermentazione, per l'aroma","Ajouter du houblon pendant ou après la fermentation, pour l'arôme","Adding hops during or after fermentation, for aroma"],["Essiccare i coni di luppolo","Sécher les cônes de houblon","Drying the hop cones"],["Bollire il luppolo senz'acqua","Faire bouillir le houblon sans eau","Boiling hops without water"],["Aggiungere luppolo all'inizio della bollitura","Ajouter du houblon au début de l'ébullition","Adding hops at the start of the boil"]],"e":["Il dry hopping avviene a temperatura più bassa, dopo la bollitura, e dà aroma.","Le dry hopping a lieu à plus basse température, après l'ébullition, et donne de l'arôme.","Dry hopping happens at a lower temperature, after the boil, and adds aroma."],"d":["L'essiccazione dei coni è un'altra cosa, e il luppolo aggiunto all'inizio della bollitura serve per l'amaro.","Le séchage des cônes est autre chose, et le houblon ajouté en début d'ébullition sert à l'amertume.","Drying cones is something else, and hops added at the start of the boil are for bitterness."]},{"id":"b1843e1e3","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi si usano da tempo in alcuni stili belgi tradizionali?","Quels aromates utilise-t-on depuis longtemps dans certains styles belges traditionnels ?","Which flavourings have long been used in certain traditional Belgian styles?"],"o":[["Frutta (ciliegie, lamponi), scorza d'agrumi, semi di coriandolo","Fruits (cerise, framboise), écorce d'agrumes, graines de coriandre","Fruit (cherries, raspberries), citrus peel, coriander seed"],["Solo luppolo americano","Uniquement du houblon américain","Only American hops"],["Trucioli di rovere","Copeaux de chêne","Oak chips"],["Kōji","Kōji","Kōji"]],"e":["Frutta, scorza d'agrumi e coriandolo fanno parte della tradizione belga.","Fruits, écorce d'agrumes et coriandre font partie de la tradition belge.","Fruit, citrus peel and coriander are part of Belgian tradition."],"d":["Il kōji è del sake; il luppolo americano è un fenomeno moderno, non la tradizione belga.","Le kōji appartient au saké ; le houblon américain est un phénomène moderne, pas la tradition belge.","Kōji belongs to sake; American hops are a modern trend, not Belgian tradition."]},{"id":"b1b4a1342","c":"b04","p":0,"q":["Nella maggior parte dei Paesi, che limiti ci sono per gli aromi aggiunti alla birra?","Dans la plupart des pays, quelles limites y a-t-il pour les aromates ajoutés à la bière ?","In most countries, what limits apply to flavourings added to beer?"],"o":[["Nessuno, purché sia commestibile e pratico","Aucune, tant que c'est comestible et pratique","None, as long as it is edible and practical"],["Solo luppolo ammesso","Seul le houblon est autorisé","Only hops are allowed"],["Solo frutta ammessa","Seuls les fruits sont autorisés","Only fruit is allowed"],["Solo erbe europee","Seulement des herbes européennes","Only European herbs"]],"e":["Zucca, miele, peperoncino o caffè: si può usare ciò che è commestibile e pratico.","Citrouille, miel, piment ou café : tout ce qui est comestible et pratique peut servir.","Pumpkin, honey, chilli or coffee: anything edible and practical can be used."],"d":["Il luppolo è il più usato, ma non l'unico ammesso.","Le houblon est le plus utilisé, mais pas le seul autorisé.","Hops are the most used, but not the only ones allowed."]},{"id":"b1521e1fa","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Qual è il compito principale del lievito nella birra?","Quel est le rôle principal de la levure dans la bière ?","What is yeast's main job in beer?"],"o":[["Creare l'alcol","Créer l'alcool","To create alcohol"],["Dare amaro","Donner de l'amertume","To give bitterness"],["Dare colore","Donner de la couleur","To give colour"],["Convertire l'amido","Convertir l'amidon","To convert starch"]],"e":["Il lievito trasforma lo zucchero in alcol; può anche dare aromi.","La levure transforme le sucre en alcool ; elle peut aussi donner des arômes.","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol; it can also add aromas."],"d":["L'amaro viene dal luppolo, il colore dal malto, la conversione dell'amido dagli enzimi del malto.","L'amertume vient du houblon, la couleur du malt, la conversion de l'amidon des enzymes du malt.","Bitterness comes from hops, colour from malt, starch conversion from malt enzymes."]},{"id":"b14a49e29","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde al lievito ale?","Quelle description correspond à la levure ale ?","Which description fits ale yeast?"],"o":[["Fermenta in fretta, più al caldo, con molti aromi fruttati e speziati","Fermente vite, plus au chaud, avec beaucoup d'arômes fruités et épicés","Ferments quickly, warmer, with many fruity and spicy aromas"],["Fermenta lentamente, al fresco, con pochi aromi","Fermente lentement, au frais, avec peu d'arômes","Ferments slowly, cool, with little aroma"],["Si usa solo nella fermentazione spontanea","S'utilise seulement en fermentation spontanée","Used only in spontaneous fermentation"],["Rende la birra acida","Rend la bière acide","Makes beer sour"]],"e":["Il lievito ale è veloce, ama il caldo relativo e può dare molti aromi.","La levure ale est rapide, aime une chaleur relative et peut donner beaucoup d'arômes.","Ale yeast is quick, likes relative warmth and can give many aromas."],"d":["Lento, fresco e poco aromatico descrive il lievito lager. L'acidità viene dai batteri lattici.","Lent, frais et peu aromatique décrit la levure lager. L'acidité vient des bactéries lactiques.","Slow, cool and low-aroma describes lager yeast. Sourness comes from lactic bacteria."]},{"id":"b16a1b0fa","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Come si chiamano le birre fatte con lievito lager?","Comment appelle-t-on les bières faites avec de la levure lager ?","What are beers made with lager yeast called?"],"o":[["Lager","Lagers","Lagers"],["Ale","Ales","Ales"],["Sour","Sours","Sours"],["Stout","Stouts","Stouts"]],"e":["Lievito lager → lager; lievito ale → ale.","Levure lager → lagers ; levure ale → ales.","Lager yeast → lagers; ale yeast → ales."],"d":["Le stout sono ale; «sour» indica stili acidi dovuti ai batteri.","Les stouts sont des ales ; « sour » désigne des styles acides dus aux bactéries.","Stouts are ales; 'sour' refers to acidic styles from bacteria."]},{"id":"b1bdd9b27","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Perché i birrai scelgono un preciso ceppo di lievito ale?","Pourquoi les brasseurs choisissent-ils une souche précise de levure ale ?","Why do brewers choose a particular ale yeast strain?"],"o":[["Ogni ceppo crea la sua firma di aromi","Chaque souche crée sa propre signature aromatique","Each strain creates its own signature set of aromas"],["Tutti i ceppi danno lo stesso risultato","Toutes les souches donnent le même résultat","All strains give the same result"],["Per cambiare il colore","Pour changer la couleur","To change the colour"],["Per eliminare il luppolo","Pour supprimer le houblon","To remove the hops"]],"e":["I ceppi ale sono molti e diversi: si sceglie quello che dà gli aromi giusti per lo stile.","Les souches ale sont nombreuses et différentes : on choisit celle qui donne les bons arômes.","There are many different ale strains: the one with the right aromas for the style is chosen."],"d":["Il lievito non decide il colore e non elimina il luppolo.","La levure ne décide pas de la couleur et n'élimine pas le houblon.","Yeast does not set colour or remove hops."]},{"id":"b1b46525c","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi può dare il Brettanomyces?","Quels arômes peut donner le Brettanomyces ?","What aromas can Brettanomyces give?"],"o":[["Ananas maturo, pesca, aia, cuoio, fieno, terra","Ananas mûr, pêche, basse-cour, cuir, foin, terre","Ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth"],["Caffè e cioccolato","Café et chocolat","Coffee and chocolate"],["Solo acidità","Seulement de l'acidité","Only sourness"],["Nessun aroma","Aucun arôme","No aroma at all"]],"e":["Il Brett dà aromi complessi, fruttati e «rustici».","Le Brett donne des arômes complexes, fruités et « rustiques ».","Brett gives complex fruity and 'rustic' aromas."],"d":["Caffè e cioccolato vengono dal malto tostato; l'acidità soprattutto dai batteri lattici.","Café et chocolat viennent du malt torréfié ; l'acidité surtout des bactéries lactiques.","Coffee and chocolate come from roasted malt; sourness mainly from lactic bacteria."]},{"id":"b1a7edabd","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Che cosa portano i batteri lattici alla birra?","Qu'apportent les bactéries lactiques à la bière ?","What do lactic acid bacteria bring to beer?"],"o":[["Acidità","De l'acidité","Acidity (sourness)"],["Amaro","De l'amertume","Bitterness"],["Colore scuro","Une couleur sombre","A dark colour"],["Più alcol","Plus d'alcool","More alcohol"]],"e":["I batteri lattici, come nello yogurt, rendono la birra acida.","Les bactéries lactiques, comme dans le yaourt, rendent la bière acide.","Lactic bacteria, as in yoghurt, make beer sour."],"d":["L'amaro è del luppolo, il colore del malto, l'alcol del lievito.","L'amertume vient du houblon, la couleur du malt, l'alcool de la levure.","Bitterness is from hops, colour from malt, alcohol from yeast."]},{"id":"b13680b00","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Con quale lievito si fa quasi tutta la birra?","Avec quelle levure fait-on presque toute la bière ?","What yeast is nearly all beer made with?"],"o":[["Lieviti coltivati, selezionati in laboratorio","Des levures cultivées, sélectionnées en laboratoire","Cultured yeast, selected and grown in a lab"],["Lieviti dell'ambiente","Des levures ambiantes","Ambient yeast from the surroundings"],["Lievito di pane","De la levure de boulanger","Baker's yeast"],["Nessun lievito","Aucune levure","No yeast"]],"e":["Quasi tutte le birre partono da un ceppo coltivato di ale o lager.","Presque toutes les bières partent d'une souche cultivée d'ale ou de lager.","Nearly all beers start from a cultured ale or lager strain."],"d":["I lieviti dell'ambiente si usano solo nella fermentazione spontanea, che è rara. Senza lievito non c'è alcol.","Les levures ambiantes ne servent qu'en fermentation spontanée, qui est rare. Sans levure, pas d'alcool.","Ambient yeast is used only in spontaneous fermentation, which is rare. No yeast, no alcohol."]},{"id":"b16bcc3d5","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Che cos'è la fermentazione spontanea?","Qu'est-ce que la fermentation spontanée ?","What is spontaneous fermentation?"],"o":[["Non si aggiungono lieviti o batteri coltivati: lavorano quelli dell'ambiente","On n'ajoute ni levures ni bactéries cultivées : ce sont celles de l'environnement qui agissent","No cultured yeast or bacteria are added: ambient ones do the work"],["Una fermentazione molto veloce","Une fermentation très rapide","A very fast fermentation"],["Una fermentazione senza zucchero","Une fermentation sans sucre","A fermentation without sugar"],["Una fermentazione con un solo ceppo di laboratorio","Une fermentation avec une seule souche de laboratoire","A fermentation with one lab strain"]],"e":["Il birraio si affida ai lieviti e batteri del birrificio e dei dintorni.","Le brasseur s'en remet aux levures et bactéries de la brasserie et des environs.","The brewer relies on yeast and bacteria living in and around the brewery."],"d":["Un solo ceppo di laboratorio è l'opposto: lievito coltivato. Il termine non riguarda la velocità.","Une seule souche de laboratoire, c'est l'inverse : de la levure cultivée. Le terme ne concerne pas la vitesse.","One lab strain is the opposite: cultured yeast. The term is not about speed."]},{"id":"b1c4582a2","c":"b05","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede di solito nel mosto con la fermentazione spontanea?","Que se passe-t-il généralement dans le moût en fermentation spontanée ?","What usually happens in the wort with spontaneous fermentation?"],"o":[["Crescono molti tipi diversi di lieviti e batteri","De nombreux types de levures et de bactéries se développent","Many different types of yeast and bacteria grow"],["Cresce un solo ceppo di lager","Une seule souche de lager se développe","A single lager strain grows"],["Non cresce nulla","Rien ne se développe","Nothing grows"],["Cresce solo muffa del kōji","Seule la moisissure du kōji se développe","Only kōji mould grows"]],"e":["Senza aggiunte coltivate, nel mosto si sviluppa una comunità varia di microrganismi.","Sans ajout cultivé, une communauté variée de micro-organismes se développe dans le moût.","Without cultured additions, a varied community of microorganisms develops."],"d":["Un solo ceppo è tipico del lievito coltivato; il kōji appartiene al sake.","Une seule souche est typique de la levure cultivée ; le kōji appartient au saké.","A single strain is typical of cultured yeast; kōji belongs to sake."]},{"id":"b1f75b4fb","c":"b06","p":0,"q":["Perché serve uno sfondo bianco durante la degustazione della birra?","Pourquoi faut-il un fond blanc pour déguster la bière ?","Why is a white background used when tasting beer?"],"o":[["Per valutare il colore","Pour évaluer la couleur","To assess the colour"],["Per sentire meglio gli aromi","Pour mieux sentir les arômes","To smell aromas better"],["Per raffreddare la birra","Pour refroidir la bière","To cool the beer"],["Per aumentare la schiuma","Pour augmenter la mousse","To increase the foam"]],"e":["Tenendo il bicchiere davanti al bianco si vede meglio il colore.","En tenant le verre devant un fond blanc, on voit mieux la couleur.","Holding the glass against white makes the colour easier to judge."],"d":["Lo sfondo non agisce su aromi, temperatura o schiuma.","Le fond n'agit ni sur les arômes, ni sur la température, ni sur la mousse.","The background has no effect on aroma, temperature or foam."]},{"id":"b10c7c76f","c":"b06","p":0,"q":["Come si valuta la limpidezza di una birra?","Comment évalue-t-on la limpidité d'une bière ?","How is a beer's clarity assessed?"],"o":[["Guardando attraverso il bicchiere verso la luce","En regardant à travers le verre vers la lumière","By looking through the glass towards the light"],["Annusando il bicchiere","En sentant le verre","By smelling the glass"],["Assaggiando un sorso","En goûtant une gorgée","By tasting a sip"],["Misurando la temperatura","En mesurant la température","By measuring the temperature"]],"e":["Per la limpidezza si guarda attraverso il liquido verso la luce: limpida, velata o opaca.","Pour la limpidité, on regarde à travers le liquide vers la lumière : limpide, voilée ou opaque.","For clarity, look through the liquid towards the light: clear, hazy or opaque."],"d":["Naso e bocca sono altre fasi; la temperatura non indica la limpidezza.","Le nez et la bouche sont d'autres étapes ; la température n'indique pas la limpidité.","Nose and palate are other stages; temperature does not show clarity."]},{"id":"b11762a4b","c":"b06","p":0,"q":["Quale sequenza di colori usa la griglia di degustazione della birra, dal più chiaro al più scuro?","Quelle suite de couleurs la grille de dégustation de la bière utilise-t-elle, de la plus claire à la plus foncée ?","Which colour scale does the beer tasting grid use, from palest to darkest?"],"o":[["Paglierino, dorato, ambrato, ramato, marrone, nero","Paille, doré, ambré, cuivré, brun, noir","Straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black"],["Dorato, paglierino, ramato, ambrato, nero, marrone","Doré, paille, cuivré, ambré, noir, brun","Gold, straw, copper, amber, black, brown"],["Limone, oro, ambra, marrone","Citron, or, ambre, brun","Lemon, gold, amber, brown"],["Rosa, rosso, granato, mattone","Rose, rouge, grenat, tuile","Pink, red, garnet, tawny"]],"e":["La scala va da paglierino a nero, passando per dorato, ambrato, ramato e marrone.","L'échelle va de paille à noir, en passant par doré, ambré, cuivré et brun.","The scale runs from straw to black, via gold, amber, copper and brown."],"d":["Le altre scale sono in ordine sbagliato o appartengono alla degustazione del vino.","Les autres échelles sont dans le mauvais ordre ou appartiennent à la dégustation du vin.","The other scales are out of order or belong to wine tasting."]},{"id":"b1dd1c148","c":"b06","p":0,"q":["Quale di questi aromi viene tipicamente dal LIEVITO?","Lequel de ces arômes vient typiquement de la LEVURE ?","Which of these aromas typically comes from YEAST?"],"o":[["Chiodo di garofano","Clou de girofle","Clove"],["Crosta di pane","Croûte de pain","Bread crust"],["Pino","Pin","Pine"],["Caffè","Café","Coffee"]],"e":["Le spezie come il chiodo di garofano e il pepe sono aromi da lievito.","Les épices comme le clou de girofle et le poivre sont des arômes de levure.","Spice notes such as clove and peppercorn come from yeast."],"d":["Crosta di pane e caffè vengono dal malto, il pino dal luppolo.","Croûte de pain et café viennent du malt, le pin du houblon.","Bread crust and coffee come from malt, pine from hops."]},{"id":"b11d3dd16","c":"b06","p":0,"q":["Quale famiglia di aromi viene dal LUPPOLO?","Quelle famille d'arômes vient du HOUBLON ?","Which aroma family comes from HOPS?"],"o":[["Agrumi, frutta tropicale, fiori, erbe, pino","Agrumes, fruits tropicaux, fleurs, herbes, pin","Citrus, tropical fruit, floral, herbal, pine"],["Pane, biscotto, caramello","Pain, biscuit, caramel","Bread, biscuit, caramel"],["Banana, gomma da masticare, smalto","Banane, chewing-gum, vernis","Banana, bubblegum, nail varnish"],["Uvetta, prugna, dattero","Raisin sec, pruneau, datte","Raisin, prune, date"]],"e":["Il luppolo dà note floreali, fruttate (agrumi, tropicale…), erbacee e di pino.","Le houblon donne des notes florales, fruitées (agrumes, tropical…), herbacées et de pin.","Hops give floral, fruity (citrus, tropical…), herbal and pine notes."],"d":["Pane, caramello e frutta secca vengono dal malto; banana, gomma e smalto dal lievito.","Pain, caramel et fruits secs viennent du malt ; banane, chewing-gum et vernis de la levure.","Bread, caramel and dried fruit come from malt; banana, bubblegum and nail varnish from yeast."]},{"id":"b1d9a11fc","c":"b06","p":0,"q":["Che cosa si valuta in bocca oltre agli aromi?","Qu'évalue-t-on en bouche en plus des arômes ?","Besides aromas, what is assessed on the palate?"],"o":[["Intensità, carbonazione, corpo, alcol, amaro, dolcezza, acidità","Intensité, carbonatation, corps, alcool, amertume, douceur, acidité","Intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness, acidity"],["Solo il colore","Seulement la couleur","Only colour"],["Altezza della schiuma","La hauteur de la mousse","Height of the foam"],["Limpidezza","La limpidité","Clarity"]],"e":["In bocca si giudicano struttura e sensazioni, oltre agli aromi.","En bouche, on juge la structure et les sensations, en plus des arômes.","On the palate you judge structure and sensations as well as aromas."],"d":["Colore, schiuma e limpidezza appartengono all'aspetto.","Couleur, mousse et limpidité appartiennent à l'aspect.","Colour, foam and clarity belong to appearance."]},{"id":"b1ca8318d","c":"b07","p":0,"q":["Che colore ha di solito una birra fatta solo con malti base?","Quelle couleur a en général une bière faite uniquement de malts de base ?","What colour is a beer made only with base malts usually?"],"o":[["Paglierino o dorato","Paille ou dorée","Straw or gold"],["Ramato","Cuivrée","Copper"],["Marrone","Brune","Brown"],["Nero","Noire","Black"]],"e":["I malti base danno birre paglierine o dorate.","Les malts de base donnent des bières paille ou dorées.","Base malts give straw or gold beers."],"d":["I colori più scuri richiedono malti speciali.","Les couleurs plus foncées demandent des malts spéciaux.","Darker colours need speciality malts."]},{"id":"b1f65c64e","c":"b07","p":0,"q":["Che effetto ha l'uso di riso, zucchero o sciroppi in una lager chiara?","Quel effet a l'utilisation de riz, sucre ou sirop dans une lager pâle ?","What effect does using rice, sugar or syrup have in a pale lager?"],"o":[["Aromi meno intensi e corpo più leggero","Des arômes moins intenses et un corps plus léger","Lighter aroma intensity and body"],["Colore più scuro","Une couleur plus foncée","A darker colour"],["Più amaro","Plus d'amertume","More bitterness"],["Più acidità","Plus d'acidité","More sourness"]],"e":["Rispetto a una birra 100% malto, si ottiene una birra più leggera e meno aromatica.","Par rapport à une bière 100 % malt, on obtient une bière plus légère et moins aromatique.","Compared with an all-malt beer, the result is lighter and less aromatic."],"d":["Colore, amaro e acidità non dipendono da questi ingredienti.","La couleur, l'amertume et l'acidité ne dépendent pas de ces ingrédients.","Colour, bitterness and sourness do not depend on these ingredients."]},{"id":"b135294c0","c":"b07","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde a una lager chiara americana o internazionale?","Quelle description correspond à une lager pâle américaine ou internationale ?","Which description fits an American or international pale lager?"],"o":[["Paglierina o dorata, aroma leggero, amaro basso-medio, carbonazione alta","Paille ou dorée, arôme léger, amertume faible-moyenne, carbonatation élevée","Straw or gold, light aroma, low-medium bitterness, high carbonation"],["Nera, caffè e cioccolato, alcol molto alto","Noire, café et chocolat, alcool très élevé","Black, coffee and chocolate, very high alcohol"],["Torbida, banana e chiodi di garofano","Trouble, banane et girofle","Hazy, banana and clove"],["Acida e con aromi di aia","Acide avec des arômes de basse-cour","Sour with farmyard aromas"]],"e":["È la birra chiara e facile più bevuta al mondo.","C'est la bière pâle et facile la plus bue au monde.","It is the world's most popular easy-drinking pale beer."],"d":["Le altre descrivono stout, weissbier e birre acide come la geuze.","Les autres décrivent stout, weissbier et bières acides comme la geuze.","The others describe stout, weissbier and sour beers such as geuze."]},{"id":"b1f03e412","c":"b07","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa «hell» in Munich helles?","Que signifie « hell » dans Munich helles ?","What does 'hell' mean in Munich helles?"],"o":[["Chiaro, luminoso","Clair, lumineux","Bright, light or pale"],["Scuro","Sombre","Dark"],["Frumento","Blé","Wheat"],["Forte","Fort","Strong"]],"e":["«Hell» in tedesco significa chiaro: la helles è una lager dorata.","« Hell » signifie clair en allemand : la helles est une lager dorée.","'Hell' is German for bright or pale: helles is a gold lager."],"d":["«Dunkel» vuol dire scuro, «Weizen» frumento.","« Dunkel » veut dire sombre, « Weizen » blé.","'Dunkel' means dark and 'Weizen' wheat."]},{"id":"b1491f609","c":"b07","p":0,"q":["La Munich helles è…","La Munich helles est…","Munich helles is…"],"o":[["una lager dorata con malto di mollica e luppolo sottile","une lager dorée au malt de mie et houblon subtil","a gold lager with bread-crumb malt and subtle hops"],["un'ale nera molto tostata","une ale noire très torréfiée","a heavily roasted black ale"],["un'ale di frumento torbida","une ale de blé trouble","a hazy wheat ale"],["una birra acida a fermentazione spontanea","une bière acide à fermentation spontanée","a spontaneously fermented sour beer"]],"e":["Lager dorata, mollica o cracker, note sottili di luppolo, amaro basso-medio, alcol medio.","Lager dorée, mie ou cracker, subtiles notes de houblon, amertume faible-moyenne, alcool moyen.","Gold lager, bread crumb or cracker, subtle hop notes, low-medium bitterness, medium alcohol."],"d":["È una lager, non un'ale; non è scura, torbida o acida.","C'est une lager, pas une ale ; elle n'est ni sombre, ni trouble, ni acide.","It is a lager, not an ale, and is neither dark, hazy nor sour."]},{"id":"b18817035","c":"b07","p":0,"q":["Quale stile di malto con soli malti base è un'ALE?","Quel style de malt aux seuls malts de base est une ALE ?","Which base-malt-only malt-driven style is an ALE?"],"o":[["Blonde ale","Blonde ale","Blonde ale"],["Munich helles","Munich helles","Munich helles"],["Lager chiara internazionale","Lager pâle internationale","International pale lager"],["Munich dunkel","Munich dunkel","Munich dunkel"]],"e":["La blonde ale (o golden ale) è l'ale del gruppo, accanto a due lager.","La blonde ale (ou golden ale) est l'ale du groupe, à côté de deux lagers.","Blonde (golden) ale is the ale of the group, next to two lagers."],"d":["Helles e lager internazionale sono lager; la dunkel è una lager con malti speciali.","Helles et lager internationale sont des lagers ; la dunkel est une lager aux malts spéciaux.","Helles and international lager are lagers; dunkel is a lager with speciality malts."]},{"id":"b1fed19a3","c":"b07","p":0,"q":["Con quale altro nome si trova a volte la blonde ale?","Sous quel autre nom trouve-t-on parfois la blonde ale ?","What other name is blonde ale sometimes labelled with?"],"o":[["Golden ale","Golden ale","Golden ale"],["Brown ale","Brown ale","Brown ale"],["Blanche","Blanche","Blanche"],["Barley wine","Barley wine","Barley wine"]],"e":["Blonde ale e golden ale indicano lo stesso stile facile e dorato.","Blonde ale et golden ale désignent le même style facile et doré.","Blonde ale and golden ale name the same easy, gold style."],"d":["«Blanche» è la witbier; brown ale e barley wine sono stili con malti speciali.","« Blanche » désigne la witbier ; brown ale et barley wine utilisent des malts spéciaux.","'Blanche' is witbier; brown ale and barley wine use speciality malts."]},{"id":"b1d7ad998","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significa «dunkel»?","Que signifie « dunkel » ?","What does 'dunkel' mean?"],"o":[["Scuro","Sombre","Dark"],["Chiaro","Clair","Pale"],["Bianco","Blanc","White"],["Doppio","Double","Double"]],"e":["«Dunkel» in tedesco vuol dire scuro.","« Dunkel » signifie sombre en allemand.","'Dunkel' is German for dark."],"d":["Chiaro è «hell», bianco «weiss»; «doppio» ricorda dubbel.","Clair se dit « hell », blanc « weiss » ; « double » rappelle dubbel.","Pale is 'hell', white is 'weiss'; 'double' recalls dubbel."]},{"id":"b1ae7f00d","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde alla Munich dunkel?","Quelle description correspond à la Munich dunkel ?","Which description fits Munich dunkel?"],"o":[["Lager ramata-marrone con pane tostato e nocciola tostata","Lager cuivrée-brune au pain grillé et à la noisette grillée","Copper-brown lager with toast and toasted nut"],["Ale nera con caffè e alcol molto alto","Ale noire au café et alcool très élevé","Black ale with coffee and very high alcohol"],["Lager paglierina molto amara","Lager paille très amère","Very bitter straw lager"],["Ale torbida con coriandolo","Ale trouble à la coriandre","Hazy ale with coriander"]],"e":["Lager scura con malti speciali: tostato, crosta di pane, nocciola, talvolta caramello o cioccolato.","Lager sombre aux malts spéciaux : grillé, croûte de pain, noisette, parfois caramel ou chocolat.","A dark lager with speciality malts: toast, bread crust, nut, sometimes caramel or chocolate."],"d":["La seconda descrive una imperial stout, la terza una pils, la quarta una witbier.","La deuxième décrit une imperial stout, la troisième une pils, la quatrième une witbier.","The second describes an imperial stout, the third a pilsner, the fourth a witbier."]},{"id":"b1afc7853","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Che cosa vale per amaro e alcol nella brown ale?","Qu'en est-il de l'amertume et de l'alcool dans la brown ale ?","What is true of bitterness and alcohol in brown ale?"],"o":[["Entrambi vanno da bassi ad alti","Tous deux vont de faibles à élevés","Both range from low to high"],["Sono sempre molto alti","Ils sont toujours très élevés","They are always very high"],["Amaro sempre nullo","Amertume toujours nulle","Bitterness is always absent"],["Alcol sempre sotto il 4%","Alcool toujours sous 4 %","Alcohol always under 4%"]],"e":["La brown ale è uno stile ampio: amaro e alcol variano molto.","La brown ale est un style large : amertume et alcool varient beaucoup.","Brown ale is a broad style: bitterness and alcohol vary a lot."],"d":["Le opzioni con «sempre» sono troppo rigide per questo stile.","Les options avec « toujours » sont trop rigides pour ce style.","Options with 'always' are too rigid for this style."]},{"id":"b130faba6","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi di malto sono tipici di porter e stout?","Quels arômes de malt sont typiques des porters et stouts ?","Which malt aromas are typical of porter and stout?"],"o":[["Caffè e cioccolato","Café et chocolat","Coffee and chocolate"],["Mollica e cracker","Mie et cracker","Bread crumb and water cracker"],["Banana e chiodi di garofano","Banane et girofle","Banana and clove"],["Pompelmo e rabarbaro","Pamplemousse et rhubarbe","Grapefruit and rhubarb"]],"e":["I malti tostati danno caffè, cioccolato e talvolta caramello, con colore marrone o nero.","Les malts torréfiés donnent café, chocolat et parfois caramel, avec une couleur brune ou noire.","Roasted malts give coffee, chocolate and sometimes caramel, with a brown or black colour."],"d":["Mollica e cracker sono da malti base; banana e chiodi di garofano dal lievito; pompelmo e rabarbaro sono tipici della geuze.","Mie et cracker viennent des malts de base ; banane et girofle de la levure ; pamplemousse et rhubarbe sont typiques de la geuze.","Crumb and cracker are base-malt notes; banana and clove come from yeast; grapefruit and rhubarb suit geuze."]},{"id":"b149060a6","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Che cosa indica di solito la parola «imperial» nel nome di una stout?","Qu'indique généralement le mot « imperial » dans le nom d'une stout ?","What does 'imperial' usually indicate in a stout's name?"],"o":[["Alcol molto alto e aromi tostati pronunciati","Un alcool très élevé et des arômes torréfiés prononcés","Very high alcohol and pronounced roasted aromas"],["Una birra prodotta in Inghilterra","Une bière produite en Angleterre","A beer made in England"],["Una birra senza alcol","Une bière sans alcool","An alcohol-free beer"],["Una birra acida","Une bière acide","A sour beer"]],"e":["Le versioni «imperial» sono molto alcoliche e molto tostate.","Les versions « imperial » sont très alcoolisées et très torréfiées.","'Imperial' versions are very strong and strongly roasted."],"d":["Il termine non indica un'origine geografica, né acidità o assenza di alcol.","Le terme n'indique ni une origine, ni une acidité, ni l'absence d'alcool.","The term shows neither origin, sourness nor absence of alcohol."]},{"id":"b11e3aca7","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde al barley wine?","Quelle description correspond au barley wine ?","Which description fits barley wine?"],"o":[["Ale spesso ambrata, malto intenso, corpo pieno, dolce, alcol alto o molto alto","Ale souvent ambrée, malt intense, corps plein, douce, alcool élevé ou très élevé","Often amber ale, intense malt, full body, sweet, high or very high alcohol"],["Vino fatto con orzo","Vin fait à partir d'orge","A wine made from barley"],["Lager leggera e secca","Lager légère et sèche","A light, dry lager"],["Birra acida di frumento","Bière acide de blé","A sour wheat beer"]],"e":["Nonostante il nome è una birra: un'ale ricca, dolce e molto alcolica.","Malgré son nom, c'est une bière : une ale riche, douce et très alcoolisée.","Despite the name it is a beer: a rich, sweet, strong ale."],"d":["Non è vino né lager né birra acida.","Ce n'est ni un vin, ni une lager, ni une bière acide.","It is not wine, lager or a sour beer."]},{"id":"b1cab6622","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Quale stile di malto si presta spesso all'invecchiamento?","Quel style de malt se prête souvent au vieillissement ?","Which malt-driven style is often suitable for ageing?"],"o":[["Barley wine","Barley wine","Barley wine"],["Lager chiara internazionale","Lager pâle internationale","International pale lager"],["Munich helles","Munich helles","Munich helles"],["Blonde ale","Blonde ale","Blonde ale"]],"e":["Il barley wine, ricco e molto alcolico, è spesso adatto all'invecchiamento.","Le barley wine, riche et très alcoolisé, se prête souvent au vieillissement.","Rich, strong barley wine is often suitable for ageing."],"d":["Lager chiare, helles e blonde ale sono birre fresche da bere giovani.","Les lagers pâles, helles et blonde ales sont des bières fraîches à boire jeunes.","Pale lagers, helles and blonde ales are fresh beers best drunk young."]},{"id":"b18afaaa0","c":"b08","p":0,"q":["Una birra nera con aromi di caffè e cioccolato: quale stile è più probabile?","Une bière noire aux arômes de café et de chocolat : quel style est le plus probable ?","A black beer with coffee and chocolate aromas: which style is most likely?"],"o":[["Porter o stout","Porter ou stout","Porter or stout"],["Munich helles","Munich helles","Munich helles"],["Hazy IPA","Hazy IPA","Hazy IPA"],["Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse"]],"e":["Colore nero e aromi tostati indicano porter o stout.","Couleur noire et arômes torréfiés indiquent porter ou stout.","Black colour and roasted aromas point to porter or stout."],"d":["Helles, hazy IPA e Berliner weisse sono chiare, dal paglierino al dorato.","Helles, hazy IPA et Berliner weisse sont claires, de paille à dorée.","Helles, hazy IPA and Berliner weisse are pale, straw to gold."]},{"id":"b16103e2f","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Come si ottiene un amaro marcato con aroma di luppolo contenuto?","Comment obtient-on une amertume marquée avec un arôme de houblon retenu ?","How is pronounced bitterness with restrained hop aroma achieved?"],"o":[["Quasi tutto il luppolo a inizio bollitura e poco alla fine","L'essentiel du houblon en début d'ébullition et peu à la fin","Most hops early in the boil and few at the end"],["Solo dry hopping","Uniquement du dry hopping","Dry hopping only"],["Nessun luppolo","Aucun houblon","No hops at all"],["Tutto il luppolo alla fine della bollitura","Tout le houblon en fin d'ébullition","All hops at the end of the boil"]],"e":["Luppolo presto = amaro; poco luppolo tardi = poco aroma.","Houblon tôt = amertume ; peu de houblon tard = peu d'arôme.","Early hops = bitterness; few late hops = little aroma."],"d":["Dry hopping e luppolo tardivo danno soprattutto aroma, non amaro.","Le dry hopping et le houblon tardif donnent surtout de l'arôme, pas de l'amertume.","Dry hopping and late hops mainly give aroma, not bitterness."]},{"id":"b17f3b86c","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Quale stile è una lager luppolata con luppoli tradizionali?","Quel style est une lager houblonnée aux houblons traditionnels ?","Which style is a hop-driven lager with traditional hops?"],"o":[["Pils tradizionale ceca o tedesca","Pils tchèque ou allemande traditionnelle","Traditional Czech or German pilsner"],["Bitter","Bitter","Bitter"],["American IPA","American IPA","American IPA"],["Munich dunkel","Munich dunkel","Munich dunkel"]],"e":["La pils ceca o tedesca è la lager del gruppo luppolato tradizionale.","La pils tchèque ou allemande est la lager du groupe houblonné traditionnel.","Czech or German pilsner is the lager of the traditional hop-driven group."],"d":["Il bitter è un'ale, l'American IPA usa luppoli del Nuovo Mondo, la dunkel è uno stile di malto.","Le bitter est une ale, l'American IPA utilise des houblons du Nouveau Monde, la dunkel est un style de malt.","Bitter is an ale, American IPA uses New World hops, dunkel is malt-driven."]},{"id":"b14519a28","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde alla pils ceca o tedesca tradizionale?","Quelle description correspond à la pils tchèque ou allemande traditionnelle ?","Which description fits traditional Czech or German pilsner?"],"o":[["Paglierina-dorata, luppolo sottile speziato o floreale, amaro medio-alto","Paille-dorée, houblon subtil épicé ou floral, amertume moyenne-élevée","Straw-gold, subtle spicy or floral hops, medium-high bitterness"],["Torbida, molto tropicale, poco amara","Trouble, très tropicale, peu amère","Hazy, very tropical, little bitterness"],["Nera, tostata, alcol molto alto","Noire, torréfiée, alcool très élevé","Black, roasted, very high alcohol"],["Acida, con sciroppo di lampone","Acide, avec sirop de framboise","Sour, with raspberry syrup"]],"e":["Pasta di pane o miele leggero, luppolo sottile, amaro da medio ad alto, alcol medio.","Pâte à pain ou miel léger, houblon subtil, amertume moyenne à élevée, alcool moyen.","Bread dough or light honey, subtle hops, medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol."],"d":["Le altre descrivono hazy IPA, imperial stout e Berliner weisse.","Les autres décrivent hazy IPA, imperial stout et Berliner weisse.","The others describe hazy IPA, imperial stout and Berliner weisse."]},{"id":"b19ef19fb","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Da quale Paese è originario il bitter?","De quel pays le bitter est-il originaire ?","Which country does bitter come from originally?"],"o":[["Inghilterra","Angleterre","England"],["Germania","Allemagne","Germany"],["Belgio","Belgique","Belgium"],["Stati Uniti","États-Unis","United States"]],"e":["Il bitter è un'ale luppolata nata in Inghilterra.","Le bitter est une ale houblonnée née en Angleterre.","Bitter is a hop-driven ale from England."],"d":["Germania e Belgio sono associati ad altri stili (helles, dubbel…); gli Stati Uniti all'APA e all'IPA americana.","L'Allemagne et la Belgique sont associées à d'autres styles (helles, dubbel…) ; les États-Unis à l'APA et à l'IPA américaine.","Germany and Belgium are linked to other styles (helles, dubbel…); the USA to APA and American IPA."]},{"id":"b1d27fad7","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde al bitter?","Quelle description correspond au bitter ?","Which description fits bitter?"],"o":[["Ale ambrata-ramata, biscotto o caramello, luppolo sottile, amaro medio-alto","Ale ambrée-cuivrée, biscuit ou caramel, houblon subtil, amertume moyenne-élevée","Amber-copper ale, biscuit or caramel, subtle hops, medium-high bitterness"],["Lager paglierina con luppolo tropicale intenso","Lager paille au houblon tropical intense","Straw lager with intense tropical hops"],["Ale torbida di frumento con banana","Ale trouble de blé à la banane","Hazy wheat ale with banana"],["Lager nera molto dolce","Lager noire très douce","Very sweet black lager"]],"e":["Il bitter unisce malti tostati e caramello a un luppolo tradizionale sottile.","Le bitter associe malts grillés et caramel à un houblon traditionnel subtil.","Bitter pairs toasty, caramel malt with subtle traditional hops."],"d":["Il bitter è un'ale, non una lager, e non ha aromi di banana.","Le bitter est une ale, pas une lager, sans arômes de banane.","Bitter is an ale, not a lager, and has no banana aromas."]},{"id":"b17b48ed6","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Come si ottengono amaro alto E aromi di luppolo intensi?","Comment obtient-on une amertume élevée ET des arômes de houblon intenses ?","How are high bitterness AND intense hop aromas achieved?"],"o":[["Luppolo a inizio bollitura, più tardi e in dry hopping","Houblon en début d'ébullition, plus tard et en dry hopping","Hops early in the boil, later on, and dry hopping"],["Solo luppolo a inizio bollitura","Seulement du houblon en début d'ébullition","Only early hops"],["Solo malti speciali","Seulement des malts spéciaux","Only speciality malts"],["Fermentazione spontanea","Fermentation spontanée","Spontaneous fermentation"]],"e":["Presto per l'amaro, tardi per il sapore e dry hopping per l'aroma.","Tôt pour l'amertume, tard pour la saveur et dry hopping pour l'arôme.","Early for bitterness, late for flavour and dry hopping for aroma."],"d":["Solo luppolo precoce darebbe amaro con poco aroma; malti e fermentazione spontanea non c'entrano.","Seul un houblonnage précoce donnerait de l'amertume avec peu d'arôme ; malts et fermentation spontanée n'ont rien à voir.","Early hops alone give bitterness with little aroma; malts and spontaneous fermentation are unrelated."]},{"id":"b1372361f","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Quale stile è spesso etichettato «APA»?","Quel style est souvent étiqueté « APA » ?","Which style is sometimes labelled 'APA'?"],"o":[["American pale ale","American pale ale","American pale ale"],["American IPA","American IPA","American IPA"],["Pils tedesca","Pils allemande","German pilsner"],["Blonde ale","Blonde ale","Blonde ale"]],"e":["APA è l'abbreviazione di American pale ale.","APA est l'abréviation d'American pale ale.","APA stands for American pale ale."],"d":["IPA significa India pale ale; pils e blonde ale non usano questa sigla.","IPA signifie India pale ale ; pils et blonde ale n'utilisent pas ce sigle.","IPA means India pale ale; pilsner and blonde ale do not use this abbreviation."]},{"id":"b143d4752","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Come si può descrivere l'American IPA rispetto all'American pale ale?","Comment décrire l'American IPA par rapport à l'American pale ale ?","How can American IPA be described compared with American pale ale?"],"o":[["Più forte, con ancora più amaro e aroma di luppolo","Plus forte, avec encore plus d'amertume et d'arôme de houblon","Stronger, with even more bitterness and hop aroma"],["Più leggera e meno amara","Plus légère et moins amère","Lighter and less bitter"],["Più scura e tostata","Plus sombre et torréfiée","Darker and more roasted"],["Più acida","Plus acide","More sour"]],"e":["L'American IPA è come una APA più forte, più amara e più aromatica.","L'American IPA est comme une APA plus forte, plus amère et plus aromatique.","American IPA is like a stronger, more bitter, more aromatic APA."],"d":["Il colore resta da dorato ad ambrato, senza tostature né acidità.","La couleur reste dorée à ambrée, sans torréfaction ni acidité.","Colour stays gold to amber, with no roast or sourness."]},{"id":"b1a41d302","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi di luppolo definiscono l'American IPA?","Quels arômes de houblon définissent l'American IPA ?","Which hop aromas define American IPA?"],"o":[["Pino, resina, agrumi, frutta tropicale e a nocciolo","Pin, résine, agrumes, fruits tropicaux et à noyau","Pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit"],["Speziati, erbacei, terrosi sottili","Épicés, herbacés, terreux subtils","Subtle spicy, herbal, earthy"],["Banana e chiodi di garofano","Banane et girofle","Banana and clove"],["Caffè e cioccolato","Café et chocolat","Coffee and chocolate"]],"e":["Luppoli del Nuovo Mondo: pino, resina, agrumi, frutta tropicale e a nocciolo.","Houblons du Nouveau Monde : pin, résine, agrumes, fruits tropicaux et à noyau.","New World hops: pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit."],"d":["Speziati e terrosi sottili sono i luppoli europei tradizionali; banana e chiodi di garofano vengono dal lievito; caffè e cioccolato dal malto.","Épicés et terreux subtils sont les houblons européens traditionnels ; banane et girofle viennent de la levure ; café et chocolat du malt.","Subtle spicy and earthy notes are traditional European hops; banana and clove come from yeast; coffee and chocolate from malt."]},{"id":"b19e41152","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Rispetto a una American IPA, la hazy IPA è di solito…","Par rapport à une American IPA, la hazy IPA est en général…","Compared with an American IPA, a hazy IPA is typically…"],"o":[["meno amara","moins amère","less bitter"],["più amara","plus amère","more bitter"],["più scura","plus sombre","darker"],["più acida","plus acide","more sour"]],"e":["La hazy IPA ha amaro da basso a medio: punta sull'aroma.","La hazy IPA a une amertume faible à moyenne : elle mise sur l'arôme.","Hazy IPA has low to medium bitterness: it focuses on aroma."],"d":["È paglierina o dorata, non scura, e non è uno stile acido.","Elle est paille ou dorée, pas sombre, et ce n'est pas un style acide.","It is straw or gold, not dark, and not a sour style."]},{"id":"b1b7e49f5","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Con quale altro nome si trova la hazy IPA?","Sous quel autre nom trouve-t-on la hazy IPA ?","What other name is hazy IPA labelled with?"],"o":[["New England IPA","New England IPA","New England IPA"],["India pale lager","India pale lager","India pale lager"],["Imperial stout","Imperial stout","Imperial stout"],["Golden ale","Golden ale","Golden ale"]],"e":["Hazy IPA e New England IPA sono lo stesso stile.","Hazy IPA et New England IPA sont le même style.","Hazy IPA and New England IPA are the same style."],"d":["Golden ale è l'altro nome della blonde ale; imperial stout è una stout molto forte.","Golden ale est l'autre nom de la blonde ale ; imperial stout est une stout très forte.","Golden ale is another name for blonde ale; imperial stout is a very strong stout."]},{"id":"b11d36c61","c":"b09","p":0,"q":["Una birra paglierina, nettamente torbida, con molta frutta tropicale e amaro moderato: quale stile?","Une bière paille, nettement trouble, très tropicale et à l'amertume modérée : quel style ?","A straw-coloured, distinctly hazy beer with lots of tropical fruit and moderate bitterness: which style?"],"o":[["Hazy IPA","Hazy IPA","Hazy IPA"],["Weissbier","Weissbier","Weissbier"],["Bitter","Bitter","Bitter"],["Munich helles","Munich helles","Munich helles"]],"e":["Torbida + luppolo tropicale + amaro basso-medio = hazy IPA.","Trouble + houblon tropical + amertume faible-moyenne = hazy IPA.","Hazy + tropical hops + low-medium bitterness = hazy IPA."],"d":["Anche la weissbier è torbida, ma i suoi aromi sono banana e chiodi di garofano del lievito. Bitter ed helles sono limpide.","La weissbier est aussi trouble, mais ses arômes sont banane et girofle de la levure. Bitter et helles sont limpides.","Weissbier is also hazy, but its aromas are yeast-driven banana and clove. Bitter and helles are clear."]},{"id":"b1151581e","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Perché gli stili «di lievito» sono tutti ale?","Pourquoi les styles « de levure » sont-ils tous des ales ?","Why are yeast-driven styles all ales?"],"o":[["Perché le lager hanno di solito pochi aromi di lievito","Parce que les lagers ont en général peu d'arômes de levure","Because lagers typically have few yeast aromas"],["Perché le lager non hanno lievito","Parce que les lagers n'ont pas de levure","Because lagers contain no yeast"],["Perché le ale non hanno luppolo","Parce que les ales n'ont pas de houblon","Because ales have no hops"],["Per legge","Par la loi","Because of the law"]],"e":["Il lievito lager dà pochi aromi; quello ale ne dà molti, fruttati e speziati.","La levure lager donne peu d'arômes ; la levure ale en donne beaucoup, fruités et épicés.","Lager yeast gives little aroma; ale yeast gives a lot, fruity and spicy."],"d":["Anche le lager si fanno con lievito, e le ale usano luppolo; non c'è una legge in merito.","Les lagers aussi sont faites avec de la levure, et les ales utilisent du houblon ; aucune loi n'intervient.","Lagers are made with yeast too, and ales use hops; no law is involved."]},{"id":"b110d51ae","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi di lievito caratterizzano la weissbier?","Quels arômes de levure caractérisent la weissbier ?","Which yeast aromas characterise weissbier?"],"o":[["Banana e chiodi di garofano","Banane et clou de girofle","Banana and clove"],["Pino e resina","Pin et résine","Pine and resin"],["Caffè e cioccolato","Café et chocolat","Coffee and chocolate"],["Aia e cuoio","Basse-cour et cuir","Farmyard and leather"]],"e":["Banana (fruttato) e chiodi di garofano (speziato) vengono dal lievito della weissbier.","Banane (fruité) et girofle (épicé) viennent de la levure de la weissbier.","Banana (fruity) and clove (spicy) come from weissbier yeast."],"d":["Pino e resina sono luppolo, caffè e cioccolato malto tostato, aia e cuoio tipici del Brett.","Pin et résine viennent du houblon, café et chocolat du malt torréfié, basse-cour et cuir sont typiques du Brett.","Pine and resin are hops, coffee and chocolate roasted malt, farmyard and leather typical of Brett."]},{"id":"b113b21ef","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Con quale altro nome è nota la weissbier?","Sous quel autre nom connaît-on la weissbier ?","What is weissbier also known as?"],"o":[["Hefeweizen","Hefeweizen","Hefeweizen"],["Blanche","Blanche","Blanche"],["Dunkel","Dunkel","Dunkel"],["Gueuze","Gueuze","Gueuze"]],"e":["Weissbier e hefeweizen indicano la stessa birra di frumento tedesca.","Weissbier et hefeweizen désignent la même bière de blé allemande.","Weissbier and hefeweizen are the same German wheat beer."],"d":["«Blanche» è la witbier, «dunkel» una lager scura, «gueuze» una birra acida.","« Blanche » désigne la witbier, « dunkel » une lager sombre, « gueuze » une bière acide.","'Blanche' is witbier, 'dunkel' a dark lager, 'gueuze' a sour beer."]},{"id":"b1a538c55","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Che cosa significano «Weiss» e «Weizen»?","Que signifient « Weiss » et « Weizen » ?","What do 'Weiss' and 'Weizen' mean?"],"o":[["Bianco e frumento","Blanc et blé","White and wheat"],["Chiaro e scuro","Clair et sombre","Pale and dark"],["Doppio e triplo","Double et triple","Double and triple"],["Lievito e luppolo","Levure et houblon","Yeast and hops"]],"e":["Weiss = bianco, Weizen = frumento: entrambi indicano birre di frumento in Germania.","Weiss = blanc, Weizen = blé : les deux désignent les bières de blé en Allemagne.","Weiss = white, Weizen = wheat: both name wheat beers in Germany."],"d":["Chiaro e scuro sono «hell» e «dunkel»; doppio e triplo ricordano dubbel e tripel.","Clair et sombre se disent « hell » et « dunkel » ; double et triple rappellent dubbel et tripel.","Pale and dark are 'hell' and 'dunkel'; double and triple recall dubbel and tripel."]},{"id":"b149f62ea","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi aggiunti caratterizzano la witbier?","Quels aromates ajoutés caractérisent la witbier ?","Which added flavourings characterise witbier?"],"o":[["Semi di coriandolo e scorza d'arancia","Graines de coriandre et écorce d'orange","Coriander seed and orange peel"],["Caffè e vaniglia","Café et vanille","Coffee and vanilla"],["Zucca e cannella","Citrouille et cannelle","Pumpkin and cinnamon"],["Sciroppo di lampone","Sirop de framboise","Raspberry syrup"]],"e":["Coriandolo e scorza d'arancia danno note di agrumi e fiori alla witbier.","Coriandre et écorce d'orange donnent à la witbier des notes d'agrumes et de fleurs.","Coriander and orange peel give witbier citrus and floral notes."],"d":["Lo sciroppo di lampone si aggiunge a volte alla Berliner weisse al momento del servizio.","Le sirop de framboise s'ajoute parfois à la Berliner weisse au service.","Raspberry syrup is sometimes added to Berliner weisse when served."]},{"id":"b1cddad74","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Quale termine francese si trova a volte sull'etichetta della witbier?","Quel terme français trouve-t-on parfois sur l'étiquette de la witbier ?","Which French term is sometimes on a witbier label?"],"o":[["Blanche","Blanche","Blanche"],["Brune","Brune","Brune"],["Saison","Saison","Saison"],["Ambrée","Ambrée","Ambrée"]],"e":["«Blanche» significa «bianca», come «wit» in olandese.","« Blanche » signifie la même chose que « wit » en néerlandais.","'Blanche' means 'white', like 'wit' in Dutch."],"d":["Saison è un altro stile di lievito; «brune» e «ambrée» descrivono colori.","La saison est un autre style de levure ; « brune » et « ambrée » décrivent des couleurs.","Saison is another yeast-driven style; 'brune' and 'ambrée' describe colours."]},{"id":"b1390812f","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde alla dubbel?","Quelle description correspond à la dubbel ?","Which description fits dubbel?"],"o":[["Ramata-marrone, mela, prugna, chiodi di garofano, alcol alto, sedimento","Cuivrée-brune, pomme, prune, girofle, alcool élevé, dépôt","Copper-brown, apple, plum, clove, high alcohol, sediment"],["Dorata, arancia, banana, alcol molto alto","Dorée, orange, banane, alcool très élevé","Gold, orange, banana, very high alcohol"],["Paglierina, acida, alcol basso","Paille, acide, alcool faible","Straw, sour, low alcohol"],["Nera, caffè, imperial","Noire, café, imperial","Black, coffee, imperial"]],"e":["La dubbel unisce frutta e spezie del lievito a pane tostato, caramello e frutta secca.","La dubbel associe fruits et épices de la levure à pain grillé, caramel et fruits secs.","Dubbel pairs yeast fruit and spice with toast, caramel and dried fruit."],"d":["La seconda è la tripel, la terza la Berliner weisse, la quarta una imperial stout.","La deuxième est la tripel, la troisième la Berliner weisse, la quatrième une imperial stout.","The second is tripel, the third Berliner weisse, the fourth an imperial stout."]},{"id":"b15dc05d1","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Tra dubbel e tripel, quale ha di solito più alcol e quale colore ha?","Entre dubbel et tripel, laquelle est en général la plus alcoolisée et de quelle couleur est-elle ?","Between dubbel and tripel, which usually has more alcohol, and what colour is it?"],"o":[["La tripel, dorata","La tripel, dorée","Tripel, gold"],["La dubbel, marrone","La dubbel, brune","Dubbel, brown"],["La tripel, nera","La tripel, noire","Tripel, black"],["Hanno lo stesso alcol","Elles ont le même alcool","They have the same alcohol"]],"e":["La tripel è dorata e ha alcol alto o molto alto, anche più della dubbel.","La tripel est dorée et a un alcool élevé ou très élevé, plus encore que la dubbel.","Tripel is gold with high or very high alcohol, even higher than dubbel."],"d":["La dubbel è ramata-marrone ma meno alcolica; la tripel non è nera.","La dubbel est cuivrée-brune mais moins alcoolisée ; la tripel n'est pas noire.","Dubbel is copper-brown but less strong; tripel is not black."]},{"id":"b10782f5a","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi caratterizzano la tripel?","Quels arômes caractérisent la tripel ?","Which aromas characterise tripel?"],"o":[["Arancia, banana, pepe, chiodi di garofano dal lievito; miele leggero","Orange, banane, poivre, girofle de la levure ; miel léger","Orange, banana, pepper, clove from yeast; light honey"],["Caffè e cioccolato tostati","Café et chocolat torréfiés","Roasted coffee and chocolate"],["Pino e resina intensi","Pin et résine intenses","Intense pine and resin"],["Aceto e burro rancido","Vinaigre et beurre rance","Vinegar and rancid butter"]],"e":["Nella tripel dominano frutta e spezie del lievito, con malto leggero.","Dans la tripel dominent fruits et épices de la levure, avec un malt léger.","In tripel, yeast fruit and spice dominate over light malt."],"d":["Aceto e burro rancido sono difetti da infezione batterica. Caffè e pino non sono tipici della tripel.","Vinaigre et beurre rance sont des défauts d'infection bactérienne. Café et pin ne sont pas typiques de la tripel.","Vinegar and rancid butter are bacterial-infection faults. Coffee and pine are not typical of tripel."]},{"id":"b178e3bf0","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Quale stile di lievito può essere leggermente acido?","Quel style de levure peut être légèrement acide ?","Which yeast-driven style can be slightly sour?"],"o":[["Saison","Saison","Saison"],["Weissbier","Weissbier","Weissbier"],["Tripel","Tripel","Tripel"],["Dubbel","Dubbel","Dubbel"]],"e":["La saison, fruttata e pepata, può avere una leggera acidità.","La saison, fruitée et poivrée, peut avoir une légère acidité.","Fruity, peppery saison can be slightly sour."],"d":["Weissbier, tripel e dubbel non sono descritte come acide.","Weissbier, tripel et dubbel ne sont pas décrites comme acides.","Weissbier, tripel and dubbel are not described as sour."]},{"id":"b156b157f","c":"b10","p":0,"q":["Quali tratti condividono di solito dubbel, tripel e saison?","Quels traits partagent généralement dubbel, tripel et saison ?","What do dubbel, tripel and saison usually share?"],"o":[["Sedimento da rifermentazione in bottiglia e alta carbonazione","Un dépôt de refermentation en bouteille et une carbonatation élevée","Sediment from bottle-conditioning and high carbonation"],["Colore nero","Une couleur noire","Black colour"],["Fermentazione spontanea","Une fermentation spontanée","Spontaneous fermentation"],["Lievito lager","Une levure lager","Lager yeast"]],"e":["Sono ale molto carbonate, spesso rifermentate in bottiglia, con sedimento.","Ce sont des ales très pétillantes, souvent refermentées en bouteille, avec dépôt.","They are highly carbonated ales, often bottle-conditioned with sediment."],"d":["Sono ale, non lager; non sono nere né a fermentazione spontanea.","Ce sont des ales, pas des lagers ; ni noires ni à fermentation spontanée.","They are ales, not lagers, and neither black nor spontaneously fermented."]},{"id":"b1b60465d","c":"b11","p":0,"q":["Da dove viene il carattere acido degli stili acidi?","D'où vient le caractère acide des styles acides ?","Where does the sour character of sour styles come from?"],"o":[["Da batteri, come i batteri lattici","De bactéries, comme les bactéries lactiques","From bacteria, such as lactic acid bacteria"],["Dal luppolo","Du houblon","From hops"],["Da succo di limone aggiunto","Du jus de citron ajouté","From added lemon juice"],["Dal malto tostato","Du malt torréfié","From roasted malt"]],"e":["I batteri lattici, attivi in fermentazione e maturazione, aggiungono acidità.","Les bactéries lactiques, actives en fermentation et maturation, ajoutent de l'acidité.","Lactic bacteria, active in fermentation and maturation, add acidity."],"d":["Il luppolo dà amaro, il malto tostato caffè e cioccolato; non si aggiunge limone.","Le houblon donne l'amertume, le malt torréfié café et chocolat ; on n'ajoute pas de citron.","Hops give bitterness, roasted malt coffee and chocolate; no lemon is added."]},{"id":"b1f45eb0a","c":"b11","p":0,"q":["Quale descrizione corrisponde alla Berliner weisse?","Quelle description correspond à la Berliner weisse ?","Which description fits Berliner weisse?"],"o":[["Paglierina, velata, moderatamente acida, corpo leggero, alcol basso","Paille, voilée, modérément acide, corps léger, alcool faible","Straw, hazy, moderately sour, light body, low alcohol"],["Dorata, molto acida, alcol alto, fermentazione spontanea","Dorée, très acide, alcool élevé, fermentation spontanée","Gold, very sour, high alcohol, spontaneous fermentation"],["Nera e tostata","Noire et torréfiée","Black and roasted"],["Ambrata e molto amara","Ambrée et très amère","Amber and very bitter"]],"e":["È una birra di frumento leggera e moderatamente acida, con amaro basso o nullo.","C'est une bière de blé légère et modérément acide, à l'amertume faible ou nulle.","It is a light, moderately sour wheat beer with low or no bitterness."],"d":["La seconda opzione è più vicina alla geuze (che però ha alcol medio-alto). La Berliner weisse non è scura né amara.","La deuxième option est plus proche de la geuze. La Berliner weisse n'est ni sombre ni amère.","The second option is closer to geuze. Berliner weisse is neither dark nor bitter."]},{"id":"b1b1c9b0d","c":"b11","p":0,"q":["Con quali sciroppi si serve a volte la Berliner weisse?","Avec quels sirops sert-on parfois la Berliner weisse ?","Which syrups is Berliner weisse sometimes served with?"],"o":[["Lampone o asperula","Framboise ou aspérule","Raspberry or woodruff"],["Menta o limone","Menthe ou citron","Mint or lemon"],["Caramello o vaniglia","Caramel ou vanille","Caramel or vanilla"],["Cola o zenzero","Cola ou gingembre","Cola or ginger"]],"e":["Lampone o asperula, un'erba amarognola che ricorda il fieno dolce.","Framboise ou aspérule, une herbe légèrement amère qui rappelle le foin doux.","Raspberry or woodruff, a slightly bitter herb reminiscent of sweet hay."],"d":["Le altre combinazioni non sono quelle tradizionali per questo stile.","Les autres associations ne sont pas traditionnelles pour ce style.","The other options are not the traditional ones for this style."]},{"id":"b1e2a7b55","c":"b11","p":0,"q":["Come si fa di solito la Berliner weisse?","Comment fait-on généralement la Berliner weisse ?","How is Berliner weisse typically made?"],"o":[["Con lieviti e batteri coltivati","Avec des levures et des bactéries cultivées","With cultured yeast and bacteria"],["Con fermentazione spontanea","Par fermentation spontanée","By spontaneous fermentation"],["Senza lievito","Sans levure","Without yeast"],["Con lievito lager soltanto","Avec seulement de la levure lager","With lager yeast only"]],"e":["La Berliner weisse usa lieviti e batteri coltivati.","La Berliner weisse utilise des levures et des bactéries cultivées.","Berliner weisse uses cultured yeast and bacteria."],"d":["La fermentazione spontanea è il metodo della geuze. Senza lievito non c'è alcol, e un solo lievito lager non darebbe acidità.","La fermentation spontanée est la méthode de la geuze. Sans levure, pas d'alcool, et une levure lager seule ne donnerait pas d'acidité.","Spontaneous fermentation is geuze's method. Without yeast there is no alcohol, and lager yeast alone gives no sourness."]},{"id":"b11f844e3","c":"b11","p":0,"q":["Quale stile acido si fa con fermentazione spontanea?","Quel style acide est fait par fermentation spontanée ?","Which sour style is made by spontaneous fermentation?"],"o":[["Geuze (gueuze)","Geuze (gueuze)","Geuze (gueuze)"],["Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse"],["Saison","Saison","Saison"],["Witbier","Witbier","Witbier"]],"e":["La geuze nasce da lieviti e batteri dell'ambiente, tra cui Brett e batteri lattici.","La geuze naît des levures et bactéries ambiantes, dont le Brett et les bactéries lactiques.","Geuze comes from ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brett and lactic bacteria."],"d":["La Berliner weisse usa microrganismi coltivati; saison e witbier sono stili di lievito, non acidi in senso stretto.","La Berliner weisse utilise des micro-organismes cultivés ; saison et witbier sont des styles de levure.","Berliner weisse uses cultured microbes; saison and witbier are yeast-driven styles."]},{"id":"b1e73880b","c":"b11","p":0,"q":["Quali aromi sono tipici della geuze?","Quels arômes sont typiques de la geuze ?","Which aromas are typical of geuze?"],"o":[["Aia (terra, fieno) e frutta come pompelmo, mela, albicocca, rabarbaro","Basse-cour (terre, foin) et fruits comme pamplemousse, pomme, abricot, rhubarbe","Farmyard (earth, hay) and fruit such as grapefruit, apple, apricot, rhubarb"],["Caffè e cioccolato","Café et chocolat","Coffee and chocolate"],["Banana e chiodi di garofano","Banane et clou de girofle","Banana and clove"],["Caramello e uvetta","Caramel et raisin sec","Caramel and raisin"]],"e":["La geuze è complessa: note di aia e molta frutta, con un filo di mollica.","La geuze est complexe : notes de basse-cour et beaucoup de fruit, avec une pointe de mie.","Geuze is complex: farmyard notes and lots of fruit, with a hint of bread crumb."],"d":["Caffè e cioccolato sono da stout, banana e chiodi di garofano da weissbier, caramello e uvetta da birre maltate come il barley wine.","Café et chocolat évoquent la stout, banane et girofle la weissbier, caramel et raisin sec des bières maltées comme le barley wine.","Coffee and chocolate suggest stout, banana and clove weissbier, caramel and raisin malty beers such as barley wine."]},{"id":"b1a571140","c":"b11","p":0,"q":["Quale affermazione sulla geuze è corretta?","Quelle affirmation sur la geuze est correcte ?","Which statement about geuze is correct?"],"o":[["È acida, dorata, con amaro basso o nullo e molto carbonata","Elle est acide, dorée, à l'amertume faible ou nulle et très pétillante","It is sour, gold, with low or no bitterness and highly carbonated"],["È nera e molto amara","Elle est noire et très amère","It is black and very bitter"],["È una lager","C'est une lager","It is a lager"],["Ha alcol molto basso, sotto il 2%","Elle a un alcool très faible, sous 2 %","It has very low alcohol, under 2%"]],"e":["Geuze: dorata, acida, amaro basso o nullo, alcol medio-alto, sedimento e molte bollicine.","Geuze : dorée, acide, amertume faible ou nulle, alcool moyen-élevé, dépôt et beaucoup de bulles.","Geuze: gold, sour, low or no bitterness, medium-high alcohol, sediment and lots of bubbles."],"d":["Non è nera né amara, non è una lager e il suo alcol è medio-alto.","Elle n'est ni noire ni amère, ce n'est pas une lager et son alcool est moyen à élevé.","It is not black or bitter, not a lager, and its alcohol is medium to high."]},{"id":"b1ad1de48","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Quali sono i tre nemici principali della birra in conservazione?","Quels sont les trois principaux ennemis de la bière en conservation ?","What are the three main enemies of beer in storage?"],"o":[["Ossigeno, calore e luce","Oxygène, chaleur et lumière","Oxygen, heat and light"],["Freddo, buio e umidità","Froid, obscurité et humidité","Cold, darkness and humidity"],["Anidride carbonica, freddo e vetro","Dioxyde de carbone, froid et verre","Carbon dioxide, cold and glass"],["Zucchero, lievito e luppolo","Sucre, levure et houblon","Sugar, yeast and hops"]],"e":["Ossigeno, calore e luce rovinano facilmente la birra.","Oxygène, chaleur et lumière abîment facilement la bière.","Oxygen, heat and light easily damage beer."],"d":["Freddo e buio la proteggono; l'anidride carbonica del fusto la difende dall'ossigeno.","Le froid et l'obscurité la protègent ; le CO2 du fût la défend contre l'oxygène.","Cold and darkness protect it; keg CO2 shields it from oxygen."]},{"id":"b147b2545","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Che cosa succede di solito a una birra conservata troppo a lungo?","Qu'arrive-t-il généralement à une bière conservée trop longtemps ?","What usually happens to a beer kept too long?"],"o":[["Amaro e aromi di luppolo calano; compaiono note di carta o cartone","Amertume et arômes de houblon baissent ; des notes de papier ou de carton apparaissent","Hop aroma and bitterness fade; paper or cardboard notes appear"],["Diventa più amara e più luppolata","Elle devient plus amère et plus houblonnée","It becomes more bitter and hoppy"],["Diventa più alcolica","Elle devient plus alcoolisée","It becomes stronger in alcohol"],["Prende più bollicine","Elle gagne des bulles","It gains more bubbles"]],"e":["È l'invecchiamento ossidativo (staling): luppolo e amaro svaniscono, arriva il cartone.","C'est le vieillissement oxydatif (staling) : houblon et amertume s'estompent, le carton arrive.","This is staling: hops and bitterness fade, cardboard notes arrive."],"d":["Col tempo l'amaro diminuisce, non aumenta; l'alcol non cresce e le bollicine tendono a calare.","Avec le temps, l'amertume diminue au lieu d'augmenter ; l'alcool ne monte pas et les bulles tendent à baisser.","Over time bitterness falls rather than rises; alcohol does not increase and bubbles tend to drop."]},{"id":"b11f99e55","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Quale contenitore protegge PEGGIO la birra dalla luce?","Quel contenant protège le MOINS la bière de la lumière ?","Which container protects beer LEAST from light?"],"o":[["Bottiglia trasparente","Bouteille transparente","Clear glass bottle"],["Bottiglia marrone","Bouteille brune","Brown bottle"],["Lattina","Canette","Can"],["Fusto","Fût","Keg"]],"e":["Vetro trasparente (o verde) protegge poco o nulla: meglio tenerlo in scatole chiuse.","Le verre transparent (ou vert) protège peu ou pas : mieux vaut le garder en cartons fermés.","Clear (or green) glass gives little or no protection: keep it in sealed boxes."],"d":["Lattine e fusti sono opachi; il vetro marrone blocca quasi tutta la luce dannosa.","Canettes et fûts sont opaques ; le verre brun arrête presque toute la lumière nocive.","Cans and kegs are opaque; brown glass blocks almost all damaging light."]},{"id":"b13eb9d33","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Perché la birra in fusto resta fresca più a lungo?","Pourquoi la bière en fût reste-t-elle fraîche plus longtemps ?","Why does keg beer stay fresh longer?"],"o":[["È confezionata con anidride carbonica, che la protegge dall'ossigeno","Elle est conditionnée avec du CO2, qui la protège de l'oxygène","It is packed with carbon dioxide, which protects it from oxygen"],["Contiene conservanti","Elle contient des conservateurs","It contains preservatives"],["Ha più alcol","Elle a plus d'alcool","It has more alcohol"],["È pastorizzata due volte","Elle est pasteurisée deux fois","It is pasteurised twice"]],"e":["Il fusto è riempito con CO2, che tiene lontano l'ossigeno.","Le fût est rempli de CO2, qui tient l'oxygène à distance.","The keg is packed with CO2, which keeps oxygen away."],"d":["Le altre ragioni non sono quelle indicate: è la protezione dall'ossigeno a fare la differenza.","Les autres raisons ne sont pas en cause : c'est la protection contre l'oxygène qui fait la différence.","The other reasons are not the point: protection from oxygen makes the difference."]},{"id":"b1733f5e2","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Una bottiglia di birra è stata aperta: quando va bevuta?","Une bouteille de bière a été ouverte : quand faut-il la boire ?","A bottle of beer has been opened: when should it be drunk?"],"o":[["Subito","Tout de suite","Straight away"],["Entro una settimana in frigo","Dans la semaine au réfrigérateur","Within a week in the fridge"],["Entro un mese","Dans le mois","Within a month"],["Quando si vuole, se chiusa con il tappo","Quand on veut, si on la rebouche","Whenever, if recapped"]],"e":["Una volta aperte, bottiglie e lattine vanno bevute subito per non perdere aromi e bollicine.","Une fois ouvertes, bouteilles et canettes se boivent tout de suite pour garder arômes et bulles.","Once opened, bottles and cans should be drunk at once to keep aroma and carbonation."],"d":["La birra non è come il sake o il vino: aperta perde bollicine e freschezza in fretta.","La bière n'est pas comme le saké ou le vin : ouverte, elle perd vite bulles et fraîcheur.","Beer is unlike sake or wine: opened, it quickly loses bubbles and freshness."]},{"id":"b167862e8","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Che cosa provoca il «colpo di luce» (skunking)?","Qu'est-ce qui provoque le « goût de lumière » (skunking) ?","What causes light strike (skunking)?"],"o":[["La luce che agisce sui composti del luppolo","La lumière qui agit sur les composés du houblon","Light acting on hop compounds"],["Batteri nelle linee di spillatura","Des bactéries dans les lignes de tirage","Bacteria in beer lines"],["Troppo malto tostato","Trop de malt torréfié","Too much roasted malt"],["Il freddo eccessivo","Un froid excessif","Excessive cold"]],"e":["La luce trasforma composti del luppolo e crea odori sgradevoli.","La lumière transforme des composés du houblon et crée des odeurs désagréables.","Light changes hop compounds and creates unpleasant smells."],"d":["I batteri nelle linee danno aceto e burro rancido. Malto tostato e freddo non causano questo difetto.","Les bactéries des lignes donnent vinaigre et beurre rance. Le malt torréfié et le froid ne causent pas ce défaut.","Bacteria in lines give vinegar and rancid butter. Roasted malt and cold do not cause this fault."]},{"id":"b180f0178","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Quali odori indicano un colpo di luce?","Quelles odeurs signalent un goût de lumière ?","Which smells indicate light strike?"],"o":[["Puzzola, capelli bruciati, urina di gatto","Mouffette, cheveux brûlés, urine de chat","Skunky, scorched hair, cat urine"],["Carta e cartone bagnato","Papier et carton mouillé","Paper and wet cardboard"],["Aceto e burro rancido","Vinaigre et beurre rance","Vinegar and rancid butter"],["Caramello e toffee","Caramel et caramel au beurre","Caramel and toffee"]],"e":["Il colpo di luce dà un odore di puzzola, capelli bruciati o urina di gatto.","Le goût de lumière donne une odeur de mouffette, de cheveux brûlés ou d'urine de chat.","Light strike gives a skunky, scorched-hair or cat-urine smell."],"d":["Carta e cartone indicano staling; aceto e burro rancido infezione batterica.","Papier et carton signalent le staling ; vinaigre et beurre rance une infection bactérienne.","Paper and cardboard signal staling; vinegar and rancid butter bacterial infection."]},{"id":"b1ed693f8","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Una birra alla spina sa di aceto e burro rancido. Qual è la causa più probabile?","Une bière pression sent le vinaigre et le beurre rance. Quelle est la cause la plus probable ?","A draught beer tastes of vinegar and rancid butter. What is the most likely cause?"],"o":[["Infezione batterica nelle linee di spillatura sporche","Infection bactérienne dans des lignes de tirage sales","Bacterial infection in poorly maintained beer lines"],["Colpo di luce","Goût de lumière","Light strike"],["Bicchiere troppo freddo","Verre trop froid","A glass that is too cold"],["Troppo luppolo","Trop de houblon","Too much hops"]],"e":["Batteri nei tubi che collegano fusto e rubinetto danno aceto e burro rancido.","Des bactéries dans les tuyaux reliant fût et robinet donnent vinaigre et beurre rance.","Bacteria in the hoses connecting keg and tap give vinegar and rancid butter."],"d":["Il colpo di luce ha odori diversi (puzzola) e il fusto è opaco. Il freddo e il luppolo non creano aceto.","Le goût de lumière a d'autres odeurs (mouffette) et le fût est opaque. Le froid et le houblon ne créent pas de vinaigre.","Light strike smells different (skunky) and kegs are opaque. Cold and hops do not create vinegar."]},{"id":"b13a971a5","c":"b12","p":0,"q":["Che cosa accelera l'invecchiamento ossidativo (staling)?","Qu'est-ce qui accélère le vieillissement oxydatif (staling) ?","What speeds up staling?"],"o":[["Calore e ossigeno","Chaleur et oxygène","Heat and oxygen"],["Freddo e buio","Froid et obscurité","Cold and darkness"],["Bottiglie marroni","Bouteilles brunes","Brown bottles"],["Anidride carbonica","Dioxyde de carbone","Carbon dioxide"]],"e":["Lo staling arriva prima con il caldo e l'ossigeno.","Le staling arrive plus vite avec la chaleur et l'oxygène.","Staling comes faster with heat and oxygen."],"d":["Freddo, buio, vetro marrone e CO2 proteggono la birra, non la invecchiano.","Froid, obscurité, verre brun et CO2 protègent la bière au lieu de la vieillir.","Cold, dark, brown glass and CO2 protect beer rather than ageing it."]},{"id":"b12a0aacb","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Dopo aver versato la birra, si vedono bollicine attaccate alle pareti del bicchiere. Che cosa indicano?","Après le service, des bulles restent accrochées aux parois du verre. Qu'indiquent-elles ?","After pouring, bubbles cling to the sides of the glass. What does this show?"],"o":[["Che il bicchiere non è perfettamente pulito","Que le verre n'est pas parfaitement propre","The glass is not completely clean"],["Che la birra è molto fresca","Que la bière est très fraîche","The beer is very fresh"],["Che la birra è rifermentata in bottiglia","Que la bière est refermentée en bouteille","The beer is bottle-conditioned"],["Che il bicchiere è troppo stretto","Que le verre est trop étroit","The glass is too narrow"]],"e":["Bollicine attaccate alle pareti sono il segno di residui o sporco sul vetro.","Des bulles accrochées aux parois signalent des résidus ou de la saleté sur le verre.","Clinging bubbles signal residue or dirt on the glass."],"d":["Non dipendono da freschezza, rifermentazione o forma del bicchiere.","Elles ne dépendent ni de la fraîcheur, ni de la refermentation, ni de la forme du verre.","They do not depend on freshness, bottle-conditioning or glass shape."]},{"id":"b1c7e9fc8","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Quale caratteristica del bicchiere aiuta la tenuta della schiuma?","Quelle caractéristique du verre aide la tenue de la mousse ?","Which glass feature helps head retention?"],"o":[["Una forma stretta","Une forme étroite","A narrow shape"],["Una coppa molto larga e aperta","Un calice très large et ouvert","A very wide, open bowl"],["Un bicchiere caldo","Un verre chaud","A warm glass"],["Residui di detersivo","Des résidus de détergent","Detergent residue"]],"e":["I bicchieri stretti aiutano la schiuma a durare.","Les verres étroits aident la mousse à tenir.","Narrow glasses help the foam last."],"d":["Una coppa arrotondata aiuta a far roteare, le pareti che si stringono trattengono gli aromi. Il detersivo danneggia la schiuma.","Un calice arrondi aide à faire tourner, des parois resserrées retiennent les arômes. Le détergent nuit à la mousse.","A rounded bowl helps swirling, inward walls hold aromas. Detergent harms the foam."]},{"id":"b1dff5ce5","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Spillando dal fusto, fino a che punto si versa con il bicchiere inclinato a 45°?","Au tirage, jusqu'où verse-t-on avec le verre incliné à 45° ?","Pouring from the keg, how far do you fill with the glass tilted at 45°?"],"o":[["Fino a circa il 70%","Jusqu'à environ 70 %","To about 70% full"],["Fino all'orlo","Jusqu'au bord","Right to the brim"],["Fino al 20%","Jusqu'à 20 %","To 20%"],["Non si inclina mai il bicchiere","On n'incline jamais le verre","The glass is never tilted"]],"e":["Si versa lungo la parete fino al 70% circa, poi si raddrizza e si versa al centro per la schiuma.","On verse le long de la paroi jusqu'à environ 70 %, puis on redresse et on verse au centre pour la mousse.","Pour down the side to about 70%, then upright and pour into the centre for foam."],"d":["Riempire tutto inclinato lascerebbe poca schiuma; il 20% è troppo presto.","Tout remplir incliné laisserait peu de mousse ; 20 %, c'est trop tôt.","Filling entirely tilted would leave little foam; 20% is too early."]},{"id":"b11766930","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Quale regola vale per il rubinetto durante la spillatura?","Quelle règle s'applique au robinet pendant le tirage ?","Which rule applies to the tap when pouring keg beer?"],"o":[["Non deve toccare né la birra né il bicchiere","Il ne doit toucher ni la bière ni le verre","It must not touch the beer or the glass"],["Va immerso nella birra","Il doit plonger dans la bière","It should be dipped in the beer"],["Va aperto solo a metà","Il ne s'ouvre qu'à moitié","It is opened only halfway"],["Va appoggiato al bordo del bicchiere","Il doit reposer sur le bord du verre","It should rest on the glass rim"]],"e":["Il rubinetto non tocca mai birra o bicchiere, per igiene; si apre completamente.","Le robinet ne touche jamais la bière ni le verre, par hygiène ; on l'ouvre complètement.","The tap never touches beer or glass, for hygiene; it is opened fully."],"d":["Il rubinetto va aperto del tutto, non a metà, e non va immerso né appoggiato.","Le robinet s'ouvre en entier, pas à moitié, et ne doit être ni plongé ni appuyé.","The tap is opened fully, not halfway, and is never dipped or rested on the glass."]},{"id":"b1b8079a5","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Come si apre correttamente una bottiglia con tappo a corona?","Comment ouvre-t-on correctement une bouteille capsulée ?","How is a crown-capped bottle opened correctly?"],"o":[["Bottiglia ferma con una mano, tappo tolto con l'apribottiglie in un solo gesto","Bouteille tenue d'une main, capsule retirée au décapsuleur en un seul geste","Steady the bottle with one hand; remove the cap with the opener in one motion"],["Con piccoli colpi ripetuti","Par petits coups répétés","With several small taps"],["Scuotendo prima la bottiglia","En secouant d'abord la bouteille","By shaking the bottle first"],["Con un cavatappi","Avec un tire-bouchon","With a corkscrew"]],"e":["Un gesto unico e deciso, tenendo ferma la bottiglia.","Un seul geste franc, en tenant la bouteille.","One single, smooth motion while steadying the bottle."],"d":["Colpi ripetuti o scuotere la bottiglia fanno schiumare la birra; il cavatappi serve per i tappi di sughero.","Des petits coups ou secouer la bouteille font mousser la bière ; le tire-bouchon sert aux bouchons de liège.","Tapping or shaking makes the beer foam over; a corkscrew is for corks."]},{"id":"b1a29efc0","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Si serve una birra rifermentata in bottiglia con sedimento. Che cosa si fa?","On sert une bière refermentée en bouteille avec dépôt. Que fait-on ?","A bottle-conditioned beer with sediment is being served. What do you do?"],"o":[["Si versa con cura e ci si ferma quando il deposito arriva al collo","On verse avec soin et on s'arrête quand le dépôt arrive au goulot","Pour carefully and stop when the sediment reaches the neck"],["Si agita la bottiglia e si versa tutto","On secoue la bouteille et on verse tout","Shake the bottle and pour everything"],["Si filtra la birra con un tovagliolo","On filtre la bière avec une serviette","Filter the beer through a napkin"],["Si butta il primo terzo della bottiglia","On jette le premier tiers de la bouteille","Throw away the first third"]],"e":["Si tiene la bottiglia inclinata e si smette appena il sedimento si avvicina al collo; un po' di birra resta nella bottiglia.","On garde la bouteille inclinée et on s'arrête dès que le dépôt approche du goulot ; il reste un peu de bière.","Keep the bottle tilted and stop as the sediment nears the neck; a little beer stays behind."],"d":["Agitare e versare tutto è la tecnica per weissbier e witbier, non per le birre in cui si vuole la birra limpida.","Secouer et tout verser, c'est la technique de la weissbier et de la witbier, pas des bières qu'on veut limpides.","Rolling and pouring everything is for weissbier and witbier, not beers meant to stay clear."]},{"id":"b1c80f3ca","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Perché si lascia la bottiglia sul tavolo dopo aver servito una birra con sedimento?","Pourquoi laisse-t-on la bouteille sur la table après avoir servi une bière avec dépôt ?","Why leave the bottle on the table after serving a beer with sediment?"],"o":[["Perché chi beve possa scegliere se aggiungere il sedimento","Pour que le client puisse choisir d'ajouter le dépôt","So the drinker can choose to add the sediment"],["Per mostrare il prezzo","Pour montrer le prix","To show the price"],["Perché è vietato buttarla","Parce qu'il est interdit de la jeter","Because throwing it away is banned"],["Per farla raffreddare","Pour la refroidir","To let it cool"]],"e":["È il cliente a decidere se vuole il sedimento nel bicchiere.","C'est au client de décider s'il veut le dépôt dans son verre.","The drinker decides whether to have the sediment in the glass."],"d":["La scelta è di gusto personale: le altre ragioni non hanno senso.","C'est une question de goût personnel : les autres raisons n'ont pas de sens.","It is about personal choice: the other reasons make no sense."]},{"id":"b19591fb6","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Come si servono di solito weissbier e witbier in bottiglia?","Comment sert-on généralement la weissbier et la witbier en bouteille ?","How are bottled weissbier and witbier usually served?"],"o":[["Si fa rotolare piano la bottiglia prima di aprirla e si versa tutto","On fait rouler doucement la bouteille avant de l'ouvrir et on verse tout","Gently roll the bottle before opening and pour everything"],["Si lascia il sedimento nella bottiglia","On laisse le dépôt dans la bouteille","Leave the sediment in the bottle"],["Si filtrano","On les filtre","Filter them"],["Si servono calde","On les sert chaudes","Serve them warm"]],"e":["Sono torbide per natura: il sedimento va reincorporato.","Elles sont naturellement troubles : on réincorpore le dépôt.","They are naturally hazy: the sediment is mixed back in."],"d":["Per questi stili non si lascia il sedimento; la weissbier si serve ben fredda.","Pour ces styles, on ne laisse pas le dépôt ; la weissbier se sert bien fraîche.","For these styles the sediment is not left behind; weissbier is served well chilled."]},{"id":"b1aef8b30","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["A quale temperatura si serve una pils o una weissbier?","À quelle température sert-on une pils ou une weissbier ?","At what temperature is a pilsner or weissbier served?"],"o":[["Ben fredda, 3–7 °C","Bien fraîche, 3–7 °C","Well chilled, 3–7 °C"],["Fresca, 7–12 °C","Fraîche, 7–12 °C","Chilled, 7–12 °C"],["Leggermente fresca, 12–15 °C","Légèrement rafraîchie, 12–15 °C","Lightly chilled, 12–15 °C"],["Ambiente, 20 °C","Ambiante, 20 °C","Room temperature, 20 °C"]],"e":["Aroma leggero-medio e alcol basso-medio: ben fredda, 3–7 °C.","Arôme léger-moyen et alcool faible-moyen : bien fraîche, 3–7 °C.","Light-medium aroma and low-medium alcohol: well chilled, 3–7 °C."],"d":["7–12 °C è per porter e IPA, 12–15 °C per barley wine e dubbel.","7–12 °C convient aux porters et IPA, 12–15 °C au barley wine et à la dubbel.","7–12 °C suits porter and IPA, 12–15 °C barley wine and dubbel."]},{"id":"b1ca4458c","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["A quale temperatura conviene servire un barley wine?","À quelle température servir un barley wine ?","At what temperature should a barley wine be served?"],"o":[["Leggermente fresco, 12–15 °C","Légèrement rafraîchi, 12–15 °C","Lightly chilled, 12–15 °C"],["Ben freddo, 3–7 °C","Bien frais, 3–7 °C","Well chilled, 3–7 °C"],["Fresco, 7–12 °C","Frais, 7–12 °C","Chilled, 7–12 °C"],["Sotto zero","Sous zéro","Below freezing"]],"e":["Stili complessi e molto alcolici: 12–15 °C per apprezzarne gli aromi.","Styles complexes et très alcoolisés : 12–15 °C pour en apprécier les arômes.","Complex, high-alcohol styles: 12–15 °C to enjoy their aromas."],"d":["Troppo freddo coprirebbe gli aromi complessi del barley wine.","Trop froid masquerait les arômes complexes du barley wine.","Too cold would mute the barley wine's complex aromas."]},{"id":"b1f469e0b","c":"b13","p":0,"q":["Porter, American pale ale e American IPA si servono di solito…","Porter, American pale ale et American IPA se servent généralement…","Porter, American pale ale and American IPA are usually served…"],"o":[["fresche, 7–12 °C","fraîches, 7–12 °C","chilled, 7–12 °C"],["ben fredde, 3–7 °C","bien fraîches, 3–7 °C","well chilled, 3–7 °C"],["leggermente fresche, 12–15 °C","légèrement rafraîchies, 12–15 °C","lightly chilled, 12–15 °C"],["calde, 40 °C","chaudes, 40 °C","warm, 40 °C"]],"e":["Aroma medio-pronunciato, alcol medio-alto: 7–12 °C.","Arôme moyen à prononcé, alcool moyen à élevé : 7–12 °C.","Medium to pronounced aroma, medium to high alcohol: 7–12 °C."],"d":["3–7 °C è per lager e weissbier, 12–15 °C per barley wine e dubbel.","3–7 °C pour lagers et weissbier, 12–15 °C pour barley wine et dubbel.","3–7 °C is for lagers and weissbier, 12–15 °C for barley wine and dubbel."]},{"id":"b1c890127","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Che effetto hanno sale e acidità nel cibo sulla birra?","Quel effet ont le sel et l'acidité du plat sur la bière ?","What effect do salt and acidity in food have on beer?"],"o":[["Più dolce, meno acida, meno amara","Plus douce, moins acide, moins amère","Sweeter, less acidic, less bitter"],["Meno dolce, più acida, più amara","Moins douce, plus acide, plus amère","Less sweet, more acidic, more bitter"],["Più alcolica","Plus alcoolisée","More alcoholic"],["Nessun effetto","Aucun effet","No effect"]],"e":["Sale e acidità «ammorbidiscono» la birra.","Le sel et l'acidité « adoucissent » la bière.","Salt and acidity soften the beer."],"d":["Meno dolce, più acida e più amara è l'effetto di dolcezza e umami. Il piccante aumenta l'alcol percepito.","Moins douce, plus acide et plus amère : c'est l'effet du sucré et de l'umami. Le piquant augmente l'alcool perçu.","Less sweet, more acidic and more bitter is the effect of sweetness and umami. Chilli raises perceived alcohol."]},{"id":"b14dc1389","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Un dolce molto zuccherino come cambia la percezione della birra?","Comment un dessert très sucré change-t-il la perception de la bière ?","How does a very sweet dessert change the perception of beer?"],"o":[["Meno dolce, più acida e più amara","Moins douce, plus acide et plus amère","Less sweet, more acidic and more bitter"],["Più dolce e meno amara","Plus douce et moins amère","Sweeter and less bitter"],["Più alcolica","Plus alcoolisée","More alcoholic"],["Più frizzante","Plus pétillante","More fizzy"]],"e":["La dolcezza nel cibo riduce la dolcezza della birra e ne aumenta acidità e amaro.","Le sucré du plat réduit la douceur de la bière et augmente son acidité et son amertume.","Sweetness in food lowers beer's sweetness and raises its acidity and bitterness."],"d":["L'effetto «più dolce, meno amara» viene da sale e acidità.","L'effet « plus douce, moins amère » vient du sel et de l'acidité.","The 'sweeter, less bitter' effect comes from salt and acidity."]},{"id":"b19a50d73","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Che cosa fa il piccante del peperoncino a una birra?","Que fait le piquant du piment à une bière ?","What does chilli heat do to a beer?"],"o":[["Aumenta la percezione dell'alcol","Il augmente la perception de l'alcool","Increases the perception of alcohol"],["La rende più dolce","Il la rend plus douce","Makes it sweeter"],["Toglie l'amaro","Il enlève l'amertume","Removes bitterness"],["Nessun effetto","Aucun effet","No effect"]],"e":["Il piccante accentua la sensazione di alcol, soprattutto nelle birre forti.","Le piquant accentue la sensation d'alcool, surtout dans les bières fortes.","Chilli heat accentuates the sense of alcohol, especially in strong beers."],"d":["Il piccante non addolcisce la birra né toglie amaro.","Le piquant n'adoucit pas la bière et n'enlève pas l'amertume.","Chilli neither sweetens the beer nor removes bitterness."]},{"id":"b191f7ee1","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Un piatto molto piccante: quale birra rischia di bruciare di più?","Un plat très épicé : quelle bière risque de brûler le plus ?","A very spicy dish: which beer is most likely to burn?"],"o":[["Una tripel o un barley wine","Une tripel ou un barley wine","A tripel or a barley wine"],["Una Berliner weisse","Une Berliner weisse","A Berliner weisse"],["Una lager chiara leggera","Une lager pâle légère","A light pale lager"],["Una blonde ale","Une blonde ale","A blonde ale"]],"e":["Gli stili ad alcol alto o molto alto aumentano molto il bruciore del piccante.","Les styles à l'alcool élevé ou très élevé augmentent fortement la brûlure du piquant.","High or very high-alcohol styles greatly increase the chilli burn."],"d":["Berliner weisse, lager leggere e blonde ale hanno alcol basso o medio.","Berliner weisse, lagers légères et blonde ales ont un alcool faible ou moyen.","Berliner weisse, light lagers and blonde ales have low or medium alcohol."]},{"id":"b1c1df800","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Con un piatto ricco di umami, quale stile rischia di sembrare ancora più amaro?","Avec un plat riche en umami, quel style risque de paraître encore plus amer ?","With an umami-rich dish, which style may seem even more bitter?"],"o":[["American IPA","American IPA","American IPA"],["Weissbier","Weissbier","Weissbier"],["Munich helles","Munich helles","Munich helles"],["Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse"]],"e":["Gli stili molto amari come l'American IPA diventano ancora più amari con umami, dolcezza o amaro.","Les styles très amers comme l'American IPA deviennent encore plus amers avec umami, sucré ou amer.","High-bitterness styles like American IPA get even more bitter with umami, sweetness or bitterness."],"d":["Weissbier e Berliner weisse hanno amaro basso; la helles da basso a medio.","Weissbier et Berliner weisse ont une amertume faible ; la helles faible à moyenne.","Weissbier and Berliner weisse have low bitterness; helles low to medium."]},{"id":"b1f50333e","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Perché una geuze può diventare difficile con un dolce?","Pourquoi une geuze peut-elle devenir difficile avec un dessert ?","Why can a geuze become difficult with a dessert?"],"o":[["La dolcezza del cibo la fa sembrare ancora più acida","Le sucré du plat la fait paraître encore plus acide","Sweetness in the food makes it seem even more acidic"],["La dolcezza la fa sembrare più alcolica","Le sucré la fait paraître plus alcoolisée","Sweetness makes it seem stronger"],["Il dolce la rende torbida","Le dessert la rend trouble","The dessert makes it cloudy"],["Il dolce toglie le bollicine","Le dessert enlève les bulles","The dessert removes the bubbles"]],"e":["Gli stili molto acidi sembrano ancora più acidi con dolcezza o umami nel cibo.","Les styles très acides paraissent encore plus acides avec du sucré ou de l'umami.","High-acidity styles seem even more acidic with sweetness or umami in food."],"d":["Il dolce non agisce su alcol, limpidezza o bollicine.","Le dessert n'agit ni sur l'alcool, ni sur la limpidité, ni sur les bulles.","Dessert does not affect alcohol, clarity or bubbles."]},{"id":"b187b9263","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Perché birra e piatto dovrebbero avere un'intensità di sapore simile?","Pourquoi bière et plat doivent-ils avoir une intensité de saveur proche ?","Why should beer and dish have a similar flavour intensity?"],"o":[["Perché uno non copra l'altro","Pour que l'un n'écrase pas l'autre","So one does not overpower the other"],["Perché la birra sia più fredda","Pour que la bière soit plus fraîche","So the beer is colder"],["Per aumentare l'alcol","Pour augmenter l'alcool","To increase the alcohol"],["Per ridurre le bollicine","Pour réduire les bulles","To reduce the bubbles"]],"e":["Con intensità diverse, il più forte copre il più delicato.","Avec des intensités différentes, le plus fort écrase le plus délicat.","With different intensities, the stronger one masks the more delicate."],"d":["L'intensità non riguarda temperatura, alcol o bollicine della birra.","L'intensité ne concerne ni la température, ni l'alcool, ni les bulles.","Intensity has nothing to do with temperature, alcohol or bubbles."]},{"id":"b1bedfeb3","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Una stout con note di caffè e cioccolato con un dolce al cacao: su quale principio si basa l'abbinamento?","Une stout aux notes de café et de chocolat avec un dessert au cacao : sur quel principe repose l'accord ?","A stout with coffee and chocolate notes alongside a cocoa dessert: which principle does this pairing use?"],"o":[["Aromi simili o complementari tra birra e cibo","Des arômes semblables ou complémentaires entre bière et plat","Similar or complementary aromas in beer and food"],["Il sale riduce l'amaro","Le sel réduit l'amertume","Salt reduces bitterness"],["Il piccante aumenta l'alcol","Le piquant augmente l'alcool","Chilli raises alcohol"],["Contrasto di colore","Le contraste de couleur","Colour contrast"]],"e":["Aromi simili creano un legame familiare tra birra e piatto.","Des arômes semblables créent un lien familier entre bière et plat.","Similar aromas create a familiar connection between beer and dish."],"d":["Qui non ci sono sale o piccante in gioco, e il colore non è un criterio di abbinamento.","Il n'y a ici ni sel ni piquant, et la couleur n'est pas un critère d'accord.","No salt or chilli is involved here, and colour is not a pairing criterion."]},{"id":"b12d7d356","c":"b14","p":0,"q":["Perché lo stesso abbinamento può piacere a una persona e non a un'altra?","Pourquoi un même accord peut-il plaire à une personne et pas à une autre ?","Why can the same pairing please one person and not another?"],"o":[["Ognuno ha preferenze e sensibilità diverse","Chacun a des préférences et des sensibilités différentes","People have different preferences and sensitivities"],["Perché la birra cambia da un bicchiere all'altro","Parce que la bière change d'un verre à l'autre","Because the beer changes from glass to glass"],["Perché esistono regole fisse","Parce qu'il existe des règles fixes","Because there are fixed rules"],["Non succede mai","Cela n'arrive jamais","It never happens"]],"e":["Le persone percepiscono gusti e aromi in modo diverso: le interazioni sono principi, non regole.","Chacun perçoit saveurs et arômes différemment : les interactions sont des principes, pas des règles.","People perceive tastes and aromas differently: interactions are principles, not rules."],"d":["Proprio perché non ci sono regole fisse bisogna tener conto della persona.","C'est justement parce qu'il n'y a pas de règles fixes qu'il faut tenir compte de la personne.","Precisely because there are no fixed rules, the individual matters."]}],"lessons":[{"c":"b01","t":["Che cos'è la birra","Qu'est-ce que la bière ?","What beer is"],"p":[["La birra è una categoria molto varia: si va dalle pils dorate e limpide alle stout nere e impenetrabili. Eppure tutte hanno qualcosa in comune: sono bevande alcoliche fermentate, fatte di solito con malto (cereali maltati), acqua e lievito, e aromatizzate con il luppolo.","La bière est une catégorie très variée : des pils dorées et limpides aux stouts noires et opaques. Toutes ont pourtant des points communs : ce sont des boissons alcoolisées fermentées, faites en général avec du malt (céréales maltées), de l'eau et de la levure, et aromatisées au houblon.","Beer is a hugely varied category, from clear golden pilsners to opaque black stouts. Yet they all share something: they are fermented alcoholic drinks, usually made from malt (malted grains), water and yeast, and flavoured with hops."],["Per fare alcol serve un liquido zuccherino. Si aggiunge il lievito, che consuma lo zucchero e lo trasforma in alcol, producendo nello stesso tempo anidride carbonica (CO2) e aromi: è la fermentazione. Il grado alcolico si misura in percentuale sul volume: 5% vol. significa che il 5% del liquido è alcol. Per la birra conviene pensare a una scala: bassa fino al 4%, media 4,1–5,9%, alta 6–9%, molto alta oltre il 9%.","Pour faire de l'alcool, il faut un liquide sucré. On ajoute la levure, qui consomme le sucre et le transforme en alcool, en produisant en même temps du dioxyde de carbone (CO2) et des arômes : c'est la fermentation. Le degré d'alcool s'exprime en pourcentage du volume : 5 % vol. signifie que 5 % du liquide est de l'alcool. Pour la bière, on peut retenir une échelle : faible jusqu'à 4 %, moyen 4,1–5,9 %, élevé 6–9 %, très élevé au-delà de 9 %.","To make alcohol you need a sugary liquid. Yeast is added; it eats the sugar and turns it into alcohol, producing carbon dioxide (CO2) and aromas at the same time: this is fermentation. Alcohol is measured as alcohol by volume: 5% abv means 5% of the liquid is alcohol. For beer, a handy scale is: low up to 4%, medium 4.1–5.9%, high 6–9%, very high above 9%."]],"k":[["Birra: bevanda alcolica fermentata da malto, acqua, lievito, aromatizzata con luppolo","Bière : boisson alcoolisée fermentée à base de malt, eau, levure, aromatisée au houblon","Beer: fermented alcoholic drink from malt, water and yeast, flavoured with hops"],["Fermentazione: zucchero + lievito → alcol + CO2 + aromi","Fermentation : sucre + levure → alcool + CO2 + arômes","Fermentation: sugar + yeast → alcohol + CO2 + aromas"],["Alcol: basso ≤4% · medio 4,1–5,9% · alto 6–9% · molto alto >9%","Alcool : faible ≤4 % · moyen 4,1–5,9 % · élevé 6–9 % · très élevé >9 %","Alcohol: low ≤4% · medium 4.1–5.9% · high 6–9% · very high >9%"]]},{"c":"b01","t":["Quattro ingredienti e una conversione","Quatre ingrédients et une conversion","Four ingredients and one conversion"],"p":[["Il malto fornisce lo zucchero che il lievito trasformerà in alcol, dà gran parte del colore e può portare molti aromi. L'acqua, in volume, è l'ingrediente principale: è l'ambiente liquido in cui il lievito lavora, e il birrificio ne usa tanta, quindi ha bisogno di una fonte abbondante e affidabile. Il luppolo (il cono della pianta) un tempo serviva soprattutto per le sue proprietà antibatteriche; oggi si apprezza per amaro e aromi. Il lievito crea alcol e anidride carbonica e può dare aromi.","Le malt fournit le sucre que la levure transformera en alcool, donne l'essentiel de la couleur et peut apporter de nombreux arômes. L'eau est, en volume, l'ingrédient principal : c'est le milieu liquide où travaille la levure, et la brasserie en consomme beaucoup, d'où le besoin d'une source abondante et fiable. Le houblon (le cône de la plante) servait d'abord pour ses propriétés antibactériennes ; on l'apprécie aujourd'hui pour l'amertume et les arômes. La levure crée l'alcool et le gaz carbonique et peut donner des arômes.","Malt supplies the sugar that yeast will turn into alcohol, gives most of the colour and can bring many aromas. Water is, by volume, the main ingredient: it is the liquid in which the yeast works, and breweries use a lot of it, so they need a plentiful, reliable supply. Hops (the cones of the plant) were first used mainly for their antibacterial, preserving effect; today they are prized for bitterness and aroma. Yeast creates the alcohol and carbonation and can add aromas."],["Il malto però arriva al birrificio senza zucchero: i chicchi sono pieni di amido, cioè zuccheri legati in lunghe catene che il lievito non può mangiare. Servono gli enzimi, sostanze che accelerano le reazioni e spezzano l'amido in zuccheri più corti: è la conversione dell'amido. Per fortuna il malto stesso porta sia l'amido sia gli enzimi: quando il malto macinato incontra acqua calda, gli enzimi trasformano l'amido in zucchero, che si scioglie formando un liquido zuccherino.","Mais le malt arrive à la brasserie sans sucre : les grains sont pleins d'amidon, c'est-à-dire de sucres liés en longues chaînes que la levure ne peut pas consommer. Il faut des enzymes, des substances qui accélèrent les réactions et coupent l'amidon en sucres plus courts : c'est la conversion de l'amidon. Heureusement, le malt apporte à la fois l'amidon et les enzymes : quand le malt concassé rencontre l'eau chaude, les enzymes transforment l'amidon en sucre, qui se dissout pour former un liquide sucré.","Malt, however, reaches the brewery with no sugar: the grains are full of starch, sugars bonded into long chains that yeast cannot eat. Enzymes are needed: catalysts that speed up reactions and break starch into shorter sugars. This is starch conversion. Conveniently, malt supplies both the starch and the enzymes: when milled malt meets hot water, the enzymes turn the starch into sugar, which dissolves into a sugary liquid."]],"k":[["Malto: zucchero, colore, aromi","Malt : sucre, couleur, arômes","Malt: sugar, colour, aromas"],["Acqua: l'ingrediente principale in volume","Eau : l'ingrédient principal en volume","Water: the main ingredient by volume"],["Luppolo: un tempo conservante, oggi amaro e aromi","Houblon : autrefois conservateur, aujourd'hui amertume et arômes","Hops: once a preservative, now bitterness and aroma"],["Il malto porta amido ed enzimi: con acqua calda l'amido diventa zucchero","Le malt apporte amidon et enzymes : avec l'eau chaude, l'amidon devient sucre","Malt brings starch and enzymes: with hot water starch becomes sugar"]]},{"c":"b02","t":["La vita di un chicco e la maltazione","La vie d'un grain et le maltage","The life of a grain, and malting"],"p":[["Per i birrai il cereale più importante è l'orzo, ma si usano anche frumento, mais, avena, segale, riso e sorgo. Un chicco è fatto di un embrione (la futura piantina), di una riserva di energia sotto forma di amido e di un involucro protettivo, la buccia. In primavera, con caldo e umidità, l'embrione comincia a crescere e, per nutrirsi, libera enzimi che trasformano l'amido in zuccheri.","Pour les brasseurs, la céréale la plus importante est l'orge, mais on utilise aussi le blé, le maïs, l'avoine, le seigle, le riz et le sorgho. Un grain se compose d'un embryon (la future plante), d'une réserve d'énergie sous forme d'amidon et d'une enveloppe protectrice, la balle. Au printemps, avec la chaleur et l'humidité, l'embryon commence à pousser et, pour se nourrir, libère des enzymes qui transforment l'amidon en sucres.","For brewers the most important grain is barley, but wheat, maize (corn), oats, rye, rice and sorghum are used too. A grain is made of an embryo (the future plant), an energy store in the form of starch, and a protective casing, the husk. In spring, when it is warm and wet enough, the embryo starts to grow and, to feed itself, releases enzymes that turn the starch into sugars."],["La maltazione imita questa primavera. 1. Macerazione: i chicchi vengono immersi in acqua. 2. Germinazione: assorbita abbastanza acqua, l'embrione cresce e dentro il chicco si formano gli enzimi. 3. Essiccazione (kilning): bisogna fermare la crescita, altrimenti l'embrione consumerebbe l'amido; si scaldano e si asciugano i chicchi con aria calda in un forno. Il malto secco, con amido ed enzimi, si conserva fino all'uso; l'essiccazione crea anche colore e aromi.","Le maltage imite ce printemps. 1. Trempe : les grains sont immergés dans l'eau. 2. Germination : une fois assez d'eau absorbée, l'embryon pousse et des enzymes se forment dans le grain. 3. Touraillage : il faut arrêter la croissance, sinon l'embryon consommerait l'amidon ; on chauffe et sèche les grains à l'air chaud dans un four, la touraille. Le malt sec, avec amidon et enzymes, se conserve jusqu'à l'emploi ; le touraillage crée aussi couleur et arômes.","Malting mimics that spring. 1. Steeping: the grains are submerged in water. 2. Germination: once they have absorbed enough water, the embryo grows and enzymes form inside the grain. 3. Kilning: growth must be stopped, or the embryo would use up the starch; the grains are heated and dried with warm air in a kiln. The dry malt, holding starch and enzymes, keeps until the brewer needs it, and kilning also creates colour and aromas."]],"k":[["Orzo il cereale principale; anche frumento, mais, avena, segale, riso, sorgo","Orge la céréale principale ; aussi blé, maïs, avoine, seigle, riz, sorgho","Barley first; also wheat, maize, oats, rye, rice, sorghum"],["Chicco: embrione, amido (riserva), buccia","Grain : embryon, amidon (réserve), balle","Grain: embryo, starch (energy store), husk"],["Maltazione: macerazione → germinazione (enzimi) → essiccazione","Maltage : trempe → germination (enzymes) → touraillage","Malting: steeping → germination (enzymes) → kilning"],["L'essiccazione ferma la crescita e crea colore e aromi","Le touraillage stoppe la croissance et crée couleur et arômes","Kilning stops growth and creates colour and aromas"]]},{"c":"b02","t":["Malti base e malti speciali","Malts de base et malts spéciaux","Base malts and speciality malts"],"p":[["Cambiando temperatura e durata dell'essiccazione si ottengono malti diversi; alcuni vengono anche tostati. I malti base sono la maggior parte del malto usato: sono essiccati alle temperature più basse, così gli enzimi restano intatti per lavorare poi nell'ammostamento. Danno aromi di cracker, pasta di pane, mollica, miele leggero e, da soli, una birra paglierina o dorata.","En variant la température et la durée du touraillage, on obtient des malts différents ; certains sont aussi torréfiés. Les malts de base forment l'essentiel du malt utilisé : touraillés aux températures les plus basses, ils gardent leurs enzymes intactes pour le brassage. Ils donnent des arômes de cracker, pâte à pain, mie de pain, miel léger et, seuls, une bière paille ou dorée.","Varying the temperature and length of kilning gives different malts; some are roasted too. Base malts make up most of the malt a brewer uses: they are kilned at the lowest temperatures, so their enzymes survive to work later during mashing. They give aromas of water cracker, bread dough, bread crumb and light honey and, used alone, a straw or gold beer."],["I malti speciali servono per colore e aromi e si usano di solito in piccole quantità, insieme ai malti base. Si ottengono con un'essiccazione più calda o più lunga, oppure tostando il malto a temperature ancora più alte: gli enzimi si danneggiano o si distruggono. Aromi possibili: biscotto digestive, crosta di pane, pane tostato, frutta a guscio tostata, caramello, frutta secca, zucchero filato, caffè, cioccolato. Colori: ambra, rame, marrone, perfino nero.","Les malts spéciaux servent à la couleur et aux arômes et s'emploient généralement en petites quantités, avec les malts de base. On les obtient par un touraillage plus chaud ou plus long, ou en torréfiant le malt à des températures encore plus élevées : leurs enzymes sont abîmées ou détruites. Arômes possibles : biscuit digestive, croûte de pain, pain grillé, fruits à coque grillés, caramel, fruits secs, barbe à papa, café, chocolat. Couleurs : ambre, cuivre, brun, voire noir.","Speciality malts are used for colour and aroma, usually in small amounts alongside base malts. They are made by kilning hotter or longer, or by roasting malt at even higher temperatures, which damages or destroys their enzymes. Possible aromas: digestive biscuit (graham cracker), bread crust, toast, toasted nuts, caramel, dried fruit, candy floss, coffee and chocolate. Colours: amber, copper, brown, even black."]],"k":[["Malti base: essiccati a bassa temperatura, enzimi intatti, la maggior parte della ricetta","Malts de base : touraillés à basse température, enzymes intactes, l'essentiel de la recette","Base malts: kilned lowest, enzymes intact, most of the recipe"],["Malti base: cracker, pasta di pane, mollica, miele leggero; colore paglierino o dorato","Malts de base : cracker, pâte à pain, mie, miel léger ; couleur paille ou dorée","Base malts: water cracker, bread dough, crumb, light honey; straw or gold colour"],["Malti speciali: più calore o tostatura, enzimi danneggiati, piccole dosi","Malts spéciaux : plus de chaleur ou torréfaction, enzymes abîmées, petites doses","Speciality malts: more heat or roasting, enzymes damaged, small amounts"],["Speciali: biscotto, tostato, caramello, frutta secca, caffè, cioccolato; da ambra a nero","Spéciaux : biscuit, grillé, caramel, fruits secs, café, chocolat ; de l'ambre au noir","Speciality: biscuit, toast, caramel, dried fruit, coffee, chocolate; amber to black"]]},{"c":"b02","t":["Altre fonti di zucchero e la ricetta dei cereali","Autres sources de sucre et la recette des céréales","Other sugar sources and the grain bill"],"p":[["A volte insieme al malto si usano altri cereali, zuccheri o sciroppi: forniscono zuccheri da fermentare e possono cambiare consistenza e aromi. Riso e mais, come la maggior parte di zuccheri e sciroppi, tendono a dare una birra con aromi meno intensi e corpo più leggero. Il frumento, invece, può dare una consistenza morbida e cremosa e contribuire alla torbidità.","On utilise parfois, avec le malt, d'autres céréales, des sucres ou des sirops : ils fournissent des sucres à fermenter et peuvent modifier texture et arômes. Le riz et le maïs, comme la plupart des sucres et sirops, donnent plutôt une bière moins aromatique et plus légère en corps. Le blé, lui, peut donner une texture douce et crémeuse et contribuer au trouble.","Other grains, sugars or syrups are sometimes used alongside malt: they provide fermentable sugar and can change texture and aroma. Rice and maize, like most sugars and syrups, tend to give lighter aroma intensity and lighter body. Wheat, on the other hand, can give a smooth, creamy texture and add to haziness."],["La ricetta dei cereali (in inglese «grain bill») elenca tipi e quantità di malti e cereali usati per una birra. Può essere un solo malto, ma di solito è un mix: un malto base costituisce la maggior parte e porta amido e tanti enzimi per la conversione, mentre piccole quantità di malti speciali regolano colore, aromi e complessità.","La recette des céréales (le « grain bill » des anglophones) liste les types et quantités de malts et de céréales d'une bière. Elle peut se limiter à un seul malt, mais c'est le plus souvent un mélange : un malt de base en constitue l'essentiel et apporte l'amidon et beaucoup d'enzymes pour la conversion, tandis que de petites quantités de malts spéciaux règlent couleur, arômes et complexité.","The grain bill is the recipe listing the types and amounts of malts and grains in a beer. It can be a single malt, but most recipes use a mix: a base malt makes up the majority, bringing starch and plenty of enzymes for conversion, while small amounts of speciality malts set the colour, aromas and complexity."]],"k":[["Riso, mais, zuccheri, sciroppi: aromi meno intensi, corpo più leggero","Riz, maïs, sucres, sirops : arômes moins intenses, corps plus léger","Rice, maize, sugars, syrups: lighter aroma intensity and body"],["Frumento: consistenza cremosa e torbidità","Blé : texture crémeuse et trouble","Wheat: smooth, creamy texture and haze"],["Ricetta dei cereali: soprattutto malto base + poco malto speciale","Recette des céréales : surtout malt de base + un peu de malt spécial","Grain bill: mostly base malt + a little speciality malt"]]},{"c":"b03","t":["Macinare e ammostare","Concasser et brasser","Milling and mashing"],"p":[["La produzione segue sei tappe: macinatura, ammostamento, bollitura del mosto, fermentazione, carbonazione e confezionamento. Si comincia macinando (frantumando) i chicchi di malto: il malto macinato si chiama «grist» e passa subito alla tappa successiva.","L'élaboration suit six étapes : concassage, brassage (empâtage), ébullition du moût, fermentation, carbonatation et conditionnement. On commence par concasser les grains de malt : le malt concassé s'appelle la mouture (« grist ») et passe aussitôt à l'étape suivante.","Production follows six key stages: milling, mashing, wort boiling, fermentation, carbonation and packaging. It starts by milling (crushing) the malted grains: the milled grain is called grist and moves straight on to the next stage."],["L'ammostamento comincia quando il grist si mescola con acqua calda, formando l'impasto (mash). Gli enzimi del malto trasformano l'amido in zuccheri, che si sciolgono in un liquido zuccherino ancora mescolato a parti solide, soprattutto bucce. Alla fine il liquido viene separato dai solidi: il liquido si chiama mosto (wort), i solidi rimasti trebbie (spent grains).","Le brassage commence quand la mouture est mélangée à l'eau chaude pour former la maische. Les enzymes du malt transforment l'amidon en sucres, qui se dissolvent dans un liquide sucré encore mêlé de particules solides, surtout des balles. À la fin, on sépare le liquide des solides : le liquide s'appelle le moût, les solides restants les drêches.","Mashing begins when the grist is mixed with hot water, making the mash. The malt enzymes turn the starch into sugars, which dissolve into a sugary liquid still mixed with solid bits, mainly husks. At the end the liquid is separated from the solids: the liquid is called wort and the leftover solids are spent grains."]],"k":[["Sei tappe: macinatura, ammostamento, bollitura, fermentazione, carbonazione, confezionamento","Six étapes : concassage, brassage, ébullition, fermentation, carbonatation, conditionnement","Six stages: milling, mashing, boiling, fermentation, carbonation, packaging"],["Malto macinato = grist","Malt concassé = mouture (grist)","Milled malt = grist"],["Grist + acqua calda = mash; enzimi: amido → zucchero","Mouture + eau chaude = maische ; enzymes : amidon → sucre","Grist + hot water = mash; enzymes turn starch to sugar"],["Liquido separato = mosto (wort); solidi = trebbie","Liquide séparé = moût ; solides = drêches","Separated liquid = wort; solids = spent grains"]]},{"c":"b03","t":["Bollire, raffreddare, fermentare","Bouillir, refroidir, fermenter","Boiling, cooling, fermenting"],"p":[["Il mosto viene bollito. La bollitura uccide i microrganismi, evita che la birra si guasti e aiuta a renderla sicura da bere; ed è il momento delle principali aggiunte di luppolo. Dopo la bollitura il mosto si raffredda rapidamente fino a una temperatura adatta alla fermentazione.","Le moût est porté à ébullition. L'ébullition tue les micro-organismes, évite que la bière ne se gâte et contribue à la rendre sûre ; c'est aussi le moment des principaux ajouts de houblon. Après l'ébullition, le moût est refroidi rapidement jusqu'à une température propice à la fermentation.","The wort is then boiled. Boiling kills microorganisms, prevents spoilage and helps make the beer safe to drink; it is also when the main hop additions are made. After boiling, the wort is cooled rapidly to a temperature suitable for fermentation."],["Il mosto freddo passa in un recipiente di fermentazione dove si aggiunge il lievito. Durante la fermentazione il lievito consuma gli zuccheri e crea alcol, anidride carbonica e aromi. Ricorda l'ordine: macinare → ammostare → bollire (con luppolo) → raffreddare → fermentare (con lievito).","Le moût refroidi passe dans une cuve de fermentation où l'on ajoute la levure. Pendant la fermentation, la levure consomme les sucres et crée alcool, gaz carbonique et arômes. Retenez l'ordre : concasser → brasser → bouillir (avec le houblon) → refroidir → fermenter (avec la levure).","The cooled wort goes into a fermentation vessel where yeast is added. During fermentation the yeast eats the sugars and creates alcohol, carbon dioxide and aromas. Remember the order: mill → mash → boil (with hops) → cool → ferment (with yeast)."]],"k":[["Bollitura: uccide i microrganismi, rende la birra sicura","Ébullition : tue les micro-organismes, rend la bière sûre","Boiling: kills microorganisms, makes beer safe"],["Le aggiunte principali di luppolo avvengono durante la bollitura","Les principaux ajouts de houblon ont lieu pendant l'ébullition","Main hop additions happen during the boil"],["Raffreddamento rapido, poi lievito nel fermentatore","Refroidissement rapide, puis levure dans la cuve","Rapid cooling, then yeast in the fermenter"]]},{"c":"b03","t":["Bollicine e confezioni","Bulles et conditionnement","Bubbles and packaging"],"p":[["Quando una birra viene carbonata, l'anidride carbonica si scioglie nel liquido sotto pressione: le bollicine salgono nel bicchiere, si sentono in bocca e formano la schiuma. Il lievito produce già CO2 durante la fermentazione; per completare il livello si può iniettare anidride carbonica comprata o recuperata da fermentazioni precedenti. Oppure si fa una seconda fermentazione in bottiglia chiusa: è la rifermentazione in bottiglia, che lascia un sedimento di lievito sul fondo.","Quand on carbonate une bière, le dioxyde de carbone se dissout dans le liquide sous pression : les bulles montent dans le verre, se sentent en bouche et forment la mousse. La levure produit déjà du CO2 pendant la fermentation ; pour compléter, on peut injecter du gaz carbonique acheté ou récupéré de fermentations précédentes. On peut aussi faire une seconde fermentation en bouteille fermée : c'est la refermentation en bouteille, qui laisse un dépôt de levure au fond.","When beer is carbonated, carbon dioxide dissolves in it under pressure: the bubbles rise in the glass, are felt in the mouth and build the foam. Yeast already makes some CO2 during fermentation; to top this up, carbon dioxide that was bought or recovered from earlier fermentations can be injected. Alternatively, a further fermentation can take place in the sealed bottle: this is bottle-conditioning, which leaves a yeast sediment at the bottom."],["Infine la birra va confezionata per essere venduta e distribuita. I contenitori più usati sono lattine, bottiglie e fusti (keg).","Enfin, la bière doit être conditionnée pour être vendue et distribuée. Les contenants les plus courants sont les canettes, les bouteilles et les fûts.","Finally, the beer must be packaged so it can be sold and distributed. The most widely used containers are cans, bottles and kegs."]],"k":[["Carbonazione: CO2 sciolta sotto pressione → bollicine e schiuma","Carbonatation : CO2 dissous sous pression → bulles et mousse","Carbonation: CO2 dissolved under pressure → bubbles and foam"],["CO2 dalla fermentazione, più CO2 iniettata (comprata o recuperata)","CO2 de la fermentation, plus CO2 injecté (acheté ou récupéré)","CO2 from fermentation, topped up by injected CO2 (bought or recovered)"],["Rifermentazione in bottiglia: sedimento di lievito","Refermentation en bouteille : dépôt de levure","Bottle-conditioning: yeast sediment"],["Confezioni: lattine, bottiglie, fusti","Conditionnement : canettes, bouteilles, fûts","Packaging: cans, bottles, kegs"]]},{"c":"b04","t":["La pianta del luppolo e le sue varietà","La plante de houblon et ses variétés","The hop plant and its varieties"],"p":[["Il luppolo è una pianta rampicante. Ogni primavera spinge nuovi germogli dal terreno; i fusti che crescono (in inglese «bines») producono durante l'anno i coni, la parte che interessa ai birrai. In autunno i fusti si tagliano vicino al suolo e si raccolgono i coni, che vengono essiccati per conservarli a lungo senza che marciscano. Si possono usare così, ma è raro: molto più spesso i coni secchi vengono macinati e pressati in pellet, che occupano meno spazio. Il luppolo si confeziona e si tiene in frigorifero per conservare amaro e aromi.","Le houblon est une plante grimpante. Chaque printemps, il pousse de nouvelles tiges depuis le sol ; ces tiges volubiles produisent au fil de l'année les cônes, la partie qui intéresse les brasseurs. À l'automne, on coupe les tiges près du sol et on récolte les cônes, que l'on sèche pour les conserver longtemps sans qu'ils pourrissent. On peut les employer tels quels, mais c'est rare : bien plus souvent, les cônes secs sont broyés et pressés en pellets, plus compacts. Le houblon est emballé et réfrigéré pour garder amertume et arômes.","Hops are climbing plants. Each spring new shoots come up from the ground; the bines that grow from them produce hop cones over the year, the part brewers want. In autumn the bines are cut near the ground and the cones are harvested, then dried so they can be kept a long time without rotting. Dried cones can be used as they are, but that is relatively rare: far more often they are milled and pressed into space-saving pellets. Hops are packed and refrigerated to keep their bitterness and aroma."],["Esistono centinaia di varietà, ognuna con aromi, intensità e amaro un po' diversi e con un clima preferito. Per questo i grandi Paesi produttori sono associati a stili di luppolo. I luppoli tradizionali tedeschi, cechi o britannici hanno aromi sottili: speziati, floreali, erbacei, terrosi o fruttati. I luppoli americani, neozelandesi o australiani tendono ad avere note intense di agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, frutta tropicale o pino. Ogni anno però escono nuove varietà, e ogni Paese può produrre aromi molto diversi.","Il existe des centaines de variétés, chacune avec des arômes, une intensité et une amertume un peu différents et un climat de prédilection. Les grands pays producteurs sont donc associés à des profils de houblon. Les houblons traditionnels allemands, tchèques ou britanniques ont des arômes subtils : épicés, floraux, herbacés, terreux ou fruités. Les houblons américains, néo-zélandais ou australiens tendent vers des notes intenses d'agrumes, de fruits à noyau, de fruits tropicaux ou de pin. Mais de nouvelles variétés sortent chaque année, et chaque pays peut produire des arômes très variés.","There are hundreds of hop varieties, each with slightly different aromas, aroma intensity and bitterness, and each with a climate it grows best in. So the well-known hop countries are linked with hop styles. Traditional German, Czech or British hops are known for subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity aromas. American, New Zealand or Australian hops tend to show intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical fruit or pine notes. New varieties appear every year, though, so every hop country can produce a wide range of aromas."]],"k":[["Il cono è la parte usata; si essicca e di solito si trasforma in pellet","Le cône est la partie utilisée ; on le sèche et le plus souvent on en fait des pellets","The cone is the part used; dried, usually turned into pellets"],["Luppolo confezionato e refrigerato per conservare amaro e aromi","Houblon emballé et réfrigéré pour garder amertume et arômes","Packed and refrigerated to keep bitterness and aroma"],["Tedeschi, cechi, britannici: sottili, speziati, floreali, erbacei, terrosi, fruttati","Allemands, tchèques, britanniques : subtils, épicés, floraux, herbacés, terreux, fruités","German, Czech, British: subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy, fruity"],["Americani, neozelandesi, australiani: intensi, agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, tropicale, pino","Américains, néo-zélandais, australiens : intenses, agrumes, fruits à noyau, tropicaux, pin","American, NZ, Australian: intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine"]]},{"c":"b04","t":["Quando aggiungere il luppolo, e gli altri aromi","Quand ajouter le houblon, et les autres aromates","When to add hops, and other flavourings"],"p":[["Il luppolo si aggiunge al mosto in bollitura per estrarne amaro e aromi, e il momento cambia il risultato. Per l'amaro va messo all'inizio della bollitura, perché serve calore e tempo. Per l'aroma va messo verso la fine, perché gli aromi volano via se bolle troppo a lungo. Si può aggiungere luppolo anche più tardi, durante o dopo la fermentazione, a temperatura più bassa: è il dry hopping, che dà aroma. Il birraio può usare una sola varietà o un mix; alcune varietà servono per l'amaro, altre per l'aroma, altre per entrambi.","Le houblon s'ajoute au moût en ébullition pour en extraire amertume et arômes, et le moment change le résultat. Pour l'amertume, on l'ajoute au début de l'ébullition, car il faut de la chaleur et du temps. Pour l'arôme, on l'ajoute vers la fin, car les arômes s'envolent si l'ébullition dure trop. On peut aussi en ajouter plus tard, pendant ou après la fermentation, à plus basse température : c'est le houblonnage à froid (dry hopping), qui donne de l'arôme. Le brasseur peut utiliser une seule variété ou un assemblage ; certaines servent à l'amertume, d'autres à l'arôme, d'autres aux deux.","Hops go into the boiling wort to extract bitterness and aroma, and timing decides what they give. For bitterness they go in near the start of the boil, as bitterness needs heat and time. For aroma they go in near the end, because aromas escape if boiled too long. Hops can also be added later, during or after fermentation, at a lower temperature: this dry hopping adds aroma. Brewers may use one variety or a blend; some varieties are for bitterness, some for aroma, others for both."],["Il luppolo è l'aroma più usato, ma non l'unico. Prima della sua diffusione si usavano erbe e spezie per dare aroma o amaro, e alcuni birrai lo fanno ancora. In certi stili tradizionali belgi si usano da tempo frutti come ciliegie e lamponi, scorza d'agrumi e semi di coriandolo. Nella maggior parte dei Paesi non ci sono limiti, purché l'ingrediente sia commestibile e pratico: tra i più insoliti ci sono zucca, miele, peperoncino e caffè.","Le houblon est l'aromate le plus utilisé, mais pas le seul. Avant sa diffusion, on employait des herbes et des épices pour l'arôme ou l'amertume, et certains brasseurs le font encore. Certains styles belges traditionnels utilisent depuis longtemps des fruits comme la cerise et la framboise, de l'écorce d'agrumes et des graines de coriandre. Dans la plupart des pays, il n'y a pas de limite tant que l'ingrédient est comestible et pratique : parmi les plus originaux, la citrouille, le miel, le piment et le café.","Hops are the most widely used flavouring, but not the only one. Before hops spread, herbs and spices gave aroma or bitterness, and some brewers still use them. Fruits such as cherries and raspberries, plus citrus peel and coriander seed, have long featured in certain traditional Belgian styles. In most countries there are no limits as long as the ingredient is edible and practical: more unusual choices include pumpkin, honey, chilli and coffee."]],"k":[["Inizio bollitura → amaro (serve calore e tempo)","Début d'ébullition → amertume (chaleur et temps)","Early in the boil → bitterness (needs heat and time)"],["Fine bollitura → aroma (gli aromi volano via)","Fin d'ébullition → arôme (les arômes s'envolent)","Late in the boil → aroma (aromas escape)"],["Dry hopping: durante o dopo la fermentazione, a freddo, per l'aroma","Dry hopping : pendant ou après la fermentation, à froid, pour l'arôme","Dry hopping: during or after fermentation, cooler, for aroma"],["Altri aromi: erbe, spezie; frutta, scorza d'agrumi, coriandolo negli stili belgi","Autres aromates : herbes, épices ; fruits, écorce d'agrumes, coriandre dans les styles belges","Other flavourings: herbs, spices; fruit, citrus peel, coriander in Belgian styles"]]},{"c":"b05","t":["Lievito ale e lievito lager","Levure ale et levure lager","Ale yeast and lager yeast"],"p":[["Il compito principale del lievito è creare l'alcol, ma può influire molto anche sull'aroma. Nella birra si usano due specie principali, chiamate lievito ale e lievito lager: si comportano in modo diverso e danno origine alla grande divisione degli stili tra ale e lager.","Le rôle principal de la levure est de créer l'alcool, mais elle peut aussi beaucoup influencer l'arôme. En brasserie, on utilise deux espèces principales, appelées levure ale et levure lager : elles se comportent différemment et sont à l'origine de la grande division des styles entre ales et lagers.","Yeast's main job is to create alcohol, but it can also have a big effect on aroma. Brewing uses two main species, known as ale yeast and lager yeast: they behave differently and are behind one of the main divisions of beer styles, ales versus lagers."],["Il lievito ale fermenta in fretta e a temperature relativamente calde, e può produrre un'ampia gamma di aromi fruttati e speziati; ne esistono molti ceppi, ognuno con la sua «firma», quindi si scelgono per creare stili precisi. Le birre fatte con lievito ale si chiamano ale. Il lievito lager di solito fermenta più lentamente e più al fresco, ha meno ceppi e dà meno aromi. Le birre fatte con lievito lager si chiamano lager.","La levure ale fermente vite et à des températures relativement chaudes, et peut produire une large gamme d'arômes fruités et épicés ; elle compte de nombreuses souches, chacune avec sa « signature », que l'on choisit pour créer des styles précis. Les bières faites avec de la levure ale s'appellent ales. La levure lager fermente en général plus lentement et plus au frais, compte moins de souches et apporte moins d'arômes. Les bières qu'elle produit s'appellent lagers.","Ale yeast ferments quickly at relatively warm temperatures and can produce a wide range of fruity and spicy aromas; there are many strains, each with its own signature, so strains are chosen to create particular styles. Beers made with ale yeast are ales. Lager yeast usually ferments more slowly and at a cooler temperature, has fewer strains and contributes less aroma. Beers made with lager yeast are lagers."]],"k":[["Due specie principali: ale e lager → divisione ale/lager","Deux espèces principales : ale et lager → division ales/lagers","Two main species: ale and lager → the ale/lager split"],["Ale: veloce, più calda, aromi fruttati e speziati, molti ceppi","Ale : rapide, plus chaude, arômes fruités et épicés, nombreuses souches","Ale: quick, warmer, fruity and spicy aromas, many strains"],["Lager: più lenta, più fresca, meno aromi, meno ceppi","Lager : plus lente, plus fraîche, moins d'arômes, moins de souches","Lager: slower, cooler, less aroma, fewer strains"]]},{"c":"b05","t":["Brett, batteri e fermentazione spontanea","Brett, bactéries et fermentation spontanée","Brett, bacteria and spontaneous fermentation"],"p":[["Oltre ai due lieviti principali si usano altri lieviti e perfino batteri. Il Brettanomyces (Brett) dà aromi complessi: fruttati come ananas maturo e pesca, e poi aia, cuoio, fieno e terra. I batteri lattici, gli stessi dello yogurt e del kimchi, danno acidità alla birra.","En plus des deux levures principales, on utilise d'autres levures et même des bactéries. Le Brettanomyces (Brett) donne des arômes complexes : fruités comme l'ananas mûr et la pêche, puis basse-cour, cuir, foin et terre. Les bactéries lactiques, celles du yaourt et du kimchi, apportent de l'acidité à la bière.","Besides the two main yeasts, other yeasts and even bacteria are used. Brettanomyces (Brett) adds complex aromas: fruity ones such as ripe pineapple and peach, and farmyard, leather, hay and earth. Lactic acid bacteria, the same kind used for yoghurt and kimchi, give beer acidity (sourness)."],["Il lievito è ovunque, nell'aria e sulle superfici, ma quasi tutte le birre usano lieviti coltivati, selezionati e moltiplicati in laboratorio: di solito un solo ceppo di ale o lager, a volte con Brett o batteri lattici coltivati. Alcune birre invece nascono da fermentazione spontanea: il birraio non aggiunge mai lieviti o batteri coltivati e si affida a quelli presenti nell'ambiente del birrificio, così nel mosto crescono molti tipi diversi.","La levure est partout, dans l'air et sur les surfaces, mais presque toutes les bières utilisent des levures cultivées, sélectionnées et multipliées en laboratoire : le plus souvent une seule souche d'ale ou de lager, parfois avec du Brett ou des bactéries lactiques cultivés. Certaines bières naissent en revanche d'une fermentation spontanée : le brasseur n'ajoute jamais de levures ni de bactéries cultivées et s'en remet à celles de l'environnement de la brasserie, si bien que de nombreux types se développent dans le moût.","Yeast is all around us, in the air and on surfaces, but nearly all beers use cultured yeast, selected and grown in a lab: usually a single strain of ale or lager yeast, sometimes alongside cultured Brett or lactic acid bacteria. Some beers, however, are made by spontaneous fermentation: the brewer never adds cultured yeast or bacteria and relies on the ambient ones living in and around the brewery, so many different types grow in the wort."]],"k":[["Brett: ananas maturo, pesca, aia, cuoio, fieno, terra","Brett : ananas mûr, pêche, basse-cour, cuir, foin, terre","Brett: ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth"],["Batteri lattici: acidità","Bactéries lactiques : acidité","Lactic acid bacteria: sourness"],["Quasi tutte le birre: lievito coltivato (di solito un ceppo)","Presque toutes les bières : levure cultivée (souvent une souche)","Nearly all beers: cultured yeast (usually one strain)"],["Fermentazione spontanea: niente coltivati, solo lieviti e batteri dell'ambiente","Fermentation spontanée : rien de cultivé, seulement levures et bactéries ambiantes","Spontaneous fermentation: nothing cultured, only ambient yeast and bacteria"]]},{"c":"b06","t":["Prepararsi e guardare la birra","Se préparer et regarder la bière","Getting ready and looking at the beer"],"p":[["Per degustare bene serve lo stesso metodo per ogni birra. Prima: niente odori o rumori che distraggano; buona luce e uno sfondo bianco; un bicchiere pulito con coppa ampia che si stringe in alto, per concentrare gli aromi; un palato pulito, senza aglio, dentifricio o caffè. La griglia di degustazione divide l'assaggio in tre parti: aspetto, naso, bocca.","Pour bien déguster, il faut la même méthode pour chaque bière. Avant tout : pas d'odeurs ni de bruits gênants ; une bonne lumière et un fond blanc ; un verre propre au calice large qui se resserre vers le haut, pour concentrer les arômes ; une bouche propre, sans ail, dentifrice ni café. La grille de dégustation découpe l'analyse en trois parties : aspect, nez, bouche.","Good tasting needs the same method for every beer. First: no distracting smells or noises; good lighting and a white background; a clean glass with a wide bowl narrowing at the top to concentrate aromas; a clean palate, free of garlic, toothpaste or coffee. The tasting grid splits tasting into three parts: appearance, nose and palate."],["Aspetto: per la limpidezza si guarda attraverso il bicchiere verso la luce (limpida, velata, opaca); per il colore si tiene il bicchiere davanti a uno sfondo bianco: paglierino, dorato, ambrato, ramato, marrone, nero. Si osserva anche la schiuma (la «testa»): quanto è alta e quanto dura.","Aspect : pour la limpidité, on regarde à travers le verre vers la lumière (limpide, voilée, opaque) ; pour la couleur, on tient le verre devant un fond blanc : paille, dorée, ambrée, cuivrée, brune, noire. On observe aussi la mousse (le « col ») : sa hauteur et sa tenue.","Appearance: for clarity, look through the glass towards the light (clear, hazy, opaque); for colour, hold the glass against a white background: straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black. Also note the foam (the head): how big it is and how long it lasts."]],"k":[["Niente odori e rumori; luce buona, sfondo bianco","Pas d'odeurs ni de bruits ; bonne lumière, fond blanc","No smells or noise; good light, white background"],["Bicchiere pulito, coppa ampia che si stringe; palato pulito","Verre propre, calice large qui se resserre ; bouche propre","Clean glass, wide bowl narrowing; clean palate"],["Limpidezza: limpida – velata – opaca","Limpidité : limpide – voilée – opaque","Clarity: clear – hazy – opaque"],["Colore: paglierino, dorato, ambrato, ramato, marrone, nero; schiuma","Couleur : paille, doré, ambré, cuivré, brun, noir ; mousse","Colour: straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black; foam"]]},{"c":"b06","t":["Naso, bocca e da dove vengono gli aromi","Nez, bouche et origine des arômes","Nose, palate and where aromas come from"],"p":[["Naso: si annusa prima tenendo il bicchiere per lo stelo sotto il naso, poi con il naso dentro il bicchiere; si fa roteare la birra per liberare altri aromi e si annusa di nuovo con colpi brevi o uno più lungo. Bocca: si prende un sorso, lo si muove in bocca e poi si deglutisce o si sputa. Spesso gli aromi in bocca sono gli stessi del naso; in più si valutano intensità, carbonazione, corpo, alcol, amaro, dolcezza e acidità.","Nez : on sent d'abord en tenant le verre par la tige sous le nez, puis le nez dans le verre ; on fait tourner la bière pour libérer d'autres arômes et on sent de nouveau, par petites inspirations ou une plus longue. Bouche : on prend une gorgée, on la fait circuler en bouche puis on avale ou on recrache. Les arômes en bouche sont souvent ceux du nez ; on évalue en plus l'intensité, la carbonatation, le corps, l'alcool, l'amertume, la douceur et l'acidité.","Nose: first sniff with the glass held by the stem below your nose, then with your nose in the glass; swirl to release more aromas and sniff again with short sniffs or a longer one. Palate: take a sip, move it round your mouth, then swallow or spit. Aromas on the palate are often the same as on the nose; also judge intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness and acidity."],["Gli aromi si raggruppano per origine. Dal malto e dai cereali: pane (pasta di pane, cracker, mollica, crosta, biscotto, pane tostato o bruciato), dolci (miele, caramello, zucchero filato, melassa), frutta secca (uvetta, prugna, dattero, fico) e frutta a guscio o tostati (nocciola tostata, cioccolato, caffè, cacao). Dal luppolo: fiori, frutti di bosco, mela e pera, agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, frutta tropicale, note erbacee (erba, fieno) ed erbe aromatiche (menta, tè), più pino, spezie, terra. Dal lievito: frutta (banana, mela, agrumi…), spezie (chiodi di garofano, pepe), aia e cuoio, e altro come gomma da masticare o smalto.","Les arômes se regroupent selon leur origine. Du malt et des céréales : pain (pâte à pain, cracker, mie, croûte, biscuit, pain grillé ou brûlé), confiserie (miel, caramel, barbe à papa, mélasse), fruits secs (raisin sec, pruneau, datte, figue) et fruits à coque ou torréfiés (noisette grillée, chocolat, café, cacao). Du houblon : fleurs, fruits rouges, pomme et poire, agrumes, fruits à noyau, fruits tropicaux, notes herbacées (herbe, foin) et aromatiques (menthe, thé), plus pin, épices, terre. De la levure : fruits (banane, pomme, agrumes…), épices (clou de girofle, poivre), basse-cour et cuir, et d'autres comme le chewing-gum ou le vernis à ongles.","Aromas are grouped by source. From malt and grain: bread (bread dough, water cracker, crumb, crust, digestive biscuit, toasted or burnt bread), confectionery (honey, caramel, candy floss, treacle), dried fruit (raisin, prune, date, fig) and nut or roasted notes (toasted nut, chocolate, coffee, cocoa). From hops: floral, berries, apple and pear, citrus, stone fruit, tropical fruit, herbaceous (grass, hay) and herbal (mint, tea), plus pine, spice and earth. From yeast: fruit (banana, apple, citrus and more), spice (clove, peppercorn), farmyard and leather, and others such as bubblegum or nail varnish."]],"k":[["Naso: sotto il naso, dentro il bicchiere, poi roteare e riannusare","Nez : sous le nez, dans le verre, puis faire tourner et sentir à nouveau","Nose: below the nose, in the glass, then swirl and sniff again"],["Bocca: intensità, carbonazione, corpo, alcol, amaro, dolcezza, acidità","Bouche : intensité, carbonatation, corps, alcool, amertume, douceur, acidité","Palate: intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness, acidity"],["Malto: pane, miele, caramello, frutta secca, caffè, cioccolato","Malt : pain, miel, caramel, fruits secs, café, chocolat","Malt: bread, honey, caramel, dried fruit, coffee, chocolate"],["Luppolo: fiori, agrumi, tropicale, pino, erbe · Lievito: banana, chiodi di garofano, pepe, aia","Houblon : fleurs, agrumes, tropical, pin, herbes · Levure : banane, girofle, poivre, basse-cour","Hops: floral, citrus, tropical, pine, herbal · Yeast: banana, clove, pepper, farmyard"]]},{"c":"b07","t":["Stili di malto: solo malti base","Styles de malt : malts de base seuls","Malt-driven styles: base malts only"],"p":[["Uno stile è un insieme di caratteristiche, ottenuto con certi ingredienti e certe tecniche, legato a un nome. La birra più bevuta al mondo è una lager chiara e facile, prodotta ovunque. Per questi stili si usano solo malti base (orzo maltato poco essiccato): ale o lager che siano, il colore è paglierino o dorato e gli aromi ricordano mollica, pasta di pane o cracker. Se nella ricetta entrano zucchero, sciroppi o cereali neutri come il riso, la birra ha aromi meno intensi e corpo più leggero di una birra 100% malto.","Un style est un ensemble de caractéristiques, obtenu avec certains ingrédients et certaines techniques, associé à un nom. La bière la plus bue au monde est une lager pâle et facile, brassée partout. Pour ces styles, on n'utilise que des malts de base (orge maltée peu touraillée) : ale ou lager, la couleur est paille ou dorée et les arômes évoquent la mie, la pâte à pain ou le cracker. Si la recette inclut du sucre, du sirop ou des céréales neutres comme le riz, la bière a des arômes moins intenses et un corps plus léger qu'une bière 100 % malt.","A beer style is a set of characteristics, achieved with a certain mix of ingredients and techniques, linked to a name. The world's most popular beer is an easy-drinking pale lager, made everywhere. For these styles brewers use only base malts (lightly kilned malted barley): whether ale or lager, the colour is straw or gold and the aromas recall bread crumb, bread dough or water cracker. If sugar, syrup or neutral grains such as rice go into the recipe, the beer has lighter aroma intensity and body than an all-malt beer."],["Lager chiara americana o internazionale: paglierina o dorata, aroma leggero (pasta di pane, cracker, a volte un filo di luppolo), amaro basso o medio, alcol medio, carbonazione alta. Munich helles («hell» in tedesco vuol dire chiaro, luminoso): lager di solito dorata, con mollica o cracker e note sottili speziate, erbacee o floreali dal luppolo; amaro da basso a medio, alcol medio. Blonde ale (a volte «golden ale»): ale facile, da paglierina a dorata, con mollica leggera, alcol da basso a medio, amaro medio, a volte un tocco fruttato dal lievito e un luppolo discreto.","Lager pâle américaine ou internationale : paille ou dorée, arôme léger (pâte à pain, cracker, parfois un soupçon de houblon), amertume faible ou moyenne, alcool moyen, carbonatation élevée. Munich helles (« hell » signifie clair, lumineux en allemand) : lager généralement dorée, avec mie ou cracker et de subtiles notes épicées, herbacées ou florales du houblon ; amertume faible à moyenne, alcool moyen. Blonde ale (parfois « golden ale ») : ale facile, paille à dorée, à la mie légère, alcool faible à moyen, amertume moyenne, parfois une touche fruitée de levure et un houblon discret.","American or international pale lager: straw or gold, light aroma intensity (bread dough, water cracker, sometimes a little hop), low or medium bitterness, medium alcohol, high carbonation. Munich helles ('hell' is German for bright or pale): a lager, usually gold, with bread crumb or water cracker plus subtle spicy, herbal or floral hop notes; low to medium bitterness, medium alcohol. Blonde ale (sometimes 'golden ale'): an easy ale, straw to gold, with subtle bread crumb, low to medium alcohol, medium bitterness, maybe a touch of fruit from the yeast and subtle hops."]],"k":[["Solo malti base: paglierino o dorato; mollica, pasta di pane, cracker","Malts de base seuls : paille ou doré ; mie, pâte à pain, cracker","Base malts only: straw or gold; crumb, dough, cracker"],["Riso, sciroppi, zucchero → aromi e corpo più leggeri","Riz, sirops, sucre → arômes et corps plus légers","Rice, syrups, sugar → lighter aroma and body"],["Lager chiara internazionale: aroma leggero, carbonazione alta","Lager pâle internationale : arôme léger, carbonatation élevée","International pale lager: light aroma, high carbonation"],["Munich helles (lager dorata) · blonde/golden ale (ale)","Munich helles (lager dorée) · blonde/golden ale (ale)","Munich helles (gold lager) · blonde/golden ale (ale)"]]},{"c":"b08","t":["Munich dunkel e brown ale","Munich dunkel et brown ale","Munich dunkel and brown ale"],"p":[["Aggiungendo piccole quantità di malti speciali ai malti base arrivano aromi di biscotto, crosta di pane, pane tostato, nocciola tostata, caramello, frutta secca, caffè, cioccolato, e colori ambra, rame, marrone o nero. Munich dunkel («dunkel» in tedesco vuol dire scuro) è una lager da ramata a marrone, con pane tostato, crosta di pane, nocciola tostata e talvolta caramello o cioccolato, a volte note sottili speziate, erbacee o floreali di luppolo; amaro da basso a medio, alcol medio.","En ajoutant de petites quantités de malts spéciaux aux malts de base, on obtient des arômes de biscuit, croûte de pain, pain grillé, noisette grillée, caramel, fruits secs, café, chocolat, et des couleurs ambre, cuivre, brune ou noire. La Munich dunkel (« dunkel » signifie sombre en allemand) est une lager cuivrée à brune, avec pain grillé, croûte de pain, noisette grillée et parfois caramel ou chocolat, parfois de subtiles notes épicées, herbacées ou florales de houblon ; amertume faible à moyenne, alcool moyen.","Adding small amounts of speciality malts to base malts brings aromas of biscuit, bread crust, toast, toasted nuts, caramel, dried fruit, coffee and chocolate, and amber, copper, brown or black colours. Munich dunkel ('dunkel' is German for dark) is a copper to brown lager with toasted bread, bread crust, toasted nut and sometimes caramel or chocolate, plus at times subtle spicy, herbal or floral hop notes; low to medium bitterness, medium alcohol."],["La brown ale è un'ale da ambrata a marrone, con nocciola tostata, pane tostato e talvolta cioccolato o caramello, a volte aromi fruttati dal lievito. Alcune versioni hanno luppolo sottile (fruttato, terroso, erbaceo), altre note più intense di agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, tropicale o pino. Amaro e alcol vanno da bassi ad alti: è uno stile molto ampio.","La brown ale est une ale ambrée à brune, avec noisette grillée, pain grillé et parfois chocolat ou caramel, parfois des arômes fruités de levure. Certaines versions ont un houblon subtil (fruité, terreux, herbacé), d'autres des notes plus intenses d'agrumes, de fruits à noyau, tropicaux ou de pin. Amertume et alcool vont de faibles à élevés : c'est un style très large.","Brown ale is an amber to brown ale with toasted nut, toasted bread and sometimes chocolate or caramel, sometimes with fruity yeast aromas. Some versions have subtle fruity, earthy or herbal hops, others more intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine notes. Bitterness and alcohol both range from low to high: it is a broad style."]],"k":[["Malti speciali in piccole dosi: biscotto, tostato, caramello, caffè, cioccolato; da ambra a nero","Malts spéciaux en petites doses : biscuit, grillé, caramel, café, chocolat ; ambre à noir","Small amounts of speciality malt: biscuit, toast, caramel, coffee, chocolate; amber to black"],["Munich dunkel: lager ramata-marrone, pane tostato, nocciola; amaro basso-medio","Munich dunkel : lager cuivrée-brune, pain grillé, noisette ; amertume faible-moyenne","Munich dunkel: copper-brown lager, toast, nut; low-medium bitterness"],["Brown ale: ale ambra-marrone, nocciola tostata; amaro e alcol da bassi ad alti","Brown ale : ale ambrée-brune, noisette grillée ; amertume et alcool de faibles à élevés","Brown ale: amber-brown ale, toasted nut; bitterness and alcohol low to high"]]},{"c":"b08","t":["Porter, stout e barley wine","Porter, stout et barley wine","Porter, stout and barley wine"],"p":[["Porter e stout sono due famiglie di ale molto vicine. Sono marroni o nere, con aromi di malto come caffè o cioccolato e talvolta caramello. Alcune hanno luppolo sottile, altre più intenso (agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, tropicale, pino); a volte si sentono note fruttate di lievito. Amaro da basso ad alto, alcol da basso a molto alto. Le versioni ad alcol molto alto, con aromi tostati pronunciati, hanno spesso la parola «imperial» nel nome.","Porters et stouts sont deux familles d'ales très proches. Brunes ou noires, elles ont des arômes de malt comme le café ou le chocolat et parfois le caramel. Certaines ont un houblon subtil, d'autres plus intense (agrumes, fruits à noyau, tropicaux, pin) ; on perçoit parfois des notes fruitées de levure. Amertume faible à élevée, alcool faible à très élevé. Les versions très alcoolisées, aux arômes torréfiés prononcés, portent souvent le mot « imperial » dans leur nom.","Porters and stouts are two closely related families of ales. They are brown or black, with malt aromas such as coffee or chocolate and sometimes caramel. Some have subtle hops, others more intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine notes; fruity yeast aromas sometimes show too. Bitterness is low to high and alcohol low to very high. Very high-alcohol versions with pronounced roasted aromas often have 'imperial' in their name."],["Il barley wine è un'ale spesso ambrata (ma può andare dal dorato al marrone), con aromi di malto intensi: pane tostato, caramello, biscotto, frutta secca. A volte ha note fruttate di lievito. Di solito ha corpo pieno, dolcezza evidente e alcol alto o molto alto. Il luppolo va da sottile (terroso, floreale, fruttato) a più marcato (pino, agrumi, frutta tropicale), con amaro da basso ad alto. Spesso si presta all'invecchiamento.","Le barley wine est une ale souvent ambrée (mais qui peut aller du doré au brun), aux arômes de malt intenses : pain grillé, caramel, biscuit, fruits secs. Il a parfois des notes fruitées de levure. En général, corps plein, douceur marquée et alcool élevé ou très élevé. Le houblon va de subtil (terreux, floral, fruité) à plus marqué (pin, agrumes, fruits tropicaux), avec une amertume faible à élevée. Il se prête souvent au vieillissement.","Barley wine is an ale, often amber (though it can range from gold to brown), with intense malt aromas: toasted bread, caramel, digestive biscuit, dried fruit. It sometimes has fruity yeast notes. It is typically full-bodied with notable sweetness and high or very high alcohol. Hops range from subtle earthy, floral, fruity notes to more prominent pine, citrus or tropical fruit, with low to high bitterness. Barley wines are often suitable for ageing."]],"k":[["Porter e stout: ale marroni o nere, caffè e cioccolato","Porter et stout : ales brunes ou noires, café et chocolat","Porter and stout: brown or black ales, coffee and chocolate"],["«Imperial»: versioni ad alcol molto alto, molto tostate","« Imperial » : versions très alcoolisées, très torréfiées","'Imperial': very high-alcohol, strongly roasted versions"],["Barley wine: spesso ambra, malto intenso, corpo pieno, dolce, alcol alto o molto alto","Barley wine : souvent ambré, malt intense, corps plein, doux, alcool élevé ou très élevé","Barley wine: often amber, intense malt, full body, sweet, high or very high alcohol"],["Barley wine: spesso adatto all'invecchiamento","Barley wine : souvent apte au vieillissement","Barley wine: often suitable for ageing"]]},{"c":"b09","t":["Due modi di essere luppolati; pils e bitter","Deux façons d'être houblonné ; pils et bitter","Two ways to be hoppy; pilsner and bitter"],"p":[["Il luppolo porta due cose: amaro e aromi. Alcuni stili hanno amaro medio o marcato con aroma di luppolo contenuto: si mette quasi tutto il luppolo all'inizio della bollitura e poco alla fine, e si usano luppoli tradizionali britannici, cechi o tedeschi (sottili, speziati, floreali, erbacei, terrosi o fruttati). Altri stili hanno amaro alto E aromi pronunciati: luppolo all'inizio (amaro), più tardi (sapore) e in dry hopping (aroma), con luppoli americani, neozelandesi o australiani (agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, tropicale, pino). Di recente alcune di queste birre puntano più sull'aroma che sull'amaro, e molti stili di malto oggi si fanno anche in versioni molto luppolate.","Le houblon apporte deux choses : amertume et arômes. Certains styles ont une amertume moyenne ou marquée avec un arôme de houblon retenu : on met l'essentiel du houblon au début de l'ébullition et peu à la fin, avec des houblons traditionnels britanniques, tchèques ou allemands (subtils, épicés, floraux, herbacés, terreux ou fruités). D'autres ont une amertume élevée ET des arômes prononcés : houblon au début (amertume), plus tard (saveur) et en dry hopping (arôme), avec des houblons américains, néo-zélandais ou australiens (agrumes, fruits à noyau, tropicaux, pin). Récemment, certaines de ces bières misent davantage sur l'arôme que sur l'amertume, et beaucoup de styles de malt existent aujourd'hui en versions très houblonnées.","Hops bring two things: bitterness and aroma. Some styles have medium or pronounced bitterness with restrained hop aroma: most hops go in early in the boil and few at the end, using traditional British, Czech or German hops (subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity). Others have high bitterness AND pronounced hop aroma: hops early (bitterness), later (flavour) and dry hopped (aroma), using American, New Zealand or Australian hops (citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine). Recently some of these beers focus more on hop aroma than on bitterness, and many malt-driven styles now also appear in much hoppier versions."],["Pils tradizionale ceca o tedesca: lager da paglierina a dorata, con pasta di pane, miele leggero o mollica e luppolo sottile speziato, floreale o erbaceo; amaro da medio ad alto, alcol medio. Bitter: ale luppolata nata in Inghilterra, da ambrata a ramata, con pane tostato, crosta di pane, biscotto o caramello, luppolo sottile fruttato, terroso o erbaceo e a volte note fruttate di lievito; amaro da medio ad alto, alcol da basso ad alto.","Pils tchèque ou allemande traditionnelle : lager paille à dorée, avec pâte à pain, miel léger ou mie et un houblon subtil épicé, floral ou herbacé ; amertume moyenne à élevée, alcool moyen. Bitter : ale houblonnée née en Angleterre, ambrée à cuivrée, avec pain grillé, croûte de pain, biscuit ou caramel, un houblon subtil fruité, terreux ou herbacé et parfois des notes fruitées de levure ; amertume moyenne à élevée, alcool faible à élevé.","Traditional Czech or German pilsner: a straw to gold lager with bread dough, light honey or bread crumb, and subtle spicy, floral or herbal hops; medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol. Bitter: a hop-driven ale from England, amber to copper, with toasted bread, bread crust, digestive biscuit or caramel, subtle fruity, earthy or herbal hops and sometimes fruity yeast notes; medium to high bitterness, alcohol low to high."]],"k":[["Amaro con aroma contenuto: luppolo soprattutto a inizio bollitura, luppoli tradizionali europei","Amertume avec arôme retenu : houblon surtout en début d'ébullition, houblons européens traditionnels","Bitterness with restrained aroma: hops mostly early, traditional European hops"],["Amaro alto e aroma intenso: luppolo presto, tardi e dry hopping, luppoli del Nuovo Mondo","Amertume élevée et arôme intense : houblon tôt, tard et dry hopping, houblons du Nouveau Monde","High bitterness and intense aroma: early, late and dry hops, New World hops"],["Pils ceca o tedesca: lager paglierina-dorata, amaro medio-alto","Pils tchèque ou allemande : lager paille-dorée, amertume moyenne-élevée","Czech or German pilsner: straw-gold lager, medium-high bitterness"],["Bitter: ale inglese ambra-rame, biscotto e caramello, amaro medio-alto","Bitter : ale anglaise ambre-cuivre, biscuit et caramel, amertume moyenne-élevée","Bitter: English amber-copper ale, biscuit and caramel, medium-high bitterness"]]},{"c":"b09","t":["American pale ale, American IPA, hazy IPA","American pale ale, American IPA, hazy IPA","American pale ale, American IPA, hazy IPA"],"p":[["American pale ale (APA): da dorata ad ambrata, con luppolo che va da agrumi, frutta a nocciolo e tropicale fino al pino, e malto discreto (mollica, a volte pane tostato o biscotto); a volte note fruttate di lievito. Amaro da medio ad alto, alcol medio. American IPA (India pale ale): si può pensare come una APA più forte, con ancora più amaro e aroma di luppolo; da dorata ad ambrata, definita da amaro alto e aromi di pino, resina, agrumi, frutta tropicale e a nocciolo, malto discreto e alcol da medio ad alto.","American pale ale (APA) : dorée à ambrée, avec un houblon allant des agrumes, fruits à noyau et tropicaux jusqu'au pin, et un malt discret (mie, parfois pain grillé ou biscuit) ; parfois des notes fruitées de levure. Amertume moyenne à élevée, alcool moyen. American IPA (India pale ale) : on peut la voir comme une APA plus forte, encore plus amère et houblonnée ; dorée à ambrée, définie par une amertume élevée et des arômes de pin, résine, agrumes, fruits tropicaux et à noyau, un malt discret et un alcool moyen à élevé.","American pale ale (APA): gold to amber, with hop aromas from citrus, stone and tropical fruit to pine, and subtle malt (bread crumb, sometimes toast or digestive biscuit); sometimes fruity yeast notes. Medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol. American IPA (India pale ale) can be seen as a stronger APA with even more bitterness and hop aroma: gold to amber, defined by high bitterness and pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit aromas, with subtle malt and medium to high alcohol."],["Hazy IPA (o New England IPA): da paglierina a dorata e nettamente torbida, con malto leggero (cracker, mollica), luppolo di frutta a nocciolo, tropicale e agrumi, a volte note fruttate di lievito. È di solito MENO amara di una American IPA (amaro da basso a medio), con alcol da medio ad alto: è l'esempio delle birre che puntano sull'aroma più che sull'amaro.","Hazy IPA (ou New England IPA) : paille à dorée et nettement trouble, avec un malt léger (cracker, mie), un houblon de fruits à noyau, tropicaux et d'agrumes, parfois des notes fruitées de levure. Elle est en général MOINS amère qu'une American IPA (amertume faible à moyenne), avec un alcool moyen à élevé : c'est l'exemple des bières qui misent sur l'arôme plutôt que sur l'amertume.","Hazy IPA (also New England IPA): straw to gold and distinctly hazy, with subtle malt (water cracker, bread crumb), stone fruit, tropical and citrus hop aromas and sometimes fruity yeast notes. It is typically LESS bitter than American IPA (low to medium bitterness), with medium to high alcohol: the example of beers focused on hop aroma rather than bitterness."]],"k":[["APA: dorata-ambrata, luppolo agrumi-tropicale-pino, amaro medio-alto, alcol medio","APA : dorée-ambrée, houblon agrumes-tropical-pin, amertume moyenne-élevée, alcool moyen","APA: gold-amber, citrus-tropical-pine hops, medium-high bitterness, medium alcohol"],["American IPA: APA più forte, amaro alto, pino e resina, alcol medio-alto","American IPA : APA plus forte, amertume élevée, pin et résine, alcool moyen-élevé","American IPA: stronger APA, high bitterness, pine and resin, medium-high alcohol"],["Hazy/New England IPA: torbida, paglierina-dorata, molto aromatica, MENO amara","Hazy/New England IPA : trouble, paille-dorée, très aromatique, MOINS amère","Hazy/New England IPA: hazy, straw-gold, very aromatic, LESS bitter"]]},{"c":"b10","t":["Weissbier e witbier","Weissbier et witbier","Weissbier and witbier"],"p":[["Negli stili di lievito sono gli aromi del lievito il tratto distintivo. Visto che le lager hanno pochi aromi di lievito, sono tutte ale: fruttati (tropicali, mela e pera, agrumi) e talvolta speziati (chiodi di garofano, pepe). La weissbier (detta anche hefeweizen) è di solito da paglierina a dorata e torbida: aromi di banana e chiodi di garofano dal lievito bilanciati da mollica di pane del frumento; amaro basso, alcol medio, carbonazione di solito alta. «Weiss» in tedesco vuol dire bianco, «Weizen» frumento: entrambe le parole indicano le birre di frumento tedesche.","Dans les styles de levure, ce sont les arômes de levure qui font la signature. Les lagers ayant peu d'arômes de levure, ce sont toutes des ales : fruités (tropicaux, pomme et poire, agrumes) et parfois épicés (girofle, poivre). La weissbier (aussi appelée hefeweizen) est en général paille à dorée et trouble : arômes de banane et de girofle de la levure équilibrés par la mie de pain du blé ; amertume faible, alcool moyen, carbonatation généralement élevée. « Weiss » signifie blanc en allemand, « Weizen » blé : les deux mots désignent les bières de blé allemandes.","In yeast-driven styles the yeast aromas are the signature. Since lagers have few yeast aromas, these are all ales: fruity (tropical, pome, citrus) and sometimes spicy (clove, peppercorn). Weissbier (also called hefeweizen) is typically straw to gold and cloudy/hazy: banana and clove from the yeast balance bread crumb from the wheat; low bitterness, medium alcohol, typically high carbonation. 'Weiss' is German for white and 'Weizen' for wheat: both words name German wheat beers."],["La witbier è torbida, da paglierina a dorata, con aromi sottili fruttati e speziati di lievito, spesso accompagnati da note di agrumi e fiori dovute ai semi di coriandolo e alla scorza d'arancia usati come aromi. Ha aromi sottili di mollica o miele leggero dal frumento e a volte un filo di luppolo speziato o erbaceo; amaro basso, alcol medio. In etichetta può comparire il termine francese «blanche», cioè «bianca».","La witbier est trouble, paille à dorée, avec de subtils arômes fruités et épicés de levure, souvent complétés par des notes d'agrumes et florales venant des graines de coriandre et de l'écorce d'orange utilisées comme aromates. Elle a de subtils arômes de mie ou de miel léger du blé et parfois un soupçon de houblon épicé ou herbacé ; amertume faible, alcool moyen. L'étiquette peut porter le mot français « blanche ».","Witbier is hazy and straw to gold, with subtle fruity and spicy yeast aromas, often complemented by citrus and floral notes from the coriander seed and orange peel used as flavourings. It has subtle bread crumb or light honey from the wheat and sometimes subtle spicy or herbal hops; low bitterness, medium alcohol. It may be labelled with the French term blanche, meaning 'white'."]],"k":[["Stili di lievito: tutte ale; aromi fruttati e speziati dal lievito","Styles de levure : toutes des ales ; arômes fruités et épicés de levure","Yeast-driven styles: all ales; fruity and spicy yeast aromas"],["Weissbier/hefeweizen: torbida, banana e chiodi di garofano, frumento, amaro basso, carbonazione alta","Weissbier/hefeweizen : trouble, banane et girofle, blé, amertume faible, carbonatation élevée","Weissbier/hefeweizen: hazy, banana and clove, wheat, low bitterness, high carbonation"],["Weiss = bianco, Weizen = frumento","Weiss = blanc, Weizen = blé","Weiss = white, Weizen = wheat"],["Witbier/blanche: torbida, coriandolo e scorza d'arancia, amaro basso","Witbier/blanche : trouble, coriandre et écorce d'orange, amertume faible","Witbier/blanche: hazy, coriander and orange peel, low bitterness"]]},{"c":"b10","t":["Dubbel, tripel e saison","Dubbel, tripel et saison","Dubbel, tripel and saison"],"p":[["La dubbel è ramata o marrone, con aromi fruttati di mela, prugna e prugna secca e note speziate di chiodi di garofano o pepe, dal lievito, bilanciati da pane tostato, caramello o frutta secca del malto o di zuccheri caramellati, e talvolta luppolo sottile. Alcol alto, amaro medio; di solito ha sedimento da rifermentazione in bottiglia ed è molto carbonata. La tripel è dorata, con aromi fruttati marcati (arancia, banana) e speziati (pepe, chiodi di garofano) del lievito, e malto sottile di miele leggero o mollica. Alcol alto o molto alto, persino più della dubbel; amaro medio; anch'essa con sedimento e molto carbonata.","La dubbel est cuivrée ou brune, avec des arômes fruités de pomme, prune et pruneau et des notes épicées de girofle ou de poivre, issus de la levure, équilibrés par le pain grillé, le caramel ou les fruits secs du malt ou de sucres caramélisés, et parfois un houblon subtil. Alcool élevé, amertume moyenne ; elle a en général un dépôt de refermentation en bouteille et elle est très pétillante. La tripel est dorée, avec des arômes fruités marqués (orange, banane) et épicés (poivre, girofle) de la levure, et un malt subtil de miel léger ou de mie. Alcool élevé ou très élevé, plus encore que la dubbel ; amertume moyenne ; elle aussi avec dépôt et très pétillante.","Dubbel is copper to brown, with fruity apple, plum and prune and spicy clove or peppercorn from the yeast, balanced by toast, caramel or dried fruit from malt or caramelised sugars, and sometimes subtle hops. High alcohol, medium bitterness; it generally has sediment from bottle-conditioning and is highly carbonated. Tripel is gold, with prominent fruity (orange, banana) and spicy (peppercorn, clove) yeast aromas and subtle light honey or bread crumb malt. High or very high alcohol, even higher than a dubbel; medium bitterness; also bottle-conditioned with sediment and highly carbonated."],["La saison è per lo più da dorata ad ambrata, con aromi fruttati e speziati di lievito (arancia, pesca, mela, una nota di pepe), malto di mollica, pane tostato o biscotto e luppolo speziato, floreale, fruttato o terroso. Può essere leggermente acida. Spesso ha sedimento da rifermentazione in bottiglia ed è molto carbonata; amaro di solito medio, alcol da basso ad alto.","La saison est le plus souvent dorée à ambrée, avec des arômes fruités et épicés de levure (orange, pêche, pomme, une note de poivre), un malt de mie, pain grillé ou biscuit et un houblon épicé, floral, fruité ou terreux. Elle peut être légèrement acide. Elle a souvent un dépôt de refermentation en bouteille et elle est très pétillante ; amertume généralement moyenne, alcool faible à élevé.","Saison is most commonly gold to amber, with fruity and spicy yeast aromas (orange, peach, apple, a peppercorn note), bread crumb, toast or digestive biscuit from malt, and spicy, floral, fruity or earthy hops. It can be slightly sour. It often has sediment from bottle-conditioning and is highly carbonated; bitterness is typically medium and alcohol low to high."]],"k":[["Dubbel: ramata-marrone, mela, prugna, chiodi di garofano; alcol alto; sedimento","Dubbel : cuivrée-brune, pomme, prune, girofle ; alcool élevé ; dépôt","Dubbel: copper-brown, apple, plum, clove; high alcohol; sediment"],["Tripel: dorata, arancia, banana, pepe; alcol alto o molto alto (più della dubbel)","Tripel : dorée, orange, banane, poivre ; alcool élevé ou très élevé (plus que la dubbel)","Tripel: gold, orange, banana, pepper; high or very high alcohol (above dubbel)"],["Saison: dorata-ambrata, arancia, pesca, pepe; può essere leggermente acida","Saison : dorée-ambrée, orange, pêche, poivre ; peut être légèrement acide","Saison: gold-amber, orange, peach, pepper; can be slightly sour"],["Tutte e tre molto carbonate, spesso rifermentate in bottiglia","Toutes trois très pétillantes, souvent refermentées en bouteille","All three highly carbonated, often bottle-conditioned"]]},{"c":"b11","t":["Da dove viene l'acidità; Berliner weisse","D'où vient l'acidité ; Berliner weisse","Where sourness comes from; Berliner weisse"],"p":[["Negli stili acidi il carattere acido arriva da batteri, come i batteri lattici, attivi durante fermentazione e maturazione: aggiungono acidità alla birra finita. A volte influisce anche il Brettanomyces, con aromi complessi di aia, fieno, ananas maturo e cuoio.","Dans les styles acides, le caractère acide vient de bactéries, comme les bactéries lactiques, actives pendant la fermentation et la maturation : elles ajoutent de l'acidité à la bière finie. Le Brettanomyces peut aussi intervenir, avec des arômes complexes de basse-cour, foin, ananas mûr et cuir.","In sour styles the sour character comes from bacteria, such as lactic acid bacteria, active during fermentation and maturation: they add acidity to the finished beer. Brettanomyces can also play a part, adding complex farmyard, hay, ripe pineapple and leather aromas."],["La Berliner weisse è paglierina e velata, con aromi sottili di pasta di pane dal frumento e dal malto e note fruttate leggere dalla fermentazione. È moderatamente acida, con corpo leggero, alcol basso e amaro basso o quasi nullo. A volte si serve con sciroppi: lampone o asperula (un'erba amarognola che ricorda il fieno dolce). Si fa di solito con lieviti e batteri coltivati.","La Berliner weisse est paille et voilée, avec de subtils arômes de pâte à pain venant du blé et du malt et de légères notes fruitées de la fermentation. Elle est modérément acide, avec un corps léger, un alcool faible et une amertume faible ou imperceptible. On la sert parfois avec des sirops : framboise ou aspérule (une herbe légèrement amère qui rappelle le foin doux). Elle est généralement faite avec des levures et des bactéries cultivées.","Berliner weisse is straw-coloured and hazy, with subtle bread dough from wheat and malt and light fruity notes from fermentation. It is moderately sour, with light body, low alcohol and low or no perceptible bitterness. It is sometimes served with syrups: raspberry or woodruff (a slightly bitter herb reminiscent of sweet hay). It is typically made with cultured yeast and bacteria."]],"k":[["Stili acidi: acidità da batteri (lattici) in fermentazione e maturazione","Styles acides : acidité due aux bactéries (lactiques) en fermentation et maturation","Sour styles: sourness from bacteria (lactic) during fermentation and maturation"],["A volte anche Brett: aia, fieno, ananas, cuoio","Parfois aussi le Brett : basse-cour, foin, ananas, cuir","Sometimes Brett too: farmyard, hay, pineapple, leather"],["Berliner weisse: paglierina, velata, moderatamente acida, leggera, alcol basso","Berliner weisse : paille, voilée, modérément acide, légère, alcool faible","Berliner weisse: straw, hazy, moderately sour, light, low alcohol"],["A volte servita con sciroppo di lampone o asperula; lieviti e batteri coltivati","Parfois servie avec sirop de framboise ou d'aspérule ; levures et bactéries cultivées","Sometimes served with raspberry or woodruff syrup; cultured yeast and bacteria"]]},{"c":"b11","t":["Geuze: la fermentazione spontanea","Geuze : la fermentation spontanée","Geuze: spontaneous fermentation"],"p":[["La geuze (o gueuze) è dorata, con aromi complessi di aia (terra e fieno) e fruttati come pompelmo, arancia, mela, albicocca o rabarbaro, più una sottile nota di mollica. È acida, con amaro basso o nullo e alcol da medio ad alto. Di solito ha sedimento da rifermentazione in bottiglia ed è molto carbonata.","La geuze (ou gueuze) est dorée, avec des arômes complexes de basse-cour (terre et foin) et fruités comme le pamplemousse, l'orange, la pomme, l'abricot ou la rhubarbe, plus une subtile note de mie. Elle est acide, avec une amertume faible ou nulle et un alcool moyen à élevé. Elle a en général un dépôt de refermentation en bouteille et elle est très pétillante.","Geuze (gueuze) is gold, with complex farmyard aromas (earth and hay) and fruity ones such as grapefruit, orange, apple, apricot or rhubarb, plus subtle bread crumb. It is sour, with low or no bitterness and medium to high alcohol. It generally has sediment from bottle-conditioning and is highly carbonated."],["La differenza chiave con la Berliner weisse è il metodo: la geuze nasce da fermentazione spontanea ed è influenzata da molti lieviti e batteri dell'ambiente, tra cui Brettanomyces e batteri lattici. La Berliner weisse, invece, usa lieviti e batteri coltivati.","La différence clé avec la Berliner weisse est la méthode : la geuze naît d'une fermentation spontanée et elle est influencée par de nombreuses levures et bactéries ambiantes, dont le Brettanomyces et les bactéries lactiques. La Berliner weisse, elle, utilise des levures et des bactéries cultivées.","The key difference from Berliner weisse is method: geuze is made by spontaneous fermentation and shaped by a range of ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brettanomyces and lactic acid bacteria. Berliner weisse, by contrast, uses cultured yeast and bacteria."]],"k":[["Geuze: dorata, acida, aia, pompelmo, mela, albicocca; amaro basso o nullo","Geuze : dorée, acide, basse-cour, pamplemousse, pomme, abricot ; amertume faible ou nulle","Geuze: gold, sour, farmyard, grapefruit, apple, apricot; low or no bitterness"],["Alcol medio-alto; sedimento, molto carbonata","Alcool moyen-élevé ; dépôt, très pétillante","Medium-high alcohol; sediment, highly carbonated"],["Fermentazione spontanea: lieviti e batteri dell'ambiente, incluso Brett","Fermentation spontanée : levures et bactéries ambiantes, dont le Brett","Spontaneous fermentation: ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brett"]]},{"c":"b12","t":["Conservare la birra","Conserver la bière","Storing beer"],"p":[["La birra comincia a cambiare appena fatta e si rovina facilmente con ossigeno, calore e luce. Bevila fresca: alcune birre migliorano con il tempo, ma la maggior parte dà il meglio da giovane; col tempo amaro e aromi di luppolo svaniscono e compaiono odori di carta o cartone bagnato. Conviene controllare le date «imbottigliato il» o «da consumarsi preferibilmente entro». Tienila al fresco, idealmente in frigorifero anche per poco tempo: a temperatura ambiente invecchia più in fretta, e il caldo la degrada rapidamente.","La bière commence à évoluer dès qu'elle est brassée et s'abîme facilement à cause de l'oxygène, de la chaleur et de la lumière. Buvez-la fraîche : certaines bières gagnent à vieillir, mais la plupart sont meilleures jeunes ; avec le temps, amertume et arômes de houblon s'estompent et des odeurs de papier ou de carton mouillé apparaissent. Vérifiez les dates « embouteillé le » ou « à consommer de préférence avant ». Gardez-la au frais, idéalement au réfrigérateur même pour peu de temps : à température ambiante, elle vieillit plus vite, et la chaleur la dégrade rapidement.","Beer starts changing as soon as it is brewed and is easily damaged by oxygen, heat and light. Drink it fresh: some beers benefit from ageing, but most are best young; over time hop aroma and bitterness fade and paper or wet cardboard notes appear. Check for a 'bottled on' or 'best before/use by' date. Keep it cool, ideally refrigerated even for short-term storage: at room temperature it goes stale faster, and warmth degrades it quickly."],["Proteggila dalla luce, naturale o artificiale, che può creare odori sgradevoli: è il «colpo di luce». Lattine e fusti sono opachi e proteggono la birra; le bottiglie marroni bloccano quasi tutta la luce dannosa; quelle verdi o trasparenti proteggono poco o nulla e andrebbero tenute in scatole chiuse. Tienila chiusa, per proteggerla dall'ossigeno e conservare aromi e bollicine: una bottiglia o lattina aperta va bevuta subito. La birra in fusto è confezionata con anidride carbonica, che la protegge dall'ossigeno e la mantiene fresca più a lungo.","Protégez-la de la lumière, naturelle ou artificielle, qui peut créer des odeurs désagréables : c'est le « goût de lumière ». Canettes et fûts sont opaques et protègent la bière ; les bouteilles brunes arrêtent presque toute la lumière nocive ; les vertes ou transparentes protègent peu ou pas du tout et doivent rester dans des cartons fermés. Gardez-la fermée, pour la protéger de l'oxygène et préserver arômes et bulles : une bouteille ou canette ouverte se boit tout de suite. La bière en fût est conditionnée avec du gaz carbonique, qui la protège de l'oxygène et la garde fraîche plus longtemps.","Protect it from daylight and artificial light, which can create unpleasant aromas known as light strike. Cans and kegs are opaque and protect the beer; brown bottles block almost all damaging light; green or clear bottles give little or no protection and should be stored in sealed boxes. Keep it sealed to protect it from oxygen and keep aromas and carbonation: once opened, bottles and cans should be drunk straight away. Keg beer is packed with carbon dioxide, which protects it from oxygen and keeps it fresh for longer."]],"k":[["Bere fresca: col tempo calano luppolo e amaro, arriva il cartone; guardare le date","Boire fraîche : avec le temps, houblon et amertume baissent, le carton arrive ; vérifier les dates","Drink fresh: hops and bitterness fade, cardboard appears; check dates"],["Al fresco, idealmente in frigo","Au frais, idéalement au réfrigérateur","Keep cool, ideally refrigerated"],["Lontano dalla luce: lattine e fusti opachi, bottiglie marroni ok, verdi e trasparenti in scatole chiuse","À l'abri de la lumière : canettes et fûts opaques, bouteilles brunes ok, vertes et transparentes en cartons fermés","Away from light: cans and kegs opaque, brown bottles fine, green or clear in sealed boxes"],["Chiusa: aperta si beve subito; il fusto con CO2 resta fresco più a lungo","Fermée : ouverte, elle se boit tout de suite ; le fût sous CO2 reste frais plus longtemps","Sealed: drink at once when opened; CO2-filled kegs stay fresh longer"]]},{"c":"b12","t":["Tre difetti da riconoscere","Trois défauts à reconnaître","Three faults to recognise"],"p":[["Una cattiva conservazione o manutenzione può dare odori e sapori sgradevoli. Ossidazione da invecchiamento (staling): capita a quasi tutte le birre col tempo ed è accelerata da calore e ossigeno; amaro e aromi di luppolo svaniscono e compaiono note di carta o cartone bagnato. Colpo di luce (skunking): la luce colpisce i composti del luppolo e crea un odore sgradevole di puzzola, capelli bruciati o urina di gatto.","Une mauvaise conservation ou un mauvais entretien peut donner des odeurs et des goûts désagréables. Le vieillissement oxydatif (staling) touche presque toutes les bières avec le temps et s'accélère avec la chaleur et l'oxygène ; amertume et arômes de houblon s'estompent et des notes de papier ou de carton mouillé apparaissent. Le goût de lumière (skunking) : la lumière agit sur les composés du houblon et crée une odeur désagréable de mouffette, de cheveux brûlés ou d'urine de chat.","Poor storage or maintenance can cause unpleasant aromas and flavours. Staling happens to most beers over time and is sped up by heat and oxygen: hop aromas and bitterness fade and paper or wet cardboard notes appear. Light strike (skunking) is caused when light hits hop compounds, giving an unpleasant skunky, scorched-hair or cat-urine smell."],["Infezione batterica: si deve spesso a batteri che crescono in linee di spillatura mal pulite (i tubi che collegano i fusti ai rubinetti) e dà una combinazione di note sgradevoli come aceto e burro rancido. La prevenzione è semplice: birra fresca, fredda, al buio, chiusa, e impianti puliti.","L'infection bactérienne vient souvent de bactéries qui se développent dans des lignes de tirage mal entretenues (les tuyaux qui relient les fûts aux robinets) et donne un mélange de notes désagréables comme le vinaigre et le beurre rance. La prévention est simple : bière fraîche, au froid, à l'abri de la lumière, fermée, et installations propres.","Bacterial infection is commonly caused by bacteria growing in poorly maintained beer lines (the hoses connecting kegs to taps) and gives a mix of unwelcome flavours such as vinegar and rancid butter. Prevention is simple: fresh, cold, dark, sealed beer and clean equipment."]],"k":[["Staling: carta, cartone bagnato; luppolo e amaro svaniti; calore e ossigeno","Staling : papier, carton mouillé ; houblon et amertume estompés ; chaleur et oxygène","Staling: paper, wet cardboard; hops and bitterness faded; heat and oxygen"],["Colpo di luce: puzzola, capelli bruciati, urina di gatto; luce sui composti del luppolo","Goût de lumière : mouffette, cheveux brûlés, urine de chat ; lumière sur le houblon","Light strike: skunky, scorched hair, cat urine; light on hop compounds"],["Infezione batterica: aceto, burro rancido; linee di spillatura sporche","Infection bactérienne : vinaigre, beurre rance ; lignes de tirage sales","Bacterial infection: vinegar, rancid butter; dirty beer lines"]]},{"c":"b13","t":["Bicchieri e spillatura","Verres et tirage","Glassware and pouring from the keg"],"p":[["Ci sono moltissimi bicchieri e contano gusto personale, tradizione e cultura. Per degustare aiutano alcune caratteristiche: una coppa arrotondata facilita la rotazione, pareti che si stringono in alto trattengono gli aromi, un bicchiere stretto aiuta la tenuta della schiuma. In ogni caso il bicchiere deve essere pulito: senza odori né residui di detersivo, sali della lavastoviglie o sporco di panni non puliti. Bollicine attaccate alle pareti dopo il servizio sono il segno di un bicchiere non perfettamente pulito.","Il existe une multitude de verres, et le goût personnel, la tradition et la culture comptent. Pour déguster, quelques caractéristiques aident : un calice arrondi facilite la rotation, des parois qui se resserrent retiennent les arômes, un verre étroit aide la tenue de la mousse. Dans tous les cas, le verre doit être propre : sans odeur ni résidu de détergent, de sel de lave-vaisselle ou de saleté de torchon. Des bulles accrochées aux parois après le service signalent un verre pas tout à fait propre.","There is a huge range of glassware, and personal preference, tradition and culture all matter. For tasting, a few features help: a rounded bowl helps swirling, inward-sloping walls capture aromas, and narrow glasses help head retention. Whatever the shape, the glass must be clean: odourless and free of detergent, dishwasher salts or dirt from unclean cloths. Bubbles clinging to the sides after pouring are a sign the glass is not completely clean."],["Spillare dal fusto: tieni il bicchiere sotto il rubinetto inclinato a 45°, senza che il rubinetto tocchi la birra o il bicchiere ed evitando di toccare la parte alta del bicchiere con la mano. Apri completamente il rubinetto e versa lungo la parete finché il bicchiere è pieno per circa il 70%. Poi raddrizza il bicchiere e continua a versare al centro per formare la schiuma; chiudi il rubinetto a volume raggiunto.","Tirer au fût : tenez le verre sous le robinet, incliné à 45°, sans que le robinet touche la bière ou le verre et en évitant de toucher le haut du verre avec la main. Ouvrez complètement le robinet et versez le long de la paroi jusqu'à ce que le verre soit rempli à environ 70 %. Redressez ensuite le verre et continuez à verser au centre pour former la mousse ; fermez le robinet une fois le volume atteint.","Pouring keg beer: hold the glass below the tap at 45°, with the tap never touching the beer or the glass, and avoid touching the upper part of the glass with your hand. Open the tap fully and pour down the side until the glass is about 70% full. Then bring the glass upright and keep pouring into the centre to form a foam; turn off the tap at the right volume."]],"k":[["Coppa arrotondata: rotazione; pareti strette in alto: aromi; bicchiere stretto: schiuma","Calice arrondi : rotation ; parois resserrées : arômes ; verre étroit : mousse","Rounded bowl: swirling; inward walls: aromas; narrow glass: head retention"],["Bicchiere pulito: bollicine attaccate = non pulito","Verre propre : bulles accrochées = pas propre","Clean glass: clinging bubbles = not clean"],["Fusto: 45°, rubinetto aperto del tutto, lungo la parete fino al 70%, poi dritto al centro","Fût : 45°, robinet grand ouvert, le long de la paroi jusqu'à 70 %, puis droit au centre","Keg: 45°, tap fully open, down the side to 70%, then upright into the centre"],["Il rubinetto non tocca birra né bicchiere","Le robinet ne touche ni la bière ni le verre","The tap never touches beer or glass"]]},{"c":"b13","t":["Bottiglie, sedimento e temperature","Bouteilles, dépôt et températures","Bottles, sediment and temperatures"],"p":[["Aprire una bottiglia con tappo a corona: tieni ferma la bottiglia con una mano e con l'altra togli il tappo con l'apribottiglie in un solo gesto. Versare: bicchiere inclinato a 45° (senza toccarne la parte alta), birra versata piano lungo la parete; quando il bicchiere è pieno al 50–70%, raddrizzalo e versa al centro per creare schiuma. Senza sedimento si versa tutto. Con sedimento (birre rifermentate in bottiglia) si versa con attenzione, tenendo la bottiglia inclinata finché il deposito arriva vicino al collo, poi ci si ferma: un po' di birra resta sempre nella bottiglia. Lascia la bottiglia sul tavolo: chi beve può decidere di aggiungere il sedimento. Weissbier e witbier, naturalmente torbide, fanno eccezione: si fa rotolare piano la bottiglia o la lattina prima di aprirla e si versa tutto.","Ouvrir une bouteille capsulée : tenez la bouteille d'une main et retirez la capsule de l'autre avec le décapsuleur, en un seul geste. Verser : verre incliné à 45° (sans toucher le haut), bière versée doucement le long de la paroi ; quand le verre est plein à 50–70 %, redressez-le et versez au centre pour créer la mousse. Sans dépôt, on verse tout. Avec dépôt (bières refermentées en bouteille), on verse avec soin, en gardant la bouteille inclinée jusqu'à ce que le dépôt arrive près du goulot, puis on s'arrête : il reste toujours un peu de bière dans la bouteille. Laissez la bouteille sur la table : le client peut choisir d'ajouter le dépôt. Weissbier et witbier, naturellement troubles, font exception : on fait rouler doucement la bouteille ou la canette avant de l'ouvrir et on verse tout.","Opening a crown-capped bottle: steady the bottle with one hand and remove the cap with the opener in one single motion with the other. Pouring: hold the glass at 45° (not touching its upper part) and pour gently down the side; when the glass is 50–70% full, bring it upright and pour into the centre to create foam. With no sediment, pour the whole bottle. With sediment (bottle-conditioned beers), pour carefully, keeping the bottle tilted until the sediment nears the neck, then stop: a little beer always stays in the bottle. Leave the bottle on the table so the drinker can choose to swirl in the sediment. Weissbier and witbier, naturally hazy, are the exception: gently roll the bottle or can before opening and pour everything."],["Per la temperatura conta molto il gusto personale, ma ci sono regole generali. Stili con aroma da leggero a medio e alcol da basso a medio (lager internazionale, pils, weissbier): ben freddi, 3–7 °C. Stili con aroma da medio a pronunciato e alcol medio-alto (porter, APA, American IPA): freschi, 7–12 °C. Stili complessi, molto aromatici e con alcol alto o molto alto (barley wine, dubbel): leggermente freschi, 12–15 °C.","Pour la température, le goût personnel compte beaucoup, mais il existe des règles générales. Styles à l'arôme léger à moyen et à l'alcool faible à moyen (lager internationale, pils, weissbier) : bien frais, 3–7 °C. Styles à l'arôme moyen à prononcé et à l'alcool moyen à élevé (porter, APA, American IPA) : frais, 7–12 °C. Styles complexes, très aromatiques, à l'alcool élevé ou très élevé (barley wine, dubbel) : légèrement rafraîchis, 12–15 °C.","Personal preference matters a lot for temperature, but there are general rules. Light to medium aroma, low to medium alcohol (international lager, pilsner, weissbier): well chilled, 3–7 °C (37–45 °F). Medium to pronounced aroma, medium to high alcohol (porter, APA, American IPA): chilled, 7–12 °C (45–54 °F). Complex, pronounced aroma, high to very high alcohol (barley wine, dubbel): lightly chilled, 12–15 °C (54–59 °F)."]],"k":[["Tappo a corona: bottiglia ferma, un solo gesto","Capsule : bouteille tenue, un seul geste","Crown cap: steady bottle, one single motion"],["Bottiglia: 45°, lungo la parete, al 50–70% raddrizzare e versare al centro","Bouteille : 45°, le long de la paroi, à 50–70 % redresser et verser au centre","Bottle: 45°, down the side, at 50–70% upright and pour into the centre"],["Con sedimento: fermarsi quando arriva al collo; bottiglia lasciata sul tavolo; weissbier e witbier: far rotolare e versare tutto","Avec dépôt : s'arrêter quand il arrive au goulot ; bouteille laissée sur la table ; weissbier et witbier : rouler et tout verser","With sediment: stop when it reaches the neck; leave bottle on table; weissbier/witbier: roll and pour all"],["3–7 °C lager, pils, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel","3–7 °C lager, pils, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel","3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel"]]},{"c":"b14","t":["Preferenze e interazioni primarie","Préférences et interactions primaires","Preferences and primary interactions"],"p":[["Ognuno ha una sensibilità diversa ai gusti e agli aromi: un abbinamento perfetto per qualcuno può sembrare banale o sbagliato a un altro, quindi bisogna tenere conto di preferenze e sensibilità della persona. Il cibo cambia sempre il modo in cui percepiamo una bevanda; quanto, dipende dalla persona e da quanto sono forti gli elementi in gioco. Più che «regole», sono principi di percezione.","Chacun a une sensibilité différente aux saveurs et aux arômes : un accord parfait pour l'un peut sembler banal ou raté pour un autre, il faut donc tenir compte des préférences et des sensibilités de la personne. Le plat modifie toujours la perception d'une boisson ; dans quelle mesure, cela dépend de la personne et de l'intensité des éléments en jeu. Plus que des « règles », ce sont des principes de perception.","People differ in their sensitivity to tastes and aromas: a perfect pairing for one person may seem ordinary or even unsuccessful to another, so pairings should take the individual's preferences and sensitivities into account. Food always influences how a drink tastes; how much depends on the person and on the level of the interacting elements. These are principles of perception rather than 'rules'."],["Interazioni primarie sulla birra. Dolcezza nel cibo: birra meno dolce, più acida e più amara. Umami: uguale, birra meno dolce, più acida e più amara. Acidità nel cibo: birra più dolce, meno acida e meno amara. Sale: uguale, birra più dolce, meno acida e meno amara. Inoltre il piccante aumenta la percezione dell'alcol e l'amaro nel cibo aumenta l'amaro della birra.","Interactions primaires sur la bière. Sucré dans le plat : bière moins douce, plus acide et plus amère. Umami : pareil, bière moins douce, plus acide et plus amère. Acidité dans le plat : bière plus douce, moins acide et moins amère. Sel : pareil, bière plus douce, moins acide et moins amère. En outre, le piquant augmente la perception de l'alcool et l'amertume du plat augmente celle de la bière.","Primary interactions on beer. Sweetness in food: beer seems less sweet, more acidic and more bitter. Umami: the same, less sweet, more acidic and more bitter. Acidity in food: beer seems sweeter, less acidic and less bitter. Salt: the same, sweeter, less acidic and less bitter. Also, chilli heat increases the perception of alcohol, and bitterness in food increases bitterness in the beer."]],"k":[["Preferenze e sensibilità personali prima di tutto","Préférences et sensibilités personnelles avant tout","Personal preferences and sensitivities first"],["Dolce e umami nel cibo: birra meno dolce, più acida, più amara","Sucré et umami dans le plat : bière moins douce, plus acide, plus amère","Sweet and umami food: beer less sweet, more acidic, more bitter"],["Acidità e sale nel cibo: birra più dolce, meno acida, meno amara","Acidité et sel dans le plat : bière plus douce, moins acide, moins amère","Acid and salt food: beer sweeter, less acidic, less bitter"],["Piccante: più alcol percepito; amaro nel cibo: birra più amara","Piquant : plus d'alcool perçu ; amertume du plat : bière plus amère","Chilli: more perceived alcohol; bitter food: more bitter beer"]]},{"c":"b14","t":["Stili «sensibili», intensità e aromi","Styles « sensibles », intensité et arômes","Sensitive styles, intensity and aromas"],"p":[["Le birre sono in genere molto amiche del cibo, ma alcuni stili interagiscono di più. Stili molto amari come l'American IPA sembrano ancora più amari con cibi dolci, ricchi di umami o amari. Stili molto acidi come la geuze sembrano ancora più acidi con dolcezza o umami. Stili con alcol alto o molto alto, come barley wine e tripel, aumentano nettamente il bruciore del piccante.","Les bières sont en général très accommodantes à table, mais certains styles interagissent davantage. Les styles très amers comme l'American IPA paraissent encore plus amers avec des plats sucrés, riches en umami ou amers. Les styles très acides comme la geuze paraissent encore plus acides avec du sucré ou de l'umami. Les styles à l'alcool élevé ou très élevé, comme le barley wine et la tripel, augmentent nettement la brûlure du piquant.","Beers are generally very food-friendly, but some styles interact more. High-bitterness styles such as American IPA can seem even more bitter with sweetness, umami or bitterness in the food. High-acidity styles such as geuze can seem even more acidic with sweetness or umami. High or very high-alcohol styles such as barley wine and tripel can notably increase the burning sensation of chilli heat."],["Altre due considerazioni. Intensità: piatto e birra dovrebbero avere un'intensità di sapore simile, altrimenti uno copre l'altro. Aromi: le birre ricordano molti cibi (pane, miele, cioccolato e caffè dal malto; frutta, tè ed erbe dal luppolo; frutta e spezie dal lievito). Cercare aromi simili o complementari tra birra e piatto crea un legame familiare e può dare abbinamenti splendidi, come una stout al cioccolato con un dolce al cacao.","Deux autres considérations. Intensité : plat et bière doivent avoir une intensité de saveur proche, sinon l'un écrase l'autre. Arômes : les bières rappellent de nombreux aliments (pain, miel, chocolat et café du malt ; fruits, thé et herbes du houblon ; fruits et épices de la levure). Chercher des arômes semblables ou complémentaires entre la bière et le plat crée un lien familier et peut donner de superbes accords, comme une stout chocolatée avec un dessert au cacao.","Two other considerations. Intensity: dish and beer should have a similar flavour intensity, or one will overpower the other. Aromas: beers recall many foods (bread, honey, chocolate and coffee from malt; fruit, tea and herbs from hops; fruit and spice from yeast). Looking for similar or complementary aromas in beer and food creates a familiar connection and can lead to wonderful pairings, such as a chocolatey stout with a cocoa dessert."]],"k":[["Molto amare (American IPA): peggio con dolce, umami, amaro","Très amères (American IPA) : pire avec sucré, umami, amer","High bitterness (American IPA): worse with sweet, umami, bitter"],["Molto acide (geuze): peggio con dolce e umami","Très acides (geuze) : pire avec sucré et umami","High acidity (geuze): worse with sweet and umami"],["Molto alcoliche (barley wine, tripel): più bruciore col piccante","Très alcoolisées (barley wine, tripel) : plus de brûlure avec le piquant","High alcohol (barley wine, tripel): more chilli burn"],["Intensità simile; aromi simili o complementari","Intensité proche ; arômes semblables ou complémentaires","Similar intensity; similar or complementary aromas"]]}],"flash":[{"c":"b01","f":["Ingredienti della birra","Ingrédients de la bière","Beer ingredients"],"b":["Malto, acqua, luppolo, lievito.","Malt, eau, houblon, levure.","Malt, water, hops, yeast."]},{"c":"b01","f":["Fermentazione","Fermentation","Fermentation"],"b":["Zucchero + lievito → alcol + CO2 + aromi.","Sucre + levure → alcool + CO2 + arômes.","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + CO2 + aromas."]},{"c":"b01","f":["Scala dell'alcol nella birra","Échelle d'alcool de la bière","Beer alcohol scale"],"b":["Bassa ≤4% · media 4,1–5,9% · alta 6–9% · molto alta >9%.","Faible ≤4 % · moyen 4,1–5,9 % · élevé 6–9 % · très élevé >9 %.","Low ≤4% · medium 4.1–5.9% · high 6–9% · very high >9%."]},{"c":"b01","f":["Conversione dell'amido","Conversion de l'amidon","Starch conversion"],"b":["Gli enzimi del malto spezzano l'amido in zuccheri fermentabili.","Les enzymes du malt coupent l'amidon en sucres fermentescibles.","Malt enzymes break starch into fermentable sugars."]},{"c":"b02","f":["Maltazione","Maltage","Malting"],"b":["Macerazione → germinazione → essiccazione (kilning).","Trempe → germination → touraillage.","Steeping → germination → kilning."]},{"c":"b02","f":["Malti base","Malts de base","Base malts"],"b":["Essiccati a bassa temperatura, enzimi intatti; pane, cracker, miele; paglierino/dorato.","Touraillés bas, enzymes intactes ; pain, cracker, miel ; paille/doré.","Kilned low, enzymes intact; bread, cracker, honey; straw/gold."]},{"c":"b02","f":["Malti speciali","Malts spéciaux","Speciality malts"],"b":["Più calore o tostatura; biscotto, caramello, caffè, cioccolato; da ambra a nero.","Plus de chaleur ou torréfaction ; biscuit, caramel, café, chocolat ; ambre à noir.","Hotter kilning or roasting; biscuit, caramel, coffee, chocolate; amber to black."]},{"c":"b02","f":["Grain bill","Grain bill (recette des céréales)","Grain bill"],"b":["Ricetta dei cereali: soprattutto malto base + poco malto speciale.","Recette des céréales : surtout malt de base + un peu de malt spécial.","Recipe of malts and grains: mostly base malt + a little speciality malt."]},{"c":"b03","f":["Grist","Mouture (grist)","Grist"],"b":["Malto macinato.","Malt concassé.","Milled malt."]},{"c":"b03","f":["Mash · mosto · trebbie","Maische · moût · drêches","Mash · wort · spent grains"],"b":["Grist + acqua calda · liquido zuccherino separato · solidi rimasti.","Mouture + eau chaude · liquide sucré séparé · solides restants.","Grist + hot water · separated sugary liquid · leftover solids."]},{"c":"b03","f":["Bollitura del mosto","Ébullition du moût","Wort boiling"],"b":["Uccide i microrganismi; aggiunte principali di luppolo; poi raffreddamento rapido.","Tue les micro-organismes ; principaux ajouts de houblon ; puis refroidissement rapide.","Kills microorganisms; main hop additions; then rapid cooling."]},{"c":"b03","f":["Rifermentazione in bottiglia","Refermentation en bouteille","Bottle-conditioning"],"b":["Seconda fermentazione in bottiglia chiusa; lascia sedimento di lievito.","Seconde fermentation en bouteille fermée ; laisse un dépôt de levure.","Further fermentation in the sealed bottle; leaves yeast sediment."]},{"c":"b04","f":["Luppolo: forma più usata","Houblon : forme la plus utilisée","Hops: most common form"],"b":["Pellet di coni secchi macinati e pressati, tenuti al freddo.","Pellets de cônes secs broyés et pressés, gardés au froid.","Pellets of dried, milled, pressed cones, kept cold."]},{"c":"b04","f":["Luppoli tedeschi, cechi, britannici","Houblons allemands, tchèques, britanniques","German, Czech, British hops"],"b":["Sottili: speziati, floreali, erbacei, terrosi, fruttati.","Subtils : épicés, floraux, herbacés, terreux, fruités.","Subtle: spicy, floral, herbal, earthy, fruity."]},{"c":"b04","f":["Luppoli USA, Nuova Zelanda, Australia","Houblons USA, Nouvelle-Zélande, Australie","US, NZ, Australian hops"],"b":["Intensi: agrumi, frutta a nocciolo, tropicale, pino.","Intenses : agrumes, fruits à noyau, tropicaux, pin.","Intense: citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine."]},{"c":"b04","f":["Luppolo presto / tardi / dry hopping","Houblon tôt / tard / dry hopping","Early / late hops / dry hopping"],"b":["Inizio bollitura = amaro; fine = aroma; dopo, a freddo = aroma.","Début d'ébullition = amertume ; fin = arôme ; après, à froid = arôme.","Start of boil = bitterness; end = aroma; later, cool = aroma."]},{"c":"b05","f":["Lievito ale","Levure ale","Ale yeast"],"b":["Veloce, più calda, aromi fruttati e speziati, molti ceppi → ale.","Rapide, plus chaude, arômes fruités et épicés, nombreuses souches → ales.","Quick, warmer, fruity and spicy aromas, many strains → ales."]},{"c":"b05","f":["Lievito lager","Levure lager","Lager yeast"],"b":["Più lenta, più fresca, meno aromi, meno ceppi → lager.","Plus lente, plus fraîche, moins d'arômes, moins de souches → lagers.","Slower, cooler, less aroma, fewer strains → lagers."]},{"c":"b05","f":["Brettanomyces","Brettanomyces","Brettanomyces"],"b":["Lievito: ananas maturo, pesca, aia, cuoio, fieno, terra.","Levure : ananas mûr, pêche, basse-cour, cuir, foin, terre.","Yeast: ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth."]},{"c":"b05","f":["Fermentazione spontanea","Fermentation spontanée","Spontaneous fermentation"],"b":["Nessun lievito o batterio coltivato: solo quelli dell'ambiente.","Aucune levure ni bactérie cultivée : seulement celles de l'environnement.","No cultured yeast or bacteria: only ambient ones."]},{"c":"b06","f":["Aspetto della birra","Aspect de la bière","Beer appearance"],"b":["Limpida–velata–opaca; paglierino → nero; schiuma.","Limpide–voilée–opaque ; paille → noir ; mousse.","Clear–hazy–opaque; straw → black; foam."]},{"c":"b06","f":["Aromi dal lievito","Arômes de levure","Yeast aromas"],"b":["Frutta (banana…), spezie (chiodi di garofano, pepe), aia, gomma, smalto.","Fruits (banane…), épices (girofle, poivre), basse-cour, chewing-gum, vernis.","Fruit (banana…), spice (clove, pepper), farmyard, bubblegum, nail varnish."]},{"c":"b07","f":["Lager chiara americana/internazionale","Lager pâle américaine/internationale","American/international pale lager"],"b":["Paglierina-dorata, aroma leggero, amaro basso-medio, alcol medio, carbonazione alta.","Paille-dorée, arôme léger, amertume faible-moyenne, alcool moyen, carbonatation élevée.","Straw-gold, light aroma, low-medium bitterness, medium alcohol, high carbonation."]},{"c":"b07","f":["Munich helles","Munich helles","Munich helles"],"b":["Lager dorata, mollica, luppolo sottile; amaro basso-medio. «Hell» = chiaro.","Lager dorée, mie, houblon subtil ; amertume faible-moyenne. « Hell » = clair.","Gold lager, bread crumb, subtle hops; low-medium bitterness. 'Hell' = pale."]},{"c":"b07","f":["Blonde ale","Blonde ale","Blonde ale"],"b":["Ale facile paglierina-dorata, mollica sottile, amaro medio; detta anche golden ale.","Ale facile paille-dorée, mie subtile, amertume moyenne ; aussi golden ale.","Easy straw-gold ale, subtle crumb, medium bitterness; also golden ale."]},{"c":"b08","f":["Munich dunkel","Munich dunkel","Munich dunkel"],"b":["Lager ramata-marrone, pane tostato, nocciola; «dunkel» = scuro.","Lager cuivrée-brune, pain grillé, noisette ; « dunkel » = sombre.","Copper-brown lager, toast, nut; 'dunkel' = dark."]},{"c":"b08","f":["Porter / stout","Porter / stout","Porter / stout"],"b":["Ale marroni o nere, caffè e cioccolato; «imperial» = alcol molto alto.","Ales brunes ou noires, café et chocolat ; « imperial » = alcool très élevé.","Brown or black ales, coffee and chocolate; 'imperial' = very high alcohol."]},{"c":"b08","f":["Barley wine","Barley wine","Barley wine"],"b":["Ale spesso ambrata, malto intenso, corpo pieno, dolce, alcol alto/molto alto; invecchia.","Ale souvent ambrée, malt intense, corps plein, douce, alcool élevé/très élevé ; vieillit.","Often amber ale, intense malt, full, sweet, high/very high alcohol; ages well."]},{"c":"b09","f":["Pils ceca o tedesca","Pils tchèque ou allemande","Czech or German pilsner"],"b":["Lager paglierina-dorata, luppolo sottile speziato-floreale, amaro medio-alto.","Lager paille-dorée, houblon subtil épicé-floral, amertume moyenne-élevée.","Straw-gold lager, subtle spicy-floral hops, medium-high bitterness."]},{"c":"b09","f":["Bitter","Bitter","Bitter"],"b":["Ale inglese ambra-rame, biscotto/caramello, luppolo sottile, amaro medio-alto.","Ale anglaise ambre-cuivre, biscuit/caramel, houblon subtil, amertume moyenne-élevée.","English amber-copper ale, biscuit/caramel, subtle hops, medium-high bitterness."]},{"c":"b09","f":["APA · American IPA · hazy IPA","APA · American IPA · hazy IPA","APA · American IPA · hazy IPA"],"b":["Amaro medio-alto · amaro alto, più forte · torbida, meno amara.","Amertume moyenne-élevée · amertume élevée, plus forte · trouble, moins amère.","Medium-high bitterness · high bitterness, stronger · hazy, less bitter."]},{"c":"b10","f":["Weissbier / hefeweizen","Weissbier / hefeweizen","Weissbier / hefeweizen"],"b":["Torbida, banana e chiodi di garofano, frumento, amaro basso, molto frizzante.","Trouble, banane et girofle, blé, amertume faible, très pétillante.","Hazy, banana and clove, wheat, low bitterness, highly carbonated."]},{"c":"b10","f":["Witbier / blanche","Witbier / blanche","Witbier / blanche"],"b":["Torbida, coriandolo e scorza d'arancia, frumento, amaro basso.","Trouble, coriandre et écorce d'orange, blé, amertume faible.","Hazy, coriander and orange peel, wheat, low bitterness."]},{"c":"b10","f":["Dubbel vs tripel","Dubbel vs tripel","Dubbel vs tripel"],"b":["Dubbel ramata-marrone, alcol alto; tripel dorata, alcol ancora più alto.","Dubbel cuivrée-brune, alcool élevé ; tripel dorée, alcool encore plus élevé.","Dubbel copper-brown, high alcohol; tripel gold, even higher alcohol."]},{"c":"b10","f":["Saison","Saison","Saison"],"b":["Dorata-ambrata, arancia, pesca, pepe; può essere leggermente acida.","Dorée-ambrée, orange, pêche, poivre ; peut être légèrement acide.","Gold-amber, orange, peach, pepper; can be slightly sour."]},{"c":"b11","f":["Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse","Berliner weisse"],"b":["Paglierina, velata, moderatamente acida, alcol basso; lieviti e batteri coltivati.","Paille, voilée, modérément acide, alcool faible ; levures et bactéries cultivées.","Straw, hazy, moderately sour, low alcohol; cultured yeast and bacteria."]},{"c":"b11","f":["Geuze (gueuze)","Geuze (gueuze)","Geuze (gueuze)"],"b":["Dorata, acida, aia e frutta; fermentazione spontanea; molto frizzante.","Dorée, acide, basse-cour et fruits ; fermentation spontanée ; très pétillante.","Gold, sour, farmyard and fruit; spontaneous fermentation; highly carbonated."]},{"c":"b12","f":["Quattro regole di conservazione","Quatre règles de conservation","Four storage rules"],"b":["Bere fresca, tenere al fresco, al riparo dalla luce, chiusa.","Boire fraîche, garder au frais, à l'abri de la lumière, fermée.","Drink fresh, keep cool, protect from light, keep sealed."]},{"c":"b12","f":["Staling","Staling","Staling"],"b":["Luppolo e amaro svaniti, carta o cartone bagnato; calore e ossigeno.","Houblon et amertume estompés, papier ou carton mouillé ; chaleur et oxygène.","Faded hops and bitterness, paper or wet cardboard; heat and oxygen."]},{"c":"b12","f":["Colpo di luce (skunking)","Goût de lumière (skunking)","Light strike (skunking)"],"b":["Luce sui composti del luppolo: puzzola, capelli bruciati, urina di gatto.","Lumière sur le houblon : mouffette, cheveux brûlés, urine de chat.","Light on hop compounds: skunky, scorched hair, cat urine."]},{"c":"b12","f":["Infezione batterica","Infection bactérienne","Bacterial infection"],"b":["Linee di spillatura sporche: aceto, burro rancido.","Lignes de tirage sales : vinaigre, beurre rance.","Dirty beer lines: vinegar, rancid butter."]},{"c":"b12","f":["Bottiglie e luce","Bouteilles et lumière","Bottles and light"],"b":["Marrone: protegge quasi del tutto; verde o trasparente: poco o nulla.","Brune : protège presque totalement ; verte ou transparente : peu ou pas.","Brown: almost full protection; green or clear: little or none."]},{"c":"b13","f":["Spillare dal fusto","Tirer au fût","Pouring keg beer"],"b":["45°, rubinetto aperto, lungo la parete fino al 70%, poi dritto al centro.","45°, robinet ouvert, le long de la paroi jusqu'à 70 %, puis droit au centre.","45°, tap fully open, down the side to 70%, then upright into the centre."]},{"c":"b13","f":["Birra con sedimento","Bière avec dépôt","Beer with sediment"],"b":["Versare piano, fermarsi quando il deposito arriva al collo; bottiglia sul tavolo.","Verser doucement, s'arrêter quand le dépôt arrive au goulot ; bouteille sur la table.","Pour gently, stop when sediment reaches the neck; leave bottle on the table."]},{"c":"b13","f":["Temperature di servizio","Températures de service","Serving temperatures"],"b":["3–7 °C lager, pils, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel.","3–7 °C lager, pils, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel.","3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel."]},{"c":"b14","f":["Dolce e umami nel cibo","Sucré et umami dans le plat","Sweet and umami food"],"b":["Birra meno dolce, più acida, più amara.","Bière moins douce, plus acide, plus amère.","Beer less sweet, more acidic, more bitter."]},{"c":"b14","f":["Acidità e sale nel cibo","Acidité et sel dans le plat","Acid and salt food"],"b":["Birra più dolce, meno acida, meno amara.","Bière plus douce, moins acide, moins amère.","Beer sweeter, less acidic, less bitter."]},{"c":"b14","f":["Stili «sensibili» a tavola","Styles « sensibles » à table","Food-sensitive styles"],"b":["American IPA (amaro), geuze (acidità), barley wine e tripel (alcol col piccante).","American IPA (amertume), geuze (acidité), barley wine et tripel (alcool et piquant).","American IPA (bitterness), geuze (acidity), barley wine and tripel (alcohol with chilli)."]}],"ui":{"tab_study":["Birra 1","Bière 1","Beer 1"],"l2Title":["Esame Birra 1","Examen Bière 1","Beer 1 exam"],"l2Intro":["Lezioni, quiz e flashcard su ingredienti, birrificazione, stili e servizio della birra.","Leçons, quiz et flashcards sur les ingrédients, le brassage, les styles et le service de la bière.","Lessons, quizzes and flashcards on beer ingredients, brewing, styles and service."],"l2FlD":["Ripassa ingredienti, stili e termini della birra","Révisez ingrédients, styles et termes de la bière","Review beer ingredients, styles and terms"],"l2RevT":["Tutto Birra 1","Tout Bière 1","All of Beer 1"],"l2RevI":["Lezioni, flashcard ed errori: solo il programma di Birra 1.","Leçons, flashcards et erreurs : uniquement le programme Bière 1.","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Beer 1 syllabus."],"l2PlayT":["Giochi di Birra 1","Jeux Bière 1","Beer 1 games"],"l2PlayI":["Giochi brevi sulle domande e sui termini di Birra 1.","Des jeux courts sur les questions et les termes de Bière 1.","Short games on Beer 1 questions and terms."],"obHi":["Ciao! Sono la tua capra della birra 🍺","Bonjour ! Je suis votre chèvre de la bière 🍺","Hi! I'm your beer goat 🍺"],"obHiP":["Ti preparo un percorso su misura per passare l'esame Birra 1. Bastano 5 domande veloci.","Je vous prépare un parcours sur mesure pour réussir l'examen Bière 1. Il suffit de 5 questions rapides.","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Beer 1 exam. It takes 5 quick questions."]}};
window.TWG_ESX=Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX||{es:{},ar:{}},{});Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX.es,{"What beer is":"Qué es la cerveza","Beer is a hugely varied category, from clear golden pilsners to opaque black stouts. Yet they all share something: they are fermented alcoholic drinks, usually made from malt (malted grains), water and yeast, and flavoured with hops.":"La cerveza es una categoría muy variada: desde pilsners doradas y transparentes hasta stouts negras y opacas. Pero todas comparten algo: son bebidas alcohólicas fermentadas, hechas normalmente con malta (cereales malteados), agua y levadura, y aromatizadas con lúpulo.","To make alcohol you need a sugary liquid. Yeast is added; it eats the sugar and turns it into alcohol, producing carbon dioxide (CO2) and aromas at the same time: this is fermentation. Alcohol is measured as alcohol by volume: 5% abv means 5% of the liquid is alcohol. For beer, a handy scale is: low up to 4%, medium 4.1–5.9%, high 6–9%, very high above 9%.":"Para hacer alcohol hace falta un líquido azucarado. Se añade la levadura, que consume el azúcar y lo convierte en alcohol, produciendo a la vez dióxido de carbono (CO2) y aromas: es la fermentación. La graduación se mide en porcentaje de volumen: 5 % vol. significa que el 5 % del líquido es alcohol. Para la cerveza conviene una escala: baja hasta el 4 %, media 4,1–5,9 %, alta 6–9 %, muy alta por encima del 9 %.","Beer: fermented alcoholic drink from malt, water and yeast, flavoured with hops":"Cerveza: bebida alcohólica fermentada de malta, agua y levadura, aromatizada con lúpulo","Fermentation: sugar + yeast → alcohol + CO2 + aromas":"Fermentación: azúcar + levadura → alcohol + CO2 + aromas","Alcohol: low ≤4% · medium 4.1–5.9% · high 6–9% · very high >9%":"Alcohol: baja ≤4 % · media 4,1–5,9 % · alta 6–9 % · muy alta >9 %","Four ingredients and one conversion":"Cuatro ingredientes y una conversión","Malt supplies the sugar that yeast will turn into alcohol, gives most of the colour and can bring many aromas. Water is, by volume, the main ingredient: it is the liquid in which the yeast works, and breweries use a lot of it, so they need a plentiful, reliable supply. Hops (the cones of the plant) were first used mainly for their antibacterial, preserving effect; today they are prized for bitterness and aroma. Yeast creates the alcohol and carbonation and can add aromas.":"La malta aporta el azúcar que la levadura convertirá en alcohol, da la mayor parte del color y puede aportar muchos aromas. El agua es, en volumen, el ingrediente principal: es el medio líquido donde trabaja la levadura, y la cervecera usa mucha, así que necesita una fuente abundante y fiable. El lúpulo (los conos de la planta) se usó al principio sobre todo por su efecto antibacteriano y conservante; hoy se valora por el amargor y los aromas. La levadura crea el alcohol y el gas y puede aportar aromas.","Malt, however, reaches the brewery with no sugar: the grains are full of starch, sugars bonded into long chains that yeast cannot eat. Enzymes are needed: catalysts that speed up reactions and break starch into shorter sugars. This is starch conversion. Conveniently, malt supplies both the starch and the enzymes: when milled malt meets hot water, the enzymes turn the starch into sugar, which dissolves into a sugary liquid.":"Pero la malta llega a la cervecera sin azúcar: los granos están llenos de almidón, azúcares unidos en largas cadenas que la levadura no puede comer. Hacen falta enzimas, sustancias que aceleran las reacciones y rompen el almidón en azúcares más cortos: es la conversión del almidón. Por suerte, la propia malta aporta el almidón y las enzimas: cuando la malta molida se encuentra con agua caliente, las enzimas convierten el almidón en azúcar, que se disuelve formando un líquido azucarado.","Malt: sugar, colour, aromas":"Malta: azúcar, color, aromas","Water: the main ingredient by volume":"Agua: el ingrediente principal en volumen","Hops: once a preservative, now bitterness and aroma":"Lúpulo: antes conservante, hoy amargor y aromas","Malt brings starch and enzymes: with hot water starch becomes sugar":"La malta aporta almidón y enzimas: con agua caliente el almidón se vuelve azúcar","The life of a grain, and malting":"La vida de un grano y el malteado","For brewers the most important grain is barley, but wheat, maize (corn), oats, rye, rice and sorghum are used too. A grain is made of an embryo (the future plant), an energy store in the form of starch, and a protective casing, the husk. In spring, when it is warm and wet enough, the embryo starts to grow and, to feed itself, releases enzymes that turn the starch into sugars.":"Para los cerveceros el cereal más importante es la cebada, aunque también se usan trigo, maíz, avena, centeno, arroz y sorgo. Un grano tiene un embrión (la futura planta), una reserva de energía en forma de almidón y una envoltura protectora, la cascarilla. En primavera, con calor y humedad, el embrión empieza a crecer y, para alimentarse, libera enzimas que convierten el almidón en azúcares.","Malting mimics that spring. 1. Steeping: the grains are submerged in water. 2. Germination: once they have absorbed enough water, the embryo grows and enzymes form inside the grain. 3. Kilning: growth must be stopped, or the embryo would use up the starch; the grains are heated and dried with warm air in a kiln. The dry malt, holding starch and enzymes, keeps until the brewer needs it, and kilning also creates colour and aromas.":"El malteado imita esa primavera. 1. Remojo: los granos se sumergen en agua. 2. Germinación: cuando han absorbido suficiente agua, el embrión crece y dentro del grano se forman enzimas. 3. Secado en horno (kilning): hay que detener el crecimiento, porque si no el embrión gastaría el almidón; los granos se calientan y secan con aire caliente en un horno. La malta seca, con almidón y enzimas, se conserva hasta su uso, y el secado también crea color y aromas.","Barley first; also wheat, maize, oats, rye, rice, sorghum":"Cebada la principal; también trigo, maíz, avena, centeno, arroz, sorgo","Grain: embryo, starch (energy store), husk":"Grano: embrión, almidón (reserva), cascarilla","Malting: steeping → germination (enzymes) → kilning":"Malteado: remojo → germinación (enzimas) → secado en horno","Kilning stops growth and creates colour and aromas":"El secado detiene el crecimiento y crea color y aromas","Base malts and speciality malts":"Maltas base y maltas especiales","Varying the temperature and length of kilning gives different malts; some are roasted too. Base malts make up most of the malt a brewer uses: they are kilned at the lowest temperatures, so their enzymes survive to work later during mashing. They give aromas of water cracker, bread dough, bread crumb and light honey and, used alone, a straw or gold beer.":"Variando la temperatura y la duración del secado se obtienen maltas distintas; algunas además se tuestan. Las maltas base son la mayor parte de la malta usada: se secan a las temperaturas más bajas, así sus enzimas siguen intactas para trabajar luego en la maceración. Dan aromas de galleta salada, masa de pan, miga y miel suave y, solas, una cerveza pajiza o dorada.","Speciality malts are used for colour and aroma, usually in small amounts alongside base malts. They are made by kilning hotter or longer, or by roasting malt at even higher temperatures, which damages or destroys their enzymes. Possible aromas: digestive biscuit (graham cracker), bread crust, toast, toasted nuts, caramel, dried fruit, candy floss, coffee and chocolate. Colours: amber, copper, brown, even black.":"Las maltas especiales se usan para el color y los aromas, normalmente en pequeñas cantidades junto a las maltas base. Se obtienen secando más caliente o más tiempo, o tostando la malta a temperaturas aún más altas, lo que daña o destruye sus enzimas. Aromas posibles: galleta tipo digestive, corteza de pan, pan tostado, frutos secos tostados, caramelo, fruta pasa, algodón de azúcar, café y chocolate. Colores: ámbar, cobre, marrón, incluso negro.","Base malts: kilned lowest, enzymes intact, most of the recipe":"Maltas base: secadas a baja temperatura, enzimas intactas, la mayor parte de la receta","Base malts: water cracker, bread dough, crumb, light honey; straw or gold colour":"Maltas base: galleta salada, masa de pan, miga, miel; color pajizo o dorado","Speciality malts: more heat or roasting, enzymes damaged, small amounts":"Maltas especiales: más calor o tostado, enzimas dañadas, pequeñas dosis","Speciality: biscuit, toast, caramel, dried fruit, coffee, chocolate; amber to black":"Especiales: galleta, tostado, caramelo, fruta pasa, café, chocolate; de ámbar a negro","Other sugar sources and the grain bill":"Otras fuentes de azúcar y la receta de cereales","Other grains, sugars or syrups are sometimes used alongside malt: they provide fermentable sugar and can change texture and aroma. Rice and maize, like most sugars and syrups, tend to give lighter aroma intensity and lighter body. Wheat, on the other hand, can give a smooth, creamy texture and add to haziness.":"A veces se usan junto a la malta otros cereales, azúcares o jarabes: aportan azúcares fermentables y pueden cambiar textura y aromas. El arroz y el maíz, como la mayoría de azúcares y jarabes, tienden a dar menos intensidad aromática y un cuerpo más ligero. El trigo, en cambio, puede dar una textura suave y cremosa y contribuir a la turbidez.","The grain bill is the recipe listing the types and amounts of malts and grains in a beer. It can be a single malt, but most recipes use a mix: a base malt makes up the majority, bringing starch and plenty of enzymes for conversion, while small amounts of speciality malts set the colour, aromas and complexity.":"La receta de cereales («grain bill» en inglés) enumera los tipos y cantidades de maltas y cereales de una cerveza. Puede ser una sola malta, pero casi siempre es una mezcla: una malta base forma la mayor parte y aporta almidón y muchas enzimas para la conversión, mientras que pequeñas cantidades de maltas especiales ajustan color, aromas y complejidad.","Rice, maize, sugars, syrups: lighter aroma intensity and body":"Arroz, maíz, azúcares, jarabes: menos intensidad aromática y cuerpo más ligero","Wheat: smooth, creamy texture and haze":"Trigo: textura cremosa y turbidez","Grain bill: mostly base malt + a little speciality malt":"Receta de cereales: sobre todo malta base + poca malta especial","Milling and mashing":"Moler y macerar","Production follows six key stages: milling, mashing, wort boiling, fermentation, carbonation and packaging. It starts by milling (crushing) the malted grains: the milled grain is called grist and moves straight on to the next stage.":"La producción sigue seis pasos: molienda, maceración, cocción del mosto, fermentación, carbonatación y envasado. Se empieza moliendo (triturando) los granos de malta: la malta molida se llama «grist» y pasa enseguida al paso siguiente.","Mashing begins when the grist is mixed with hot water, making the mash. The malt enzymes turn the starch into sugars, which dissolve into a sugary liquid still mixed with solid bits, mainly husks. At the end the liquid is separated from the solids: the liquid is called wort and the leftover solids are spent grains.":"La maceración empieza cuando el grist se mezcla con agua caliente y forma el macerado (mash). Las enzimas de la malta convierten el almidón en azúcares, que se disuelven en un líquido azucarado aún mezclado con partes sólidas, sobre todo cascarillas. Al final se separa el líquido de los sólidos: el líquido se llama mosto (wort) y los sólidos restantes, bagazo.","Six stages: milling, mashing, boiling, fermentation, carbonation, packaging":"Seis pasos: molienda, maceración, cocción, fermentación, carbonatación, envasado","Milled malt = grist":"Malta molida = grist","Grist + hot water = mash; enzymes turn starch to sugar":"Grist + agua caliente = mash; enzimas: almidón → azúcar","Separated liquid = wort; solids = spent grains":"Líquido separado = mosto; sólidos = bagazo","Boiling, cooling, fermenting":"Hervir, enfriar, fermentar","The wort is then boiled. Boiling kills microorganisms, prevents spoilage and helps make the beer safe to drink; it is also when the main hop additions are made. After boiling, the wort is cooled rapidly to a temperature suitable for fermentation.":"El mosto se hierve. La cocción mata los microorganismos, evita que la cerveza se estropee y ayuda a que sea segura; también es el momento de las principales adiciones de lúpulo. Tras la cocción, el mosto se enfría rápidamente hasta una temperatura adecuada para fermentar.","The cooled wort goes into a fermentation vessel where yeast is added. During fermentation the yeast eats the sugars and creates alcohol, carbon dioxide and aromas. Remember the order: mill → mash → boil (with hops) → cool → ferment (with yeast).":"El mosto frío pasa a un fermentador donde se añade la levadura. Durante la fermentación la levadura consume los azúcares y crea alcohol, dióxido de carbono y aromas. Recuerda el orden: moler → macerar → hervir (con lúpulo) → enfriar → fermentar (con levadura).","Boiling: kills microorganisms, makes beer safe":"Cocción: mata microorganismos, hace la cerveza segura","Main hop additions happen during the boil":"Las principales adiciones de lúpulo se hacen en la cocción","Rapid cooling, then yeast in the fermenter":"Enfriado rápido, después levadura en el fermentador","Bubbles and packaging":"Burbujas y envases","When beer is carbonated, carbon dioxide dissolves in it under pressure: the bubbles rise in the glass, are felt in the mouth and build the foam. Yeast already makes some CO2 during fermentation; to top this up, carbon dioxide that was bought or recovered from earlier fermentations can be injected. Alternatively, a further fermentation can take place in the sealed bottle: this is bottle-conditioning, which leaves a yeast sediment at the bottom.":"Al carbonatar una cerveza, el dióxido de carbono se disuelve en ella a presión: las burbujas suben en el vaso, se notan en boca y forman la espuma. La levadura ya produce CO2 al fermentar; para completarlo se puede inyectar dióxido de carbono comprado o recuperado de fermentaciones anteriores. También se puede hacer una segunda fermentación en la botella cerrada: es el acondicionamiento en botella, que deja un sedimento de levadura en el fondo.","Finally, the beer must be packaged so it can be sold and distributed. The most widely used containers are cans, bottles and kegs.":"Por último, la cerveza se envasa para venderla y distribuirla. Los envases más usados son latas, botellas y barriles (kegs).","Carbonation: CO2 dissolved under pressure → bubbles and foam":"Carbonatación: CO2 disuelto a presión → burbujas y espuma","CO2 from fermentation, topped up by injected CO2 (bought or recovered)":"CO2 de la fermentación, más CO2 inyectado (comprado o recuperado)","Bottle-conditioning: yeast sediment":"Acondicionamiento en botella: sedimento de levadura","Packaging: cans, bottles, kegs":"Envases: latas, botellas, barriles","What are the four main ingredients of beer?":"¿Cuáles son los cuatro ingredientes principales de la cerveza?","Malt, water, hops, yeast":"Malta, agua, lúpulo, levadura","Rice, kōji, water, yeast":"Arroz, kōji, agua, levadura","Malt, sugar, hops, neutral alcohol":"Malta, azúcar, lúpulo, alcohol neutro","Barley, grapes, water, yeast":"Cebada, uva, agua, levadura","Malt, water, hops and yeast are the four main ingredients.":"Malta, agua, lúpulo y levadura son los cuatro ingredientes principales.","Rice and kōji are sake ingredients. Sugar is sometimes used but is not one of the four; grapes belong to wine.":"Arroz y kōji son ingredientes del sake. El azúcar se usa a veces, pero no es uno de los cuatro; la uva es del vino.","During fermentation, yeast turns sugar into alcohol and also produces…":"Durante la fermentación, la levadura convierte el azúcar en alcohol y además produce…","carbon dioxide and aromas":"dióxido de carbono y aromas","starch and enzymes":"almidón y enzimas","hops and colour":"lúpulo y color","oxygen and water":"oxígeno y agua","Yeast creates alcohol, carbon dioxide (CO2) and aromas.":"La levadura crea alcohol, dióxido de carbono (CO2) y aromas.","Starch and enzymes come from the malt. Colour mostly comes from malt, and hops are an added ingredient.":"Almidón y enzimas vienen de la malta. El color viene sobre todo de la malta, y el lúpulo es un ingrediente añadido.","A beer is 5% abv. Which alcohol band is it in?":"Una cerveza tiene un 5 % vol. ¿En qué franja de alcohol está?","Medium":"Media","Low":"Baja","High":"Alta","Very high":"Muy alta","Medium = 4.1–5.9% abv.":"Media = del 4,1 al 5,9 %.","Low is up to 4%, high 6–9%, very high above 9%.":"Baja hasta el 4 %, alta 6–9 %, muy alta más del 9 %.","Above what alcohol level is a beer 'very high' in alcohol?":"¿A partir de qué graduación una cerveza es «muy alta» en alcohol?","Above 9%":"Más del 9 %","Above 4%":"Más del 4 %","Above 6%":"Más del 6 %","Above 15%":"Más del 15 %","Very high = above 9% abv.":"Muy alta = más del 9 % vol.","6–9% is 'high' and 4.1–5.9% 'medium'.":"Del 6 al 9 % es «alta» y del 4,1 al 5,9 % «media».","By volume, what is the main ingredient in beer?":"En volumen, ¿cuál es el ingrediente principal de la cerveza?","Water":"El agua","Malt":"La malta","Hops":"El lúpulo","Yeast":"La levadura","Water is by far the largest ingredient, so breweries need a reliable supply.":"El agua es con diferencia el ingrediente más abundante; por eso hace falta una fuente fiable.","Malt gives sugar and colour, hops bitterness and aroma, yeast alcohol: but all are far smaller in quantity than water.":"La malta da azúcar y color, el lúpulo amargor y aromas, la levadura alcohol: pero todos en cantidad mucho menor que el agua.","Why were hops originally used in beer?":"¿Por qué se usó al principio el lúpulo en la cerveza?","For their antibacterial properties, to help preserve the beer":"Por sus propiedades antibacterianas, que conservaban la cerveza","To give a dark colour":"Para dar color oscuro","To provide sugar":"Para aportar azúcar","To create alcohol":"Para crear alcohol","Hops were first used to preserve; today they are prized mainly for bitterness and aroma.":"Al principio el lúpulo servía para conservar; hoy se valora sobre todo por amargor y aromas.","Colour and sugar come from malt, alcohol from yeast.":"El color y el azúcar vienen de la malta, el alcohol de la levadura.","Why can yeast not use the starch in malt directly?":"¿Por qué la levadura no puede usar directamente el almidón de la malta?","Because starch is sugars bonded into long chains":"Porque el almidón son azúcares unidos en largas cadenas","Because starch is too bitter":"Porque el almidón es demasiado amargo","Because starch is already alcohol":"Porque el almidón ya es alcohol","Because yeast only eats hops":"Porque la levadura solo come lúpulo","Yeast can only eat shorter sugars: the starch must first be broken up by enzymes.":"La levadura solo consume azúcares más cortos: primero las enzimas deben romper el almidón.","Starch is neither bitter nor alcoholic, and yeast feeds on sugars, not hops.":"El almidón no es amargo ni alcohólico, y la levadura se alimenta de azúcares, no de lúpulo.","In beer, where do the enzymes that convert starch to sugar come from?":"En la cerveza, ¿de dónde vienen las enzimas que convierten el almidón en azúcar?","The malt":"De la malta","The hops":"Del lúpulo","Kōji":"Del kōji","The water":"Del agua","Malt supplies both the starch and the enzymes to convert it.":"La malta aporta el almidón y las enzimas para convertirlo.","Kōji supplies the enzymes in sake, not beer. Hops and water do not bring conversion enzymes.":"El kōji aporta las enzimas en el sake, no en la cerveza. Ni el lúpulo ni el agua aportan las enzimas de conversión.","What are enzymes?":"¿Qué son las enzimas?","Substances that speed up reactions, such as starch conversion":"Sustancias que aceleran reacciones, como la conversión del almidón","Types of yeast":"Tipos de levadura","Hop varieties":"Variedades de lúpulo","Bacteria that make beer sour":"Bacterias que vuelven ácida la cerveza","Enzymes are catalysts: here they break starch into sugars.":"Las enzimas son catalizadores: aquí rompen el almidón en azúcares.","They are not microorganisms like yeast or bacteria, nor plants like hops.":"No son microorganismos como la levadura o las bacterias, ni plantas como el lúpulo.","Which grain is the most important for brewers?":"¿Qué cereal es el más importante para los cerveceros?","Barley":"Cebada","Rice":"Arroz","Maize (corn)":"Maíz","Sorghum":"Sorgo","Barley is the most used grain and the one most often malted.":"La cebada es el cereal más usado y el que más se maltea.","Rice, maize and sorghum are also used, but as extras.":"Arroz, maíz y sorgo también se usan, pero como complemento.","What are the three key steps of malting?":"¿Cuáles son los tres pasos clave del malteado?","Steeping, germination, kilning":"Remojo, germinación, secado en horno","Milling, mashing, boiling":"Molienda, maceración, cocción","Polishing, washing, steaming":"Pulido, lavado, cocción al vapor","Fermentation, carbonation, packaging":"Fermentación, carbonatación, envasado","The grain is soaked, sprouts, and is then dried in a kiln.":"El grano se remoja, germina y luego se seca en el horno.","Milling, mashing, boiling, fermentation and so on are brewing steps, after malting. Polishing applies to sake rice.":"Molienda, maceración, cocción, fermentación, etc. son pasos de la elaboración, después del malteado. El pulido es del arroz del sake.","What happens during germination?":"¿Qué ocurre durante la germinación?","The embryo grows and enzymes form inside the grain":"El embrión crece y se forman enzimas en el grano","The grain is roasted until black":"El grano se tuesta hasta quedar negro","The yeast makes alcohol":"La levadura produce alcohol","Hops are added":"Se añade el lúpulo","With water absorbed, the embryo wakes up and produces enzymes.":"Con el agua absorbida, el embrión se despierta y produce enzimas.","Roasting comes later, for some speciality malts. Yeast and hops come in at the brewery, not during malting.":"El tostado viene después, para algunas maltas especiales. Levadura y lúpulo entran en la cervecera, no en el malteado.","Why must germination be stopped by kilning?":"¿Por qué hay que detener la germinación con el secado?","Otherwise the embryo would use up the starch":"Si no, el embrión consumiría el almidón","To create alcohol in the grain":"Para crear alcohol en el grano","To remove the enzymes":"Para eliminar las enzimas","To grow the hops":"Para hacer crecer el lúpulo","If the grain kept growing, the starch the brewer needs would go into the plant.":"Si el grano siguiera creciendo, el almidón que necesita el cervecero se iría en la planta.","Kilning keeps the enzymes (especially in base malts) rather than removing them, and makes no alcohol.":"El secado conserva las enzimas (sobre todo en las maltas base), no las quita, y no crea alcohol.","Besides stopping germination, what does kilning produce?":"Además de detener la germinación, ¿qué produce el secado en horno?","Colour and aromas in the malt":"Color y aromas en la malta","Alcohol and carbon dioxide":"Alcohol y dióxido de carbono","Hop bitterness":"Amargor de lúpulo","Lactic sourness":"Acidez láctica","Kiln heat creates colour and aromas; more heat, more colour.":"El calor del horno crea color y aromas; más calor, más color.","Alcohol and CO2 come from yeast, bitterness from hops, lactic sourness from bacteria.":"Alcohol y CO2 vienen de la levadura, el amargor del lúpulo y la acidez láctica de las bacterias.","Why are base malts kilned at the lowest temperatures?":"¿Por qué las maltas base se secan a las temperaturas más bajas?","To avoid damaging the enzymes needed in mashing":"Para no dañar las enzimas que se necesitan en la maceración","To get a black colour":"Para obtener un color negro","To give coffee aromas":"Para dar aromas de café","To remove the starch":"Para eliminar el almidón","Low heat = intact enzymes, ready to convert starch in the mash.":"Calor bajo = enzimas intactas, listas para convertir el almidón en la maceración.","Black colour and coffee come from heavily roasted malts with destroyed enzymes. The starch must stay: it is the sugar source.":"El negro y el café vienen de maltas muy tostadas, con enzimas destruidas. El almidón debe quedarse: es la fuente de azúcar.","Which aromas do base malts typically give?":"¿Qué aromas dan normalmente las maltas base?","Water cracker, bread dough, bread crumb, light honey":"Galleta salada, masa de pan, miga, miel suave","Coffee and chocolate":"Café y chocolate","Banana and clove":"Plátano y clavo","Grapefruit and pine":"Pomelo y pino","Base malts give light bready, cereal aromas and a straw or gold colour.":"Las maltas base dan aromas ligeros de pan y cereal, con color pajizo o dorado.","Coffee and chocolate come from roasted speciality malts; banana and clove from yeast; grapefruit and pine from hops.":"Café y chocolate vienen de maltas especiales tostadas; plátano y clavo de la levadura; pomelo y pino del lúpulo.","A beer made with base malts only: what colour will it be?":"Una cerveza hecha solo con maltas base: ¿de qué color será?","Straw or gold":"Pajiza o dorada","Copper":"Cobre","Brown":"Marrón","Black":"Negra","On their own, base malts give a straw or gold beer.":"Solas, las maltas base dan una cerveza pajiza o dorada.","Amber, copper, brown and black need speciality malts.":"Ámbar, cobre, marrón y negro necesitan maltas especiales.","How are speciality malts made?":"¿Cómo se obtienen las maltas especiales?","By kilning hotter or longer, or by roasting the malt":"Secando más caliente o más tiempo, o tostando la malta","By skipping germination":"Saltándose la germinación","By adding hops during malting":"Añadiendo lúpulo durante el malteado","By boiling the grains":"Hirviendo los granos","More heat (or roasting) gives more colour and aroma but damages the enzymes.":"Más calor (o tostado) da más color y aromas, pero daña las enzimas.","Germination is part of all malting; hops go in during the boil, not malting.":"La germinación forma parte de todo malteado; el lúpulo se añade en la cocción, no en el malteado.","What happens to the enzymes in speciality malts?":"¿Qué les pasa a las enzimas en las maltas especiales?","They are damaged or destroyed by the heat":"Se dañan o se destruyen por el calor","They multiply":"Se multiplican","They turn into yeast":"Se convierten en levadura","They stay more active than in base malts":"Siguen más activas que en las maltas base","The high temperatures for speciality malts damage or destroy the enzymes.":"Las altas temperaturas de las maltas especiales dañan o destruyen las enzimas.","That is why a recipe needs base malt: it brings the enzymes to convert the starch of the whole mash.":"Por eso la receta necesita malta base: aporta las enzimas para convertir el almidón de todo el macerado.","Which of these aromas typically comes from a roasted speciality malt?":"¿Cuál de estos aromas viene normalmente de una malta especial tostada?","Coffee":"Café","Bread crumb":"Miga de pan","Grapefruit":"Pomelo","Clove":"Clavo","Coffee and chocolate are aromas of heavily roasted malts.":"Café y chocolate son aromas de maltas muy tostadas.","Bread crumb comes from base malt, grapefruit from hops, clove from yeast.":"La miga viene de las maltas base, el pomelo del lúpulo y el clavo de la levadura.","What effect do rice and maize tend to have in the recipe?":"¿Qué efecto suelen tener el arroz y el maíz en la receta?","Lighter aroma intensity and lighter body":"Menos intensidad aromática y cuerpo más ligero","More colour and roasted aromas":"Más color y aromas tostados","Creamy texture and haze":"Textura cremosa y turbidez","More bitterness":"Más amargor","Rice, maize and most sugars and syrups lighten aroma and body.":"Arroz, maíz y la mayoría de azúcares y jarabes aligeran aromas y cuerpo.","Creaminess and haze are typical of wheat; roasted colour of speciality malts; bitterness of hops.":"Cremosidad y turbidez son propias del trigo; color tostado de las maltas especiales; amargor del lúpulo.","Which grain can give a smooth, creamy texture and contribute to haze?":"¿Qué cereal puede dar una textura suave y cremosa y contribuir a la turbidez?","Wheat":"Trigo","Maize":"Maíz","Heavily roasted barley":"Cebada muy tostada","Wheat brings smoothness and haze, as in wheat beers.":"El trigo da suavidad y turbidez, como en las cervezas de trigo.","Rice and maize lighten; roasted barley gives dark colour and coffee aromas.":"Arroz y maíz aligeran; la cebada tostada da color oscuro y aromas de café.","What is the grain bill?":"¿Qué es la «receta de cereales» (grain bill)?","The list of types and amounts of malts and grains in a beer":"La lista de tipos y cantidades de maltas y cereales de una cerveza","The cost of the grain":"El coste de los cereales","The list of hops":"La lista de lúpulos","The amount of yeast":"La cantidad de levadura","It is the cereal recipe: which malts and grains, and in what proportion.":"Es la receta de cereales: qué maltas y cereales y en qué proporción.","It is not about cost, hops or yeast, only the grains.":"No trata de costes, lúpulo ni levadura, solo de los cereales.","In a typical recipe, which malt makes up the majority?":"En una receta típica, ¿qué malta forma la mayor parte?","A base malt":"Una malta base","A black roasted malt":"Una malta negra tostada","A caramel malt":"Una malta caramelo","No malt: only sugar":"Ninguna malta: solo azúcar","Base malt brings starch and enzymes; speciality malts are used in small amounts.":"La malta base aporta almidón y enzimas; las especiales se usan en pequeñas dosis.","Black and caramel malts are speciality malts, added in small amounts for colour and aroma.":"Las maltas negra y caramelo son especiales, añadidas en pequeñas cantidades para color y aroma.","What is milled malt called?":"¿Cómo se llama la malta molida?","Grist":"Grist","Wort":"Mosto","Spent grains":"Bagazo","The milled grains are called grist.":"Los granos molidos se llaman grist.","Wort is the sugary liquid and spent grains the leftover solids; kōji belongs to sake.":"El mosto es el líquido azucarado y el bagazo los sólidos restantes; el kōji es del sake.","Which order of production steps is correct?":"¿Qué orden de los pasos de producción es correcto?","Milling, mashing, wort boiling, fermentation, carbonation, packaging":"Molienda, maceración, cocción, fermentación, carbonatación, envasado","Mashing, milling, fermentation, boiling, packaging, carbonation":"Maceración, molienda, fermentación, cocción, envasado, carbonatación","Milling, fermentation, mashing, boiling, carbonation, packaging":"Molienda, fermentación, maceración, cocción, carbonatación, envasado","Boiling, milling, mashing, fermentation, packaging, carbonation":"Cocción, molienda, maceración, fermentación, envasado, carbonatación","Mill, mash, boil the wort, ferment, carbonate and package.":"Se muele, se macera, se hierve el mosto, se fermenta, se carbonata y se envasa.","Yeast cannot ferment before mashing because there is no sugar yet; boiling comes after mashing.":"La levadura no puede fermentar antes de macerar porque aún no hay azúcar; la cocción va después de la maceración.","What happens during mashing?":"¿Qué ocurre durante la maceración?","Malt enzymes turn starch into sugars in hot water":"Las enzimas de la malta convierten el almidón en azúcares en agua caliente","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol":"La levadura convierte el azúcar en alcohol","Most of the hops are added":"Se añade la mayor parte del lúpulo","The beer is carbonated":"La cerveza se carbonata","Grist + hot water: the enzymes convert the starch and the sugar dissolves.":"Grist + agua caliente: las enzimas convierten el almidón y el azúcar se disuelve.","Alcohol forms in fermentation; hops go in mainly during the boil; carbonation comes later.":"El alcohol se forma al fermentar; el lúpulo se añade sobre todo en la cocción; la carbonatación viene después.","At the end of mashing, what is the sugary liquid separated from the solids called?":"Al final de la maceración, ¿cómo se llama el líquido azucarado separado de los sólidos?","Mash":"Macerado (mash)","The separated sugary liquid is called wort.":"El líquido azucarado separado se llama mosto.","Mash is the grist-and-water mix before separation; spent grains are the solids left.":"El macerado es la mezcla de grist y agua antes de separar; el bagazo son los sólidos restantes.","What are spent grains?":"¿Qué es el bagazo (spent grains)?","The solids left after the wort is separated":"Los sólidos que quedan tras separar el mosto","Grains not yet malted":"Los granos aún sin maltear","The yeast sediment in the bottle":"El sedimento de levadura en la botella","Used hop cones":"Los conos de lúpulo usados","They are the solid leftovers of the mash, mainly husks.":"Son los restos sólidos del macerado, sobre todo cascarillas.","The bottle sediment is yeast from bottle-conditioning; unmalted grain and hops are different things.":"El sedimento en botella es levadura del acondicionamiento; los granos sin maltear y el lúpulo son otra cosa.","Why is the wort boiled?":"¿Por qué se hierve el mosto?","To kill microorganisms and add the hops":"Para matar microorganismos y añadir el lúpulo","To turn starch into sugar":"Para convertir el almidón en azúcar","To make the grains germinate":"Para hacer germinar los granos","To create the alcohol":"Para crear el alcohol","Boiling makes the beer safe and is when the main hop additions happen.":"La cocción hace la cerveza segura y es el momento de las principales adiciones de lúpulo.","Conversion happens in mashing, germination in malting, alcohol in fermentation.":"La conversión ocurre al macerar, la germinación al maltear y el alcohol al fermentar.","What happens right after the wort is boiled?":"¿Qué se hace justo después de hervir el mosto?","It is cooled rapidly":"Se enfría rápidamente","It is canned":"Se enlata","It is milled":"Se muele","It is kept hot for days":"Se deja caliente varios días","The wort is cooled quickly to a temperature suitable for the yeast.":"El mosto se enfría deprisa a una temperatura adecuada para la levadura.","Yeast would not survive in boiling wort; milling and packaging are other steps.":"La levadura no sobreviviría en mosto hirviendo; molienda y envasado son otros pasos.","At which stage is yeast added?":"¿En qué paso se añade la levadura?","At fermentation, to the cooled wort":"En la fermentación, al mosto enfriado","At milling":"En la molienda","At mashing":"En la maceración","During the boil":"Durante la cocción","The cooled wort goes into a fermentation vessel, where yeast is added.":"El mosto frío pasa al fermentador, donde se añade la levadura.","The boil would kill yeast; at milling and mashing there is no wort ready to ferment yet.":"En la cocción la levadura moriría; en la molienda y la maceración aún no hay mosto listo.","What does carbonation do?":"¿Qué hace la carbonatación?","Dissolves carbon dioxide in the beer under pressure":"Disuelve dióxido de carbono en la cerveza a presión","Adds alcohol":"Añade alcohol","Removes bitterness":"Quita el amargor","Colours the beer":"Colorea la cerveza","Dissolved CO2 gives bubbles in the mouth and foam in the glass.":"El CO2 disuelto da burbujas en boca y espuma en el vaso.","Carbonation changes neither alcohol, bitterness nor colour.":"La carbonatación no cambia el alcohol, el amargor ni el color.","Where can the CO2 injected to top up carbonation come from?":"¿De dónde puede venir el CO2 inyectado para completar la carbonatación?","Bought in or recovered from earlier fermentations":"Comprado o recuperado de fermentaciones anteriores","From boiled hops":"Del lúpulo hervido","From the brewery air":"Del aire de la cervecera","From the spent grains":"Del bagazo","Bought CO2 or CO2 recovered from earlier fermentations is used.":"Se usa CO2 comprado o recuperado de fermentaciones anteriores.","Hops, air and spent grains are not CO2 sources for carbonation.":"Ni el lúpulo, ni el aire, ni el bagazo son fuentes de CO2 para la carbonatación.","What is bottle-conditioning?":"¿Qué es el acondicionamiento en botella?","A further fermentation in the sealed bottle, leaving a yeast sediment":"Una segunda fermentación en la botella cerrada, que deja sedimento de levadura","Storing beer in a cellar":"Guardar la cerveza en una bodega","Adding hops in the bottle":"Añadir lúpulo en la botella","Pasteurising the bottle":"Pasteurizar la botella","Yeast ferments again in the bottle, creating bubbles and a deposit at the bottom.":"La levadura vuelve a fermentar en la botella: crea burbujas y un poso en el fondo.","It is not mere storage, nor a hop addition or heat treatment.":"No es simple conservación, ni una adición de lúpulo o un tratamiento térmico.","What are the most widely used beer containers?":"¿Cuáles son los envases más usados para la cerveza?","Cans, bottles, kegs":"Latas, botellas, barriles","Oak casks and amphorae":"Barricas de roble y ánforas","Cartons and pouches":"Briks y bolsas","Glass demijohns":"Damajuanas de vidrio","Cans, bottles and kegs are the main containers.":"Latas, botellas y barriles son los envases principales.","The other options exist in special cases but are not the usual beer packages.":"Las demás opciones existen en casos concretos, pero no son los envases habituales.","Beer ingredients":"Ingredientes de la cerveza","Malt, water, hops, yeast.":"Malta, agua, lúpulo, levadura.","Fermentation":"Fermentación","Sugar + yeast → alcohol + CO2 + aromas.":"Azúcar + levadura → alcohol + CO2 + aromas.","Beer alcohol scale":"Escala de alcohol de la cerveza","Low ≤4% · medium 4.1–5.9% · high 6–9% · very high >9%.":"Baja ≤4 % · media 4,1–5,9 % · alta 6–9 % · muy alta >9 %.","Starch conversion":"Conversión del almidón","Malt enzymes break starch into fermentable sugars.":"Las enzimas de la malta rompen el almidón en azúcares fermentables.","Malting":"Malteado","Steeping → germination → kilning.":"Remojo → germinación → secado en horno.","Base malts":"Maltas base","Kilned low, enzymes intact; bread, cracker, honey; straw/gold.":"Secadas a baja temperatura, enzimas intactas; pan, galleta, miel; pajizo/dorado.","Speciality malts":"Maltas especiales","Hotter kilning or roasting; biscuit, caramel, coffee, chocolate; amber to black.":"Más calor o tostado; galleta, caramelo, café, chocolate; de ámbar a negro.","Grain bill":"Grain bill (receta de cereales)","Recipe of malts and grains: mostly base malt + a little speciality malt.":"Receta de cereales: sobre todo malta base + poca malta especial.","Milled malt.":"Malta molida.","Mash · wort · spent grains":"Mash · mosto · bagazo","Grist + hot water · separated sugary liquid · leftover solids.":"Grist + agua caliente · líquido azucarado separado · sólidos restantes.","Wort boiling":"Cocción del mosto","Kills microorganisms; main hop additions; then rapid cooling.":"Mata microorganismos; principales adiciones de lúpulo; después enfriado rápido.","Bottle-conditioning":"Acondicionamiento en botella","Further fermentation in the sealed bottle; leaves yeast sediment.":"Segunda fermentación en botella cerrada; deja sedimento de levadura.","The hop plant and its varieties":"La planta del lúpulo y sus variedades","Hops are climbing plants. Each spring new shoots come up from the ground; the bines that grow from them produce hop cones over the year, the part brewers want. In autumn the bines are cut near the ground and the cones are harvested, then dried so they can be kept a long time without rotting. Dried cones can be used as they are, but that is relatively rare: far more often they are milled and pressed into space-saving pellets. Hops are packed and refrigerated to keep their bitterness and aroma.":"El lúpulo es una planta trepadora. Cada primavera brota del suelo con nuevos tallos, que a lo largo del año producen los conos, la parte que interesa a los cerveceros. En otoño se cortan los tallos cerca del suelo y se recogen los conos, que se secan para conservarlos mucho tiempo sin que se pudran. Se pueden usar así, pero es poco habitual: mucho más a menudo los conos secos se muelen y se prensan en pellets, que ocupan menos. El lúpulo se envasa y se refrigera para conservar amargor y aromas.","There are hundreds of hop varieties, each with slightly different aromas, aroma intensity and bitterness, and each with a climate it grows best in. So the well-known hop countries are linked with hop styles. Traditional German, Czech or British hops are known for subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity aromas. American, New Zealand or Australian hops tend to show intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical fruit or pine notes. New varieties appear every year, though, so every hop country can produce a wide range of aromas.":"Hay cientos de variedades, cada una con aromas, intensidad y amargor algo distintos y con su clima preferido. Por eso los grandes países productores se asocian a perfiles de lúpulo. Los lúpulos tradicionales alemanes, checos o británicos tienen aromas sutiles: especiados, florales, herbales, terrosos o frutales. Los lúpulos estadounidenses, neozelandeses o australianos tienden a notas intensas de cítricos, fruta de hueso, fruta tropical o pino. Aun así cada año salen variedades nuevas, y cada país puede producir aromas muy variados.","The cone is the part used; dried, usually turned into pellets":"El cono es la parte usada; se seca y normalmente se hace pellet","Packed and refrigerated to keep bitterness and aroma":"Envasado y refrigerado para conservar amargor y aromas","German, Czech, British: subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy, fruity":"Alemanes, checos, británicos: sutiles, especiados, florales, herbales, terrosos, frutales","American, NZ, Australian: intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine":"Estadounidenses, neozelandeses, australianos: intensos, cítricos, hueso, tropical, pino","When to add hops, and other flavourings":"Cuándo añadir el lúpulo, y otros aromatizantes","Hops go into the boiling wort to extract bitterness and aroma, and timing decides what they give. For bitterness they go in near the start of the boil, as bitterness needs heat and time. For aroma they go in near the end, because aromas escape if boiled too long. Hops can also be added later, during or after fermentation, at a lower temperature: this dry hopping adds aroma. Brewers may use one variety or a blend; some varieties are for bitterness, some for aroma, others for both.":"El lúpulo se añade al mosto en cocción para extraer amargor y aromas, y el momento cambia el resultado. Para el amargor se añade al principio de la cocción, porque hace falta calor y tiempo. Para el aroma, hacia el final, porque los aromas se escapan si hierve demasiado. También se puede añadir más tarde, durante o después de la fermentación, a menor temperatura: es el dry hopping, que aporta aroma. El cervecero puede usar una variedad o una mezcla; unas sirven para el amargor, otras para el aroma y otras para ambas cosas.","Hops are the most widely used flavouring, but not the only one. Before hops spread, herbs and spices gave aroma or bitterness, and some brewers still use them. Fruits such as cherries and raspberries, plus citrus peel and coriander seed, have long featured in certain traditional Belgian styles. In most countries there are no limits as long as the ingredient is edible and practical: more unusual choices include pumpkin, honey, chilli and coffee.":"El lúpulo es el aromatizante más usado, pero no el único. Antes de que se extendiera se usaban hierbas y especias para dar aroma o amargor, y algunos cerveceros lo siguen haciendo. En ciertos estilos belgas tradicionales se usan desde hace mucho frutas como cerezas y frambuesas, piel de cítricos y semillas de cilantro. En la mayoría de países no hay límites mientras el ingrediente sea comestible y práctico: entre los más curiosos, calabaza, miel, guindilla y café.","Early in the boil → bitterness (needs heat and time)":"Al principio de la cocción → amargor (calor y tiempo)","Late in the boil → aroma (aromas escape)":"Al final de la cocción → aroma (los aromas se escapan)","Dry hopping: during or after fermentation, cooler, for aroma":"Dry hopping: durante o después de fermentar, en frío, para el aroma","Other flavourings: herbs, spices; fruit, citrus peel, coriander in Belgian styles":"Otros aromatizantes: hierbas, especias; fruta, piel de cítricos, cilantro en estilos belgas","Ale yeast and lager yeast":"Levadura ale y levadura lager","Yeast's main job is to create alcohol, but it can also have a big effect on aroma. Brewing uses two main species, known as ale yeast and lager yeast: they behave differently and are behind one of the main divisions of beer styles, ales versus lagers.":"La función principal de la levadura es crear alcohol, pero también puede influir mucho en el aroma. En cervecería se usan dos especies principales, llamadas levadura ale y levadura lager: se comportan de forma distinta y dan lugar a la gran división de estilos entre ales y lagers.","Ale yeast ferments quickly at relatively warm temperatures and can produce a wide range of fruity and spicy aromas; there are many strains, each with its own signature, so strains are chosen to create particular styles. Beers made with ale yeast are ales. Lager yeast usually ferments more slowly and at a cooler temperature, has fewer strains and contributes less aroma. Beers made with lager yeast are lagers.":"La levadura ale fermenta rápido y a temperaturas relativamente cálidas, y puede producir una amplia gama de aromas frutales y especiados; tiene muchas cepas, cada una con su «firma», que se eligen para crear estilos concretos. Las cervezas hechas con levadura ale se llaman ales. La levadura lager suele fermentar más despacio y más fresca, tiene menos cepas y aporta menos aromas. Las cervezas hechas con ella se llaman lagers.","Two main species: ale and lager → the ale/lager split":"Dos especies principales: ale y lager → división ale/lager","Ale: quick, warmer, fruity and spicy aromas, many strains":"Ale: rápida, más cálida, aromas frutales y especiados, muchas cepas","Lager: slower, cooler, less aroma, fewer strains":"Lager: más lenta, más fresca, menos aromas, menos cepas","Brett, bacteria and spontaneous fermentation":"Brett, bacterias y fermentación espontánea","Besides the two main yeasts, other yeasts and even bacteria are used. Brettanomyces (Brett) adds complex aromas: fruity ones such as ripe pineapple and peach, and farmyard, leather, hay and earth. Lactic acid bacteria, the same kind used for yoghurt and kimchi, give beer acidity (sourness).":"Además de las dos levaduras principales se usan otras levaduras e incluso bacterias. El Brettanomyces (Brett) aporta aromas complejos: frutales como piña madura y melocotón, y también corral, cuero, heno y tierra. Las bacterias lácticas, las mismas del yogur y el kimchi, dan acidez a la cerveza.","Yeast is all around us, in the air and on surfaces, but nearly all beers use cultured yeast, selected and grown in a lab: usually a single strain of ale or lager yeast, sometimes alongside cultured Brett or lactic acid bacteria. Some beers, however, are made by spontaneous fermentation: the brewer never adds cultured yeast or bacteria and relies on the ambient ones living in and around the brewery, so many different types grow in the wort.":"La levadura está en todas partes, en el aire y en las superficies, pero casi todas las cervezas usan levaduras cultivadas, seleccionadas y criadas en laboratorio: normalmente una sola cepa de ale o lager, a veces junto con Brett o bacterias lácticas cultivadas. Algunas cervezas, en cambio, nacen de la fermentación espontánea: el cervecero no añade nunca levaduras ni bacterias cultivadas y confía en las del entorno de la cervecera, así que en el mosto crecen muchos tipos distintos.","Brett: ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth":"Brett: piña madura, melocotón, corral, cuero, heno, tierra","Lactic acid bacteria: sourness":"Bacterias lácticas: acidez","Nearly all beers: cultured yeast (usually one strain)":"Casi todas: levadura cultivada (normalmente una cepa)","Spontaneous fermentation: nothing cultured, only ambient yeast and bacteria":"Fermentación espontánea: nada cultivado, solo levaduras y bacterias del ambiente","Getting ready and looking at the beer":"Prepararse y mirar la cerveza","Good tasting needs the same method for every beer. First: no distracting smells or noises; good lighting and a white background; a clean glass with a wide bowl narrowing at the top to concentrate aromas; a clean palate, free of garlic, toothpaste or coffee. The tasting grid splits tasting into three parts: appearance, nose and palate.":"Para catar bien hace falta el mismo método con cada cerveza. Antes: ningún olor ni ruido que distraiga; buena luz y un fondo blanco; un vaso limpio de cáliz amplio que se estrecha arriba, para concentrar los aromas; la boca limpia, sin ajo, pasta de dientes ni café. La cuadrícula de cata divide la cata en tres partes: aspecto, nariz y boca.","Appearance: for clarity, look through the glass towards the light (clear, hazy, opaque); for colour, hold the glass against a white background: straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black. Also note the foam (the head): how big it is and how long it lasts.":"Aspecto: para la limpidez se mira a través del vaso hacia la luz (transparente, turbia, opaca); para el color se pone el vaso delante de un fondo blanco: pajizo, dorado, ámbar, cobrizo, marrón, negro. También se observa la espuma (la «corona»): su altura y cuánto dura.","No smells or noise; good light, white background":"Sin olores ni ruidos; buena luz, fondo blanco","Clean glass, wide bowl narrowing; clean palate":"Vaso limpio, cáliz amplio que se estrecha; boca limpia","Clarity: clear – hazy – opaque":"Limpidez: transparente – turbia – opaca","Colour: straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black; foam":"Color: pajizo, dorado, ámbar, cobrizo, marrón, negro; espuma","Nose, palate and where aromas come from":"Nariz, boca y de dónde vienen los aromas","Nose: first sniff with the glass held by the stem below your nose, then with your nose in the glass; swirl to release more aromas and sniff again with short sniffs or a longer one. Palate: take a sip, move it round your mouth, then swallow or spit. Aromas on the palate are often the same as on the nose; also judge intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness and acidity.":"Nariz: primero se huele con el vaso, sujeto por el pie, bajo la nariz; después con la nariz dentro del vaso; se hace girar la cerveza para liberar más aromas y se vuelve a oler con inspiraciones cortas o una más larga. Boca: se toma un sorbo, se mueve por la boca y se traga o se escupe. A menudo los aromas en boca son los mismos que en nariz; además se valoran intensidad, carbonatación, cuerpo, alcohol, amargor, dulzor y acidez.","Aromas are grouped by source. From malt and grain: bread (bread dough, water cracker, crumb, crust, digestive biscuit, toasted or burnt bread), confectionery (honey, caramel, candy floss, treacle), dried fruit (raisin, prune, date, fig) and nut or roasted notes (toasted nut, chocolate, coffee, cocoa). From hops: floral, berries, apple and pear, citrus, stone fruit, tropical fruit, herbaceous (grass, hay) and herbal (mint, tea), plus pine, spice and earth. From yeast: fruit (banana, apple, citrus and more), spice (clove, peppercorn), farmyard and leather, and others such as bubblegum or nail varnish.":"Los aromas se agrupan por su origen. De la malta y el cereal: pan (masa, galleta salada, miga, corteza, galleta digestive, pan tostado o quemado), dulces (miel, caramelo, algodón de azúcar, melaza), fruta pasa (uva pasa, ciruela, dátil, higo) y frutos secos o tostados (avellana tostada, chocolate, café, cacao). Del lúpulo: flores, frutos rojos, manzana y pera, cítricos, fruta de hueso, tropical, notas herbáceas (hierba, heno) y de hierbas (menta, té), además de pino, especias y tierra. De la levadura: fruta (plátano, manzana, cítricos…), especias (clavo, pimienta), corral y cuero, y otras como chicle o quitaesmalte.","Nose: below the nose, in the glass, then swirl and sniff again":"Nariz: bajo la nariz, dentro del vaso, luego girar y volver a oler","Palate: intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness, acidity":"Boca: intensidad, carbonatación, cuerpo, alcohol, amargor, dulzor, acidez","Malt: bread, honey, caramel, dried fruit, coffee, chocolate":"Malta: pan, miel, caramelo, fruta pasa, café, chocolate","Hops: floral, citrus, tropical, pine, herbal · Yeast: banana, clove, pepper, farmyard":"Lúpulo: flores, cítricos, tropical, pino, hierbas · Levadura: plátano, clavo, pimienta, corral","Which part of the hop plant do brewers use?":"¿Qué parte de la planta del lúpulo usan los cerveceros?","The cone":"El cono","The root":"La raíz","The leaves":"Las hojas","The seed":"La semilla","Hop cones contain the compounds that give bitterness and aroma.":"Los conos del lúpulo contienen los compuestos que dan amargor y aromas.","Roots, leaves and seeds are not the part used in brewing.":"Raíces, hojas y semillas no son la parte que se usa.","In what form do brewers most often use hops?":"¿En qué forma usan más a menudo el lúpulo los cerveceros?","Pellets of dried, milled and pressed cones":"Pellets de conos secos molidos y prensados","Fresh cones straight from the field":"Conos frescos recién cosechados","Hop syrup":"Jarabe de lúpulo","Dried leaves":"Hojas secas","Pellets are the most common form: they save space.":"Los pellets son la forma más común: ocupan menos espacio.","Whole dried cones are used, but rarely; fresh cones would soon rot.":"Los conos secos enteros se usan, pero poco; los frescos se pudrirían pronto.","Why are hops packed and refrigerated?":"¿Por qué el lúpulo se envasa y se refrigera?","To keep their bitterness and aroma":"Para conservar amargor y aromas","To make them germinate":"Para que germinen","To turn them into malt":"Para convertirlo en malta","To make yeast from them":"Para hacer levadura","Cold protects the bitter and aromatic compounds in hops.":"El frío protege los compuestos amargos y aromáticos del lúpulo.","Germination is for grains being malted, not hops, which become neither malt nor yeast.":"La germinación es de los cereales que se maltean, no del lúpulo, que no se convierte en malta ni en levadura.","Which aromas are typical of traditional German, Czech or British hops?":"¿Qué aromas son típicos de los lúpulos tradicionales alemanes, checos o británicos?","Subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity":"Sutiles: especiados, florales, herbales, terrosos o frutales","Intense tropical fruit and pine":"Intensos de fruta tropical y pino","Traditional European hops are restrained: spice, flowers, herbs, earth, a little fruit.":"Los lúpulos europeos tradicionales son discretos: especias, flores, hierbas, tierra, algo de fruta.","Intense tropical and pine notes belong to American, NZ and Australian hops. Coffee and chocolate come from malt, banana and clove from yeast.":"Lo tropical y el pino intensos son de los lúpulos estadounidenses, neozelandeses y australianos. Café y chocolate vienen de la malta; plátano y clavo, de la levadura.","A brewer wants intense citrus, tropical fruit and pine notes. Which hops are they likely to choose?":"Un cervecero busca notas intensas de cítricos, fruta tropical y pino. ¿Qué lúpulos elegirá probablemente?","American, New Zealand or Australian":"Estadounidenses, neozelandeses o australianos","Traditional German":"Alemanes tradicionales","Traditional Czech":"Checos tradicionales","Traditional British":"Británicos tradicionales","These hops tend to give intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine aromas.":"Estos lúpulos tienden a aromas intensos de cítricos, fruta de hueso, tropical o pino.","Traditional German, Czech and British hops are subtler: spice, flowers, herbs, earth.":"Los lúpulos tradicionales alemanes, checos y británicos son más sutiles: especias, flores, hierbas, tierra.","When are hops added mainly for BITTERNESS?":"¿Cuándo se añade el lúpulo sobre todo para dar AMARGOR?","Near the start of the boil":"Al principio de la cocción","Near the end of the boil":"Al final de la cocción","After fermentation":"Después de la fermentación","During malting":"Durante el malteado","Bitterness needs heat and time, so hops go in early.":"El amargor necesita calor y tiempo: el lúpulo se añade pronto.","Late in the boil and after fermentation hops give mainly aroma. No hops are used in malting.":"Al final de la cocción y tras fermentar, el lúpulo da sobre todo aroma. En el malteado no se usa lúpulo.","Why are aroma hops added near the end of the boil?":"¿Por qué el lúpulo aromático se añade hacia el final de la cocción?","Because aromas escape if boiled too long":"Porque los aromas se escapan si hierve demasiado","Because it gives more bitterness that way":"Porque así da más amargor","To sterilise it":"Para esterilizarlo","To colour the beer":"Para colorear la cerveza","Hop aromas are volatile: a short boil keeps them.":"Los aromas del lúpulo son volátiles: una cocción corta los conserva.","More bitterness comes from boiling longer, i.e. adding early. Hops do not colour beer.":"Más amargor se obtiene hirviendo más tiempo, es decir, añadiendo pronto. El lúpulo no colorea.","What is dry hopping?":"¿Qué es el dry hopping?","Adding hops during or after fermentation, for aroma":"Añadir lúpulo durante o después de la fermentación, para el aroma","Drying the hop cones":"Secar los conos de lúpulo","Boiling hops without water":"Hervir el lúpulo sin agua","Adding hops at the start of the boil":"Añadir lúpulo al principio de la cocción","Dry hopping happens at a lower temperature, after the boil, and adds aroma.":"El dry hopping se hace a menor temperatura, tras la cocción, y aporta aroma.","Drying cones is something else, and hops added at the start of the boil are for bitterness.":"Secar los conos es otra cosa, y el lúpulo añadido al principio de la cocción es para el amargor.","Which flavourings have long been used in certain traditional Belgian styles?":"¿Qué aromatizantes se usan desde hace mucho en ciertos estilos belgas tradicionales?","Fruit (cherries, raspberries), citrus peel, coriander seed":"Fruta (cerezas, frambuesas), piel de cítricos, semillas de cilantro","Only American hops":"Solo lúpulo estadounidense","Oak chips":"Virutas de roble","Fruit, citrus peel and coriander are part of Belgian tradition.":"Fruta, piel de cítricos y cilantro forman parte de la tradición belga.","Kōji belongs to sake; American hops are a modern trend, not Belgian tradition.":"El kōji es del sake; el lúpulo estadounidense es una moda moderna, no tradición belga.","In most countries, what limits apply to flavourings added to beer?":"En la mayoría de países, ¿qué límites hay para los aromatizantes añadidos a la cerveza?","None, as long as it is edible and practical":"Ninguno, mientras sea comestible y práctico","Only hops are allowed":"Solo se permite lúpulo","Only fruit is allowed":"Solo se permite fruta","Only European herbs":"Solo hierbas europeas","Pumpkin, honey, chilli or coffee: anything edible and practical can be used.":"Calabaza, miel, guindilla o café: se puede usar lo que sea comestible y práctico.","Hops are the most used, but not the only ones allowed.":"El lúpulo es el más usado, pero no el único permitido.","What is yeast's main job in beer?":"¿Cuál es la función principal de la levadura en la cerveza?","To give bitterness":"Dar amargor","To give colour":"Dar color","To convert starch":"Convertir el almidón","Yeast turns sugar into alcohol; it can also add aromas.":"La levadura convierte azúcar en alcohol; también puede aportar aromas.","Bitterness comes from hops, colour from malt, starch conversion from malt enzymes.":"El amargor viene del lúpulo, el color de la malta y la conversión del almidón de las enzimas de la malta.","Which description fits ale yeast?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a la levadura ale?","Ferments quickly, warmer, with many fruity and spicy aromas":"Fermenta rápido, más cálida, con muchos aromas frutales y especiados","Ferments slowly, cool, with little aroma":"Fermenta lento, en frío, con pocos aromas","Used only in spontaneous fermentation":"Solo se usa en la fermentación espontánea","Makes beer sour":"Vuelve ácida la cerveza","Ale yeast is quick, likes relative warmth and can give many aromas.":"La levadura ale es rápida, prefiere un calor relativo y puede dar muchos aromas.","Slow, cool and low-aroma describes lager yeast. Sourness comes from lactic bacteria.":"Lenta, fresca y poco aromática describe la lager. La acidez viene de las bacterias lácticas.","What are beers made with lager yeast called?":"¿Cómo se llaman las cervezas hechas con levadura lager?","Lagers":"Lagers","Ales":"Ales","Sours":"Sours","Stouts":"Stouts","Lager yeast → lagers; ale yeast → ales.":"Levadura lager → lagers; levadura ale → ales.","Stouts are ales; 'sour' refers to acidic styles from bacteria.":"Las stouts son ales; «sour» se refiere a estilos ácidos por bacterias.","Why do brewers choose a particular ale yeast strain?":"¿Por qué los cerveceros eligen una cepa concreta de levadura ale?","Each strain creates its own signature set of aromas":"Cada cepa crea su propia firma de aromas","All strains give the same result":"Todas las cepas dan el mismo resultado","To change the colour":"Para cambiar el color","To remove the hops":"Para eliminar el lúpulo","There are many different ale strains: the one with the right aromas for the style is chosen.":"Hay muchas cepas ale distintas: se elige la que da los aromas adecuados al estilo.","Yeast does not set colour or remove hops.":"La levadura no decide el color ni elimina el lúpulo.","What aromas can Brettanomyces give?":"¿Qué aromas puede dar el Brettanomyces?","Ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth":"Piña madura, melocotón, corral, cuero, heno, tierra","Only sourness":"Solo acidez","No aroma at all":"Ningún aroma","Brett gives complex fruity and 'rustic' aromas.":"El Brett da aromas complejos, frutales y «rústicos».","Coffee and chocolate come from roasted malt; sourness mainly from lactic bacteria.":"Café y chocolate vienen de malta tostada; la acidez, sobre todo, de las bacterias lácticas.","What do lactic acid bacteria bring to beer?":"¿Qué aportan las bacterias lácticas a la cerveza?","Acidity (sourness)":"Acidez","Bitterness":"Amargor","A dark colour":"Color oscuro","More alcohol":"Más alcohol","Lactic bacteria, as in yoghurt, make beer sour.":"Las bacterias lácticas, como en el yogur, vuelven ácida la cerveza.","Bitterness is from hops, colour from malt, alcohol from yeast.":"El amargor es del lúpulo, el color de la malta y el alcohol de la levadura.","What yeast is nearly all beer made with?":"¿Con qué levadura se hace casi toda la cerveza?","Cultured yeast, selected and grown in a lab":"Levaduras cultivadas, seleccionadas en laboratorio","Ambient yeast from the surroundings":"Levaduras del ambiente","Baker's yeast":"Levadura de pan","No yeast":"Ninguna levadura","Nearly all beers start from a cultured ale or lager strain.":"Casi todas las cervezas parten de una cepa cultivada de ale o lager.","Ambient yeast is used only in spontaneous fermentation, which is rare. No yeast, no alcohol.":"Las levaduras del ambiente solo se usan en la fermentación espontánea, que es rara. Sin levadura no hay alcohol.","What is spontaneous fermentation?":"¿Qué es la fermentación espontánea?","No cultured yeast or bacteria are added: ambient ones do the work":"No se añaden levaduras ni bacterias cultivadas: trabajan las del ambiente","A very fast fermentation":"Una fermentación muy rápida","A fermentation without sugar":"Una fermentación sin azúcar","A fermentation with one lab strain":"Una fermentación con una sola cepa de laboratorio","The brewer relies on yeast and bacteria living in and around the brewery.":"El cervecero confía en las levaduras y bacterias de la cervecera y sus alrededores.","One lab strain is the opposite: cultured yeast. The term is not about speed.":"Una sola cepa de laboratorio es lo contrario: levadura cultivada. El término no tiene que ver con la velocidad.","What usually happens in the wort with spontaneous fermentation?":"¿Qué suele ocurrir en el mosto con la fermentación espontánea?","Many different types of yeast and bacteria grow":"Crecen muchos tipos distintos de levaduras y bacterias","A single lager strain grows":"Crece una sola cepa lager","Nothing grows":"No crece nada","Only kōji mould grows":"Solo crece moho de kōji","Without cultured additions, a varied community of microorganisms develops.":"Sin añadidos cultivados se desarrolla una comunidad variada de microorganismos.","A single strain is typical of cultured yeast; kōji belongs to sake.":"Una sola cepa es propia de la levadura cultivada; el kōji es del sake.","Why is a white background used when tasting beer?":"¿Por qué se usa un fondo blanco al catar cerveza?","To assess the colour":"Para valorar el color","To smell aromas better":"Para oler mejor los aromas","To cool the beer":"Para enfriar la cerveza","To increase the foam":"Para aumentar la espuma","Holding the glass against white makes the colour easier to judge.":"Con el vaso delante del blanco se ve mejor el color.","The background has no effect on aroma, temperature or foam.":"El fondo no influye en aromas, temperatura ni espuma.","How is a beer's clarity assessed?":"¿Cómo se valora la limpidez de una cerveza?","By looking through the glass towards the light":"Mirando a través del vaso hacia la luz","By smelling the glass":"Oliendo el vaso","By tasting a sip":"Probando un sorbo","By measuring the temperature":"Midiendo la temperatura","For clarity, look through the liquid towards the light: clear, hazy or opaque.":"Para la limpidez se mira a través del líquido hacia la luz: transparente, turbia u opaca.","Nose and palate are other stages; temperature does not show clarity.":"La nariz y la boca son otras fases; la temperatura no indica la limpidez.","Which colour scale does the beer tasting grid use, from palest to darkest?":"¿Qué escala de colores usa la cuadrícula de cata de cerveza, del más claro al más oscuro?","Straw, gold, amber, copper, brown, black":"Pajizo, dorado, ámbar, cobrizo, marrón, negro","Gold, straw, copper, amber, black, brown":"Dorado, pajizo, cobrizo, ámbar, negro, marrón","Lemon, gold, amber, brown":"Limón, oro, ámbar, marrón","Pink, red, garnet, tawny":"Rosado, rojo, granate, teja","The scale runs from straw to black, via gold, amber, copper and brown.":"La escala va de pajizo a negro, pasando por dorado, ámbar, cobrizo y marrón.","The other scales are out of order or belong to wine tasting.":"Las demás escalas están desordenadas o son de la cata de vino.","Which of these aromas typically comes from YEAST?":"¿Cuál de estos aromas viene normalmente de la LEVADURA?","Bread crust":"Corteza de pan","Pine":"Pino","Spice notes such as clove and peppercorn come from yeast.":"Las especias como el clavo y la pimienta son aromas de levadura.","Bread crust and coffee come from malt, pine from hops.":"Corteza de pan y café vienen de la malta; el pino, del lúpulo.","Which aroma family comes from HOPS?":"¿Qué familia de aromas viene del LÚPULO?","Citrus, tropical fruit, floral, herbal, pine":"Cítricos, fruta tropical, flores, hierbas, pino","Bread, biscuit, caramel":"Pan, galleta, caramelo","Banana, bubblegum, nail varnish":"Plátano, chicle, quitaesmalte","Raisin, prune, date":"Uva pasa, ciruela pasa, dátil","Hops give floral, fruity (citrus, tropical…), herbal and pine notes.":"El lúpulo da notas florales, frutales (cítricos, tropical…), herbales y de pino.","Bread, caramel and dried fruit come from malt; banana, bubblegum and nail varnish from yeast.":"Pan, caramelo y fruta pasa vienen de la malta; plátano, chicle y quitaesmalte de la levadura.","Besides aromas, what is assessed on the palate?":"Además de los aromas, ¿qué se valora en boca?","Intensity, carbonation, body, alcohol, bitterness, sweetness, acidity":"Intensidad, carbonatación, cuerpo, alcohol, amargor, dulzor, acidez","Only colour":"Solo el color","Height of the foam":"La altura de la espuma","Clarity":"La limpidez","On the palate you judge structure and sensations as well as aromas.":"En boca se juzgan estructura y sensaciones, además de aromas.","Colour, foam and clarity belong to appearance.":"Color, espuma y limpidez pertenecen al aspecto.","Hops: most common form":"Lúpulo: forma más usada","Pellets of dried, milled, pressed cones, kept cold.":"Pellets de conos secos molidos y prensados, en frío.","German, Czech, British hops":"Lúpulos alemanes, checos, británicos","Subtle: spicy, floral, herbal, earthy, fruity.":"Sutiles: especiados, florales, herbales, terrosos, frutales.","US, NZ, Australian hops":"Lúpulos de EE. UU., NZ, Australia","Intense: citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine.":"Intensos: cítricos, fruta de hueso, tropical, pino.","Early / late hops / dry hopping":"Lúpulo pronto / tarde / dry hopping","Start of boil = bitterness; end = aroma; later, cool = aroma.":"Inicio de cocción = amargor; final = aroma; después, en frío = aroma.","Ale yeast":"Levadura ale","Quick, warmer, fruity and spicy aromas, many strains → ales.":"Rápida, más cálida, aromas frutales y especiados, muchas cepas → ales.","Lager yeast":"Levadura lager","Slower, cooler, less aroma, fewer strains → lagers.":"Más lenta, más fresca, menos aromas, menos cepas → lagers.","Brettanomyces":"Brettanomyces","Yeast: ripe pineapple, peach, farmyard, leather, hay, earth.":"Levadura: piña madura, melocotón, corral, cuero, heno, tierra.","Spontaneous fermentation":"Fermentación espontánea","No cultured yeast or bacteria: only ambient ones.":"Ninguna levadura ni bacteria cultivada: solo las del ambiente.","Beer appearance":"Aspecto de la cerveza","Clear–hazy–opaque; straw → black; foam.":"Transparente–turbia–opaca; pajizo → negro; espuma.","Yeast aromas":"Aromas de levadura","Fruit (banana…), spice (clove, pepper), farmyard, bubblegum, nail varnish.":"Fruta (plátano…), especias (clavo, pimienta), corral, chicle, quitaesmalte.","Malt-driven styles: base malts only":"Estilos de malta: solo maltas base","A beer style is a set of characteristics, achieved with a certain mix of ingredients and techniques, linked to a name. The world's most popular beer is an easy-drinking pale lager, made everywhere. For these styles brewers use only base malts (lightly kilned malted barley): whether ale or lager, the colour is straw or gold and the aromas recall bread crumb, bread dough or water cracker. If sugar, syrup or neutral grains such as rice go into the recipe, the beer has lighter aroma intensity and body than an all-malt beer.":"Un estilo es un conjunto de características, logrado con ciertos ingredientes y técnicas, ligado a un nombre. La cerveza más bebida del mundo es una lager clara y fácil, elaborada en todas partes. Para estos estilos se usan solo maltas base (cebada malteada poco secada): sea ale o lager, el color es pajizo o dorado y los aromas recuerdan a miga, masa de pan o galleta salada. Si la receta incluye azúcar, jarabe o cereales neutros como el arroz, la cerveza tiene menos intensidad aromática y menos cuerpo que una 100 % malta.","American or international pale lager: straw or gold, light aroma intensity (bread dough, water cracker, sometimes a little hop), low or medium bitterness, medium alcohol, high carbonation. Munich helles ('hell' is German for bright or pale): a lager, usually gold, with bread crumb or water cracker plus subtle spicy, herbal or floral hop notes; low to medium bitterness, medium alcohol. Blonde ale (sometimes 'golden ale'): an easy ale, straw to gold, with subtle bread crumb, low to medium alcohol, medium bitterness, maybe a touch of fruit from the yeast and subtle hops.":"Lager clara estadounidense o internacional: pajiza o dorada, aroma ligero (masa de pan, galleta salada, a veces algo de lúpulo), amargor bajo o medio, alcohol medio, carbonatación alta. Munich helles («hell» significa claro, luminoso en alemán): lager normalmente dorada, con miga o galleta y sutiles notas especiadas, herbales o florales del lúpulo; amargor de bajo a medio, alcohol medio. Blonde ale (a veces «golden ale»): ale fácil, de pajiza a dorada, con miga suave, alcohol de bajo a medio, amargor medio y a veces un toque frutal de la levadura y lúpulo discreto.","Base malts only: straw or gold; crumb, dough, cracker":"Solo maltas base: pajizo o dorado; miga, masa, galleta","Rice, syrups, sugar → lighter aroma and body":"Arroz, jarabes, azúcar → aromas y cuerpo más ligeros","International pale lager: light aroma, high carbonation":"Lager clara internacional: aroma ligero, carbonatación alta","Munich helles (gold lager) · blonde/golden ale (ale)":"Munich helles (lager dorada) · blonde/golden ale (ale)","Munich dunkel and brown ale":"Munich dunkel y brown ale","Adding small amounts of speciality malts to base malts brings aromas of biscuit, bread crust, toast, toasted nuts, caramel, dried fruit, coffee and chocolate, and amber, copper, brown or black colours. Munich dunkel ('dunkel' is German for dark) is a copper to brown lager with toasted bread, bread crust, toasted nut and sometimes caramel or chocolate, plus at times subtle spicy, herbal or floral hop notes; low to medium bitterness, medium alcohol.":"Añadiendo pequeñas cantidades de maltas especiales a las maltas base aparecen aromas de galleta, corteza de pan, pan tostado, frutos secos tostados, caramelo, fruta pasa, café y chocolate, y colores ámbar, cobre, marrón o negro. La Munich dunkel («dunkel» significa oscuro en alemán) es una lager de cobriza a marrón, con pan tostado, corteza de pan, avellana tostada y a veces caramelo o chocolate, y a veces sutiles notas especiadas, herbales o florales de lúpulo; amargor de bajo a medio, alcohol medio.","Brown ale is an amber to brown ale with toasted nut, toasted bread and sometimes chocolate or caramel, sometimes with fruity yeast aromas. Some versions have subtle fruity, earthy or herbal hops, others more intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine notes. Bitterness and alcohol both range from low to high: it is a broad style.":"La brown ale es una ale de ámbar a marrón, con frutos secos tostados, pan tostado y a veces chocolate o caramelo, a veces con aromas frutales de levadura. Algunas versiones tienen lúpulo sutil (frutal, terroso, herbal) y otras notas más intensas de cítricos, fruta de hueso, tropical o pino. Amargor y alcohol van de bajos a altos: es un estilo muy amplio.","Small amounts of speciality malt: biscuit, toast, caramel, coffee, chocolate; amber to black":"Maltas especiales en pequeñas dosis: galleta, tostado, caramelo, café, chocolate; de ámbar a negro","Munich dunkel: copper-brown lager, toast, nut; low-medium bitterness":"Munich dunkel: lager cobriza-marrón, tostado, avellana; amargor bajo-medio","Brown ale: amber-brown ale, toasted nut; bitterness and alcohol low to high":"Brown ale: ale ámbar-marrón, avellana tostada; amargor y alcohol de bajos a altos","Porter, stout and barley wine":"Porter, stout y barley wine","Porters and stouts are two closely related families of ales. They are brown or black, with malt aromas such as coffee or chocolate and sometimes caramel. Some have subtle hops, others more intense citrus, stone fruit, tropical or pine notes; fruity yeast aromas sometimes show too. Bitterness is low to high and alcohol low to very high. Very high-alcohol versions with pronounced roasted aromas often have 'imperial' in their name.":"Porter y stout son dos familias de ales muy cercanas. Son marrones o negras, con aromas de malta como café o chocolate y a veces caramelo. Algunas tienen lúpulo sutil y otras más intenso (cítricos, fruta de hueso, tropical, pino); a veces se notan aromas frutales de levadura. Amargor de bajo a alto, alcohol de bajo a muy alto. Las versiones de alcohol muy alto, con aromas tostados marcados, suelen llevar la palabra «imperial» en el nombre.","Barley wine is an ale, often amber (though it can range from gold to brown), with intense malt aromas: toasted bread, caramel, digestive biscuit, dried fruit. It sometimes has fruity yeast notes. It is typically full-bodied with notable sweetness and high or very high alcohol. Hops range from subtle earthy, floral, fruity notes to more prominent pine, citrus or tropical fruit, with low to high bitterness. Barley wines are often suitable for ageing.":"El barley wine es una ale a menudo ámbar (aunque puede ir del dorado al marrón), con aromas de malta intensos: pan tostado, caramelo, galleta, fruta pasa. A veces tiene notas frutales de levadura. Suele tener cuerpo lleno, dulzor notable y alcohol alto o muy alto. El lúpulo va de sutil (terroso, floral, frutal) a más marcado (pino, cítricos, tropical), con amargor de bajo a alto. A menudo admite envejecimiento.","Porter and stout: brown or black ales, coffee and chocolate":"Porter y stout: ales marrones o negras, café y chocolate","'Imperial': very high-alcohol, strongly roasted versions":"«Imperial»: versiones de alcohol muy alto, muy tostadas","Barley wine: often amber, intense malt, full body, sweet, high or very high alcohol":"Barley wine: a menudo ámbar, malta intensa, cuerpo lleno, dulce, alcohol alto o muy alto","Barley wine: often suitable for ageing":"Barley wine: a menudo apto para envejecer","Two ways to be hoppy; pilsner and bitter":"Dos formas de ser lupulada; pilsner y bitter","Hops bring two things: bitterness and aroma. Some styles have medium or pronounced bitterness with restrained hop aroma: most hops go in early in the boil and few at the end, using traditional British, Czech or German hops (subtle spicy, floral, herbal, earthy or fruity). Others have high bitterness AND pronounced hop aroma: hops early (bitterness), later (flavour) and dry hopped (aroma), using American, New Zealand or Australian hops (citrus, stone fruit, tropical, pine). Recently some of these beers focus more on hop aroma than on bitterness, and many malt-driven styles now also appear in much hoppier versions.":"El lúpulo aporta dos cosas: amargor y aromas. Algunos estilos tienen amargor medio o marcado con aroma de lúpulo contenido: casi todo el lúpulo va al principio de la cocción y poco al final, con lúpulos tradicionales británicos, checos o alemanes (sutiles, especiados, florales, herbales, terrosos o frutales). Otros tienen amargor alto Y aromas marcados: lúpulo al principio (amargor), más tarde (sabor) y en dry hopping (aroma), con lúpulos estadounidenses, neozelandeses o australianos (cítricos, fruta de hueso, tropical, pino). Últimamente algunas de estas cervezas se centran más en el aroma que en el amargor, y muchos estilos de malta se hacen hoy también en versiones muy lupuladas.","Traditional Czech or German pilsner: a straw to gold lager with bread dough, light honey or bread crumb, and subtle spicy, floral or herbal hops; medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol. Bitter: a hop-driven ale from England, amber to copper, with toasted bread, bread crust, digestive biscuit or caramel, subtle fruity, earthy or herbal hops and sometimes fruity yeast notes; medium to high bitterness, alcohol low to high.":"Pilsner checa o alemana tradicional: lager de pajiza a dorada, con masa de pan, miel suave o miga y lúpulo sutil especiado, floral o herbal; amargor de medio a alto, alcohol medio. Bitter: ale lupulada nacida en Inglaterra, de ámbar a cobriza, con pan tostado, corteza, galleta o caramelo, lúpulo sutil frutal, terroso o herbal y a veces notas frutales de levadura; amargor de medio a alto, alcohol de bajo a alto.","Bitterness with restrained aroma: hops mostly early, traditional European hops":"Amargor con aroma contenido: lúpulo sobre todo al principio, lúpulos europeos tradicionales","High bitterness and intense aroma: early, late and dry hops, New World hops":"Amargor alto y aroma intenso: lúpulo pronto, tarde y dry hopping, lúpulos del Nuevo Mundo","Czech or German pilsner: straw-gold lager, medium-high bitterness":"Pilsner checa o alemana: lager pajiza-dorada, amargor medio-alto","Bitter: English amber-copper ale, biscuit and caramel, medium-high bitterness":"Bitter: ale inglesa ámbar-cobre, galleta y caramelo, amargor medio-alto","American pale ale, American IPA, hazy IPA":"American pale ale, American IPA, hazy IPA","American pale ale (APA): gold to amber, with hop aromas from citrus, stone and tropical fruit to pine, and subtle malt (bread crumb, sometimes toast or digestive biscuit); sometimes fruity yeast notes. Medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol. American IPA (India pale ale) can be seen as a stronger APA with even more bitterness and hop aroma: gold to amber, defined by high bitterness and pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit aromas, with subtle malt and medium to high alcohol.":"American pale ale (APA): de dorada a ámbar, con lúpulo que va de cítricos, fruta de hueso y tropical hasta pino, y malta discreta (miga, a veces tostado o galleta); a veces notas frutales de levadura. Amargor de medio a alto, alcohol medio. American IPA (India pale ale): puede verse como una APA más fuerte, con aún más amargor y aroma de lúpulo; de dorada a ámbar, definida por amargor alto y aromas de pino, resina, cítricos, fruta tropical y de hueso, malta discreta y alcohol de medio a alto.","Hazy IPA (also New England IPA): straw to gold and distinctly hazy, with subtle malt (water cracker, bread crumb), stone fruit, tropical and citrus hop aromas and sometimes fruity yeast notes. It is typically LESS bitter than American IPA (low to medium bitterness), with medium to high alcohol: the example of beers focused on hop aroma rather than bitterness.":"Hazy IPA (o New England IPA): de pajiza a dorada y claramente turbia, con malta ligera (galleta, miga), lúpulo de fruta de hueso, tropical y cítricos, y a veces notas frutales de levadura. Suele ser MENOS amarga que una American IPA (amargor de bajo a medio), con alcohol de medio a alto: es el ejemplo de las cervezas centradas en el aroma más que en el amargor.","APA: gold-amber, citrus-tropical-pine hops, medium-high bitterness, medium alcohol":"APA: dorada-ámbar, lúpulo cítrico-tropical-pino, amargor medio-alto, alcohol medio","American IPA: stronger APA, high bitterness, pine and resin, medium-high alcohol":"American IPA: APA más fuerte, amargor alto, pino y resina, alcohol medio-alto","Hazy/New England IPA: hazy, straw-gold, very aromatic, LESS bitter":"Hazy/New England IPA: turbia, pajiza-dorada, muy aromática, MENOS amarga","Weissbier and witbier":"Weissbier y witbier","In yeast-driven styles the yeast aromas are the signature. Since lagers have few yeast aromas, these are all ales: fruity (tropical, pome, citrus) and sometimes spicy (clove, peppercorn). Weissbier (also called hefeweizen) is typically straw to gold and cloudy/hazy: banana and clove from the yeast balance bread crumb from the wheat; low bitterness, medium alcohol, typically high carbonation. 'Weiss' is German for white and 'Weizen' for wheat: both words name German wheat beers.":"En los estilos de levadura, los aromas de levadura son la firma. Como las lagers tienen pocos aromas de levadura, todas son ales: frutales (tropical, manzana y pera, cítricos) y a veces especiados (clavo, pimienta). La weissbier (también llamada hefeweizen) suele ser de pajiza a dorada y turbia: plátano y clavo de la levadura equilibrados con miga de pan del trigo; amargor bajo, alcohol medio, carbonatación normalmente alta. «Weiss» significa blanco en alemán y «Weizen» trigo: ambas palabras designan las cervezas de trigo alemanas.","Witbier is hazy and straw to gold, with subtle fruity and spicy yeast aromas, often complemented by citrus and floral notes from the coriander seed and orange peel used as flavourings. It has subtle bread crumb or light honey from the wheat and sometimes subtle spicy or herbal hops; low bitterness, medium alcohol. It may be labelled with the French term blanche, meaning 'white'.":"La witbier es turbia, de pajiza a dorada, con aromas sutiles frutales y especiados de levadura, a menudo acompañados de notas cítricas y florales de las semillas de cilantro y la piel de naranja usadas como aromatizantes. Tiene notas sutiles de miga o miel suave del trigo y a veces un toque de lúpulo especiado o herbal; amargor bajo, alcohol medio. En la etiqueta puede aparecer el término francés «blanche», es decir, «blanca».","Yeast-driven styles: all ales; fruity and spicy yeast aromas":"Estilos de levadura: todas ales; aromas frutales y especiados de levadura","Weissbier/hefeweizen: hazy, banana and clove, wheat, low bitterness, high carbonation":"Weissbier/hefeweizen: turbia, plátano y clavo, trigo, amargor bajo, carbonatación alta","Weiss = white, Weizen = wheat":"Weiss = blanco, Weizen = trigo","Witbier/blanche: hazy, coriander and orange peel, low bitterness":"Witbier/blanche: turbia, cilantro y piel de naranja, amargor bajo","Dubbel, tripel and saison":"Dubbel, tripel y saison","Dubbel is copper to brown, with fruity apple, plum and prune and spicy clove or peppercorn from the yeast, balanced by toast, caramel or dried fruit from malt or caramelised sugars, and sometimes subtle hops. High alcohol, medium bitterness; it generally has sediment from bottle-conditioning and is highly carbonated. Tripel is gold, with prominent fruity (orange, banana) and spicy (peppercorn, clove) yeast aromas and subtle light honey or bread crumb malt. High or very high alcohol, even higher than a dubbel; medium bitterness; also bottle-conditioned with sediment and highly carbonated.":"La dubbel es cobriza o marrón, con aromas frutales de manzana, ciruela y ciruela pasa y notas especiadas de clavo o pimienta de la levadura, equilibrados con pan tostado, caramelo o fruta pasa de la malta o de azúcares caramelizados, y a veces lúpulo sutil. Alcohol alto, amargor medio; suele tener sedimento del acondicionamiento en botella y mucha carbonatación. La tripel es dorada, con aromas frutales marcados (naranja, plátano) y especiados (pimienta, clavo) de la levadura y malta sutil de miel suave o miga. Alcohol alto o muy alto, más aún que la dubbel; amargor medio; también con sedimento y muy carbonatada.","Saison is most commonly gold to amber, with fruity and spicy yeast aromas (orange, peach, apple, a peppercorn note), bread crumb, toast or digestive biscuit from malt, and spicy, floral, fruity or earthy hops. It can be slightly sour. It often has sediment from bottle-conditioning and is highly carbonated; bitterness is typically medium and alcohol low to high.":"La saison suele ser de dorada a ámbar, con aromas frutales y especiados de levadura (naranja, melocotón, manzana, un toque de pimienta), malta de miga, tostado o galleta y lúpulo especiado, floral, frutal o terroso. Puede ser ligeramente ácida. A menudo tiene sedimento del acondicionamiento en botella y mucha carbonatación; amargor normalmente medio, alcohol de bajo a alto.","Dubbel: copper-brown, apple, plum, clove; high alcohol; sediment":"Dubbel: cobriza-marrón, manzana, ciruela, clavo; alcohol alto; sedimento","Tripel: gold, orange, banana, pepper; high or very high alcohol (above dubbel)":"Tripel: dorada, naranja, plátano, pimienta; alcohol alto o muy alto (más que la dubbel)","Saison: gold-amber, orange, peach, pepper; can be slightly sour":"Saison: dorada-ámbar, naranja, melocotón, pimienta; puede ser ligeramente ácida","All three highly carbonated, often bottle-conditioned":"Las tres muy carbonatadas, a menudo acondicionadas en botella","Where sourness comes from; Berliner weisse":"De dónde viene la acidez; Berliner weisse","In sour styles the sour character comes from bacteria, such as lactic acid bacteria, active during fermentation and maturation: they add acidity to the finished beer. Brettanomyces can also play a part, adding complex farmyard, hay, ripe pineapple and leather aromas.":"En los estilos ácidos, la acidez viene de bacterias, como las lácticas, activas durante la fermentación y la maduración: añaden acidez a la cerveza terminada. A veces también influye el Brettanomyces, con aromas complejos de corral, heno, piña madura y cuero.","Berliner weisse is straw-coloured and hazy, with subtle bread dough from wheat and malt and light fruity notes from fermentation. It is moderately sour, with light body, low alcohol and low or no perceptible bitterness. It is sometimes served with syrups: raspberry or woodruff (a slightly bitter herb reminiscent of sweet hay). It is typically made with cultured yeast and bacteria.":"La Berliner weisse es pajiza y turbia, con notas sutiles de masa de pan del trigo y la malta y leves notas frutales de la fermentación. Es moderadamente ácida, con cuerpo ligero, alcohol bajo y amargor bajo o imperceptible. A veces se sirve con jarabes: frambuesa o asperilla (una hierba algo amarga que recuerda al heno dulce). Normalmente se hace con levaduras y bacterias cultivadas.","Sour styles: sourness from bacteria (lactic) during fermentation and maturation":"Estilos ácidos: acidez de bacterias (lácticas) al fermentar y madurar","Sometimes Brett too: farmyard, hay, pineapple, leather":"A veces también Brett: corral, heno, piña, cuero","Berliner weisse: straw, hazy, moderately sour, light, low alcohol":"Berliner weisse: pajiza, turbia, moderadamente ácida, ligera, alcohol bajo","Sometimes served with raspberry or woodruff syrup; cultured yeast and bacteria":"A veces con jarabe de frambuesa o asperilla; levaduras y bacterias cultivadas","Geuze: spontaneous fermentation":"Geuze: la fermentación espontánea","Geuze (gueuze) is gold, with complex farmyard aromas (earth and hay) and fruity ones such as grapefruit, orange, apple, apricot or rhubarb, plus subtle bread crumb. It is sour, with low or no bitterness and medium to high alcohol. It generally has sediment from bottle-conditioning and is highly carbonated.":"La geuze (o gueuze) es dorada, con aromas complejos de corral (tierra y heno) y frutales como pomelo, naranja, manzana, albaricoque o ruibarbo, además de una sutil nota de miga. Es ácida, con amargor bajo o nulo y alcohol de medio a alto. Suele tener sedimento del acondicionamiento en botella y mucha carbonatación.","The key difference from Berliner weisse is method: geuze is made by spontaneous fermentation and shaped by a range of ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brettanomyces and lactic acid bacteria. Berliner weisse, by contrast, uses cultured yeast and bacteria.":"La diferencia clave con la Berliner weisse es el método: la geuze nace de la fermentación espontánea y la marcan muchas levaduras y bacterias del ambiente, entre ellas Brettanomyces y bacterias lácticas. La Berliner weisse, en cambio, usa levaduras y bacterias cultivadas.","Geuze: gold, sour, farmyard, grapefruit, apple, apricot; low or no bitterness":"Geuze: dorada, ácida, corral, pomelo, manzana, albaricoque; amargor bajo o nulo","Medium-high alcohol; sediment, highly carbonated":"Alcohol medio-alto; sedimento, muy carbonatada","Spontaneous fermentation: ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brett":"Fermentación espontánea: levaduras y bacterias del ambiente, incluido Brett","What colour is a beer made only with base malts usually?":"¿De qué color suele ser una cerveza hecha solo con maltas base?","Base malts give straw or gold beers.":"Las maltas base dan cervezas pajizas o doradas.","Darker colours need speciality malts.":"Los colores más oscuros necesitan maltas especiales.","What effect does using rice, sugar or syrup have in a pale lager?":"¿Qué efecto tiene usar arroz, azúcar o jarabe en una lager clara?","Lighter aroma intensity and body":"Menos intensidad aromática y menos cuerpo","A darker colour":"Un color más oscuro","More sourness":"Más acidez","Compared with an all-malt beer, the result is lighter and less aromatic.":"Frente a una cerveza 100 % malta, resulta más ligera y menos aromática.","Colour, bitterness and sourness do not depend on these ingredients.":"El color, el amargor y la acidez no dependen de estos ingredientes.","Which description fits an American or international pale lager?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a una lager clara estadounidense o internacional?","Straw or gold, light aroma, low-medium bitterness, high carbonation":"Pajiza o dorada, aroma ligero, amargor bajo-medio, carbonatación alta","Black, coffee and chocolate, very high alcohol":"Negra, café y chocolate, alcohol muy alto","Hazy, banana and clove":"Turbia, plátano y clavo","Sour with farmyard aromas":"Ácida con aromas de corral","It is the world's most popular easy-drinking pale beer.":"Es la cerveza clara y fácil más bebida del mundo.","The others describe stout, weissbier and sour beers such as geuze.":"Las demás describen stout, weissbier y cervezas ácidas como la geuze.","What does 'hell' mean in Munich helles?":"¿Qué significa «hell» en Munich helles?","Bright, light or pale":"Claro, luminoso","Dark":"Oscuro","Strong":"Fuerte","'Hell' is German for bright or pale: helles is a gold lager.":"«Hell» significa claro en alemán: la helles es una lager dorada.","'Dunkel' means dark and 'Weizen' wheat.":"«Dunkel» significa oscuro y «Weizen» trigo.","Munich helles is…":"La Munich helles es…","a gold lager with bread-crumb malt and subtle hops":"una lager dorada con malta de miga y lúpulo sutil","a heavily roasted black ale":"una ale negra muy tostada","a hazy wheat ale":"una ale de trigo turbia","a spontaneously fermented sour beer":"una cerveza ácida de fermentación espontánea","Gold lager, bread crumb or cracker, subtle hop notes, low-medium bitterness, medium alcohol.":"Lager dorada, miga o galleta, notas sutiles de lúpulo, amargor bajo-medio, alcohol medio.","It is a lager, not an ale, and is neither dark, hazy nor sour.":"Es una lager, no una ale; no es oscura, ni turbia, ni ácida.","Which base-malt-only malt-driven style is an ALE?":"¿Qué estilo de malta solo con maltas base es una ALE?","Blonde ale":"Blonde ale","Munich helles":"Munich helles","International pale lager":"Lager clara internacional","Munich dunkel":"Munich dunkel","Blonde (golden) ale is the ale of the group, next to two lagers.":"La blonde ale (o golden ale) es la ale del grupo, junto a dos lagers.","Helles and international lager are lagers; dunkel is a lager with speciality malts.":"Helles y lager internacional son lagers; la dunkel es una lager con maltas especiales.","What other name is blonde ale sometimes labelled with?":"¿Con qué otro nombre aparece a veces la blonde ale?","Golden ale":"Golden ale","Brown ale":"Brown ale","Blanche":"Blanche","Barley wine":"Barley wine","Blonde ale and golden ale name the same easy, gold style.":"Blonde ale y golden ale designan el mismo estilo fácil y dorado.","'Blanche' is witbier; brown ale and barley wine use speciality malts.":"«Blanche» es la witbier; brown ale y barley wine usan maltas especiales.","What does 'dunkel' mean?":"¿Qué significa «dunkel»?","Pale":"Claro","White":"Blanco","Double":"Doble","'Dunkel' is German for dark.":"«Dunkel» significa oscuro en alemán.","Pale is 'hell', white is 'weiss'; 'double' recalls dubbel.":"Claro es «hell», blanco «weiss»; «doble» recuerda a dubbel.","Which description fits Munich dunkel?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a la Munich dunkel?","Copper-brown lager with toast and toasted nut":"Lager cobriza-marrón con pan tostado y avellana tostada","Black ale with coffee and very high alcohol":"Ale negra con café y alcohol muy alto","Very bitter straw lager":"Lager pajiza muy amarga","Hazy ale with coriander":"Ale turbia con cilantro","A dark lager with speciality malts: toast, bread crust, nut, sometimes caramel or chocolate.":"Lager oscura con maltas especiales: tostado, corteza, avellana, a veces caramelo o chocolate.","The second describes an imperial stout, the third a pilsner, the fourth a witbier.":"La segunda describe una imperial stout, la tercera una pilsner y la cuarta una witbier.","What is true of bitterness and alcohol in brown ale?":"¿Qué ocurre con el amargor y el alcohol en la brown ale?","Both range from low to high":"Ambos van de bajos a altos","They are always very high":"Siempre son muy altos","Bitterness is always absent":"El amargor siempre es nulo","Alcohol always under 4%":"Alcohol siempre por debajo del 4 %","Brown ale is a broad style: bitterness and alcohol vary a lot.":"La brown ale es un estilo amplio: amargor y alcohol varían mucho.","Options with 'always' are too rigid for this style.":"Las opciones con «siempre» son demasiado rígidas para este estilo.","Which malt aromas are typical of porter and stout?":"¿Qué aromas de malta son típicos de porter y stout?","Bread crumb and water cracker":"Miga y galleta salada","Grapefruit and rhubarb":"Pomelo y ruibarbo","Roasted malts give coffee, chocolate and sometimes caramel, with a brown or black colour.":"Las maltas tostadas dan café, chocolate y a veces caramelo, con color marrón o negro.","Crumb and cracker are base-malt notes; banana and clove come from yeast; grapefruit and rhubarb suit geuze.":"Miga y galleta son de maltas base; plátano y clavo de la levadura; pomelo y ruibarbo son propios de la geuze.","What does 'imperial' usually indicate in a stout's name?":"¿Qué indica normalmente la palabra «imperial» en el nombre de una stout?","Very high alcohol and pronounced roasted aromas":"Alcohol muy alto y aromas tostados marcados","A beer made in England":"Una cerveza hecha en Inglaterra","An alcohol-free beer":"Una cerveza sin alcohol","A sour beer":"Una cerveza ácida","'Imperial' versions are very strong and strongly roasted.":"Las versiones «imperial» son muy alcohólicas y muy tostadas.","The term shows neither origin, sourness nor absence of alcohol.":"El término no indica origen, acidez ni ausencia de alcohol.","Which description fits barley wine?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde al barley wine?","Often amber ale, intense malt, full body, sweet, high or very high alcohol":"Ale a menudo ámbar, malta intensa, cuerpo lleno, dulce, alcohol alto o muy alto","A wine made from barley":"Un vino hecho con cebada","A light, dry lager":"Lager ligera y seca","A sour wheat beer":"Cerveza ácida de trigo","Despite the name it is a beer: a rich, sweet, strong ale.":"A pesar del nombre es una cerveza: una ale rica, dulce y muy alcohólica.","It is not wine, lager or a sour beer.":"No es vino, ni lager, ni cerveza ácida.","Which malt-driven style is often suitable for ageing?":"¿Qué estilo de malta suele admitir envejecimiento?","Rich, strong barley wine is often suitable for ageing.":"El barley wine, rico y muy alcohólico, suele admitir envejecimiento.","Pale lagers, helles and blonde ales are fresh beers best drunk young.":"Lagers claras, helles y blonde ales son cervezas frescas para beber jóvenes.","A black beer with coffee and chocolate aromas: which style is most likely?":"Una cerveza negra con aromas de café y chocolate: ¿qué estilo es más probable?","Porter or stout":"Porter o stout","Hazy IPA":"Hazy IPA","Berliner weisse":"Berliner weisse","Black colour and roasted aromas point to porter or stout.":"Color negro y aromas tostados indican porter o stout.","Helles, hazy IPA and Berliner weisse are pale, straw to gold.":"Helles, hazy IPA y Berliner weisse son claras, de pajiza a dorada.","How is pronounced bitterness with restrained hop aroma achieved?":"¿Cómo se logra un amargor marcado con aroma de lúpulo contenido?","Most hops early in the boil and few at the end":"Casi todo el lúpulo al principio de la cocción y poco al final","Dry hopping only":"Solo dry hopping","No hops at all":"Nada de lúpulo","All hops at the end of the boil":"Todo el lúpulo al final de la cocción","Early hops = bitterness; few late hops = little aroma.":"Lúpulo pronto = amargor; poco lúpulo tardío = poco aroma.","Dry hopping and late hops mainly give aroma, not bitterness.":"El dry hopping y el lúpulo tardío dan sobre todo aroma, no amargor.","Which style is a hop-driven lager with traditional hops?":"¿Qué estilo es una lager lupulada con lúpulos tradicionales?","Traditional Czech or German pilsner":"Pilsner checa o alemana tradicional","Bitter":"Bitter","American IPA":"American IPA","Czech or German pilsner is the lager of the traditional hop-driven group.":"La pilsner checa o alemana es la lager del grupo lupulado tradicional.","Bitter is an ale, American IPA uses New World hops, dunkel is malt-driven.":"La bitter es una ale, la American IPA usa lúpulos del Nuevo Mundo y la dunkel es de malta.","Which description fits traditional Czech or German pilsner?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a la pilsner checa o alemana tradicional?","Straw-gold, subtle spicy or floral hops, medium-high bitterness":"Pajiza-dorada, lúpulo sutil especiado o floral, amargor medio-alto","Hazy, very tropical, little bitterness":"Turbia, muy tropical, poco amarga","Black, roasted, very high alcohol":"Negra, tostada, alcohol muy alto","Sour, with raspberry syrup":"Ácida, con jarabe de frambuesa","Bread dough or light honey, subtle hops, medium to high bitterness, medium alcohol.":"Masa de pan o miel suave, lúpulo sutil, amargor de medio a alto, alcohol medio.","The others describe hazy IPA, imperial stout and Berliner weisse.":"Las demás describen hazy IPA, imperial stout y Berliner weisse.","Which country does bitter come from originally?":"¿De qué país es originaria la bitter?","England":"Inglaterra","Germany":"Alemania","Belgium":"Bélgica","United States":"Estados Unidos","Bitter is a hop-driven ale from England.":"La bitter es una ale lupulada nacida en Inglaterra.","Germany and Belgium are linked to other styles (helles, dubbel…); the USA to APA and American IPA.":"Alemania y Bélgica se asocian a otros estilos (helles, dubbel…); EE. UU. a la APA y la IPA americana.","Which description fits bitter?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a la bitter?","Amber-copper ale, biscuit or caramel, subtle hops, medium-high bitterness":"Ale ámbar-cobriza, galleta o caramelo, lúpulo sutil, amargor medio-alto","Straw lager with intense tropical hops":"Lager pajiza con lúpulo tropical intenso","Hazy wheat ale with banana":"Ale turbia de trigo con plátano","Very sweet black lager":"Lager negra muy dulce","Bitter pairs toasty, caramel malt with subtle traditional hops.":"La bitter une malta tostada y caramelo a un lúpulo tradicional sutil.","Bitter is an ale, not a lager, and has no banana aromas.":"La bitter es una ale, no una lager, y no tiene aromas de plátano.","How are high bitterness AND intense hop aromas achieved?":"¿Cómo se logra amargor alto Y aromas de lúpulo intensos?","Hops early in the boil, later on, and dry hopping":"Lúpulo al principio de la cocción, más tarde y en dry hopping","Only early hops":"Solo lúpulo al principio","Only speciality malts":"Solo maltas especiales","Early for bitterness, late for flavour and dry hopping for aroma.":"Pronto para el amargor, tarde para el sabor y dry hopping para el aroma.","Early hops alone give bitterness with little aroma; malts and spontaneous fermentation are unrelated.":"Solo lúpulo temprano daría amargor con poco aroma; maltas y fermentación espontánea no tienen que ver.","Which style is sometimes labelled 'APA'?":"¿Qué estilo aparece a veces como «APA»?","American pale ale":"American pale ale","German pilsner":"Pilsner alemana","APA stands for American pale ale.":"APA es la abreviatura de American pale ale.","IPA means India pale ale; pilsner and blonde ale do not use this abbreviation.":"IPA significa India pale ale; pilsner y blonde ale no usan esta sigla.","How can American IPA be described compared with American pale ale?":"¿Cómo se puede describir la American IPA frente a la American pale ale?","Stronger, with even more bitterness and hop aroma":"Más fuerte, con aún más amargor y aroma de lúpulo","Lighter and less bitter":"Más ligera y menos amarga","Darker and more roasted":"Más oscura y tostada","More sour":"Más ácida","American IPA is like a stronger, more bitter, more aromatic APA.":"La American IPA es como una APA más fuerte, más amarga y más aromática.","Colour stays gold to amber, with no roast or sourness.":"El color sigue siendo de dorado a ámbar, sin tostado ni acidez.","Which hop aromas define American IPA?":"¿Qué aromas de lúpulo definen la American IPA?","Pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit":"Pino, resina, cítricos, fruta tropical y de hueso","Subtle spicy, herbal, earthy":"Especiados, herbales, terrosos sutiles","New World hops: pine, resin, citrus, tropical and stone fruit.":"Lúpulos del Nuevo Mundo: pino, resina, cítricos, fruta tropical y de hueso.","Subtle spicy and earthy notes are traditional European hops; banana and clove come from yeast; coffee and chocolate from malt.":"Lo especiado y terroso sutil es de lúpulos europeos; plátano y clavo vienen de la levadura; café y chocolate de la malta.","Compared with an American IPA, a hazy IPA is typically…":"Frente a una American IPA, la hazy IPA suele ser…","less bitter":"menos amarga","more bitter":"más amarga","darker":"más oscura","more sour":"más ácida","Hazy IPA has low to medium bitterness: it focuses on aroma.":"La hazy IPA tiene amargor de bajo a medio: apuesta por el aroma.","It is straw or gold, not dark, and not a sour style.":"Es pajiza o dorada, no oscura, y no es un estilo ácido.","What other name is hazy IPA labelled with?":"¿Con qué otro nombre aparece la hazy IPA?","New England IPA":"New England IPA","India pale lager":"India pale lager","Imperial stout":"Imperial stout","Hazy IPA and New England IPA are the same style.":"Hazy IPA y New England IPA son el mismo estilo.","Golden ale is another name for blonde ale; imperial stout is a very strong stout.":"Golden ale es otro nombre de la blonde ale; imperial stout es una stout muy fuerte.","A straw-coloured, distinctly hazy beer with lots of tropical fruit and moderate bitterness: which style?":"Una cerveza pajiza, claramente turbia, con mucha fruta tropical y amargor moderado: ¿qué estilo?","Weissbier":"Weissbier","Hazy + tropical hops + low-medium bitterness = hazy IPA.":"Turbia + lúpulo tropical + amargor bajo-medio = hazy IPA.","Weissbier is also hazy, but its aromas are yeast-driven banana and clove. Bitter and helles are clear.":"La weissbier también es turbia, pero sus aromas son plátano y clavo de la levadura. Bitter y helles son transparentes.","Why are yeast-driven styles all ales?":"¿Por qué los estilos «de levadura» son todos ales?","Because lagers typically have few yeast aromas":"Porque las lagers suelen tener pocos aromas de levadura","Because lagers contain no yeast":"Porque las lagers no tienen levadura","Because ales have no hops":"Porque las ales no tienen lúpulo","Because of the law":"Por ley","Lager yeast gives little aroma; ale yeast gives a lot, fruity and spicy.":"La levadura lager da pocos aromas; la ale da muchos, frutales y especiados.","Lagers are made with yeast too, and ales use hops; no law is involved.":"Las lagers también se hacen con levadura y las ales usan lúpulo; no hay ley al respecto.","Which yeast aromas characterise weissbier?":"¿Qué aromas de levadura caracterizan la weissbier?","Pine and resin":"Pino y resina","Farmyard and leather":"Corral y cuero","Banana (fruity) and clove (spicy) come from weissbier yeast.":"Plátano (frutal) y clavo (especiado) vienen de la levadura de la weissbier.","Pine and resin are hops, coffee and chocolate roasted malt, farmyard and leather typical of Brett.":"Pino y resina son de lúpulo, café y chocolate de malta tostada, corral y cuero propios del Brett.","What is weissbier also known as?":"¿Con qué otro nombre se conoce la weissbier?","Hefeweizen":"Hefeweizen","Dunkel":"Dunkel","Gueuze":"Gueuze","Weissbier and hefeweizen are the same German wheat beer.":"Weissbier y hefeweizen son la misma cerveza de trigo alemana.","'Blanche' is witbier, 'dunkel' a dark lager, 'gueuze' a sour beer.":"«Blanche» es la witbier, «dunkel» una lager oscura y «gueuze» una cerveza ácida.","What do 'Weiss' and 'Weizen' mean?":"¿Qué significan «Weiss» y «Weizen»?","White and wheat":"Blanco y trigo","Pale and dark":"Claro y oscuro","Double and triple":"Doble y triple","Yeast and hops":"Levadura y lúpulo","Weiss = white, Weizen = wheat: both name wheat beers in Germany.":"Weiss = blanco, Weizen = trigo: ambos designan cervezas de trigo en Alemania.","Pale and dark are 'hell' and 'dunkel'; double and triple recall dubbel and tripel.":"Claro y oscuro son «hell» y «dunkel»; doble y triple recuerdan a dubbel y tripel.","Which added flavourings characterise witbier?":"¿Qué aromatizantes añadidos caracterizan la witbier?","Coriander seed and orange peel":"Semillas de cilantro y piel de naranja","Coffee and vanilla":"Café y vainilla","Pumpkin and cinnamon":"Calabaza y canela","Raspberry syrup":"Jarabe de frambuesa","Coriander and orange peel give witbier citrus and floral notes.":"Cilantro y piel de naranja dan a la witbier notas cítricas y florales.","Raspberry syrup is sometimes added to Berliner weisse when served.":"El jarabe de frambuesa se añade a veces a la Berliner weisse al servirla.","Which French term is sometimes on a witbier label?":"¿Qué término francés aparece a veces en la etiqueta de la witbier?","Brune":"Brune","Saison":"Saison","Ambrée":"Ambrée","'Blanche' means 'white', like 'wit' in Dutch.":"«Blanche» significa «blanca», como «wit» en neerlandés.","Saison is another yeast-driven style; 'brune' and 'ambrée' describe colours.":"Saison es otro estilo de levadura; «brune» y «ambrée» describen colores.","Which description fits dubbel?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a la dubbel?","Copper-brown, apple, plum, clove, high alcohol, sediment":"Cobriza-marrón, manzana, ciruela, clavo, alcohol alto, sedimento","Gold, orange, banana, very high alcohol":"Dorada, naranja, plátano, alcohol muy alto","Straw, sour, low alcohol":"Pajiza, ácida, alcohol bajo","Black, coffee, imperial":"Negra, café, imperial","Dubbel pairs yeast fruit and spice with toast, caramel and dried fruit.":"La dubbel une fruta y especias de levadura con tostado, caramelo y fruta pasa.","The second is tripel, the third Berliner weisse, the fourth an imperial stout.":"La segunda es la tripel, la tercera la Berliner weisse y la cuarta una imperial stout.","Between dubbel and tripel, which usually has more alcohol, and what colour is it?":"Entre dubbel y tripel, ¿cuál suele tener más alcohol y de qué color es?","Tripel, gold":"La tripel, dorada","Dubbel, brown":"La dubbel, marrón","Tripel, black":"La tripel, negra","They have the same alcohol":"Tienen el mismo alcohol","Tripel is gold with high or very high alcohol, even higher than dubbel.":"La tripel es dorada y tiene alcohol alto o muy alto, más aún que la dubbel.","Dubbel is copper-brown but less strong; tripel is not black.":"La dubbel es cobriza-marrón pero menos alcohólica; la tripel no es negra.","Which aromas characterise tripel?":"¿Qué aromas caracterizan la tripel?","Orange, banana, pepper, clove from yeast; light honey":"Naranja, plátano, pimienta, clavo de la levadura; miel suave","Roasted coffee and chocolate":"Café y chocolate tostados","Intense pine and resin":"Pino y resina intensos","Vinegar and rancid butter":"Vinagre y mantequilla rancia","In tripel, yeast fruit and spice dominate over light malt.":"En la tripel dominan fruta y especias de la levadura, con malta ligera.","Vinegar and rancid butter are bacterial-infection faults. Coffee and pine are not typical of tripel.":"Vinagre y mantequilla rancia son defectos de infección bacteriana. Café y pino no son propios de la tripel.","Which yeast-driven style can be slightly sour?":"¿Qué estilo de levadura puede ser ligeramente ácido?","Tripel":"Tripel","Dubbel":"Dubbel","Fruity, peppery saison can be slightly sour.":"La saison, frutal y con pimienta, puede tener una ligera acidez.","Weissbier, tripel and dubbel are not described as sour.":"Weissbier, tripel y dubbel no se describen como ácidas.","What do dubbel, tripel and saison usually share?":"¿Qué suelen compartir dubbel, tripel y saison?","Sediment from bottle-conditioning and high carbonation":"Sedimento del acondicionamiento en botella y carbonatación alta","Black colour":"Color negro","They are highly carbonated ales, often bottle-conditioned with sediment.":"Son ales muy carbonatadas, a menudo acondicionadas en botella, con sedimento.","They are ales, not lagers, and neither black nor spontaneously fermented.":"Son ales, no lagers; no son negras ni de fermentación espontánea.","Where does the sour character of sour styles come from?":"¿De dónde viene la acidez de los estilos ácidos?","From bacteria, such as lactic acid bacteria":"De bacterias, como las lácticas","From hops":"Del lúpulo","From added lemon juice":"De zumo de limón añadido","From roasted malt":"De la malta tostada","Lactic bacteria, active in fermentation and maturation, add acidity.":"Las bacterias lácticas, activas al fermentar y madurar, añaden acidez.","Hops give bitterness, roasted malt coffee and chocolate; no lemon is added.":"El lúpulo da amargor y la malta tostada café y chocolate; no se añade limón.","Which description fits Berliner weisse?":"¿Qué descripción corresponde a la Berliner weisse?","Straw, hazy, moderately sour, light body, low alcohol":"Pajiza, turbia, moderadamente ácida, cuerpo ligero, alcohol bajo","Gold, very sour, high alcohol, spontaneous fermentation":"Dorada, muy ácida, alcohol alto, fermentación espontánea","Black and roasted":"Negra y tostada","Amber and very bitter":"Ámbar y muy amarga","It is a light, moderately sour wheat beer with low or no bitterness.":"Es una cerveza de trigo ligera y moderadamente ácida, con amargor bajo o nulo.","The second option is closer to geuze. Berliner weisse is neither dark nor bitter.":"La segunda opción se acerca más a la geuze. La Berliner weisse no es oscura ni amarga.","Which syrups is Berliner weisse sometimes served with?":"¿Con qué jarabes se sirve a veces la Berliner weisse?","Raspberry or woodruff":"Frambuesa o asperilla","Mint or lemon":"Menta o limón","Caramel or vanilla":"Caramelo o vainilla","Cola or ginger":"Cola o jengibre","Raspberry or woodruff, a slightly bitter herb reminiscent of sweet hay.":"Frambuesa o asperilla, una hierba algo amarga que recuerda al heno dulce.","The other options are not the traditional ones for this style.":"Las demás combinaciones no son las tradicionales para este estilo.","How is Berliner weisse typically made?":"¿Cómo se hace normalmente la Berliner weisse?","With cultured yeast and bacteria":"Con levaduras y bacterias cultivadas","By spontaneous fermentation":"Por fermentación espontánea","Without yeast":"Sin levadura","With lager yeast only":"Solo con levadura lager","Berliner weisse uses cultured yeast and bacteria.":"La Berliner weisse usa levaduras y bacterias cultivadas.","Spontaneous fermentation is geuze's method. Without yeast there is no alcohol, and lager yeast alone gives no sourness.":"La fermentación espontánea es el método de la geuze. Sin levadura no hay alcohol, y la lager sola no da acidez.","Which sour style is made by spontaneous fermentation?":"¿Qué estilo ácido se hace por fermentación espontánea?","Geuze (gueuze)":"Geuze (gueuze)","Witbier":"Witbier","Geuze comes from ambient yeast and bacteria, including Brett and lactic bacteria.":"La geuze nace de levaduras y bacterias del ambiente, entre ellas Brett y bacterias lácticas.","Berliner weisse uses cultured microbes; saison and witbier are yeast-driven styles.":"La Berliner weisse usa microorganismos cultivados; saison y witbier son estilos de levadura.","Which aromas are typical of geuze?":"¿Qué aromas son típicos de la geuze?","Farmyard (earth, hay) and fruit such as grapefruit, apple, apricot, rhubarb":"Corral (tierra, heno) y fruta como pomelo, manzana, albaricoque, ruibarbo","Caramel and raisin":"Caramelo y pasas","Geuze is complex: farmyard notes and lots of fruit, with a hint of bread crumb.":"La geuze es compleja: notas de corral y mucha fruta, con un toque de miga.","Coffee and chocolate suggest stout, banana and clove weissbier, caramel and raisin malty beers such as barley wine.":"Café y chocolate sugieren stout, plátano y clavo weissbier, caramelo y pasas cervezas malteadas como el barley wine.","Which statement about geuze is correct?":"¿Qué afirmación sobre la geuze es correcta?","It is sour, gold, with low or no bitterness and highly carbonated":"Es ácida, dorada, con amargor bajo o nulo y muy carbonatada","It is black and very bitter":"Es negra y muy amarga","It is a lager":"Es una lager","It has very low alcohol, under 2%":"Tiene alcohol muy bajo, por debajo del 2 %","Geuze: gold, sour, low or no bitterness, medium-high alcohol, sediment and lots of bubbles.":"Geuze: dorada, ácida, amargor bajo o nulo, alcohol medio-alto, sedimento y muchas burbujas.","It is not black or bitter, not a lager, and its alcohol is medium to high.":"No es negra ni amarga, no es una lager y su alcohol es medio-alto.","American/international pale lager":"Lager clara estadounidense/internacional","Straw-gold, light aroma, low-medium bitterness, medium alcohol, high carbonation.":"Pajiza-dorada, aroma ligero, amargor bajo-medio, alcohol medio, carbonatación alta.","Gold lager, bread crumb, subtle hops; low-medium bitterness. 'Hell' = pale.":"Lager dorada, miga, lúpulo sutil; amargor bajo-medio. «Hell» = claro.","Easy straw-gold ale, subtle crumb, medium bitterness; also golden ale.":"Ale fácil pajiza-dorada, miga sutil, amargor medio; también golden ale.","Copper-brown lager, toast, nut; 'dunkel' = dark.":"Lager cobriza-marrón, tostado, avellana; «dunkel» = oscuro.","Porter / stout":"Porter / stout","Brown or black ales, coffee and chocolate; 'imperial' = very high alcohol.":"Ales marrones o negras, café y chocolate; «imperial» = alcohol muy alto.","Often amber ale, intense malt, full, sweet, high/very high alcohol; ages well.":"Ale a menudo ámbar, malta intensa, llena, dulce, alcohol alto/muy alto; envejece.","Czech or German pilsner":"Pilsner checa o alemana","Straw-gold lager, subtle spicy-floral hops, medium-high bitterness.":"Lager pajiza-dorada, lúpulo sutil especiado-floral, amargor medio-alto.","English amber-copper ale, biscuit/caramel, subtle hops, medium-high bitterness.":"Ale inglesa ámbar-cobre, galleta/caramelo, lúpulo sutil, amargor medio-alto.","APA · American IPA · hazy IPA":"APA · American IPA · hazy IPA","Medium-high bitterness · high bitterness, stronger · hazy, less bitter.":"Amargor medio-alto · amargor alto, más fuerte · turbia, menos amarga.","Weissbier / hefeweizen":"Weissbier / hefeweizen","Hazy, banana and clove, wheat, low bitterness, highly carbonated.":"Turbia, plátano y clavo, trigo, amargor bajo, muy carbonatada.","Witbier / blanche":"Witbier / blanche","Hazy, coriander and orange peel, wheat, low bitterness.":"Turbia, cilantro y piel de naranja, trigo, amargor bajo.","Dubbel vs tripel":"Dubbel vs tripel","Dubbel copper-brown, high alcohol; tripel gold, even higher alcohol.":"Dubbel cobriza-marrón, alcohol alto; tripel dorada, alcohol aún más alto.","Gold-amber, orange, peach, pepper; can be slightly sour.":"Dorada-ámbar, naranja, melocotón, pimienta; puede ser algo ácida.","Straw, hazy, moderately sour, low alcohol; cultured yeast and bacteria.":"Pajiza, turbia, moderadamente ácida, alcohol bajo; levaduras y bacterias cultivadas.","Gold, sour, farmyard and fruit; spontaneous fermentation; highly carbonated.":"Dorada, ácida, corral y fruta; fermentación espontánea; muy carbonatada.","Storing beer":"Conservar la cerveza","Beer starts changing as soon as it is brewed and is easily damaged by oxygen, heat and light. Drink it fresh: some beers benefit from ageing, but most are best young; over time hop aroma and bitterness fade and paper or wet cardboard notes appear. Check for a 'bottled on' or 'best before/use by' date. Keep it cool, ideally refrigerated even for short-term storage: at room temperature it goes stale faster, and warmth degrades it quickly.":"La cerveza empieza a cambiar en cuanto se elabora y se estropea fácilmente con oxígeno, calor y luz. Bébela fresca: algunas mejoran con el tiempo, pero la mayoría están mejor jóvenes; con el tiempo el amargor y los aromas de lúpulo se apagan y aparecen notas de papel o cartón mojado. Conviene mirar las fechas de «embotellado el» o «consumir preferentemente antes de». Guárdala en fresco, idealmente en el frigorífico aunque sea por poco tiempo: a temperatura ambiente envejece más rápido y el calor la degrada enseguida.","Protect it from daylight and artificial light, which can create unpleasant aromas known as light strike. Cans and kegs are opaque and protect the beer; brown bottles block almost all damaging light; green or clear bottles give little or no protection and should be stored in sealed boxes. Keep it sealed to protect it from oxygen and keep aromas and carbonation: once opened, bottles and cans should be drunk straight away. Keg beer is packed with carbon dioxide, which protects it from oxygen and keeps it fresh for longer.":"Protégela de la luz, natural o artificial, que puede crear olores desagradables: es el «golpe de luz». Latas y barriles son opacos y protegen la cerveza; las botellas marrones bloquean casi toda la luz dañina; las verdes o transparentes protegen poco o nada y deben guardarse en cajas cerradas. Mantenla cerrada, para protegerla del oxígeno y conservar aromas y gas: una botella o lata abierta se bebe enseguida. La cerveza de barril se envasa con dióxido de carbono, que la protege del oxígeno y la mantiene fresca más tiempo.","Drink fresh: hops and bitterness fade, cardboard appears; check dates":"Beber fresca: el lúpulo y el amargor se apagan, aparece el cartón; mirar las fechas","Keep cool, ideally refrigerated":"En fresco, idealmente en frigorífico","Away from light: cans and kegs opaque, brown bottles fine, green or clear in sealed boxes":"Lejos de la luz: latas y barriles opacos, botellas marrones bien, verdes y transparentes en cajas cerradas","Sealed: drink at once when opened; CO2-filled kegs stay fresh longer":"Cerrada: abierta se bebe enseguida; el barril con CO2 dura más fresco","Three faults to recognise":"Tres defectos que reconocer","Poor storage or maintenance can cause unpleasant aromas and flavours. Staling happens to most beers over time and is sped up by heat and oxygen: hop aromas and bitterness fade and paper or wet cardboard notes appear. Light strike (skunking) is caused when light hits hop compounds, giving an unpleasant skunky, scorched-hair or cat-urine smell.":"Una mala conservación o un mal mantenimiento pueden dar olores y sabores desagradables. El envejecimiento oxidativo (staling) afecta a casi todas las cervezas con el tiempo y se acelera con calor y oxígeno: el amargor y los aromas de lúpulo se apagan y aparecen notas de papel o cartón mojado. El golpe de luz (skunking) se produce cuando la luz actúa sobre los compuestos del lúpulo y da un olor desagradable a mofeta, pelo chamuscado u orina de gato.","Bacterial infection is commonly caused by bacteria growing in poorly maintained beer lines (the hoses connecting kegs to taps) and gives a mix of unwelcome flavours such as vinegar and rancid butter. Prevention is simple: fresh, cold, dark, sealed beer and clean equipment.":"La infección bacteriana suele deberse a bacterias que crecen en líneas de tiraje mal mantenidas (los tubos que unen los barriles con los grifos) y da una mezcla de notas desagradables como vinagre y mantequilla rancia. La prevención es sencilla: cerveza fresca, fría, a oscuras, cerrada y equipos limpios.","Staling: paper, wet cardboard; hops and bitterness faded; heat and oxygen":"Staling: papel, cartón mojado; lúpulo y amargor apagados; calor y oxígeno","Light strike: skunky, scorched hair, cat urine; light on hop compounds":"Golpe de luz: mofeta, pelo chamuscado, orina de gato; luz sobre el lúpulo","Bacterial infection: vinegar, rancid butter; dirty beer lines":"Infección bacteriana: vinagre, mantequilla rancia; líneas de tiraje sucias","Glassware and pouring from the keg":"Vasos y tiraje del barril","There is a huge range of glassware, and personal preference, tradition and culture all matter. For tasting, a few features help: a rounded bowl helps swirling, inward-sloping walls capture aromas, and narrow glasses help head retention. Whatever the shape, the glass must be clean: odourless and free of detergent, dishwasher salts or dirt from unclean cloths. Bubbles clinging to the sides after pouring are a sign the glass is not completely clean.":"Hay muchísimos vasos y cuentan el gusto personal, la tradición y la cultura. Para catar ayudan algunas características: un cáliz redondeado facilita girar la cerveza, las paredes que se cierran hacia arriba retienen los aromas y un vaso estrecho ayuda a mantener la espuma. En cualquier caso el vaso debe estar limpio: sin olores ni restos de detergente, sales del lavavajillas o suciedad de paños. Burbujas pegadas a las paredes tras servir indican que el vaso no está del todo limpio.","Pouring keg beer: hold the glass below the tap at 45°, with the tap never touching the beer or the glass, and avoid touching the upper part of the glass with your hand. Open the tap fully and pour down the side until the glass is about 70% full. Then bring the glass upright and keep pouring into the centre to form a foam; turn off the tap at the right volume.":"Tirar del barril: sujeta el vaso bajo el grifo inclinado a 45°, sin que el grifo toque la cerveza ni el vaso y sin tocar con la mano la parte alta del vaso. Abre el grifo del todo y vierte por la pared hasta llenar el vaso un 70 % aproximadamente. Después endereza el vaso y sigue vertiendo en el centro para formar espuma; cierra el grifo al llegar al volumen.","Rounded bowl: swirling; inward walls: aromas; narrow glass: head retention":"Cáliz redondeado: girar; paredes cerradas: aromas; vaso estrecho: espuma","Clean glass: clinging bubbles = not clean":"Vaso limpio: burbujas pegadas = no limpio","Keg: 45°, tap fully open, down the side to 70%, then upright into the centre":"Barril: 45°, grifo abierto del todo, por la pared hasta el 70 %, luego recto al centro","The tap never touches beer or glass":"El grifo no toca la cerveza ni el vaso","Bottles, sediment and temperatures":"Botellas, sedimento y temperaturas","Opening a crown-capped bottle: steady the bottle with one hand and remove the cap with the opener in one single motion with the other. Pouring: hold the glass at 45° (not touching its upper part) and pour gently down the side; when the glass is 50–70% full, bring it upright and pour into the centre to create foam. With no sediment, pour the whole bottle. With sediment (bottle-conditioned beers), pour carefully, keeping the bottle tilted until the sediment nears the neck, then stop: a little beer always stays in the bottle. Leave the bottle on the table so the drinker can choose to swirl in the sediment. Weissbier and witbier, naturally hazy, are the exception: gently roll the bottle or can before opening and pour everything.":"Abrir una botella con chapa: sujeta la botella con una mano y con la otra quita la chapa con el abridor en un solo gesto. Servir: vaso inclinado a 45° (sin tocar la parte alta), cerveza vertida suavemente por la pared; cuando el vaso esté al 50–70 %, enderézalo y vierte en el centro para crear espuma. Sin sedimento se vierte todo. Con sedimento (cervezas acondicionadas en botella) se vierte con cuidado, manteniendo la botella inclinada hasta que el poso se acerque al cuello, y entonces se para: siempre queda algo de cerveza en la botella. Deja la botella en la mesa para que quien bebe decida si añade el sedimento. Weissbier y witbier, turbias por naturaleza, son la excepción: se hace rodar suavemente la botella o lata antes de abrirla y se vierte todo.","Personal preference matters a lot for temperature, but there are general rules. Light to medium aroma, low to medium alcohol (international lager, pilsner, weissbier): well chilled, 3–7 °C (37–45 °F). Medium to pronounced aroma, medium to high alcohol (porter, APA, American IPA): chilled, 7–12 °C (45–54 °F). Complex, pronounced aroma, high to very high alcohol (barley wine, dubbel): lightly chilled, 12–15 °C (54–59 °F).":"En la temperatura cuenta mucho el gusto personal, pero hay reglas generales. Aroma de ligero a medio y alcohol de bajo a medio (lager internacional, pilsner, weissbier): bien fría, 3–7 °C. Aroma de medio a pronunciado y alcohol medio-alto (porter, APA, American IPA): fría, 7–12 °C. Estilos complejos, muy aromáticos, con alcohol alto o muy alto (barley wine, dubbel): ligeramente fresca, 12–15 °C.","Crown cap: steady bottle, one single motion":"Chapa: botella sujeta, un solo gesto","Bottle: 45°, down the side, at 50–70% upright and pour into the centre":"Botella: 45°, por la pared, al 50–70 % enderezar y verter al centro","With sediment: stop when it reaches the neck; leave bottle on table; weissbier/witbier: roll and pour all":"Con sedimento: parar al llegar al cuello; botella en la mesa; weissbier y witbier: rodar y verter todo","3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel":"3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel","Preferences and primary interactions":"Preferencias e interacciones primarias","People differ in their sensitivity to tastes and aromas: a perfect pairing for one person may seem ordinary or even unsuccessful to another, so pairings should take the individual's preferences and sensitivities into account. Food always influences how a drink tastes; how much depends on the person and on the level of the interacting elements. These are principles of perception rather than 'rules'.":"Cada persona tiene una sensibilidad distinta a sabores y aromas: un maridaje perfecto para alguien puede parecer normal o incluso fallido a otra, así que hay que tener en cuenta sus preferencias y sensibilidades. La comida siempre influye en cómo se percibe una bebida; cuánto, depende de la persona y de la intensidad de los elementos. Más que «reglas», son principios de percepción.","Primary interactions on beer. Sweetness in food: beer seems less sweet, more acidic and more bitter. Umami: the same, less sweet, more acidic and more bitter. Acidity in food: beer seems sweeter, less acidic and less bitter. Salt: the same, sweeter, less acidic and less bitter. Also, chilli heat increases the perception of alcohol, and bitterness in food increases bitterness in the beer.":"Interacciones primarias sobre la cerveza. Dulzor en la comida: cerveza menos dulce, más ácida y más amarga. Umami: lo mismo, menos dulce, más ácida y más amarga. Acidez en la comida: cerveza más dulce, menos ácida y menos amarga. Sal: lo mismo, más dulce, menos ácida y menos amarga. Además, el picante aumenta la percepción del alcohol y el amargor de la comida aumenta el de la cerveza.","Personal preferences and sensitivities first":"Preferencias y sensibilidades personales ante todo","Sweet and umami food: beer less sweet, more acidic, more bitter":"Dulce y umami en la comida: cerveza menos dulce, más ácida, más amarga","Acid and salt food: beer sweeter, less acidic, less bitter":"Acidez y sal en la comida: cerveza más dulce, menos ácida, menos amarga","Chilli: more perceived alcohol; bitter food: more bitter beer":"Picante: más alcohol percibido; comida amarga: cerveza más amarga","Sensitive styles, intensity and aromas":"Estilos «sensibles», intensidad y aromas","Beers are generally very food-friendly, but some styles interact more. High-bitterness styles such as American IPA can seem even more bitter with sweetness, umami or bitterness in the food. High-acidity styles such as geuze can seem even more acidic with sweetness or umami. High or very high-alcohol styles such as barley wine and tripel can notably increase the burning sensation of chilli heat.":"Las cervezas suelen ser muy amigas de la comida, pero algunos estilos interactúan más. Los estilos muy amargos como la American IPA parecen aún más amargos con comida dulce, rica en umami o amarga. Los estilos muy ácidos como la geuze parecen aún más ácidos con dulzor o umami. Los estilos de alcohol alto o muy alto, como el barley wine y la tripel, aumentan claramente el ardor del picante.","Two other considerations. Intensity: dish and beer should have a similar flavour intensity, or one will overpower the other. Aromas: beers recall many foods (bread, honey, chocolate and coffee from malt; fruit, tea and herbs from hops; fruit and spice from yeast). Looking for similar or complementary aromas in beer and food creates a familiar connection and can lead to wonderful pairings, such as a chocolatey stout with a cocoa dessert.":"Otras dos consideraciones. Intensidad: plato y cerveza deben tener una intensidad de sabor parecida; si no, uno tapa al otro. Aromas: las cervezas recuerdan muchos alimentos (pan, miel, chocolate y café de la malta; fruta, té y hierbas del lúpulo; fruta y especias de la levadura). Buscar aromas parecidos o complementarios entre cerveza y plato crea un vínculo familiar y puede dar maridajes estupendos, como una stout achocolatada con un postre de cacao.","High bitterness (American IPA): worse with sweet, umami, bitter":"Muy amargas (American IPA): peor con dulce, umami, amargo","High acidity (geuze): worse with sweet and umami":"Muy ácidas (geuze): peor con dulce y umami","High alcohol (barley wine, tripel): more chilli burn":"Muy alcohólicas (barley wine, tripel): más ardor con el picante","Similar intensity; similar or complementary aromas":"Intensidad parecida; aromas parecidos o complementarios","What are the three main enemies of beer in storage?":"¿Cuáles son los tres enemigos principales de la cerveza al conservarla?","Oxygen, heat and light":"Oxígeno, calor y luz","Cold, darkness and humidity":"Frío, oscuridad y humedad","Carbon dioxide, cold and glass":"Dióxido de carbono, frío y vidrio","Sugar, yeast and hops":"Azúcar, levadura y lúpulo","Oxygen, heat and light easily damage beer.":"El oxígeno, el calor y la luz estropean fácilmente la cerveza.","Cold and darkness protect it; keg CO2 shields it from oxygen.":"El frío y la oscuridad la protegen; el CO2 del barril la defiende del oxígeno.","What usually happens to a beer kept too long?":"¿Qué suele pasarle a una cerveza guardada demasiado tiempo?","Hop aroma and bitterness fade; paper or cardboard notes appear":"El amargor y el lúpulo se apagan; aparecen notas de papel o cartón","It becomes more bitter and hoppy":"Se vuelve más amarga y lupulada","It becomes stronger in alcohol":"Se vuelve más alcohólica","It gains more bubbles":"Gana más burbujas","This is staling: hops and bitterness fade, cardboard notes arrive.":"Es el envejecimiento oxidativo (staling): lúpulo y amargor se apagan, llega el cartón.","Over time bitterness falls rather than rises; alcohol does not increase and bubbles tend to drop.":"Con el tiempo el amargor baja, no sube; el alcohol no aumenta y las burbujas tienden a disminuir.","Which container protects beer LEAST from light?":"¿Qué envase protege PEOR la cerveza de la luz?","Clear glass bottle":"Botella transparente","Brown bottle":"Botella marrón","Can":"Lata","Keg":"Barril","Clear (or green) glass gives little or no protection: keep it in sealed boxes.":"El vidrio transparente (o verde) protege poco o nada: mejor en cajas cerradas.","Cans and kegs are opaque; brown glass blocks almost all damaging light.":"Latas y barriles son opacos; el vidrio marrón bloquea casi toda la luz dañina.","Why does keg beer stay fresh longer?":"¿Por qué la cerveza de barril se mantiene fresca más tiempo?","It is packed with carbon dioxide, which protects it from oxygen":"Se envasa con dióxido de carbono, que la protege del oxígeno","It contains preservatives":"Contiene conservantes","It has more alcohol":"Tiene más alcohol","It is pasteurised twice":"Se pasteuriza dos veces","The keg is packed with CO2, which keeps oxygen away.":"El barril lleva CO2, que mantiene alejado el oxígeno.","The other reasons are not the point: protection from oxygen makes the difference.":"Las otras razones no son el motivo: lo que marca la diferencia es la protección frente al oxígeno.","A bottle of beer has been opened: when should it be drunk?":"Se ha abierto una botella de cerveza: ¿cuándo hay que beberla?","Straight away":"Enseguida","Within a week in the fridge":"En una semana en el frigorífico","Within a month":"En un mes","Whenever, if recapped":"Cuando se quiera, si se tapa","Once opened, bottles and cans should be drunk at once to keep aroma and carbonation.":"Una vez abiertas, botellas y latas se beben enseguida para no perder aromas y gas.","Beer is unlike sake or wine: opened, it quickly loses bubbles and freshness.":"La cerveza no es como el sake o el vino: abierta pierde pronto gas y frescura.","What causes light strike (skunking)?":"¿Qué provoca el «golpe de luz» (skunking)?","Light acting on hop compounds":"La luz que actúa sobre los compuestos del lúpulo","Bacteria in beer lines":"Bacterias en las líneas de tiraje","Too much roasted malt":"Demasiada malta tostada","Excessive cold":"El frío excesivo","Light changes hop compounds and creates unpleasant smells.":"La luz transforma compuestos del lúpulo y crea olores desagradables.","Bacteria in lines give vinegar and rancid butter. Roasted malt and cold do not cause this fault.":"Las bacterias de las líneas dan vinagre y mantequilla rancia. La malta tostada y el frío no causan este defecto.","Which smells indicate light strike?":"¿Qué olores indican golpe de luz?","Skunky, scorched hair, cat urine":"Mofeta, pelo chamuscado, orina de gato","Paper and wet cardboard":"Papel y cartón mojado","Caramel and toffee":"Caramelo y toffee","Light strike gives a skunky, scorched-hair or cat-urine smell.":"El golpe de luz da olor a mofeta, pelo chamuscado u orina de gato.","Paper and cardboard signal staling; vinegar and rancid butter bacterial infection.":"Papel y cartón indican staling; vinagre y mantequilla rancia, infección bacteriana.","A draught beer tastes of vinegar and rancid butter. What is the most likely cause?":"Una cerveza de barril sabe a vinagre y mantequilla rancia. ¿Cuál es la causa más probable?","Bacterial infection in poorly maintained beer lines":"Infección bacteriana en líneas de tiraje sucias","Light strike":"Golpe de luz","A glass that is too cold":"Un vaso demasiado frío","Too much hops":"Demasiado lúpulo","Bacteria in the hoses connecting keg and tap give vinegar and rancid butter.":"Las bacterias en los tubos que unen barril y grifo dan vinagre y mantequilla rancia.","Light strike smells different (skunky) and kegs are opaque. Cold and hops do not create vinegar.":"El golpe de luz huele distinto (mofeta) y el barril es opaco. El frío y el lúpulo no crean vinagre.","What speeds up staling?":"¿Qué acelera el envejecimiento oxidativo (staling)?","Heat and oxygen":"Calor y oxígeno","Cold and darkness":"Frío y oscuridad","Brown bottles":"Botellas marrones","Carbon dioxide":"Dióxido de carbono","Staling comes faster with heat and oxygen.":"El staling llega antes con calor y oxígeno.","Cold, dark, brown glass and CO2 protect beer rather than ageing it.":"El frío, la oscuridad, el vidrio marrón y el CO2 protegen la cerveza, no la envejecen.","After pouring, bubbles cling to the sides of the glass. What does this show?":"Tras servir, quedan burbujas pegadas a las paredes del vaso. ¿Qué indican?","The glass is not completely clean":"Que el vaso no está del todo limpio","The beer is very fresh":"Que la cerveza es muy fresca","The beer is bottle-conditioned":"Que la cerveza está acondicionada en botella","The glass is too narrow":"Que el vaso es demasiado estrecho","Clinging bubbles signal residue or dirt on the glass.":"Las burbujas pegadas indican restos o suciedad en el vaso.","They do not depend on freshness, bottle-conditioning or glass shape.":"No dependen de la frescura, del acondicionamiento ni de la forma del vaso.","Which glass feature helps head retention?":"¿Qué característica del vaso ayuda a mantener la espuma?","A narrow shape":"Una forma estrecha","A very wide, open bowl":"Un cáliz muy ancho y abierto","A warm glass":"Un vaso caliente","Detergent residue":"Restos de detergente","Narrow glasses help the foam last.":"Los vasos estrechos ayudan a que la espuma dure.","A rounded bowl helps swirling, inward walls hold aromas. Detergent harms the foam.":"Un cáliz redondeado ayuda a girar y las paredes cerradas retienen los aromas. El detergente daña la espuma.","Pouring from the keg, how far do you fill with the glass tilted at 45°?":"Al tirar del barril, ¿hasta dónde se llena con el vaso inclinado a 45°?","To about 70% full":"Hasta un 70 % aproximadamente","Right to the brim":"Hasta el borde","To 20%":"Hasta el 20 %","The glass is never tilted":"Nunca se inclina el vaso","Pour down the side to about 70%, then upright and pour into the centre for foam.":"Se vierte por la pared hasta un 70 %, luego se endereza y se vierte al centro para la espuma.","Filling entirely tilted would leave little foam; 20% is too early.":"Llenar todo inclinado dejaría poca espuma; el 20 % es demasiado pronto.","Which rule applies to the tap when pouring keg beer?":"¿Qué regla se aplica al grifo al tirar cerveza?","It must not touch the beer or the glass":"No debe tocar la cerveza ni el vaso","It should be dipped in the beer":"Debe sumergirse en la cerveza","It is opened only halfway":"Se abre solo a medias","It should rest on the glass rim":"Debe apoyarse en el borde del vaso","The tap never touches beer or glass, for hygiene; it is opened fully.":"El grifo nunca toca cerveza ni vaso, por higiene; se abre del todo.","The tap is opened fully, not halfway, and is never dipped or rested on the glass.":"El grifo se abre del todo, no a medias, y no se sumerge ni se apoya.","How is a crown-capped bottle opened correctly?":"¿Cómo se abre correctamente una botella con chapa?","Steady the bottle with one hand; remove the cap with the opener in one motion":"Botella sujeta con una mano y chapa fuera con el abridor en un solo gesto","With several small taps":"Con varios golpecitos","By shaking the bottle first":"Agitando antes la botella","With a corkscrew":"Con un sacacorchos","One single, smooth motion while steadying the bottle.":"Un solo gesto firme, sujetando la botella.","Tapping or shaking makes the beer foam over; a corkscrew is for corks.":"Los golpecitos o agitarla hacen que la cerveza rebose; el sacacorchos es para tapones de corcho.","A bottle-conditioned beer with sediment is being served. What do you do?":"Se sirve una cerveza acondicionada en botella con sedimento. ¿Qué se hace?","Pour carefully and stop when the sediment reaches the neck":"Se vierte con cuidado y se para cuando el poso llega al cuello","Shake the bottle and pour everything":"Se agita la botella y se vierte todo","Filter the beer through a napkin":"Se filtra la cerveza con una servilleta","Throw away the first third":"Se tira el primer tercio","Keep the bottle tilted and stop as the sediment nears the neck; a little beer stays behind.":"Se mantiene la botella inclinada y se para cuando el poso se acerca al cuello; queda algo de cerveza.","Rolling and pouring everything is for weissbier and witbier, not beers meant to stay clear.":"Agitar y verter todo es la técnica para weissbier y witbier, no para cervezas que se quieren limpias.","Why leave the bottle on the table after serving a beer with sediment?":"¿Por qué se deja la botella en la mesa tras servir una cerveza con sedimento?","So the drinker can choose to add the sediment":"Para que quien bebe pueda decidir si añade el sedimento","To show the price":"Para enseñar el precio","Because throwing it away is banned":"Porque está prohibido tirarla","To let it cool":"Para que se enfríe","The drinker decides whether to have the sediment in the glass.":"Es el cliente quien decide si quiere el sedimento en el vaso.","It is about personal choice: the other reasons make no sense.":"Es cuestión de gusto personal: las otras razones no tienen sentido.","How are bottled weissbier and witbier usually served?":"¿Cómo se sirven normalmente la weissbier y la witbier embotelladas?","Gently roll the bottle before opening and pour everything":"Se hace rodar suavemente la botella antes de abrirla y se vierte todo","Leave the sediment in the bottle":"Se deja el sedimento en la botella","Filter them":"Se filtran","Serve them warm":"Se sirven calientes","They are naturally hazy: the sediment is mixed back in.":"Son turbias por naturaleza: el sedimento se reincorpora.","For these styles the sediment is not left behind; weissbier is served well chilled.":"En estos estilos no se deja el sedimento; la weissbier se sirve bien fría.","At what temperature is a pilsner or weissbier served?":"¿A qué temperatura se sirve una pilsner o una weissbier?","Well chilled, 3–7 °C":"Bien fría, 3–7 °C","Chilled, 7–12 °C":"Fría, 7–12 °C","Lightly chilled, 12–15 °C":"Ligeramente fresca, 12–15 °C","Room temperature, 20 °C":"Ambiente, 20 °C","Light-medium aroma and low-medium alcohol: well chilled, 3–7 °C.":"Aroma ligero-medio y alcohol bajo-medio: bien fría, 3–7 °C.","7–12 °C suits porter and IPA, 12–15 °C barley wine and dubbel.":"7–12 °C es para porter e IPA, 12–15 °C para barley wine y dubbel.","At what temperature should a barley wine be served?":"¿A qué temperatura conviene servir un barley wine?","Below freezing":"Bajo cero","Complex, high-alcohol styles: 12–15 °C to enjoy their aromas.":"Estilos complejos y muy alcohólicos: 12–15 °C para disfrutar sus aromas.","Too cold would mute the barley wine's complex aromas.":"Demasiado frío taparía los aromas complejos del barley wine.","Porter, American pale ale and American IPA are usually served…":"Porter, American pale ale y American IPA se sirven normalmente…","chilled, 7–12 °C":"frías, 7–12 °C","well chilled, 3–7 °C":"bien frías, 3–7 °C","lightly chilled, 12–15 °C":"ligeramente frescas, 12–15 °C","warm, 40 °C":"calientes, 40 °C","Medium to pronounced aroma, medium to high alcohol: 7–12 °C.":"Aroma medio-pronunciado y alcohol medio-alto: 7–12 °C.","3–7 °C is for lagers and weissbier, 12–15 °C for barley wine and dubbel.":"3–7 °C para lagers y weissbier, 12–15 °C para barley wine y dubbel.","What effect do salt and acidity in food have on beer?":"¿Qué efecto tienen la sal y la acidez de la comida en la cerveza?","Sweeter, less acidic, less bitter":"Más dulce, menos ácida, menos amarga","Less sweet, more acidic, more bitter":"Menos dulce, más ácida, más amarga","More alcoholic":"Más alcohólica","No effect":"Ningún efecto","Salt and acidity soften the beer.":"La sal y la acidez «suavizan» la cerveza.","Less sweet, more acidic and more bitter is the effect of sweetness and umami. Chilli raises perceived alcohol.":"Menos dulce, más ácida y más amarga es el efecto del dulzor y el umami. El picante aumenta el alcohol percibido.","How does a very sweet dessert change the perception of beer?":"¿Cómo cambia un postre muy dulce la percepción de la cerveza?","Less sweet, more acidic and more bitter":"Menos dulce, más ácida y más amarga","Sweeter and less bitter":"Más dulce y menos amarga","More fizzy":"Con más burbujas","Sweetness in food lowers beer's sweetness and raises its acidity and bitterness.":"El dulzor de la comida reduce el de la cerveza y aumenta su acidez y amargor.","The 'sweeter, less bitter' effect comes from salt and acidity.":"El efecto «más dulce, menos amarga» viene de la sal y la acidez.","What does chilli heat do to a beer?":"¿Qué le hace el picante de la guindilla a una cerveza?","Increases the perception of alcohol":"Aumenta la percepción del alcohol","Makes it sweeter":"La hace más dulce","Chilli heat accentuates the sense of alcohol, especially in strong beers.":"El picante acentúa la sensación de alcohol, sobre todo en cervezas fuertes.","Chilli neither sweetens the beer nor removes bitterness.":"El picante no endulza la cerveza ni quita amargor.","A very spicy dish: which beer is most likely to burn?":"Un plato muy picante: ¿qué cerveza puede quemar más?","A tripel or a barley wine":"Una tripel o un barley wine","A Berliner weisse":"Una Berliner weisse","A light pale lager":"Una lager clara ligera","A blonde ale":"Una blonde ale","High or very high-alcohol styles greatly increase the chilli burn.":"Los estilos de alcohol alto o muy alto aumentan mucho el ardor del picante.","Berliner weisse, light lagers and blonde ales have low or medium alcohol.":"Berliner weisse, lagers ligeras y blonde ales tienen alcohol bajo o medio.","With an umami-rich dish, which style may seem even more bitter?":"Con un plato rico en umami, ¿qué estilo puede parecer aún más amargo?","High-bitterness styles like American IPA get even more bitter with umami, sweetness or bitterness.":"Los estilos muy amargos como la American IPA se vuelven aún más amargos con umami, dulzor o amargor.","Weissbier and Berliner weisse have low bitterness; helles low to medium.":"Weissbier y Berliner weisse tienen amargor bajo; la helles de bajo a medio.","Why can a geuze become difficult with a dessert?":"¿Por qué una geuze puede complicarse con un postre?","Sweetness in the food makes it seem even more acidic":"El dulzor de la comida la hace parecer aún más ácida","Sweetness makes it seem stronger":"El dulzor la hace parecer más alcohólica","The dessert makes it cloudy":"El postre la enturbia","The dessert removes the bubbles":"El postre le quita las burbujas","High-acidity styles seem even more acidic with sweetness or umami in food.":"Los estilos muy ácidos parecen aún más ácidos con dulzor o umami.","Dessert does not affect alcohol, clarity or bubbles.":"El postre no afecta al alcohol, la limpidez ni las burbujas.","Why should beer and dish have a similar flavour intensity?":"¿Por qué cerveza y plato deben tener una intensidad de sabor parecida?","So one does not overpower the other":"Para que uno no tape al otro","So the beer is colder":"Para que la cerveza esté más fría","To increase the alcohol":"Para aumentar el alcohol","To reduce the bubbles":"Para reducir las burbujas","With different intensities, the stronger one masks the more delicate.":"Con intensidades distintas, el más fuerte tapa al más delicado.","Intensity has nothing to do with temperature, alcohol or bubbles.":"La intensidad no tiene que ver con temperatura, alcohol o burbujas.","A stout with coffee and chocolate notes alongside a cocoa dessert: which principle does this pairing use?":"Una stout con notas de café y chocolate con un postre de cacao: ¿en qué principio se basa el maridaje?","Similar or complementary aromas in beer and food":"Aromas parecidos o complementarios entre cerveza y comida","Salt reduces bitterness":"La sal reduce el amargor","Chilli raises alcohol":"El picante aumenta el alcohol","Colour contrast":"Contraste de color","Similar aromas create a familiar connection between beer and dish.":"Aromas parecidos crean un vínculo familiar entre cerveza y plato.","No salt or chilli is involved here, and colour is not a pairing criterion.":"Aquí no intervienen sal ni picante, y el color no es un criterio de maridaje.","Why can the same pairing please one person and not another?":"¿Por qué el mismo maridaje puede gustar a una persona y no a otra?","People have different preferences and sensitivities":"Cada persona tiene preferencias y sensibilidades distintas","Because the beer changes from glass to glass":"Porque la cerveza cambia de un vaso a otro","Because there are fixed rules":"Porque existen reglas fijas","It never happens":"Nunca ocurre","People perceive tastes and aromas differently: interactions are principles, not rules.":"Cada persona percibe sabores y aromas de forma distinta: las interacciones son principios, no reglas.","Precisely because there are no fixed rules, the individual matters.":"Precisamente porque no hay reglas fijas hay que tener en cuenta a la persona.","Four storage rules":"Cuatro reglas de conservación","Drink fresh, keep cool, protect from light, keep sealed.":"Beber fresca, guardar en fresco, protegida de la luz, cerrada.","Staling":"Staling","Faded hops and bitterness, paper or wet cardboard; heat and oxygen.":"Lúpulo y amargor apagados, papel o cartón mojado; calor y oxígeno.","Light strike (skunking)":"Golpe de luz (skunking)","Light on hop compounds: skunky, scorched hair, cat urine.":"Luz sobre el lúpulo: mofeta, pelo chamuscado, orina de gato.","Bacterial infection":"Infección bacteriana","Dirty beer lines: vinegar, rancid butter.":"Líneas de tiraje sucias: vinagre, mantequilla rancia.","Bottles and light":"Botellas y luz","Brown: almost full protection; green or clear: little or none.":"Marrón: protege casi del todo; verde o transparente: poco o nada.","Pouring keg beer":"Tirar del barril","45°, tap fully open, down the side to 70%, then upright into the centre.":"45°, grifo abierto, por la pared hasta el 70 %, luego recto al centro.","Beer with sediment":"Cerveza con sedimento","Pour gently, stop when sediment reaches the neck; leave bottle on the table.":"Verter despacio, parar cuando el poso llega al cuello; botella en la mesa.","Serving temperatures":"Temperaturas de servicio","3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel.":"3–7 °C lager, pilsner, weissbier · 7–12 °C porter, APA, IPA · 12–15 °C barley wine, dubbel.","Sweet and umami food":"Dulce y umami en la comida","Beer less sweet, more acidic, more bitter.":"Cerveza menos dulce, más ácida, más amarga.","Acid and salt food":"Acidez y sal en la comida","Beer sweeter, less acidic, less bitter.":"Cerveza más dulce, menos ácida, menos amarga.","Food-sensitive styles":"Estilos «sensibles» en la mesa","American IPA (bitterness), geuze (acidity), barley wine and tripel (alcohol with chilli).":"American IPA (amargor), geuze (acidez), barley wine y tripel (alcohol con picante).","Malt and other sugar sources":"Malta y otras fuentes de azúcar","The brewing steps":"Los pasos de la elaboración","Hops and other flavourings":"Lúpulo y otros aromatizantes","Tasting beer":"Catar la cerveza","Malt-driven styles: some speciality malts":"Estilos de malta: con maltas especiales","Hop-driven styles":"Estilos de lúpulo","Yeast-driven styles":"Estilos de levadura","Sour styles":"Estilos ácidos","Storage and faults":"Conservación y defectos","Serving beer":"Servir la cerveza","Beer and food":"Cerveza y comida","Ingredients and production":"Ingredientes y producción","Beer styles":"Los estilos de cerveza","Storage, service and food":"Conservación, servicio y comida","Beer 1":"Cerveza 1","Beer 1 exam":"Examen Cerveza 1","Lessons, quizzes and flashcards on beer ingredients, brewing, styles and service.":"Lecciones, tests y tarjetas sobre ingredientes, elaboración, estilos y servicio de la cerveza.","Review beer ingredients, styles and terms":"Repasa ingredientes, estilos y términos de la cerveza","All of Beer 1":"Todo Cerveza 1","Lessons, flashcards and mistakes: only the Beer 1 syllabus.":"Lecciones, tarjetas y errores: solo el programa de Cerveza 1.","Beer 1 games":"Juegos de Cerveza 1","Short games on Beer 1 questions and terms.":"Juegos cortos sobre preguntas y términos de Cerveza 1.","Hi! I'm your beer goat 🍺":"¡Hola! Soy tu cabra de la cerveza 🍺","I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Beer 1 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"Te preparo un recorrido a medida para aprobar el examen Cerveza 1. Bastan 5 preguntas rápidas."});Object.assign(window.TWG_ESX.ar,{"The cooled wort goes into a fermentation vessel where yeast is added. During fermentation the yeast eats the sugars and creates alcohol, carbon dioxide and aromas. Remember the order: mill → mash → boil (with hops) → cool → ferment (with yeast).":"El mosto frío pasa a un fermentador donde se añade la levadura. Durante la fermentación la levadura consume los azúcares y crea alcohol, dióxido de carbono y aromas. Recordá el orden: moler → macerar → hervir (con lúpulo) → enfriar → fermentar (con levadura).","Enzymes are catalysts: here they break starch into sugars.":"Las enzimas son catalizadores: acá rompen el almidón en azúcares.","Adds alcohol":"Agregá alcohol","Yeast ferments again in the bottle, creating bubbles and a deposit at the bottom.":"La levadura vuelve a fermentar en la botella: creá burbujas y un poso en el fondo.","Makes beer sour":"Volvé ácida la cerveza","From added lemon juice":"De jugo de limón añadido","Pouring keg beer: hold the glass below the tap at 45°, with the tap never touching the beer or the glass, and avoid touching the upper part of the glass with your hand. Open the tap fully and pour down the side until the glass is about 70% full. Then bring the glass upright and keep pouring into the centre to form a foam; turn off the tap at the right volume.":"Tirar del barril: sujeta el vaso bajo el grifo inclinado a 45°, sin que el grifo toque la cerveza ni el vaso y sin tocar con la mano la parte alta del vaso. Abrí el grifo del todo y vierte por la pared hasta llenar el vaso un 70 % aproximadamente. Después endereza el vaso y seguí vertiendo en el centro para formar espuma; cierra el grifo al llegar al volumen.","No salt or chilli is involved here, and colour is not a pairing criterion.":"Acá no intervienen sal ni picante, y el color no es un criterio de maridaje.","Review beer ingredients, styles and terms":"Repasá ingredientes, estilos y términos de la cerveza"});
